window.FWN_UNDEAD_LEGION_CHAPTERS=(window.FWN_UNDEAD_LEGION_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1001,"title":"Chapter 1001: Judgement Has Arrived","paragraphs":["Far above the skies, space distorted silently before Michael and Wisdom stepped out from the folded void itself.","The moment Michael arrived within the vicinity of the capital, the entire atmosphere of the region subtly changed.","Unlike before, this time Michael made absolutely no effort to hide his presence. The effect was immediate.","The moment they appeared, countless powerful figures throughout the capital instantly sensed it. Several expressions changed instantly.","\"What is that...?\"","At the same time, even ordinary mortals throughout the capital subconsciously noticed something strange. Many civilians walking through the streets suddenly paused instinctively before looking upward in confusion. Some saw nothing. Others vaguely noticed a dark figure high above the clouds.","However, fortunately for them, Michael was far too high in the sky and his attention was not focused on them directly. Otherwise, merely looking at him in his current state would have been enough to seriously harm weaker mortals.","Ironically, the people suffering the most were actually the supernaturals below, thanks to their stronger senses. The moment their perception touched Michael’s presence, their expressions immediately changed drastically.","BOOM!","Inside a certain mage tower, one elderly mage suddenly coughed blood violently while stumbling backward.","\"H-Heavens...\"","His eyes trembled with horror. It felt like his senses had brushed against some terrifying abyss.","Inside another noble estate, a Grand Stage knight suddenly dropped to one knee while his instincts screamed in warning. Cold sweat poured down his face uncontrollably.","Meanwhile, several scouts and perception-focused supernaturals directly fainted on the spot after attempting to probe the figure in the sky.","Far above the capital, Michael quietly overlooked the massive city beneath him.","At the same time, deep within the royal palace, several powerful figures suddenly stood up simultaneously. Princess Priscilla’s expression changed sharply. The former king’s eyes narrowed instantly. Even Mage Lian abruptly looked toward the sky with a grave expression.","All of them had sensed it. Michael had arrived.","Meanwhile, the reactions of the two princes and Count Hallen were far more intense.","The moment they sensed Michael’s arrival, all three figures instantly lost the little composure they still possessed.","The Ninth Prince’s face turned deathly pale. He had just stood up when his legs weakened instantly beneath him and he collapsed heavily onto the floor.","\"N-No...\"","His voice trembled violently. Cold sweat poured down his body uncontrollably.","At this point, after personally sensing Michael’s terrifying presence from afar, the Ninth Prince finally realized something clearly. The person they had offended was not some genius, nor some talented young supernatural.","It was a monster. A genuine monster.","Beside him, the Tenth Prince looked no better. His body shook visibly while terror completely filled his eyes. Even Count Hallen nearly fainted outright. The pressure descending from the sky alone already made it difficult for him to breathe.","At this moment, all three finally understood just how ridiculous their previous actions had truly been.","Unfortunately, it was already too late.","The Ninth Prince suddenly crawled forward desperately.","\"Y-Your Majesty!\"","He looked toward Princess Priscilla and the former king almost pleadingly.","\"Save me! I-I was wrong! I truly did not know things would become like this!\"","His voice had completely lost all dignity now.","The Tenth Prince also hurriedly crawled forward afterward.","\"Aunt! Please! Please protect me! I-I know I was wrong! I’ll apologize! I’ll compensate him! I’ll do anything!\"","Meanwhile, Count Hallen had already completely collapsed onto the ground. His body trembled nonstop.","\"Y-Your Majesties...\"","His lips shook violently.","\"I-I only wanted to improve my standing with the empire. I never intended for things to escalate this far. I-I truly didn’t know...\"","At this point, all three looked miserable beyond words. The earlier arrogance they once carried had completely disappeared. Only fear remained.","Unfortunately for them, the expressions of everyone else inside the hall only became uglier. Especially Princess Priscilla, who no longer knew what exactly could be done anymore.","Michael had already arrived personally. And after everything that had happened, who here truly believed words alone could resolve this situation?","The former king slowly closed his eyes briefly before exhaling deeply. Even he felt a rare sense of helplessness now.","How ridiculous. A former ruler of an entire kingdom feeling helpless because of a single young man.","Yet after sensing Michael’s presence personally, the old king could no longer find the situation absurd. Even he had to admit it. That aura was far too terrifying.","Princess Priscilla slowly looked toward the three begging figures on the ground. Then she spoke coldly.","\"Do you think apologies matter now?\"","The Ninth Prince froze. The Tenth Prince’s face turned pale.","Princess Priscilla’s expression only became colder afterward.","\"You felt safe because the empire stood behind you. You believed Sir Mic could be suppressed. You believed he would fear consequences.\"","Her voice gradually sharpened.","\"But now?\"","She slowly pointed upward toward the sky beyond the palace.","\"Can you not feel it yourselves?\"","The entire hall fell silent again.","Of course they could feel it. Everyone could. That terrifying presence hanging above the capital felt less like a human being and more like some natural disaster waiting to descend at any moment.","The Ninth Prince’s body shook harder. At this point, he finally realized something truly horrifying. Michael might not even care anymore whether the kingdom protected them or not. With that kind of strength, he could simply kill them directly.","The Tenth Prince also clearly understood the same thing. Terror completely overwhelmed him.","\"Aunt... please...\"","His voice sounded desperate now.","\"You have to save me...\"","Princess Priscilla looked at him silently for several seconds. Then she slowly closed her eyes in despair.","Even if she wanted to save them, how?","Suddenly, space inside the meeting hall distorted silently.","The expressions of everyone present changed drastically.","Before anyone could even react properly, a figure appeared directly within the center of the hall.","Michael stood there calmly in black robes while faint spatial fluctuations distorted the air around him. Beside him floated Wisdom in its reduced form, its pure white eyes quietly sweeping across the room.","The entire meeting hall froze instantly.","The moment Michael’s gaze landed upon the Ninth Prince, the latter’s face instantly lost all color.","\"N-No...\"","His body trembled violently.","The Tenth Prince’s pupils also contracted sharply while Count Hallen nearly screamed outright.","Michael said nothing.","He merely looked at them quietly.","Then suddenly, the Tenth Prince’s body jerked upward violently.","\"GHHK—!\"","His feet left the ground instantly.","Both hands immediately grabbed at his throat desperately as if invisible hands had suddenly wrapped around his neck.","The surrounding space around him visibly distorted faintly.","His body slowly floated higher and higher into the air."]},{"number":1002,"title":"Chapter 1002: A Father","paragraphs":["\"T-Tenth Prince!\"","Several nearby nobles instinctively stood up in alarm.","BOOM!","A terrifying pressure suddenly exploded outward from Michael’s body.","The entire hall instantly shook violently.","Everyone who had stood up immediately froze in place.","Some weaker supernaturals directly coughed blood from the pressure alone.","Michael’s eyes remained emotionless.","The Tenth Prince continued struggling frantically in midair.","His face rapidly turned red.","Then purple.","His legs kicked wildly while both hands clawed desperately at the invisible force crushing his throat.","\"A-AUNT...!\"","His voice came out broken and hoarse.","Princess Priscilla’s expression changed sharply.","\"Sir Mic...\"","Michael finally spoke calmly.","\"Do not interfere.\"","The moment those words fell, the surrounding atmosphere became even colder.","Meanwhile, the Ninth Prince completely collapsed mentally.","\"DON’T KILL ME!\"","He suddenly screamed while crawling backward desperately across the floor.","\"I-I DIDN’T DO ANYTHING!\"","\"IT WAS HIM!\"","He pointed directly toward the floating Tenth Prince.","\"HE STARTED EVERYTHING!\"","\"HE WAS THE ONE WHO TARGETED ARIANNE!\"","The Tenth Prince’s eyes widened in disbelief even while being choked.","\"N-NINTH—!\"","Before he could finish speaking, the invisible pressure around his neck tightened further.","CRACK...!","A horrifying sound echoed faintly throughout the hall.","The Tenth Prince’s pupils shook violently from pain.","Count Hallen also completely broke down afterward.","\"I WAS WRONG!\"","He slammed his forehead repeatedly against the floor.","\"PLEASE SPARE ME!\"","\"I CAN COMPENSATE YOU!\"","\"I CAN GIVE YOU ANYTHING!\"","Michael slowly shifted his gaze toward him.","That single glance alone almost caused Count Hallen to faint.","Finally, Michael looked back toward the struggling Tenth Prince floating helplessly in the air.","For several seconds, he said nothing.","The entire meeting hall remained deathly silent aside from the choking sounds coming from the prince.","At first, Michael had truly believed this moment would make him lose control completely.","He had imagined that the moment he saw the Tenth Prince and the others responsible for everything, rage would completely consume him.","And yes...","He was angry.","But strangely enough, the fury inside him was not as explosive as he had expected.","At first, Michael did not understand why.","Then slowly...","He realized the answer himself.","They were too weak.","The moment that realization surfaced inside his mind, Michael suddenly lost all interest in dragging things out further.","The Ninth Prince.","The Tenth Prince.","Count Hallen.","Even the nobles trembling throughout the hall.","All of them were too weak. Too insignificant.","They were not enemies standing before him.","Michael suddenly understood something clearly.","The real enemy now was the empire. After killing these people, it meant he had avenged Arianne. Going after the empire was because they were now his enemies.","As for the Lionheart Kingdom, the people here were not even worthy of being called his enemies anymore.","The realization strangely calmed him further.","The invisible force around the Tenth Prince loosened slightly.","The prince immediately gasped violently for air while still floating helplessly in midair.","\"GHH...! HAA...!\"","Terror completely filled his eyes now.","Meanwhile, the Ninth Prince and Count Hallen both froze in confusion.","Michael slowly looked around the meeting hall afterward.","His calm gaze swept across every noble present.","No one dared meet his eyes.","Not even the former king, who could only watch helplessly as his two children stood at the edge of death.","Finally, Michael spoke quietly.","\"I thought I would hate all of you more.\"","\"But now that I’m here...\"","He looked toward the Tenth Prince again.","\"I only find all of this pathetic.\"","The Tenth Prince’s body trembled harder.","Michael’s eyes remained indifferent.","\"You destroyed someone’s life because you believed you could.\"","\"You cornered people because you believed there would be no consequences.\"","\"You treated others as disposable because you thought power protected you.\"","His gaze slowly shifted toward Count Hallen.","\"And you.\"","Count Hallen instantly slammed his forehead against the floor again.","\"P-PLEASE—!\"","Michael ignored him completely.","Then his eyes moved toward the Ninth Prince.","The Ninth Prince froze completely.","Michael stared at him for several seconds.","The Ninth Prince’s lips trembled violently.","\"I-I...\"","But no words came out.","Silence filled the hall once more.","Then Michael suddenly shook his head faintly.","\"This is enough.\"","Several expressions changed instantly.","Princess Priscilla’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Even the former king looked toward Michael carefully.","Meanwhile, the three people on the floor became even more terrified instead of relieved.","Michael slowly turned around afterward.","\"To continue wasting time here would only lower me further.\"","His voice echoed quietly throughout the hall.","\"The people in this kingdom are not worthy of being my enemies.\"","Those words caused countless expressions to become ugly instantly.","Some nobles lowered their heads in shame.","Others clenched their fists helplessly.","But no one could refute him.","Michael truly stood at an entirely different level now.","At that moment, the former king suddenly spoke.","\"Sir Mic.\"","His voice was calm.","The entire hall immediately turned toward him.","Michael’s gaze also shifted slowly toward the old man.","The former king looked directly at Michael without avoiding his eyes.","Even now, the old man still carried the bearing of a ruler.","For several seconds, he remained silent before finally speaking again.","\"I wish to ask one thing of you.\"","Michael looked at him quietly.","The former king continued calmly.","\"I do not wish to watch my children die with my own eyes.\"","\"They must die.\"","Michael’s answer came without hesitation.","The surrounding atmosphere immediately became heavier.","However, surprisingly—","The former king slowly nodded.","\"I know.\"","The old man’s voice sounded tired now.","\"Honestly... after everything that has happened, even I agree with you.\"","The Ninth Prince’s face instantly turned ghostly pale.","\"F-Father?!\"","The Tenth Prince also froze completely.","The former king ignored both of them entirely.","Instead, he simply looked toward Michael quietly.","\"They deserve death.\"","His words echoed heavily throughout the hall.","\"No matter their reasons, no matter their excuses, their actions brought disaster upon others and nearly destroyed this kingdom.\"","The old man slowly closed his eyes briefly.","\"But...\"","For the first time, his voice sounded older.","\"As a father... I cannot calmly sit here and watch my children die before my eyes.\""]},{"number":1003,"title":"Chapter 1003: Reflection","paragraphs":["Silence filled the hall afterward. Michael quietly stared at the old man for several seconds, and then slowly, something seemed to click within his mind. His expression changed slightly afterward, and for the first time since entering the hall, Michael looked at the former king with a somewhat complicated gaze.","The old man was not trying to save his sons anymore. He already understood that was impossible. Instead, he simply did not want to personally witness their deaths.","The former king slowly exhaled afterward before calmly taking several steps forward. \"Sir Mic,\" he said steadily, \"I hope that with my life, you will at least see some sincerity from this kingdom.\"","Several expressions changed instantly afterward. Princess Priscilla’s eyes widened sharply. \"Brother!\"","The former king ignored them all and simply continued speaking calmly. \"After this matter ends, the Lionheart Kingdom will forever treat you as an honored ally equal to the friend of our founding ancestor.\"","Many nobles immediately inhaled sharply. Then the old man continued further, \"And Mage Lian will officially become the Grand Advisor of the royal family after this matter concludes.\"","This time, even Mage Lian himself looked genuinely stunned. The former king slowly looked back toward Michael afterward. \"I cannot stop what must happen,\" he said calmly. \"But this old man still hopes the kingdom itself can survive beyond tonight.\"","Michael looked at the former king silently. For a moment, he wanted to say there was no need to go this far, but the words never left his mouth.","Because the only way to truly stop the old man from doing this was to spare his sons. And that was impossible.","The Ninth Prince had to die. The Tenth Prince had to die. No matter what the former king offered, no matter how sincere his expression looked, that result could not change.","Michael’s eyes flickered slightly afterward. Perhaps the former king understood that as well. Perhaps that was why he had chosen this path.","A father who could not save his children. A king who could not save his kingdom through strength. So in the end, he could only offer his own life as the final apology.","Princess Priscilla’s expression finally changed completely. \"Brother, stop,\" she said in a low voice. For the first time, there was something close to panic within it.","The former king did not look at her. He only smiled faintly and replied softly, \"It is fine.\"","Then, before anyone could react, he raised his hand. His palm struck the side of his own head.","PA!","The sound was not loud. There was no explosion of blood, no shattered skull, and no visible wound.","The former king simply stood there for a brief moment. Then the light in his eyes quietly went out.","His body remained upright for another second before slowly falling forward. \"Brother!\" Princess Priscilla’s voice finally broke.","The entire meeting hall descended into chaos afterward. Princess Priscilla rushed forward immediately, catching the former king’s falling body before it could hit the ground.","For the first time since Michael entered the palace, the calm and composed princess completely lost control. Her hands trembled slightly as she held the old man tightly.","\"Brother...?\" Her voice sounded hollow now. No response came.","The former king’s eyes remained slightly open, yet the life within them had already disappeared completely. Several nobles immediately knelt down in panic.","\"Your Majesty!\"","\"Your Majesty!!\"","Even some of the older generals who had followed the former king for decades lowered their heads heavily, their expressions filled with grief. The atmosphere within the hall instantly became suffocating.","Meanwhile, the Ninth Prince completely froze in place. The Tenth Prince still floated weakly in the air while staring blankly at his father’s corpse.","Neither of them had expected this outcome. Deep despair finally appeared within their eyes.","Meanwhile, Michael stood silently within the center of the hall while watching everything unfold around him. The crying, the grief, and the sorrow filling the room strangely made him feel conflicted for the first time since arriving here.","A strange heaviness slowly settled within his chest afterward. The former king was not innocent. As ruler, he naturally carried responsibility for the corruption and decay within the kingdom.","Yet at the very end, the old man still chose to die as a father instead of a king. That alone complicated Michael’s emotions more than he expected.","Michael quietly looked toward the former king’s corpse again. Then slowly, he realized something.","The world was not truly divided into simple heroes and villains. Most people only stood from their own side.","To Arianne, the Ninth Prince and Tenth Prince were monsters who ruined her life. To Michael, the people before him were guilty individuals who deserved punishment.","But to the former king, those same people were still his children. No matter how terrible they became and no matter how unforgivable their sins were, they were still his sons.","Michael’s gaze lowered slightly afterward. For the first time in a long while, he felt something close to self-reflection.","Strength truly changed perspective. Before today, Michael had subconsciously viewed himself as the one carrying out justice.","Even now, he still believed the princes deserved death. That belief had not changed in the slightest.","Yet watching the people inside the hall grieve for the former king made Michael realize another uncomfortable truth. In some people’s stories, he himself would become the villain.","Not because he believed he was wrong, but because life itself was complicated. The former king had not died because Michael directly killed him, yet everyone present understood the truth.","His death happened because Michael arrived here demanding blood. That reality could not be denied no matter how one looked at it.","Michael quietly closed his eyes briefly before slowly opening them again. For some reason, instead of making him unstable, the realization actually calmed him further.","The world was not black and white. There was no perfect justice.","No matter what path someone chose, another person somewhere would still curse them for it. And perhaps that was simply reality.","A hard truth. But strangely enough, understanding it also brought a certain clarity to Michael’s mind.","He no longer felt the need to desperately justify every action he took. Nor did he feel the need to pretend he stood entirely righteous above everyone else.","He would simply do what he believed needed to be done and accept the consequences attached to it. If others viewed him as a villain for those actions, then so be it.","Because in the end, everyone lived from their own perspective. And from Michael’s perspective, the people who destroyed Arianne’s life still had to die."]},{"number":1004,"title":"Chapter 1004: Revenge Finally Served","paragraphs":["Thanks to the former king’s final actions, Michael found his thoughts changing slightly. He was even less interested in dragging things further.","The atmosphere within the hall remained heavy with grief and panic. The Ninth Prince and Count Hallen remained frozen on the floor while the Tenth Prince floated weakly in the air.","Suddenly, all three figures jerked violently.","\"GHHK...!\"","The Ninth Prince instantly grabbed his throat. Count Hallen’s eyes widened in horror as both his hands clawed desperately at his neck. Even the Tenth Prince immediately began choking again.","Their bodies rose from the ground before being dragged directly toward Michael by an invisible force.","\"N-No...!\"","\"PLEASE...!\"","\"SPARE ME...!\"","The three screamed desperately while their bodies floated helplessly through the air. Michael’s expression remained calm throughout everything.","Princess Priscilla noticed his actions immediately, but this time she said nothing. Perhaps after her brother’s death, she no longer had the strength to interfere anymore. Or perhaps she already understood there was no point.","The surrounding nobles also remained silent despite their pale expressions.","Michael slowly turned his head afterward and glanced toward Mage Lian. The old mage stared back at him with a complicated gaze. Shock. Helplessness. Sorrow. And perhaps even slight understanding.","For several seconds, neither of them spoke. Then Michael simply gave the old mage a small nod.","The next moment, space distorted silently around Michael and the three struggling figures, and in the next instant all four disappeared from the meeting hall completely. Only the heavy atmosphere of grief remained behind.","Meanwhile, elsewhere within the royal palace, space twisted quietly once more. Michael reappeared within another location entirely.","It was a garden. A small stream flowed peacefully through the center while soft wind brushed gently against the leaves overhead. Compared to the suffocating atmosphere of the meeting hall, this place felt almost unnaturally calm.","Unfortunately, the three figures currently choking in midair could not appreciate any of it.","The Ninth Prince struggled wildly while tears streamed down his face. Count Hallen had already lost complete control of himself. Michael didn’t know if it was because of his age or something else, but the man’s bowels had let loose. The Tenth Prince still stared at Michael with pure terror within his eyes.","Michael quietly looked at the three people before him. Then finally, he spoke.","\"Initially, I planned to make the two of you suffer greatly before dying.\"","The Ninth Prince and Tenth Prince both trembled violently afterward. Michael’s eyes remained calm.","\"But in respect for your father, I changed my mind.\"","The moment those words fell, visible relief instantly appeared within the eyes of both princes. Meanwhile, Count Hallen’s face instead became even paler.","Throughout everything, Michael had completely ignored his existence. Count Hallen felt an overwhelming dread. The two princes still at least had the blood of the former king protecting them somewhat. But him? He was nothing.","Suddenly, the expressions of both princes froze completely. Their eyes instantly became vacant. Then their floating bodies dropped heavily onto the garden ground below.","THUD!","For a brief moment, neither of them moved. Count Hallen stared blankly in confusion amidst his pain.","Then suddenly, both princes began shaking violently.","\"GHH...!\"","Low grunts escaped from their mouths as their bodies started twitching nonstop across the garden floor. The Ninth Prince clawed desperately at the dirt beneath him. The Tenth Prince’s entire body arched unnaturally while veins bulged across his neck.","Yet strangely, neither of them screamed. It was as if their voices had become trapped inside their throats.","Count Hallen watched the scene unfold with widening eyes. Fear completely exploded within his heart afterward.","Despite their silent appearance, anyone could tell the two princes were currently experiencing horrifying pain. Their bodies twisted violently nonstop while muffled grunts continued escaping their mouths.","Michael quietly overlooked everything with a calm expression.","Yes. Although he had decided to honor the former king somewhat, that did not mean the two princes would simply die peacefully.","Using his law to copy the illusionary traits belonging to Purple and Blue, Michael directly dragged both princes into a mental illusion. Inside that illusion, time flowed differently. Countless things would happen to them there, and everything they experienced inside would feel as real as possible.","In the real world, both princes continued convulsing violently across the garden floor while trapped within the nightmare Michael had created for them.","Michael slowly raised his hand and dark flames quietly emerged above his palm. The moment the fire appeared, even the surrounding garden atmosphere distorted faintly.","Count Hallen’s pupils contracted violently.","This was the Abyss Flame Michael had copied from Spartan’s Law of Abyssal Pyre. A terrifying flame said to devour nearly anything it touched.","Michael calmly compressed part of the black flame until two tiny seeds formed above his fingertips. Then he casually flicked them forward. The seeds instantly entered the bodies of both princes.","The bodies of the Ninth Prince and Tenth Prince shook even harder as the Abyss Flame began devouring their lifeforce slowly from within. It would continue feeding upon them little by little until absolutely nothing remained to consume. Only when they died would the illusion finally end.","Count Hallen completely collapsed mentally after witnessing everything. His body trembled uncontrollably while terror filled every inch of his face as he noticed Michael finally turning to look at him.","Michael looked at Count Hallen quietly. \"And you...\"","His voice trailed off. For some reason, Michael felt strangely uninterested in continuing.","Initially, he had thought about asking the man several questions, but after everything that had happened tonight, Michael suddenly realized none of it would make him feel better. So in the end, he simply lost interest.","Count Hallen immediately sensed it. That cold indifference inside Michael’s eyes terrified him even more than rage would have.","\"P-Please...\" The old count’s voice completely broke apart. \"I-I was wrong. I truly was wrong.\"","Michael said nothing. He merely raised his hand once more as a tiny black flame seed appeared above his fingertips.","Count Hallen’s pupils shrank violently. \"N-No...\"","This time, Michael did not place anyone under an illusion. With a casual flick of his finger, the black seed entered Count Hallen’s body directly.","\"AAAAAAHHHHHHHH!!!\"","A horrifying scream instantly exploded throughout the entire garden. Count Hallen’s body slammed against the ground violently as he rolled across the dirt like a madman. Both hands clawed desperately at his own chest while the Abyss Flame began devouring his lifeforce from within.","Unlike the two princes who suffered silently within their illusions, Count Hallen experienced everything directly. He no longer resembled a noble. He sounded like a pig being slaughtered alive.","\"AAAAAHHHH...!\"","\"IT HURTS...!\"","\"PLEASE...!\"","\"T-TURN IT OFF...!\"","Tears, mucus, and saliva covered his face completely while his body twisted nonstop across the garden floor.","Meanwhile, Michael simply watched him quietly for several seconds. \"With this, I’ve at least paid some respects to Arianne.\"","Michael’s voice faded as he disappeared. Only Count Hallen’s miserable screams continued echoing endlessly throughout the garden."]},{"number":1005,"title":"Chapter 1005: Constructing Vassel","paragraphs":["After dealing with the three figures, Michael finally felt much of the heaviness inside his heart clear away. His thoughts became clearer again and his mind no longer felt clouded by emotion.","However, aside from the empire, Michael was now plagued with a new problem.","Arianne’s revival.","In the purple world within his storage ring, Michael slowly exhaled while rubbing the space between his brows helplessly.","According to Jester, reviving Arianne would require Michael to use his Genesis Body skill to create the perfect vessel for her soul. At first, Michael truly believed the process would not be difficult.","After all, had he not already created a clone body for himself before? Even if Michael personally considered that clone imperfect, the vessel itself had still been extremely powerful. It had perfectly housed one of his most unique undead after all.","Naturally, Michael assumed creating another body should not be overly complicated.","Only after actually beginning the process for Arianne did Michael realize just how mistaken he had been. The requirements were completely different. Creating a generic body was one thing. Creating a body specifically compatible with a particular soul was another matter entirely.","Michael sat on the ground, and before him were countless drawings and designs. Some resembled human anatomical structures. Others looked more like magical pathways.","In Michael’s hand floated a single crimson drop of blood.","Meanwhile, beside him, Jester continued drawing calmly without pause.","Scratch. Scratch.","The sound of the pen moving across paper echoed continuously throughout the quiet space.","Michael stared at the enormous pile of designs before him for several seconds before finally speaking helplessly. \"...Is all of this really necessary?\"","Jester did not stop drawing. \"The vessel is the most important part,\" he answered calmly. \"However, compatibility between the soul and vessel would naturally be best.\"","He casually pushed another completed design to the side before continuing. \"If Master simply wishes to revive this lady normally, then many shortcuts can be taken.\"","Jester finally looked up. His gaze moved toward Arianne’s corpse currently sealed peacefully within ice nearby. The young woman looked almost asleep.","\"If Master is not bothered by this lady waking up with a male reproductive organ,\" Jester said calmly while pointing toward the frozen Arianne, \"then we can skip this entire process.\"","Silence filled the purple world instantly afterward.","Michael stared at him blankly. The next second, the corner of his mouth twitched slightly.","In the end, Michael had to admit Jester was right. If he was going to do something, then he should do it properly. The thought of Arianne waking up inside an identical clone of his already felt strange enough. One had to understand that Michael’s clones were not puppets or dead shells. They were living lifeforms.","The more Michael thought about it, the stranger the entire situation became. What if Arianne woke up one morning only to discover some hard surprise waiting for her? And then there were the hormones. Michael genuinely believed that kind of situation would drive almost anyone insane eventually.","The corner of his mouth twitched slightly. \"...Fine,\" Michael finally admitted helplessly.","Jester gave a small nod before calmly continuing his drawings again.","Scratch. Scratch.","The sound echoed continuously throughout the purple world.","Michael lowered his gaze toward the countless designs spread around the floor once more. Then suddenly, his expression became strange.","\"...Wait.\"","He picked up one particular drawing. Michael stared at it for several seconds silently before slowly raising an eyebrow.","\"Jester.\"","\"Yes, Master?\"","Michael lifted the paper higher. \"I can understand creating a body identical to the original.\" His gaze narrowed slightly. \"But why exactly does this design have a tail?\"","Silence filled the surroundings briefly.","Then Jester looked over calmly at the drawing in Michael’s hand. \"Oh.\"","His tone remained completely natural. \"I simply thought perhaps Master would enjoy it. Lily told me you enjoyed watching animations of this sort when you were younger.\"","PAK!","Michael instantly smacked the back of Jester’s head. Jester’s head tilted slightly forward from the hit.","\"You undead freak.\"","Michael’s face darkened slightly.","Jester calmly rubbed the back of his head afterward. \"Master should not underestimate tails.\" He spoke with complete seriousness.","\"Based on my observations, many races throughout the universe possess them. Beastkin, dragons, fox spirits, demons, certain void races...\" Jester adjusted another paper calmly. \"Furthermore, tails improve balance. I figured we could upgrade her as we give her a new life. Is this not Master’s plan for his new subject?\"","PAK!","Michael smacked the back of his head again. Jester finally fell silent afterward while Michael stared at him with a dark expression.","For several seconds, neither of them spoke. Then eventually, Michael sighed heavily while rubbing his forehead helplessly.","Sometimes he truly wondered what exactly Jester had become after absorbing all those memories.","\"Also, she is not my subject. I don’t plan to use her for anything. Our priority is to bring her back to life. Don’t get distracted with things I did not ask you to do.\" He paused briefly before adding, \"Though I suppose I did say to help me create a perfect vessel. That one’s on me.\"","As Michael focused on constructing Arianne’s body, his thoughts drifted back to the attack on the demonic faction. It should have started by now. Unfortunately his hands were tied, and he could only hope the academy and Federation managed well.","Meanwhile, back in the Land of Origin, Michael had finally caught up with two figures who were currently resting in a forest.","After dealing with the three people who stood at the root of everything, Michael immediately went after the third prince of the empire.","Initially, he would have preferred for the Third Prince to safely arrive at the empire before him. However, Michael realized he could no longer bring himself to wait patiently.","Fortunately, thanks to the memories he absorbed from the empire’s men a few hours earlier, Michael already possessed a general understanding of the route leading back toward the empire.","*","A/N: Sorry for the late update!"]},{"number":1006,"title":"Chapter 1006: Appearance","paragraphs":["After Michael’s attack, Master Veyl did not dare to delay even slightly. The moment he escaped with the Third Prince, the old man immediately began rushing back toward the empire at full speed. Space distorted continuously around him as he crossed enormous distances without pause.","As a Great Stage being capable of moving through space itself, Master Veyl’s speed was naturally terrifying. However, the empire was simply too far away. Even at his level, crossing such an enormous distance still required time, especially while carrying another person who needed protection from the void’s influence and moving continuously without rest for hours straight.","Fortunately, they were close now. Only several more minutes remained before they reached the imperial capital, which allowed the old man to relax slightly for the first time in hours.","Beside him, the Third Prince looked miserable beyond words. His face remained pale while fear still lingered deeply within his eyes. Ever since escaping from Michael, the prince’s mental state had clearly deteriorated further and further.","Though the Third Prince had faced many assassination attempts in the past, none were like the attack today. For someone so sheltered, it had left a particularly strong impression. Unfortunately, he could not even rest properly given the constant movement Master Veyl maintained throughout their escape.","At some point, the Third Prince finally could not endure anymore.","\"Master... please...\" His voice sounded hoarse and exhausted. \"Can we stop briefly...?\"","Master Veyl frowned slightly. Under normal circumstances, stopping now did not seem wise. However, being in a familiar region made the old man somewhat more relaxed. In any case, they were close enough now. Even if the person who had attacked them somehow gave chase, as long as he kept his mind on escaping rather than fighting, things should be manageable.","Thinking this, Master Veyl finally slowed down. \"We will rest briefly,\" he said calmly. \"But only for a moment.\"","Master Veyl descended toward a forest below. The Third Prince nearly collapsed the moment they stopped moving. His breathing was ragged while sweat covered his entire body. For the past several hours, his nerves had been stretched to their limit.","Master Veyl glanced toward him briefly before sitting down cross-legged nearby. \"Rest,\" the old man said calmly. \"We will leave shortly.\"","The Third Prince nodded weakly before sitting heavily against a tree trunk.","For the next thirty minutes, neither of them spoke much. Only the sounds of insects and rustling leaves echoed quietly throughout the forest.","Eventually, after sensing the prince’s condition stabilize somewhat, Master Veyl slowly stood up once more. \"We should continue moving.\"","However, the Third Prince did not move.","Master Veyl frowned slightly. Several seconds passed before the old man spoke again.","\"Third Prince?\"","The prince still remained seated. Then slowly, he lowered his head while his hands clenched tightly.","\"...Why were we running?\"","Master Veyl’s brows furrowed instantly.","The Third Prince suddenly looked upward. His exhausted face now carried anger, humiliation, and unwillingness all mixed together.","\"You made me look like a coward.\" His voice gradually rose. \"What will my enemies think after this?\"","The prince slowly stood up while breathing heavily. \"Aren’t you close to the peak of the Great Stage?! Why didn’t you stay and fight him?!\"","Master Veyl’s face darkened immediately. However, the Third Prince continued speaking regardless.","\"If I return to the capital like this, how will Father look at me?\" His breathing became heavier and heavier. \"My brothers will use this against me forever.\"","His voice eventually rose into a near scream. \"My reputation in the capital will be ruined!\"","At this point, Master Veyl could no longer hide the frustration on his face. The old man stared at the prince silently for several seconds before finally speaking coldly.","\"...Do you truly believe reputation matters more than your life?\"","Master Veyl wanted to say far more. His expression had already become extremely ugly by now. However, after remembering the identity of the person standing before him, he forcibly suppressed part of his anger. No matter what, this was still an imperial prince.","So in the end, Master Veyl simply inhaled deeply before speaking in a restrained voice. \"...We should continue moving.\"","Unfortunately, the Third Prince immediately shook his head. \"No.\"","This time, the old man’s face genuinely darkened. Master Veyl stared directly at the prince for several long seconds before finally speaking again.","\"Your Highness.\" His voice had already turned considerably colder.","However, the Third Prince still looked unwilling.","Master Veyl finally lost the desire to continue tolerating him. \"Though I am powerful, I am not omnipotent,\" he said coldly. \"The fact that the person you offended could nearly injure me from that distance alone already proves he is most likely not someone I can defeat.\"","The Third Prince’s expression changed slightly.","Master Veyl continued. \"Do you think Great Stage cultivators are invincible?\" His tone became harsher. \"The world is far larger than you imagine.\"","His frustration finally became fully visible. \"That person’s ranged attacks alone are already terrifying enough. If I truly stayed behind to fight him, there is a real possibility both of us would have died there.\"","The Third Prince clenched his fists tightly. Yet despite hearing all of this, unwillingness still remained within his eyes. According to everything he knew, this Mic fellow was younger than him. How could he possibly be this strong? This old man was simply making excuses. He was the coward here.","Master Veyl noticed it immediately. For a moment, the old man truly wanted to curse outright.","In the end, however, he simply shook his head heavily. Just as he was about to forcefully drag the prince along, his expression changed drastically and he turned to look sharply in a certain direction.","Not far from them, a tall youth sat on a tree branch with eyes that seemed to glow faintly in the evening light. A strangely beautiful owl rested quietly on his shoulder.","Startled by Master Veyl’s sudden tension, the Third Prince turned to look in the same direction. His face changed drastically as well.","When had this figure appeared? He hadn’t even noticed. What alarmed the prince further was that even Master Veyl appeared to have been slow in sensing him."]},{"number":1007,"title":"Chapter 1007: Mic Nor","paragraphs":["In all honesty, Michael had not truly expected to catch up with these two so quickly.","After all, Master Veyl and the Third Prince had escaped long before Michael even arrived at the Lionheart capital. A Great Stage existence moving at full speed through space was not something ordinary people could casually track down.","Yet thanks to a certain owl, Michael still managed to catch up rather easily.","One had to understand that advancing to Rank 3 was entirely different from the lower ranks. At that stage, whether human or monster, one would inevitably begin touching the domain of Laws.","Even if evolution acted as a shortcut toward greater power for monsters, it still granted them the trademark ability of Rank 3 beings.","A Law.","Naturally, Wisdom possessed one as well. And fortunately, its Law was exactly what Michael had hoped for.","A spatial-related Law. Space Domination.","Compared to many law concepts Michael knew about, this one was not particularly subtle in its expression. To put it simply, it gave Wisdom an absurd degree of control over the void itself.","Unfortunately, this law was so draining it could affect even Wisdom, which could be said to possess near-infinite energy thanks to its nature as a child of the void.","Back to the present.","Thanks to Wisdom’s Law, its maximum perception distance was instantly doubled. Even if it could only be maintained for a short period, this was more than enough to catch up with the Third Prince before they reached the empire.","Upon arriving, Michael had not immediately revealed his presence. Instead, he had concealed himself using his various stealth abilities while quietly considering whether it would be better to let the prince return to the empire before settling things between them, or simply handle it here as he had done in the Lionheart capital without dragging things out further.","Since he had only just arrived when the two were already arguing and were about to leave, Michael made his decision.","It was better to avoid wasting time and simply get things over with.","There was also the added benefit that absorbing the memories of two figures of such obvious high status would give him far more detailed knowledge of the imperial family than anything Princess Priscilla had provided.","It was also because he chose to reveal himself that the other party finally sensed him.","Master Veyl’s expression immediately became vigilant. The old man slowly stepped forward, placing himself slightly in front of the Third Prince while his senses spread outward cautiously.","The closer he looked at the youth sitting casually on the tree branch, the more uneasy he became.","He could not see through him at all. Not his cultivation. Not his aura. Not even his age.","To Master Veyl, this was deeply unsettling. For someone to silently bypass his senses and appear this close without detection, the other party had to at least stand on the same level as him. And there was absolutely no way someone like that would truly look this young.","The youth before him appeared to be in his late teens or early twenties at most. His features were excessively beautiful, almost unreal beneath the darkening evening, while his eyes carried a strange calmness entirely inconsistent with his apparent age.","Master Veyl immediately concluded this appearance was a disguise. Most likely some old monster deliberately maintaining a youthful form.","In fact, because of that overly beautiful appearance, Master Veyl was not even entirely certain the person before him was truly male. The figure clearly possessed masculine features, but combined with the assumption that this appearance was merely a facade, Master Veyl even began suspecting the true identity behind it could very well belong to a woman.","After all, many powerful experts throughout the world possessed strange preferences. Some concealed their appearance. Some changed genders entirely. Others abandoned their original bodies altogether. Compared to those old monsters, merely appearing young was hardly unusual.","Master Veyl slowly cupped his fists politely. \"This old man is called Veyl,\" he said cautiously. \"I currently serve as guardian to the Third Imperial Prince of the Black Serpent Empire.\"","His eyes remained fixed firmly on Michael the entire time. \"May this sir please introduce themselves as well?\"","Even while speaking politely, Master Veyl’s body remained tense internally. Space around him subtly fluctuated as though he were already prepared to flee at any moment if things turned wrong.","Meanwhile, behind him, the Third Prince’s expression had become serious as well. Like Master Veyl, he was entirely unaware of what Michael actually looked like.","Though he had been informed that the person who had attacked the flying port was supposedly someone of exceptional appearance, he could not immediately connect the youth on the branch with Mic Nor.","Now that the prince had calmed down somewhat, he found himself thinking along the same lines as Master Veyl. Whoever had attacked them in the capital was likely closely connected to Michael, but surely could not be Michael himself. Many of the Lionheart nobles had initially reached the same conclusion as well.","Michael stared at the two figures before him for several seconds. Then his expression gradually became strange.","\"...You don’t recognize me?\"","The moment those words fell, both Master Veyl and the Third Prince frowned slightly.","Master Veyl remained cautious. \"This old man does not believe we have met before, sir.\"","Meanwhile, the Third Prince also looked confused.","Seeing their reactions, Michael genuinely became stunned. For a brief moment, he simply sat there silently on the branch while staring at them.","Then suddenly, Michael laughed.","At first the laughter sounded soft. But gradually, a trace of anger appeared within it. The sound caused Master Veyl’s vigilance to rise instantly while the Third Prince’s expression became uglier.","This figure was not being particularly respectful, the prince thought. But he kept his mouth shut. As spoiled as he was, he was not completely without sense.","Finally, Michael slowly looked toward the Third Prince.","\"You sent people after me and you didn’t even know what I looked like?\"","His voice remained calm, yet the surrounding atmosphere quietly became colder.","The Third Prince froze slightly. Michael’s laughter faded completely.","For some reason, the sheer ridiculousness of the situation genuinely angered him now. The empire. The princes. The nobles. All of them treated other people’s lives casually like pieces on a board. Yet the person standing at the center of everything had not even properly investigated his target beforehand.","Michael slowly stood up from the tree branch. The movement immediately caused Master Veyl’s expression to tighten.","\"Let me introduce myself properly. I’m Mic Nor.\"","The Third Prince’s face finally changed. Beside him, Master Veyl’s heart sank as well."]},{"number":1008,"title":"Chapter 1008: Two Punch","paragraphs":["Whether they had been directly involved with Michael or not, both the Third Prince and Master Veyl were naturally aware of the name Mic Nor.","For the Third Prince, it was simple. Mic Nor had originally just been someone he found interesting enough to toy with for entertainment. A mere genius from a small kingdom. Someone he could casually pressure to pass time while expanding his influence within the Lionheart Kingdom.","As for Master Veyl, although he never directly interfered with the prince’s affairs, he still kept track of the young man’s actions from the shadows. Naturally, he was also aware of Mic Nor’s existence.","The moment the name left Michael’s mouth, Michael’s appearance suddenly no longer seemed quite as absurd anymore. But Master Veyl still could not fully believe the youth before him was truly the real Mic Nor.","However, whether this was truly Mic Nor or some hidden old monster connected to him no longer mattered much anymore. One thing was obvious. This person was absolutely not friendly.","The instant that thought crossed his mind, Master Veyl moved without hesitation.","BOOM!","Space around the old man distorted violently as he instantly grabbed the Third Prince by the shoulder. \"Let’s go!\"","The forest exploded apart beneath his feet as Master Veyl forcefully dragged the prince into the void.","Meanwhile, standing upon the tree branch, Michael merely watched the scene calmly. Not even surprise appeared on his face.","Beside him, Wisdom slowly tilted its head while its pure white eyes glowed faintly.","Then space folded.","Master Veyl appeared hundreds of meters away high in the air. However, the instant he emerged into another location, Master Veyl’s expression changed drastically.","A figure was already waiting there.","Master Veyl’s pupils contracted violently. Before the old man could even fully react, a fist smashed directly toward him.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The surrounding air exploded instantly. Master Veyl barely managed to raise his arm defensively before the attack landed.","CRACK!","A horrifying sound echoed out. The old man’s eyes widened violently as an overwhelming force exploded through his body. It felt less like being struck by a fist and more like being rammed head-on by a mountain.","\"PUAGH...!\"","Blood immediately burst from Master Veyl’s mouth as his entire body shot backward at terrifying speed.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Master Veyl smashed through layers of air pressure before crashing violently back toward the exact forest location he had escaped from moments earlier. The ground exploded apart the moment his body slammed into it.","The Third Prince screamed. Even through Master Veyl’s focused protection, the remaining shockwaves from that punch had almost affected him directly. His internal organs churned violently while blood leaked faintly from the corner of his mouth.","Master Veyl himself looked horrified. His arms trembled violently while blood continued dripping from his lips nonstop.","Just one punch. Only one punch had already injured him this badly.","At this point, the old man did not doubt that this person truly possessed the power to kill both of them.","Unknown to him, Michael had actually held back already. Otherwise, that punch alone would have completely blown apart his upper body.","However, Master Veyl obviously did not know this. Instead, after sensing the terrifying killing force behind the attack, the old man instantly reached his own conclusion. This person was here to silence them completely, especially since that punch had not shown the slightest care toward the Third Prince’s safety.","Master Veyl’s expression became uglier than ever before. If not for his protection, the prince might have died from the aftershock alone. To Master Veyl, this only further confirmed his suspicions. This Mic Nor, or whatever monster stood behind him, had absolutely no intention of leaving survivors.","Unfortunately for him, he was mistaken once again.","Michael had actually been paying attention to the Third Prince the entire time. Although the punch itself had not discriminated between targets, Michael had already controlled the force precisely beforehand. Even if the prince’s body exploded apart from the impact, his head would still remain intact.","Despite his injuries, Master Veyl still erupted with terrifying strength. The old man forcefully suppressed the blood surging through his chest while spatial fluctuations exploded around him once more. Without the slightest hesitation, Master Veyl grabbed the Third Prince again and forcibly tore open space to escape.","The Third Prince’s vision blurred violently.","However, the moment they emerged from the void again, a calm figure was already standing there waiting for them.","Michael.","Master Veyl’s heart nearly stopped. How?!","Before the old man could even process what was happening, Michael had already moved again.","Another punch.","BOOOOOOM!!!","This time the impact was even more terrifying. Master Veyl desperately roared as layers of protection erupted around his body. Yet the moment Michael’s fist landed, CRACK! CRACK! CRACK!, every defensive layer shattered instantly like glass.","\"PUAAAGHHH...!\"","Blood sprayed wildly from Master Veyl’s mouth as his chest visibly caved inward. The force behind the punch directly sent him flying backward once more toward the exact same forest they had escaped from seconds earlier.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The earth exploded apart. Countless trees shattered while the ground collapsed into a massive crater.","This time, Master Veyl did not stand back up immediately. The old man lay buried within the shattered earth while blood continuously poured from his mouth. His arms had twisted unnaturally. Several bones throughout his body had completely shattered. That final punch had directly crippled him.","Beside him, the Third Prince rolled weakly across the ground before crashing heavily into broken dirt and shattered roots. Blood leaked faintly from the prince’s lips while terror completely overtook his face. His body trembled uncontrollably as he stared upward.","Michael slowly descended from the sky afterward.","The prince’s breathing became ragged. \"W-Wait...\" His voice trembled badly. \"We can talk about this...\"","Michael continued walking forward without replying.","The Third Prince’s face turned pale. \"I-I can compensate you!\" he shouted hurriedly. \"Resources! Women! Whatever you want, the empire can provide it!\"","Still no response.","At this point, panic finally exploded inside the prince’s heart. \"DON’T COME CLOSER!\"","Seeing Michael continue approaching silently, something inside the prince finally snapped.","\"FUCK YOU!\"","His expression twisted viciously as he suddenly crushed an unassuming black pendant."]},{"number":1009,"title":"Chapter 1009: Surprise","paragraphs":["BOOOOOOOOM!!!","A terrifying wave of energy erupted outward violently. The surrounding forest instantly collapsed under the pressure alone as black light swallowed everything nearby. The attack surged directly toward Michael with horrifying destructive power.","Yet facing the incoming attack, Michael merely narrowed his eyes slightly. \"...I was expecting this.\"","From the very beginning, Michael had remained cautious toward the Third Prince. An imperial prince backed by a massive empire possessing life-saving treasures was hardly surprising. This had even been the case for Prince Rui, a lower-ranking prince he had killed in the secret realm.","The black wave instantly devoured Michael completely. The Third Prince’s face twisted with savage hope.","However, BOOM!","The black energy suddenly exploded apart from within. Michael calmly stepped out through the collapsing attack almost entirely unharmed. Only faint black flames flickered briefly across his body before disappearing.","The Third Prince froze.","Michael looked at him and suddenly smiled. \"...Do you have more?\"","The prince’s expression became ugly instantly. Then without hesitation, CRACK!, another pendant shattered. A blood-red spear suddenly condensed in midair before firing toward Michael with enough force to split apart the earth below.","Michael raised an eyebrow before casually slapping it aside.","BOOOOM!","The spear exploded violently in the distance. Yet before Michael could even finish speaking again, CRACK!, another treasure shattered. A massive golden bell phantom instantly descended from above and crashed toward him.","Michael was genuinely caught off guard this time.","BOOOOOM!!!","The surrounding sky trembled violently from the impact. Far away, even the crippled Master Veyl stared blankly.","Michael still remained completely unharmed. Even after being struck repeatedly by treasures capable of unleashing peak Rank 3 attacks, his expression only grew more cautious. After all, this was still an imperial prince. No one knew what other ridiculous life-saving treasures he might still possess. Last time with Prince Rui, he had needed to summon multiple undead to break through his defenses quickly.","However, just as Michael prepared himself for yet another hidden attack, his expression suddenly changed slightly.","\"...Hm?\"","The Third Prince’s condition had become horrifying. The once-proud imperial prince now looked almost like a walking skeleton. His face had sunk inward violently while his skin turned pale and dry. Even his hair seemed to have lost some of its luster within moments.","Most shocking of all, his life aura had weakened drastically. It was obvious now that activating those treasures did not come freely.","Michael’s expression became thoughtful. Thinking about it carefully, it made sense. Those attacks from earlier had all reached the absolute peak of Rank 3 power. In this entire region, there were honestly not many people capable of surviving repeated attacks like that head-on. As life-saving trump cards, such treasures were naturally worth their cost, but that cost was evidently severe.","Looking at the Third Prince’s expression, it was clear that even he had not expected the consumption to be this terrifying.","Yet despite noticing the prince’s miserable condition, Michael still did not lower his guard completely. Without hesitation, a pressure exploded outward from Michael’s eyes as he sent out a mental attack.","The Third Prince’s body froze instantly. His consciousness shattered apart from the mental impact. The prince collapsed unconscious directly onto the broken forest ground.","Immediately afterward, Michael turned his gaze toward the distant crater where Master Veyl still struggled weakly. The old man’s expression changed drastically.","BOOM!","His eyes rolled backward instantly. The crippled guardian collapsed unconscious as well.","Only after both figures completely lost consciousness did Michael finally relax slightly. Even then, he still did not approach carelessly. The Third Prince had already pulled out too many ridiculous treasures tonight. Michael genuinely would not have been surprised if the man suddenly exploded after death or activated some final hidden protection the moment someone touched him.","Without hesitation, Michael first checked both bodies carefully from a distance. His senses swept repeatedly across the Third Prince and Master Veyl until he finally confirmed neither of them possessed any remaining hidden tricks capable of threatening him.","Only then did he begin accessing their memories.","Michael started with Master Veyl first. Compared to ordinary people, the old man’s mental defenses were naturally far stronger. Unfortunately for him, Michael’s spiritual strength had long surpassed ordinary Rank 3 existences. The old man’s resistance collapsed.","Fragments of memories began flowing into Michael’s mind afterward. However, after several minutes, Michael slowly frowned. The knowledge was useful, but not enough. Master Veyl clearly did not possess access to the empire’s deepest secrets.","Eventually, Michael withdrew his senses before turning toward the final target.","The Third Prince.","Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly. Then his spiritual senses directly entered the prince’s mind.","The next instant, BOOM!","Michael’s expression changed abruptly. A terrifying pressure suddenly erupted before him.","Inside the prince’s mental world stood a dignified middle-aged man dressed in black imperial robes. The man stood with both hands behind his back while an overwhelming royal aura spread from his body naturally. His gaze alone carried indescribable pressure.","Even though this was clearly only a spiritual mark left behind inside the prince’s soul, the surrounding mental space still trembled faintly under its existence.","The moment Michael saw the figure, recognition appeared within his eyes immediately. From the countless memories he had absorbed recently, he already knew exactly who this person was.","The Emperor of the Black Serpent Empire.","The moment Michael recognized the figure, the emperor’s eyes suddenly opened completely. An overwhelming pressure instantly descended upon the entire mental space.","\"Bold!\"","The low shout exploded like thunder. \"Do you wish to die?!\"","BOOOOOOM!!!","The emperor suddenly raised his hand. The next instant, a terrifying mental attack surged directly toward Michael like an ocean. The surrounding mental space distorted violently.","Michael’s expression changed slightly. Fast. Too fast.","Before he could fully retreat his senses, the attack had already reached him.","BOOM!","A sharp pain instantly exploded within Michael’s mind. His spiritual senses shook violently while his head throbbed painfully for a brief moment. Even the real-world Michael outside the mental space frowned slightly afterward.","This was the first time in a long while something had managed to directly affect his mind this way.","However, that was all. The emperor’s attack ultimately failed to break through Michael’s defenses completely.","Michael slowly steadied himself afterward.","Meanwhile, opposite him, the emperor’s expression finally changed slightly for the first time. Surprise. The middle-aged emperor stared directly at Michael now, no longer carrying the same dismissive indifference as before.","\"Who are you, and how dare you attack an imperial prince?\"","His deep voice echoed slowly throughout the mental world."]},{"number":1010,"title":"Chapter 1010: A Mental Battle","paragraphs":["Upon hearing the Black Serpent Emperor’s question, the first thing Michael truly wanted to do was raise a middle finger.","After all, the man had just attacked him mercilessly without hesitation. If not for Michael’s terrifying foundation, that strike alone might have heavily injured him.","Unfortunately, Michael was still a civilized person. Also, taunting people was not really his style. If Michael wanted to do something, he generally preferred acting directly.","And that was exactly what he did.","BOOM!","Without warning, Michael’s mental energy exploded outward violently as he directly attacked the emperor’s mental imprint. The surrounding mental space instantly trembled.","Countless black chains condensed from the void while illusionary purple mist spread rapidly across the surroundings. At the same time, strange eye-like symbols appeared behind Michael one after another.","Mental methods were actually extremely rare. Compared to direct combat techniques, spiritual attacks were far harder to cultivate and even more dangerous to use. One mistake could easily damage one’s own soul permanently.","Michael himself did not truly specialize in such techniques. However, he possessed quite a few undead who did, like Jester, Blue, and Purple. Especially Jester.","After absorbing the memories of the evil cultivator Li Yang, Jester had become horrifying in terms of mental abilities. Consciousness Erasure, Mind Nest, Memory Harvest.","Many of those abilities possessed terrifying effects even against stronger opponents. And thanks to Michael’s Law, he could directly copy portions of their traits and abilities for himself.","The next instant, BOOOOOOM!!!","The emperor’s mental imprint collided directly against Michael’s attacks. The entire mental world shook violently. Black serpentine dragons roared above while countless illusionary eyes opened throughout the void simultaneously.","For several exchanges, neither side actually managed to suppress the other immediately. This genuinely surprised Michael.","Fortunately, Michael still held the advantage overall. His mental strength was simply too monstrous. Gradually, the emperor’s imprint began destabilizing under the pressure. Cracks spread across the surrounding mental world.","Seeing this, Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly as he prepared to completely destroy the imprint in one move.","However, the emperor suddenly smiled coldly. \"You wish to search the mind of this emperor’s son?\"","The next moment, the emperor directly raised his hand.","BOOM!!!","The entire mental space instantly began collapsing. Michael’s expression changed slightly afterward.","This bastard.","The emperor had directly destroyed the Third Prince’s mental world himself. The moment the mental world began collapsing, Michael immediately withdrew his senses.","BOOM!!!","A violent force instantly expelled him from the Third Prince’s consciousness. Even Michael’s real body outside staggered back half a step afterward while a sharp headache throbbed faintly behind his eyes.","In front of him, the unconscious Third Prince suddenly convulsed violently. Then, \"GHH...!\"","Foam began leaking from the prince’s mouth while his eyes snapped open unnaturally wide. However, there was no intelligence left inside them anymore. Only emptiness.","The prince’s pupils trembled nonstop while saliva dripped down his chin. His body twitched weakly across the shattered ground as incoherent sounds escaped his throat.","\"Aah... ahhh...\"","Michael frowned slightly afterward.","The emperor had been completely ruthless. Rather than allowing Michael access to the prince’s memories, he had directly destroyed his son’s mental world entirely.","At this point, even if the Third Prince survived physically, his mind had already become crippled beyond repair. A fool. Someone who could no longer think properly.","Michael stared silently at the prince for several seconds. The once arrogant imperial prince who had treated countless lives casually now looked utterly pathetic lying in the dirt.","Eventually, Michael exhaled slowly.","Although he had failed to fully access the prince’s memories, the brief confrontation alone had still allowed him to understand several things.","First, the Black Serpent Emperor was terrifyingly powerful. Even a mere mental imprint left inside his son possessed strength capable of contending briefly against Michael.","Second, the emperor clearly valued secrecy regarding the imperial family far more than he valued the mental well-being of his own son. The implication of this made Michael even more uncertain about the information he had received from Princess Priscilla.","\"According to the princess, the empire should possess only three Legendary beings at most, but from what I can see based on the emperor’s mental imprint alone, he is most likely in the Legendary stage already.\"","With this analysis, it meant the empire had at least four Rank 4 beings. The same number as Michael.","However, this did not weaken Michael’s resolve in the slightest. After all, quantity did not equal quality. Not only did Michael have the same number of Rank 4 undead as the empire’s assumed count, each of them was also extraordinarily powerful.","Lily, who was the weakest among them, was practically impossible to kill as long as she did not go up against someone too far above her level. In fact, her opponent would be lucky if she did not simply swallow their attacks and convert them into energy.","As for Beginning, the Rank 4 demonic supernatural, and the High Drake, each of them was exceptionally strong.","The High Drake in particular was already at the absolute peak of Rank 4. Beginning, on the other hand, could use its law to fight above its class entirely.","Then there was also Michael himself to factor in. Though he had not yet reached Rank 4, he could still provide meaningful assistance to his undead against a Rank 4 opponent.","Putting all of that aside, he also had more than two thousand Rank 3 undead. However, Michael hoped he would not need to deploy his Rank 3 forces against a Rank 4 opponent, since even if they won, the losses would cause him considerable pain.","The last incident was still quite fresh in his memory.","Michael slowly turned to look at the Third Prince again.","In all honesty, the prince’s current state was quite pitiful. The once arrogant imperial prince now lay twitching weakly in the dirt with empty eyes and saliva leaking continuously from his mouth. There was no intelligence left inside those eyes anymore. Just emptiness.","However, Michael felt no pity for him. Not even slightly."]},{"number":1011,"title":"Chapter 1011: Reaction","paragraphs":["This was not some innocent person caught in unfortunate circumstances. The Third Prince had ruined countless lives simply because he could. To him, people had merely been tools, toys, and stepping stones.","Perhaps it was exactly because of his father that he had grown into this sort of person.","Thinking this, Michael could not help comparing the emperor to the old Lionheart King. The old king had been far weaker than the Black Serpent Emperor. In terms of power alone, the two were worlds apart.","Even as a father, the old king could not truly be called perfect either, but in Michael’s opinion that old man was still worthy of respect. At the very least, he had genuinely cared about his children.","As for the emperor, Michael’s eyes turned slightly colder. Compared to the old king, that man felt more like a monster wearing human skin.","Eventually, Michael lost interest in the Third Prince completely. Without bothering to continue further, Michael calmly raised his hand.","A tiny black flame appeared above his fingertips. Spartan’s Abyss Flame.","The flame drifted slowly downward before entering the Third Prince’s forehead silently. The prince’s weak twitching stopped almost instantly. Then gradually, his body began turning into black ash. Within moments, nothing remained behind.","Seeing this, Michael remained silent briefly. \"In this way, Arianne has finally been avenged.\"","Afterward, Michael turned toward Master Veyl.","Michael did not enjoy hurting innocents simply because they belonged to the empire. However, from the memories he had read from the guardian, this old man was not innocent.","In the end, Michael gave him the same ending. A black flame descended quietly. Soon afterward, only ash remained within the broken forest.","The surroundings finally fell silent completely.","Standing amidst the destroyed earth, Michael could not help narrowing his eyes slightly. The people he had encountered from the empire so far, not one of them could truly be considered good.","At this point, Michael honestly began wondering if there were even any clean people left within the upper levels of the Black Serpent Empire at all.","Eventually, Michael turned his gaze toward Wisdom resting calmly on his shoulder. The owl blinked slowly. Michael gently stroked its feathers afterward.","\"...Let’s go.\"","Wisdom let out a soft cry. The next instant, space folded quietly around the two of them before both figures disappeared from the destroyed forest entirely. Only ashes and ruins remained behind.","Meanwhile, far away within the Black Serpent Empire, inside an incomparably luxurious office decorated with black gold and ancient-looking carvings, a terrifying aura suddenly exploded outward violently.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The surrounding space distorted instantly. Not far away, two guards suddenly screamed miserably.","\"AAAHH...!\"","Blood exploded from multiple places across their bodies as invisible pressure crushed down upon them mercilessly. Both men collapsed heavily onto the ground while trembling violently.","At the center of the room stood a middle-aged man wearing black imperial robes.","If Michael were present, he would immediately recognize him. The Black Serpent Emperor.","At this moment, the emperor’s face looked incomparably cold. His eyes carried terrifying fury. The atmosphere throughout the room had become so oppressive that ordinary people would likely suffocate instantly upon entering.","However, just as the emperor’s aura continued spreading uncontrollably, a figure silently emerged from the shadows nearby. An old man dressed in black robes.","The old man bowed deeply immediately after appearing. \"Your Majesty.\" His voice remained calm and respectful. \"What has angered you so greatly?\"","The emperor slowly closed his eyes afterward. Several seconds later, the terrifying pressure filling the room gradually receded. The emperor, however, did not answer.","The old man did not seem bothered by the silence at all. Instead, he merely turned toward the two heavily injured guards still kneeling on the floor. \"You may leave and recover your injuries,\" the old man said calmly.","The two guards immediately bowed their heads deeply despite blood still dripping from their wounds. \"Yes, Eunuch Liang.\"","Neither dared to say anything else. Very quickly, both men retreated from the office trembling.","Only after they disappeared completely did Eunuch Liang bow toward the emperor once more. For several seconds, the emperor maintained his silence while Eunuch Liang remained bowed respectfully without moving in the slightest.","The office had already fallen completely silent again. Only the faint crackling sounds from shattered furniture occasionally echoed through the room.","Eventually, the emperor finally spoke. \"...The Third Prince is dead.\"","Eunuch Liang’s calm expression finally changed slightly. Surprise flickered across the old eunuch’s eyes.","He did not question how the emperor knew. There was no need. At their level, many strange methods existed. Since the emperor had said the prince was dead, then he was undoubtedly dead.","Immediately, Eunuch Liang’s tone became considerably graver. \"...Could there be a connection between the Third Prince’s death and Young Prince Rui’s previous death?\"","The emperor remained silent briefly afterward. \"...It is possible.\"","Eunuch Liang’s brows furrowed deeply. \"That is troublesome.\"","The old eunuch slowly lowered his head slightly in thought. The Black Serpent Empire possessed very few true enemies. However, every single one of those enemies was extremely terrifying.","For someone to repeatedly target imperial princes, this was no longer a small matter.","Eunuch Liang’s eyes darkened faintly. \"...Who would dare go this far against the imperial family?\" he muttered slowly. \"Are they truly not afraid of starting a war with the empire?\"","The emperor’s eyes turned cold afterward. \"...Perhaps war is exactly what they want.\"","Eunuch Liang immediately raised his head.","The emperor slowly recounted everything that had happened through the mental imprint inside the Third Prince. From Michael’s intrusion into the prince’s consciousness, to the mental confrontation, to the destruction of the prince’s mind.","The more Eunuch Liang listened, the graver his expression became. Especially after hearing that the mysterious figure had actually resisted and fought evenly against the emperor’s mental imprint for a period of time.","Finally, the emperor’s voice slowly echoed through the office once more. \"That figure...\"","The emperor’s eyes narrowed coldly. \"...Was no weaker than the two of us.\""]},{"number":1012,"title":"Chapter 1012: First Meeting","paragraphs":["The atmosphere inside the room instantly became heavier.","If Michael had heard these words, he would have first cursed the empire for concealing their true strength so deeply.","Together with Eunuch Liang, who was clearly a close confidant of the emperor, it meant the empire had at least five Legendary beings, and that was before accounting for whatever other trump cards they might possess.","Michael currently had no idea that the upper levels of the empire were already discussing him seriously and treating him as a genuine enemy.","Even if he knew, he honestly would not have found it strange. After all, with the deaths of two imperial princes, this matter had already long surpassed Arianne’s death alone.","Whatever personal grudge existed at the beginning had now escalated into something far larger.","At this point, Michael and the Black Serpent Empire could truly be considered enemies.","At this moment, Michael had already quietly entered the imperial capital itself.","Naturally, sneaking into the capital of such a massive empire was not an easy task for ordinary people. Countless magic circles covered the city walls while heavily armed guards patrolled everywhere.","Above the capital, flying knights circled slowly beneath the clouds while detection arrays continuously scanned the surroundings.","Unfortunately for the empire, Michael was not ordinary. With Wisdom’s assistance alongside his various concealment methods, entering the city silently was far easier than most would imagine.","Currently, Michael stood atop one of the capital’s tallest buildings while quietly observing the city beneath him.","Honestly, the Black Serpent Capital truly deserved its reputation as one of the finest in the world. Even Michael had to admit this place was incomparably prosperous.","The streets below stretched endlessly like black rivers beneath countless glowing spirit lamps.","Massive flying ships could be seen moving slowly through the skies at intervals while enormous towers covered in draconic carvings rose throughout the city one after another.","People filled the streets everywhere. Warriors. Merchants. Nobles. Soldiers.","The flow of mana throughout the city alone was several times richer than Lionheart’s capital. Even the weakest guards standing casually at street corners possessed cultivation levels that would already qualify them as experts in smaller kingdoms.","The deeper Michael looked, the more he understood why the Black Serpent Empire had ruled this region for so long. This was not merely a powerful nation. It was a true hegemonic force.","However, as Michael continued observing the capital, he noticed that beneath all that prosperity, the entire city felt strangely oppressive.","At first glance, everything appeared lively and glorious. Yet after observing longer, Michael slowly noticed certain details. The way ordinary civilians lowered their heads instinctively whenever nobles passed. The fear hidden within the eyes of weaker cultivators.","There were several more examples like these.","This place was a city where bloodline truly mattered. Status mattered. Birth mattered. Family mattered. It seemed to matter more than strength, perhaps even more than morality itself.","In the Black Serpent Empire, noble blood was almost law. And those standing at the very top of that hierarchy naturally possessed the right to trample everyone beneath them.","Michael quietly watched a carriage pass below after hitting an old woman on the road, escorted by armored soldiers who did not even slow down. The people on the street immediately moved aside instinctively. No one dared block the road. No one dared complain. Even the guards nearby lowered their heads respectfully.","Michael remained silent for several seconds afterward. Then eventually, he exhaled softly.","\"...No wonder.\"","No wonder the Third Prince had grown into that sort of person. In this empire, power and bloodline had already become absolute privileges long ago. Someone born at the top could likely spend their entire life without ever hearing the word no.","Thinking this, Michael’s eyes slowly turned colder again.","At the same time, Wisdom quietly perched upon his shoulder while observing the capital with glowing white eyes.","Suddenly, Michael turned to look toward the empty air beside him. \"...Since you’re already here, Emperor,\" he said calmly, \"why not come out?\"","For a brief moment, nothing happened.","Then space distorted quietly. A tall middle-aged man dressed in black robes stepped out from the void itself. His expression remained calm, yet the surrounding air instantly became heavier the moment he appeared.","The Black Serpent Emperor.","However, neither Michael nor Wisdom looked surprised in the slightest. Clearly, both of them had already noticed his presence long ago.","Michael casually stroked Wisdom’s feathers once more afterward. The owl let out a soft cry before its body dissolved silently into space.","The emperor’s gaze lingered briefly where Wisdom had disappeared. \"...That is a special bird.\" His deep voice echoed calmly across the rooftop. \"I do not know its species, but creatures capable of entering the void without a monster lineage to support them are rare even across the entire world.\"","Michael nodded slightly afterward. \"Thank you.\"","Silence fell briefly between the two. The imperial capital below remained lively and noisy as always, yet the atmosphere atop the tower felt strangely cold.","Eventually, Michael spoke first again. \"Since we both already know how this ends,\" he said calmly, \"we should probably skip the unnecessary conversation and get straight to it.\"","The emperor slowly raised an eyebrow. \"Oh?\"","His gaze sharpened slightly afterward. \"You do not seem very concerned for someone who is surrounded.\"","The emperor’s aura quietly spread across the surroundings. Meanwhile below, the ordinary civilians throughout the capital remained completely unaware of what was happening above them.","However, upon hearing the emperor’s words, Michael suddenly laughed softly. Then he shook his head.","\"No.\"","The emperor’s eyes narrowed slightly.","Michael’s smile widened faintly afterward. \"I’m not surrounded.\"","The next instant, without hesitation, the emperor’s hand shot directly toward Michael’s neck. The surrounding air exploded violently.","Unfortunately, he grabbed nothing.","The emperor’s eyes immediately lifted upward. His gaze narrowed.","High above the imperial capital, several hundred figures had already appeared silently throughout the sky. At the center of them all stood Michael calmly in midair."]},{"number":1013,"title":"Chapter 1013: Empire’s Power","paragraphs":["Michael was not particularly surprised that his entry into the imperial capital had been discovered.","After his previous clash with the emperor through the Third Prince’s mental imprint, there had already been a high possibility the empire would increase the capital’s defenses afterward.","And even if the emperor had somehow not done that, perhaps out of confidence that no sane person would willingly walk into what could become a cage at any moment, Michael still would not have underestimated the capital itself.","Legendary beings were only considered rare relative to ordinary people. To existences like the emperor, they were likely far more common than outsiders imagined.","If powerful figures at that level could casually enter and leave the emperor’s personal territory unnoticed, that would be a terrifying flaw for the empire. Michael had already expected the imperial capital to possess methods specifically designed to detect powerful intruders.","Of course, if he had managed to sneak in completely undetected, Michael would not have found that strange either. He possessed quite a few absurd concealment methods and was confident in his ability to hide when necessary.","Still, being discovered changed very little. From the very beginning, he had never truly intended to remain hidden forever.","High above the capital, cold wind swept across the night sky. Several hundred undead floated silently in formation. Terrifying energy rolled across the clouds while countless glowing eyes stared downward toward the imperial capital beneath them.","At this moment, the emperor’s expression had become noticeably colder.","Suddenly, a sharp scream echoed across the imperial capital. \"ENEMY ATTACK!\"","The voice was amplified by mana and spread throughout nearly half the city instantly. \"Highest alert level! Legendary-grade threat detected above the capital!\"","The peaceful atmosphere below shattered immediately.","BOOOOOOM!!!","One after another, countless magic circles suddenly lit up across the skies. Massive glowing formations expanded above the capital like layers of overlapping heavens. Strange runes rotated endlessly while pillars of blue light erupted upward from different regions of the city.","The entire imperial capital instantly transformed into a gigantic fortress.","At first glance, the formations did not seem to do anything directly. However, only a second later, Michael’s expression shifted slightly.","\"...Oh?\"","He immediately felt it. The void itself had been sealed. Or more accurately, locked. The surrounding space had not become inaccessible, but heavily restricted. Michael could still enter the void if he wished, yet movement through it would remain limited entirely within the boundaries of the imperial capital.","In simple terms, he was trapped.","At the same time, many of the undead behind Michael stirred slightly as they sensed the surrounding changes. The emperor, meanwhile, simply stood silently in the distance while observing him.","Michael did not look afraid at all. Instead, his eyes calmly swept across the glowing formations covering the heavens. \"...Interesting.\"","He wondered briefly whether his High Drake could forcefully break through. After all, that was a near-demigod creature.","Below, panic had already begun spreading rapidly throughout the city. Countless civilians fled into buildings while armored soldiers flooded the streets. Flying knights rapidly gathered in formation across the skies while powerful auras awakened continuously throughout the capital one after another.","The emperor slowly looked toward Michael. \"You entered the imperial capital willingly. Did you truly think leaving would be so easy?\"","Michael merely laughed softly. \"Leaving? Who said I was planning to leave immediately?\"","The emperor’s eyes narrowed faintly.","High above the capital, hundreds of undead remained floating silently like an army of death overlooking the empire itself. Cold wind swept across the skies. Michael’s expression remained extremely calm, though internally his thoughts were moving rapidly.","Michael was not reckless enough to believe attacking the Black Serpent Empire directly would be easy. This was not Lionheart. This was the strongest hegemonic force in the region.","The fact that they could lock down the void across an entire capital already proved how terrifying their foundations truly were.","Still, Michael was not without confidence. He possessed multiple Legendary undead and over two thousand Rank 3 undead.","Looking around he could also not deny that the Black Serpent Empire was truly powerful.","Just from the imperial family alone, Michael could already sense around four hundred Rank 3 knights and mages mobilizing rapidly throughout the capital. Four hundred. Even in Aurora, he had not seen such a massive number of Rank 3 existences gathered together openly like this.","Of course, this did not mean the empire was stronger than Aurora. Comparing the two directly was somewhat unfair. Aurora was a whole high-tier civilization. The structures of both powers were entirely different.","Still, the sheer military strength displayed by the empire was undeniably terrifying, and that was only the royal family itself.","As Michael’s senses swept farther outward, he quickly noticed several powerful auras rising from different noble districts as well. The great noble clans possessed their own Rank 3 experts. Some families had one. Some had three. A few had even more.","Gradually, the total number of Rank 3 beings surrounding the imperial capital climbed past five hundred. Michael’s eyes narrowed slightly. \"This probably still isn’t everything.\"","The empire had been caught somewhat unprepared tonight. Many experts were likely absent from the capital entirely. If the empire had been fully prepared beforehand, the number would have been even more absurd.","The Black Serpent Empire had existed for hundreds upon hundreds of years. Even if ascending to Rank 3 was difficult, enough time would naturally produce a terrifying accumulation.","Whether it was cultivation manuals, rare treasures, or special resources like Law Seeds, the empire almost certainly possessed enormous reserves of all of them.","Even people lacking natural talent could potentially ascend given sufficient comprehension and the right inheritance.","This was the true terror of ancient hegemonic powers. Accumulation.","As for the countless supernaturals below Rank 3 gathering throughout the city, Michael barely paid them any attention. To his current level they were honestly irrelevant. Even his ordinary Rank 3 undead could slaughter through them endlessly.","Yet despite the empire’s overwhelming numbers, the expressions on many faces below were solemn. Some were even pale."]},{"number":1014,"title":"Chapter 1014: Hidden Power","paragraphs":["Although Michael had not summoned all of his undead, there were already around eight hundred Rank 3 undead floating silently behind him. Eight hundred. In terms of sheer numbers, Michael had actually surpassed them.","Not only were they fearful, they were also confused. What noble power was bold enough to openly oppose the empire, and how had a force of this level entered the capital undetected? Were the capital guards blind?","Then suddenly, Michael’s mana erupted outward.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The skies trembled violently. The hundreds of undead floating behind him unleashed their auras simultaneously. Terrifying energy instantly flooded the surroundings.","Some weaker Rank 2 beings nearly lost control of their breathing entirely while ordinary soldiers turned pale from the pressure crushing down upon them.","At the center of it all, four especially terrifying auras slowly rose behind Michael. Five auras total, noticeably stronger than all the others.","Legendary beings! Many experts immediately realized in terror.","Fear instantly spread through the capital. None of them also realized those terrifying beings were actually undead. Only true Rank 4 existences might eventually notice abnormalities after prolonged observation.","After all, Michael’s undead were relatively human-like until they revealed their true forms. Because of this, many interpreted the eight hundred figures above as an external power rather than the force of a single person.","Even the emperor thought the same. His heart shook considerably. How had more than eight hundred beings appeared out of nowhere? Even though he could see a small coffin floating beside Michael, he did not want to believe such a treasure could truly exist. There was also a trace of genuine fear stirring in his heart. Above him floated five beings radiating Legendary auras. Who was vicious enough to want to ruin his empire? Was killing two of his sons not enough?","Meanwhile, Michael amplified his voice across the entire capital.","\"I do not care about the rest of you.\" His voice echoed like thunder throughout the skies. \"My grudge is only with the imperial family. As long as you step aside, you will not die tonight. I do not enjoy killing innocents.\"","Internally, however, Michael could not help muttering coldly to himself. As if the empire’s upper levels truly contained many innocent people.","Still, there were naturally ordinary civilians throughout the capital who had nothing to do with his conflict against the empire. Michael had no interest in massacring random people simply because they lived here.","The moment his words fell, countless expressions below only became even more solemn. Regardless of his intentions, the pressure from Michael’s side was simply too terrifying.","Then, BOOOOM!!!","Another overwhelming aura exploded into the sky. The emperor finally moved.","His figure instantly appeared high above the capital opposite Michael while terrifying pressure spread across the skies.","Beside him, an old man in black robes emerged silently from the void as well. The moment the old man appeared, another Rank 4 aura erupted outward, no weaker than any on Michael’s side.","Michael’s eyes narrowed instantly. Internally, he cursed.","Eunuch Liang.","From the memories he had devoured, Michael of course knew of this figure, but was this old man not supposed to be an ordinary Rank 3 existence? The aura radiating from the eunuch clearly belonged to a Legendary being.","These people had been hiding their strength the entire time. Then again, there had also supposedly been no public information regarding the emperor himself already being a Legendary existence either.","Clearly, the empire enjoyed pretending to be weaker than it truly was.","Looking below, Michael quickly noticed the expressions of many experts changing into visible shock. Even many of the empire’s own subjects seemed unaware of Eunuch Liang’s and the emperor’s true cultivation.","Michael’s lips twitched faintly. \"...Acting like pigs to eat tigers.\"","BOOOOM!!!","Michael’s relaxed expression soon collapsed. Several terrifying auras suddenly erupted from deep within the imperial palace itself. The skies darkened instantly. Even the clouds above the capital distorted violently under the pressure.","In merely a few breaths, five figures had already emerged high above the imperial palace. Some were old. Some middle-aged. One even appeared like a scholarly man carrying a jade scroll. Yet despite their differing appearances, the pressure radiating from every single one of them was horrifying.","Legendary beings. Each aura was no weaker than Michael’s own at the very least, and two among them seemed to be approaching the level of his stronger undead.","The expressions of countless people throughout the capital immediately changed drastically. Even many imperial experts looked stunned. Clearly, a large portion of them had absolutely no idea these existences were hidden here.","Michael stared at the scene silently for several seconds. Internally, he cursed violently, working his way through Princess Priscilla, the Tenth Prince, the Ninth Prince, the Third Prince, and finally the emperor himself.","Seven Legendary beings. Together with the emperor and Eunuch Liang, the Black Serpent Empire actually possessed seven Rank 4 existences.","At this point, even Michael could not maintain his calm expression completely. This was ridiculous. Absolutely ridiculous.","These were beings capable of becoming regional overlords anywhere they went, and yet the Black Serpent Empire had somehow hidden seven of them beneath the surface the entire time.","Below, countless nobles and soldiers stared upward in shock and disbelief. Clearly, even many members of the imperial family were unaware of the empire’s true foundations.","Michael’s lips twitched slightly. \"...What is wrong with these people?\"","Still, Michael was not scared. His heart was beating faster, but he was not scared.","Only five of the seven were genuinely formidable. The other two, though radiating strong auras, felt somewhat unstable. The fact that they could only barely match his own aura, and he was still technically a fake Rank 4, suggested they were not particularly powerful within the Rank 4 tier. Compared to his four undead, they were likely weaker.","The emperor stared at Michael silently for several seconds. Then eventually, his voice echoed across the skies.","*","A/N: Sorry for late update. Mass release tomorrow so we can reach the finalisation of this arc!!"]},{"number":1015,"title":"Chapter 1015: Eve of Battle!","paragraphs":["\"You have reached this level of strength already. That is not easy.\" The pressure around him intensified faintly. \"So I will give you one final chance. I do not know your grievance against me and my empire. Leave now, and I can pretend tonight never happened.\"","His tone carried unquestionable authority. Then his eyes turned colder. \"Or, if you truly are not afraid of dying after cultivating to this level, stay.\"","The atmosphere instantly became heavier. Even the winds around the capital seemed to freeze.","Michael looked at the emperor quietly. Then finally, he spoke.","\"I killed two imperial princes. If your empire can promise in front of everyone here that you will not pursue this matter further, then I will leave.\"","Silence.","\"But if you cannot, then let’s fight to the death.\"","The skies trembled faintly. Below, countless people held their breath.","Of course, if Michael could not defeat the empire without paying a devastating cost, he would run. But that was a thought he kept to himself.","The emperor stared at him silently. Several seconds passed.","Then finally, \"...So be it.\"","The emperor’s expression turned incomparably cold. \"EVERYONE! ATTACK!\"","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The countless massive formations above the capital erupted with blinding light. Michael’s expression changed instantly.","Space distorted violently around him. His vision blurred. An overwhelming spatial force swallowed him whole before he could fully resist.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The world changed. Everything around him transformed into endless darkness.","Michael’s eyes narrowed sharply. He had actually been forcefully dragged into the void itself.","Not only him. Behind him, roughly five hundred undead had also been pulled into the isolated space. As for the remaining undead, Michael could faintly sense them outside the void. Clearly, the empire’s formation had intentionally separated part of his forces.","Although he could still forcibly leave if he truly wished, doing so would require time and effort. They had trapped him temporarily, and the empire’s experts clearly had no intention of giving him time to break free calmly.","BOOOOOOM!!!","One after another, terrifying auras rushed toward him through the void itself. The emperor led the charge personally. Behind him followed the seven Legendary beings of the empire. The void trembled violently beneath the pressure of so many powerful existences moving simultaneously.","\"Damn.\"","The instant Michael saw the empire’s experts rushing toward him through the void, he immediately understood their plan completely.","They had divided his forces.","The roughly three hundred undead left outside would now be forced to face the empire’s subjects within the capital. Meanwhile, Michael and the larger portion of his legion had been dragged into this isolated void battlefield where the empire’s true experts could focus entirely on crushing them.","As for the five hundred Rank 3 undead beside him, the empire’s experts probably did not care much about them at all. At this level, the shockwaves from a battle between multiple Rank 4 existences alone could already destroy ordinary Rank 3 beings in large numbers. They were essentially collateral.","It was honestly an excellent strategy. No. It was a terrifyingly good one.","The empire clearly possessed extensive experience dealing with large-scale wars and powerful enemies. The emperor had not acted impulsively even after losing two sons. Instead, he had remained calm enough to instantly create the battlefield most advantageous for the empire itself.","Though Michael also wondered briefly whether part of that composure came from not particularly caring about those sons to begin with.","Either way, Michael could not help feeling slightly impressed. These old monsters truly deserved to rule a hegemonic empire.","However, impressive as the strategy was, it still had one fundamental flaw. They had underestimated him and his legion far too much.","Outside the void, the moment Michael and nearly five hundred undead vanished from the skies, many people immediately realized what had happened.","\"The Emperor trapped them! He dragged them into the void!\"","\"Focus on the ones remaining outside! Kill them before they can regroup!\"","Instantly, countless gazes turned toward the three hundred undead still floating above the capital. The expressions of many imperial experts became fierce and eager.","Even if the enemy still possessed hundreds of Rank 3 beings above the city, their true strength had been separated away.","As long as the empire eliminated the undead outside quickly enough, they could consolidate their victory before whatever was happening inside the void resolved itself.","Also they were about 200 more people than the other party. The empire side was filled with confidence. Even if the other 500 returned after this, they wouldn’t be scared since the number would be even by then.","Several hundred imperial Rank 3 experts began advancing upward with weapons drawn. The great noble clans mobilized their own forces alongside the imperial knights. It was a coordinated encirclement.","However, despite the overwhelming force closing in from every direction, the remaining undead showed absolutely no panic. Putting aside the fact they were incapable of feeling it, there was truly no need.","The imperial experts suddenly slowed as a figure in black robes stepped forward from among the undead.","It was Spartan.","Black flames quietly burned across the surface of his body. Without warning, terrifying black flames exploded outward from his body.","Several Rank 3 experts charging at the front immediately changed expressions.","\"DEFEND!\"","It was already too late. The black flames swept across the skies like a tidal wave.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The surrounding air distorted violently. One armored knight was sent flying backward instantly while coughing blood. Another mage screamed miserably as the protective barriers around his body melted apart like paper.","The charging momentum of the imperial forces was forcibly halted in a single exchange.","Countless expressions changed drastically.","\"What kind of flame is that?!\"","\"It corroded my mana!\"","\"Careful!\"","Meanwhile, Spartan merely stood silently amidst the spreading black fire. Then his voice echoed across the battlefield.","\"My master already gave you a chance. His grudge is only with the imperial family, not with the rest of you. Step aside and you will not die tonight.\"","\"But if you refuse, then all of you will die here.\""]},{"number":1016,"title":"Chapter 1016 Great Battle [1]","paragraphs":["Michael's impression of Spartan was that it was very steady. Other than Jester, it was the only other undead that could pass as human.","However, compared to Jester it was not particularly flexible. Though it could be ruthless, it lacked Jester's extreme mindset, but what it had instead was stability. Perhaps even rigidity.","When Michael had said that the empire's subjects would live if they surrendered, Jester hearing that might either comply as told or find a way to twist the words around if he had his own ideas. That way he would technically not disobey his master's words while potentially gaining more benefits for himself or his master.","Of course this depended on whether Jester had any other thoughts in the first place. As a bloodthirsty creature, there was a high chance he would simply kill before they had the chance to surrender.","But this also went to show one of Jester's greatest strengths. His flexibility.","Spartan was not quite like that. He was flexible, but not to Jester's degree. Since his master had said that if they did not surrender they would die, then they had to die. Even if Spartan had its own thoughts, its master's words were ironclad.","After seeing the effect of Spartan's attack, many of the empire's subjects were visibly shaken.","Unfortunately, while there were many who did not want a fight to the death, there were also many who were serious about fulfilling the emperor's will. With the surface advantage of their numbers and the pressure of their peers watching, no one surrendered. They immediately charged at Michael's undead legion.","Since the other party did not want to surrender, Michael's army did not hold back either.","The next moment, the sky above the capital erupted with the clashing attacks of hundreds of supernaturals.","Meanwhile, in the second layer of the void, the battle between several Rank 4 beings had begun.","Knowing the pain of losing multiple undead at once and understanding the full magnitude of this battle, Michael immediately had many of his weaker undead distance themselves from the fighting. He unsummoned the ones he could back to the netherworld.","If he had a bit more time he would have placed them inside the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten, but even a second's delay against opponents of this caliber could put him in serious trouble.","Before both parties met, as was customary between beings of their status, all parties aside from Michael greeted each other with their domains in an attempt to draw the opposing party in.","As expected, the clashing domains cancelled each other out.","Based on the intensity each opponent gave off, each party chose a target of matching strength.","The two figures whose intensity approached the High Drake immediately went for it. Knowing the destructive potential of their combined attacks, all three distanced themselves from the others.","With the High Drake gone, it remained Lily, Beginning, the Rank 4 Demonic Supernatural, and Michael.","After the High Drake, the next figure giving off the strongest aura was the Demonic Supernatural. The emperor immediately took it on alone.","Lily and Beginning each found their own opponents as well.","Meanwhile, Michael was immediately targeted by the two Legendary beings with the weakest auras.","At first glance, the empire's division of opponents was quite flawless.","KRAAAABOOOM!!!","The instant the two weaker Legendary beings rushed toward Michael, the void itself split violently.","One was an old man cloaked in dark blue-black flames. Every movement he made caused the surrounding void to corrode and distort faintly, as though the fire itself could burn space apart. The second was a middle-aged woman dressed in deep azure robes. Terrifying waves surged around her body endlessly, transforming into enormous water dragons that swam freely through the void itself.","Their attacks arrived almost simultaneously.","The old man thrust his palm forward.","KRAAABOOM!!!","Dark flames erupted like a volcanic explosion.","At the same time, the woman waved her sleeve coldly. An enormous wave instantly swallowed the surroundings like a collapsing ocean.","Michael's eyes narrowed sharply.","Without hesitation, he reached into his storage space and a dark spear instantly appeared in his grasp. The weapon radiated terrifying energy as runes flickered continuously across its surface.","The next moment, Michael thrust the spear forward directly.","As long as the use of domains remained limited, even with almost half of his engraved creatures in their summoned state, Michael dared to fight. Even if a domain was deployed, they had to catch him first before they could think about killing him.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","Black flames exploded across the void. The three attacks collided violently. The impact alone shattered the surrounding space repeatedly while enormous cracks spread throughout the void layer itself.","Michael was blasted backward immediately afterward. His body shot through the darkness like a meteor while violent force traveled up both his arms.","\"So strong...\"","Michael's expression became even more serious. These two might have been the weakest among the empire's Rank 4 existences, but they were still genuine Legendary beings.","The two opponents clearly had no intention of giving him breathing room. Both rushed after Michael instantly through the shattered void.","After personally testing their attacks with his own body, Michael actually felt a degree of confidence rather than fear. The pressure from the two Legendary beings was indeed terrifying, but not enough to crush him instantly.","As Michael shot backward through the void, he activated his law and immediately copied Beginning's trait. A ripple spread across his body as his skin turned slightly grey. The next moment, his aura changed drastically as strength surged through him.","CRACK.","Michael flexed his fingers around the dark spear.","Excitement appeared within Michael's eyes as he watched the two opponents close the distance.","There truly were not many opportunities to fight battles at this level. Ever since reaching his current strength, Michael had developed countless theories regarding how to use his abilities and Laws in combat. Unfortunately and fortunately at the same time, he rarely encountered enemies powerful enough to test those ideas properly.","But now, he finally could.","The thought had barely crossed his mind before the two opponents attacked again.","The old man suddenly spread both arms outward."]},{"number":1017,"title":"Chapter 1017 Great Battle [2]","paragraphs":["KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The blue-black flames surrounding him instantly transformed. The fire condensed into countless gigantic serpents made entirely from corrosive flame. Each serpent radiated terrifying Law fluctuations while burning holes directly through the void itself.","\"Law Skill...\"","The old man's cold voice echoed throughout the darkness.","\"Netherflame Serpent Realm.\"","HISSSSSSSS!!!","Thousands of flaming serpents instantly surged toward Michael from every direction.","At nearly the same moment, the woman in azure robes raised one hand. The ocean around her suddenly froze still for a fraction of a second. Then, KRAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The water compressed violently before exploding outward. Massive blue symbols appeared across the surrounding void while the ocean transformed into countless rotating water rings sharp enough to sever space itself.","\"Law Skill...\"","Her eyes turned icy cold.","\"Abyssal Tidal Judgment.\"","The surrounding void instantly became filled with overwhelming pressure. Two completely different Law Skills descended toward Michael simultaneously.","Law Skills.","These were the true trademark abilities of seasoned law wielders. If ordinary abilities were like weapons, then Law Skills were the crystallization of a supernatural's understanding of their law. They were centralized manifestations born directly from one's Law itself. Some civilizations referred to them as Divine Abilities, as they far surpassed ordinary supernatural techniques in both scale and power.","Of course, that did not mean ordinary attacks from a Rank 4 being were weak by comparison.","Even a casual strike from a Legendary being was already terrifying enough to kill most Rank 3 supernaturals instantly. The reasons were numerous. The purity of mana, the density of energy, the strengthening effect granted by one's Law, the transformation of their bodies after advancing into the next rank. At that level, even ordinary attacks already carried traces of one's Law unconsciously.","A slash from a Rank 4 swordsman was no longer merely a slash. A flame from a Rank 4 fire supernatural was no longer merely fire. Everything they did had already begun affecting reality itself.","Still, Law Skills were different. They represented focused expressions of one's path. The stronger and more experienced a supernatural became, the more terrifying their Law Skills naturally became as well.","And this was something Michael severely lacked.","His growth speed had simply been too absurd. Compared to other Rank 3 supernaturals who had spent decades or even centuries polishing their Laws and developing signature abilities, Michael's foundation was honestly shallow. Even if his combat strength was monstrous, his experience was not.","Because of this, many of Michael's attacks until now had honestly been quite crude. Overwhelming strength. Overwhelming mana. Overwhelming numbers of undead and copied skills. Most of the time, he simply crushed enemies head-on with sheer advantage. Michael often fought more like a brute than a refined high-level supernatural.","It worked, so that mattered. But the stronger he became, the clearer this weakness became as well. It was the same for many of his undead.","A true powerhouse could not rely on raw force forever.","Fortunately, after all this time, Michael himself had grown in many other ways beyond just raw stats.","Seeing the two Law attacks bearing down on him, Michael immediately used his law to copy the traits of the Rank 4 Demonic Supernatural. A ripple spread across his body.","Dark water suddenly erupted around Michael. The moment it appeared, the surrounding void distorted as though unable to bear its weight.","\"Law Skill...\"","Michael's voice echoed through the void.","The dark water rapidly condensed around him before forming a massive shield several dozen meters wide. Its surface resembled a perfectly still ocean at midnight.","An ocean could withstand countless storms because it accepted everything. Mountains collapsed into it. Rivers flowed into it. Rain fell endlessly upon it. Yet the ocean remained.","Michael's eyes shone faintly.","\"Eternal Abyss Barrier.\"","Michael had spent months thinking about how his Law could be used beyond simply copying traits. If he copied enough of a subject's law and studied it extensively with the source as reference, could he create a Law Skill?","Today was his first real attempt.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The Netherflame Serpent Realm crashed into the shield first. Thousands of flaming serpents slammed into the dark water surface simultaneously. The Abyssal Tidal Judgment arrived an instant later. Countless water rings capable of severing space itself descended at the same moment.","The void exploded.","For a brief moment, even the darkness of the second layer vanished beneath the collision.","The barrier trembled violently. Cracks spread across its surface. Yet the attacks that should have destroyed it immediately were instead being swallowed layer after layer, absorbed into the depths of the dark water like stones dropped into a bottomless sea.","Michael's eyes widened slightly. Then a grin slowly appeared on his face.","\"It worked.\"","For the first time since becoming this strong, Michael felt as though he had finally stepped onto the path of a true Law wielder rather than a powerful brute relying solely on overwhelming advantages. As for whether he could create Law Skills from his own Law entirely, that was left for the future him to solve. The current Michael now only wanted to use the Black Serpent Empire as a whetstone to grow stronger.","\"Let's continue!\"","As the battle between Michael and the two Legendary beings grew more intense, the other battles happening throughout the void were no weaker.","Among them, the second most violent clash was the one between the Black Serpent Emperor and the Rank 4 Demonic Undead.","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","Purple flames and black water collided once more. The resulting explosion instantly shattered several kilometers of void around them.","The Emperor's expression remained calm, but his eyes had long since turned cold and inhuman. At some point, he had already revealed his true bloodline form, causing his power to surge even further.","A gigantic black serpent over two hundred meters long coiled through the void. Its scales resembled black obsidian while purple flames burned between the gaps, and runes continuously appeared and disappeared across its body. Each movement caused space itself to tremble.","This was the true bloodline that had allowed the Black Serpent Empire to dominate the region for centuries.","The Imperial Black Serpent."]},{"number":1018,"title":"Chapter 1018 Great Battle [3]","paragraphs":["HISSSSSSSS!!!","The Emperor opened his enormous jaws. A sea of purple fire erupted forward. Unlike ordinary flames, these fires possessed a strange quality. Wherever they passed, mana itself ignited. Even the void seemed to burn.","Meanwhile, opposite him, the Rank 4 Demonic Undead remained expressionless. Dark water flowed endlessly around its body.","KRAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The black water rose like a tidal wall and crashed directly against the purple flames. The collision generated enough force to split the void repeatedly. For a moment, neither side gained an advantage.","The Emperor's Law focused on destruction and domination. His purple flames represented authority. The will to suppress. The will to conquer. The will to rule all beneath heaven.","Neither side naturally countered the other.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The gigantic serpent suddenly lunged forward. Its enormous body crossed space in an instant. At the same moment, the Demonic Undead raised one hand. The endless black water surrounding it suddenly condensed. The ocean disappeared. Then reappeared around its fist.","An entire sea compressed into a single strike.","The Emperor's pupils contracted.","\"Law Skill...\"","\"Demonic Abyss Crushing Tide.\"","The fist moved. The void collapsed.","For the first time since revealing his true form, the Emperor's expression changed. He could clearly feel it. This attack was strong enough to seriously injure him.","KRAAAAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The serpent's head and the abyssal fist collided head-on. The resulting shockwave spread across the entire second layer of the void. Far away, even Michael and the other Legendary beings felt the terrifying fluctuation and instinctively looked in that direction.","It was also at this point that Michael realized his High Drake was nowhere to be found. He immediately understood. The other party had probably dragged it into their domain.","Far away from the other battlefields, hidden within another layer of the void entirely, a completely different world existed.","The sky was dark crimson. Countless volcanoes stretched endlessly across the horizon while rivers of molten lava flowed like oceans beneath the heavens. Every few seconds, massive eruptions occurred somewhere in the distance, launching mountains of magma into the sky. The temperature alone was enough to instantly vaporize ordinary Rank 3 beings.","At the center of this world, KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","A colossal dragon nearly three hundred meters tall smashed through a volcanic mountain. Molten rock exploded in every direction.","The High Drake spread its wings. Its enormous body was covered in crimson scales, each one glowing faintly like heated metal fresh from a forge. Red flames flowed continuously across its body.","ROOOOOOAAARRR!!!","The entire volcanic world shook beneath the dragon's roar.","Opposite it stood two gigantic serpents. One burned with deep blue flames. The other burned with pink flames. Both possessed bodies over four hundred meters long. Both radiated terrifying Rank 4 pressure.","These were two of the Legendary ancestors of the Black Serpent Empire. Together with the emperor, the royal family alone had three Legendary beings. The other four were not from the family. Eunuch Liang belonged to an orphan force under the empire, while among the remaining three, one belonged to the strongest noble family after the royal family, and one was the empire's strongest military officer.","The blue-flamed serpent opened its mouth. A beam of deep blue fire shot forward. The surrounding lava instantly froze into crystal before shattering apart.","Almost simultaneously, the pink serpent attacked. Its flames transformed into countless blooming flowers made entirely from fire. Beautiful and deadly. Every flower contained enough power to erase a mountain.","The High Drake responded with overwhelming simplicity.","It inhaled.","The entire world seemed to darken.","Then, ROOOOOOAAARRR!!!","A sea of red dragon fire erupted outward. The three flames collided head-on. Red. Blue. Pink. The resulting explosion illuminated the entire volcanic world.","Volcanoes collapsed. Lava seas split apart. Space itself cracked repeatedly.","Yet despite fighting two opponents at once, the High Drake showed no signs of weakness. Instead, it was suppressing them. The dragon's red flames steadily pushed backward against both opposing Laws.","The two serpents immediately felt the pressure. Their expressions changed.","Not only was the High Drake stronger than both of them combined, but the dragon's bloodline alone was suppressing theirs.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The High Drake suddenly disappeared. The next instant, one enormous claw descended from above. The blue serpent barely raised a defensive wall of flame in time.","CRAAASH!!!","Its body was smashed directly into a volcano. The entire mountain exploded. Before the blue serpent could recover, the dragon's tail whipped around.","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The pink serpent was sent flying through dozens of kilometers of volcanic terrain. The entire world trembled.","For the first time, fear appeared in the eyes of both serpents. They had expected a difficult fight. They had not expected this.","High above the volcanic world, cracks slowly began spreading across the domain itself. The two serpents noticed immediately and their hearts sank. The cracks were being caused by the High Drake's mere presence. The domain was beginning to struggle to contain a creature infinitely approaching the Demigod realm.","\"...Where did that fool go?\" the pink serpent suddenly cursed. Its voice echoed throughout the volcanic world. \"Damn it! It has been ten years!\"","The blue serpent's expression darkened as well.","The figure they were referring to was the other Legendary ancestor of the Black Serpent Empire. One of the empire's oldest protectors, and the very same ancestor who had once crossed paths with Shojo and ultimately lost.","Unfortunately for them, they still did not know the truth. Unlike ordinary royal family members whose deaths could be tracked through life lamps and bloodline altars, Legendary beings were different. Their existence was too powerful. Once they reached that realm, many methods used to monitor lower-ranked supernaturals became unreliable, and their deaths were often difficult to confirm.","As a result, the empire still believed their missing ancestor might be alive somewhere. Neither serpent knew he had died long ago. Nor did they know that the enemy currently attacking the empire was connected to the chain of events surrounding that death.","In truth, just like the emperor, they understood almost nothing about this conflict. When the alarm had sounded, they had simply assumed some powerful force was attacking their homeland and entered battle accordingly.","Only now, while being driven backward by the High Drake, did a disturbing thought begin forming in their minds.","Who exactly was this enemy? Where had these terrifying people come from?","ROOOOOOAAARRR!!!","Their thoughts were interrupted as the High Drake spread its enormous wings. The volcanic world darkened. Red flames flooded the heavens. The cracks spreading across the domain multiplied instantly.","The expressions of both serpents changed.","The blue serpent hissed furiously. \"Forget that idiot.\"","The pink serpent nodded grimly. \"Let's survive first.\""]},{"number":1019,"title":"Chapter 1019 Great Battle [4]","paragraphs":["Back in the second layer of the void, Michael's battle had also reached a new stage.","At this moment, Michael no longer looked entirely human. His body had expanded slightly, not to the size of a true giant, but enough to give him the appearance of a miniature titan.","Grey-black patterns covered parts of his skin, while dark water and faint black flames twisted around his body like living armor. In his hand, the long dark spear hummed violently.","KRAAAABOOOOM!!!","Michael swung the spear horizontally.","The two Legendary beings attacking him were forced backward at the same time. The old man's blue-black flames shattered apart, while the woman's water rings collapsed into countless droplets across the void.","Michael's eyes were bright.","The earlier success of Eternal Abyss Barrier had opened something inside his mind. It was as though a door had finally been pushed open.","Ideas that had previously existed only as vague concepts were becoming clearer with every exchange.","Michael's understanding deepened rapidly in the middle of battle. Taking advantage of the moment, he began comprehending the one Law he was most familiar with.","Beginning's Law of Brutal Rebirth.","The Law of Brutal Rebirth was not simply about surviving injury. It was not merely regeneration, endurance, or stubborn vitality.","Its deeper concept was evolution through violence.","Beginning embodied that concept perfectly. The more damaged it became, the more terrifying its rebirth became.","Michael's eyes shone brighter.","\"So that's it...\"","The old man and woman immediately felt that something was wrong.","\"Stop him!\"","The woman shouted coldly.","The old man's flames erupted again, transforming into a massive serpent head that lunged directly toward Michael. At the same time, the woman summoned a giant spear of compressed abyssal water and hurled it forward.","Michael did not retreat.","Instead, he gripped his spear with both hands. Dark grey light erupted from his body.","\"Law Skill...\"","His voice was low, but it echoed clearly through the void.","\"Brutal Rebirth, First State.\"","KRAAAACK!","A violent sound erupted from inside Michael's body.","For a brief instant, his heartbeat became thunder. His muscles tightened, his bones creaked, and his mana surged like a dam breaking apart.","A terrifying force flooded every part of him as though his body had been forcefully dragged beyond its natural limit.","His power instantly rose by nearly fifty percent.","BOOOOOOOOM!!!","Michael disappeared.","The old man's pupils shrank.","Fast.","Too fast.","The next instant, Michael appeared directly before the serpent head of blue-black flame and thrust his spear forward.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The flame serpent exploded instantly.","Without stopping, Michael twisted his body and swung the spear again. The dark spear collided head-on with the woman's abyssal water spear.","The water spear shattered.","The woman was forced backward several hundred meters through the void, her expression filled with disbelief.","Michael remained in place, breathing slightly heavier than before.","He could feel it clearly.","This Law Skill was strong.","Very strong.","But the cost was equally obvious.","His life force was being consumed.","Even with his terrifying vitality, this was not something he could maintain casually. It was a burst-type skill and a trump card meant to decide a dangerous moment, not something to use freely in a prolonged battle.","Yet Michael's excitement only grew because he could feel that this skill was incomplete.","Beginning's Law possessed three states depending on the severity of its injuries. Michael was not arrogant enough to believe he could perfectly replicate all three right now, but he was confident he could eventually develop at least a second state.","Perhaps even a third one in the future.","What made this skill even more special was that it did not interfere with Beginning's passive Law effect. The more injured he became, the stronger he grew.","Which was to say that perhaps, in the future, Michael could achieve as many as six different burst effects.","The thought alone made his blood heat slightly.","Unfortunately, now was not the time to slowly study it.","The two Legendary beings had already recovered from their shock.","Michael slowly raised his spear again, his aura pressing down on both of them like a mountain.","\"When are the two of you planning to reveal yourselves?\"","The two immediately started looking uneasy.","When Michael had first fought them, he felt a strange sensation from the pair. The longer the battle continued, the stronger that feeling became.","After some time, he noticed that both possessed bloodline fluctuations similar to the Black Serpent royal family.","Yet neither had revealed a true bloodline form.","Not once.","That alone was abnormal.","The Emperor had transformed. The two ancestors fighting the High Drake had transformed before they disappeared.","Every bloodline warrior Michael had encountered eventually relied upon their bloodline form when pushed into a corner.","So why had these two not done so?","It was then that a shocking realization came to him.","These two were monster kin.","Bloodline warriors gave off a certain aura. Monsters gave off another.","Even if a monster transformed into a human, traces always remained.","Likewise, bloodline warriors who transformed into beasts still retained their human origins.","They were similar.","But not identical.","The same principle applied to Michael's undead.","A sufficiently powerful observer could always notice subtle differences.","When all those clues were placed together, the answer became obvious.","These two had monster origins.","Michael did not know whether they were the children of the Emperor or some other ancestor, but he had to acknowledge their adventurous spirits.","However, outside of their bloodline issue, Michael was focused on something else.","Killing humans did not provide experience points.","The same was true for other intelligent races outside the monster race.","Since these two were technically monsters, was it possible that killing them would grant experience points?","Though he suffered from the increasingly difficult requirements of leveling through experience points, these two were stronger than him and he was only a single level away from reaching the maximum.","Only one of them was needed.","Combined with the bonus he would receive from killing a higher-level opponent, he would almost certainly level up and reach the limit.","By then, his Rank Advancement Quest would finally be revealed.","And as long as he completed it, Rank 4 would not be far away."]},{"number":1020,"title":"Chapter 1020 Great Battle [5]","paragraphs":["The moment Michael exposed their secret, the atmosphere changed.","The old man's expression twisted.","The woman's face became incomparably ugly.","Their attacks instantly became more violent.","It was as though Michael had struck a hidden nerve.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","A massive serpent made of corrosive fire smashed toward Michael.","At the same time, hundreds of water blades descended from above.","Michael laughed and met them head-on.","The dark spear tore through the serpent.","His fist shattered dozens of water blades.","The battlefield immediately became chaotic.","Yet the more they fought, the more convinced Michael became.","He had guessed correctly.","Perhaps they could still be considered human since they were likely born in that form, but these two truly possessed monster blood.","Enough monster blood to affect their very existence.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The old man was forced backward again.","A trace of killing intent flashed through his eyes.","Then suddenly, his gaze met the woman's.","A silent exchange occurred.","The next moment, the surrounding void distorted.","A strange fluctuation spread outward.","Michael's expression immediately changed.","\"No!\"","Unfortunately, it was already too late.","Michael's vision blurred.","The world around him twisted. Space folded repeatedly as a familiar sensation of transportation engulfed him.","Meanwhile, the old man and woman were equally shocked.","\"What?!\"","\"He actually got pulled in?!\"","Both of them looked genuinely stunned.","Their original intention had merely been to test him and try their domain.","A domain was expensive.","Even Legendary beings did not casually activate one.","It consumed significant amounts of energy.","Usually, when two Rank 4 beings fought, their domains would clash and cancel each other out. Very rarely would one side continuously attempt to use a domain against the other.","For a brief moment, the two simply stared.","Neither knew what to think.","Had Michael made a mistake and reacted too slowly?","Or was his domain somehow weaker than theirs?","They could not understand it.","Unfortunately for them, the answer was much simpler.","Michael was not a Rank 4.","The reason he had not been dragged into a domain during the opening exchanges was because one of his undead had secretly covered for him.","Whenever the other Legendary beings attempted to spread their domains earlier, one of Michael's powerful undead had subtly interfered and neutralized the pressure.","As a result, everyone naturally assumed Michael possessed a domain of his own.","If these two had activated their domain from the very beginning of the battle, his secret might have been exposed much earlier.","Fortunately, domain activation was not something Legendary beings used casually.","That single misconception had protected Michael until now.","Unfortunately, that protection had finally disappeared.","When Michael's vision stabilized, the first thing he noticed was that the surroundings had completely changed.","The endless darkness of the void was gone.","In its place stood a vast forest.","Ancient trees stretched thousands of meters into the sky. Their trunks were wider than mountains, while countless vines hung from the heavens like green rivers.","The air itself carried an oppressive vitality.","Everything here was alive.","The ground.","The trees.","The flowers.","Even the wind.","However, Michael immediately felt a powerful suppressive force descend upon his body.","He knew this was the suppression effect of a domain.","His movements became heavier. The mana around him became sluggish.","Even his Laws felt slightly restrained.","\"So this is a domain...\"","Michael narrowed his eyes.","This was the first time he had truly experienced one alone.","Within a domain, the owner became closer to the embodiment of their Law itself. The world favored them and weakened their enemies.","At the same time, Michael felt another discomfort.","Brutal Rebirth.","The strain from the skill was accumulating.","His body was already consuming life force continuously.","Without hesitation, Michael deactivated it.","The grey-black light vanished.","The miniature giant form rapidly shrank.","His muscles returned to normal size, while the terrifying pressure surrounding him weakened considerably.","His robes, however, had suffered greatly.","The violent battle had left them tattered in several places.","Ignoring the state of his appearance, Michael stored the dark spear away with a thought.","Then he calmly reached into his storage space once more.","A different item appeared in his hand.","It was a pipa with four strings.","At the same time, the old man and woman finally stopped hiding their true forms.","Their human forms exploded apart.","In place of the old man stood a gigantic beast.","It resembled a wolf.","Yet not entirely.","Its body was covered in dark scales rather than fur. Massive antlers grew from its head, while blue-black flames burned within its eye sockets.","In place of the woman emerged a gigantic creature.","A white deer.","At least, part of it was.","The creature possessed six eyes, crystal antlers, and scales covering portions of its body.","Neither of them looked remotely similar to serpents.","Yet Michael could still sense traces of the Black Serpent bloodline within both creatures.","Michael's eyes immediately brightened.","As expected.","His earlier suspicion had been correct.","For something like this to happen, the explanations were limited.","Either two different bloodline warriors had somehow produced offspring whose bloodlines fused and mutated.","Or the possibility Michael considered far more likely.","A bloodline warrior had mated with a monster.","The resulting offspring inherited both lineages.","Half human.","Half monster.","Monster kin.","It was probably why the two had hidden their forms as well.","Their very existence was likely a secret.","Perhaps one the Black Serpent Empire did not want widely known.","The wolf-like creature stared at Michael with murderous eyes.","Its voice echoed throughout the forest.","\"You should have kept your mouth shut.\"","The six-eyed deer lowered its head.","The surrounding trees immediately began moving as they burst into flames.","Seeing this, Michael knew it was the old man's domain he had entered.","However, though he was facing stronger opponents, Michael felt more excited than afraid.","Without hesitation, he reached toward one of the strings of the pipa and plucked it.","*","A/N: Sorry for the late update dear readers!! Might sound like a silly excuse but not only did I sleep through my free time, real life issues caught up with me. I'm so sorry!!! Also thank you Daoist_Eshey for the massive support!!!"]},{"number":1021,"title":"Chapter 1021 Great Battle [6]","paragraphs":["The Sovereign Pipa had four strings, each possessing a different effect.","As a Three-Star Epic Grade item, its abilities were extremely powerful.","The first string was called Shattering Pluck. It released a concentrated sonic burst in a straight line, with the force scaling according to the amount of mana invested.","The second string was Binding Resonance. A sustained note released an invisible resonance field that anchored targets within range, restricting spatial movement, including teleportation, for as long as the note was maintained.","The third string was Soul Tremor. A plucked chord sent vibrations directly into the spiritual bodies of targets within range, destabilizing active domain effects.","The fourth string was Sovereign's Dirge. A full strum released a sweeping wave of oppressive sound that suppressed all living targets within range, reducing their combat output by twenty percent for thirty seconds.","Michael's finger rested upon the third string. The moment he touched it, he did not hesitate.","TWANG!!!","A deep note echoed across the forest. Immediately, Michael felt a terrifying amount of mana leave his body. His expression changed slightly.","\"So expensive?\"","The drain was enormous. Normally it would already have been costly, but after battling several Legendary beings, using Law Skills, activating Brutal Rebirth, and exchanging attacks continuously, his mana reserves were far from full. Even someone with Michael's absurd mana pool felt the loss instantly.","The wolf-like creature immediately noticed. Its antlers glowed.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The entire forest domain responded. Blue-black flames erupted from every tree. Countless pillars of fire shot toward Michael from every direction.","At the same time, the six-eyed deer raised its head. The air trembled. Thousands of droplets appeared above the forest, each one rapidly expanding into spears of compressed water.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The water spears rained downward. Michael immediately moved. His figure blurred through the forest as explosions erupted behind him one after another. Ancient trees collapsed. Flames devoured the landscape. Water spears blasted craters into the earth.","TWANG!!!","Michael plucked the string a second time. The sound spread farther than before. Invisible ripples flowed through the domain.","This time he immediately noticed something. Several nearby trees trembled. The blue-black flames flickered slightly. The suppression pressing down upon him weakened by a tiny amount.","Michael's eyes lit up. It was working. The effect was small, but it was undeniably working.","The wolf-like creature's expression darkened. \"Stop him!\"","It roared furiously. The six-eyed deer reacted immediately. Its six eyes glowed simultaneously.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The rivers flowing through the forest suddenly rose into the sky. The water twisted and transformed into enormous dragons. Five. Ten. Twenty. The water dragons roared as they surged toward Michael.","TWANG!!!","Michael plucked the third string. The sound became sharper. The invisible vibrations spread throughout the domain.","KRAAAACK!!!","A tiny crack appeared in the crimson sky above. The surrounding forest trembled violently. The wolf-like creature's eyes widened. The six-eyed deer immediately noticed it as well.","The domain had been damaged.","\"A supreme treasure?\"","The deer spoke coldly. Neither of them had expected Michael to possess something like this.","The wolf-like creature's killing intent intensified. Michael did not answer. He continued dodging the attacks thrown at him.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A dragon of water exploded behind him.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A sea of blue-black fire engulfed the place he had occupied moments earlier.","The domain continuously strengthened the wolf-like creature. Every tree. Every vine. Every flame. Everything within this world obeyed its will. Meanwhile, the deer continuously supported it from the side. Water spears. Water dragons. Water blades. Relentless attacks rained toward Michael.","TWANG!!!","The fourth pluck echoed across the forest. This time the effect was immediate. The invisible sound wave spread through the entire domain.","KRAAAAAACK!!!","A massive crack split open the heavens. Entire sections of forest shook violently. Countless burning leaves fell from the sky. The domain was beginning to destabilize.","The wolf-like creature finally lost its composure. \"No!\"","Its roar shook the forest. The blue-black flames throughout the domain exploded. Thousands of burning vines erupted from the earth.","The six-eyed deer joined in immediately.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","Entire rivers rose into the air. Thousands of water spears condensed simultaneously. The sky itself disappeared beneath the attacks.","For a brief moment there was nowhere left to dodge.","Michael's expression remained serious as his body flashed through countless attacks. Several water spears grazed his shoulder. A burning vine struck his back. Another attack tore through his robes.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","Michael crashed through several gigantic trees. Fresh blood appeared at the corner of his lips.","Yet when he looked upward, he smiled.","Around him were cracks. They were everywhere. The sky resembled shattered glass. The forest trembled continuously. The flames were becoming unstable. Even the domain's suppression had weakened significantly.","The wolf-like creature and the six-eyed deer both felt panic rising within their hearts.","Domains were not invincible. Once heavily damaged, the backlash would directly affect the owner. At best it would be minor damage that could be ignored. At worst it would be a crippling backlash.","Michael stood up. Blood dripped from his arm. His mana reserves had fallen dramatically.","\"This should be enough,\" he muttered as he reached for the third string again.","The wolf-like creature immediately charged. Its massive body crossed the forest in an instant. Blue-black flames gathered within its jaws.","The six-eyed deer raised all six eyes toward the sky.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A gigantic ocean suddenly appeared above the forest. Countless water spears condensed within it. Both attacks descended simultaneously.","Michael calmly plucked the third string one final time.","TWAAAAAAAAANG!!!","The sound that erupted was completely different from the previous four. The entire forest froze. The flames froze. The water froze. Even the wind stopped moving.","For a brief moment, absolute silence descended.","Then, KRAAAAAAAAAAAAAACK!!!","The sky shattered. The forest split apart. The burning trees exploded into fragments of light. The rivers suspended in the heavens collapsed. The entire domain broke apart like a shattered mirror.","The wolf-like creature coughed blood instantly. The six-eyed deer staggered backward. Both stared in disbelief.","\"No!\"","KRAAAAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The forest world collapsed completely. The endless darkness of the void returned.","Michael reappeared within the second layer of the void. His robes were torn. His mana reserves were heavily depleted. His body carried multiple injuries.","Yet the grin on his face had never been brighter."]},{"number":1022,"title":"Chapter 1022 Level Up!","paragraphs":["The wolf-like man and the six-eyed deer woman were not nearly as calm. That was what Michael called them now, as both had reverted back to their human forms.","The instant the domain shattered, blood spilled from the corners of the old man's mouth. As the domain owner, he had suffered the majority of the backlash. It was not enough to cripple him, and given some time he could even activate it again, but it was enough to affect him considerably.","Unfortunately for him, Michael had no intention of giving him time to recover. The moment he saw the two appear outside the collapsed domain, his eyes lit up.","\"Got you.\"","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","Michael shot forward like a black comet. The old man's expression changed drastically.","\"Protect me!\"","The woman reacted instantly. Hundreds of water blades appeared around her. At the same time, countless waves surged forward in an attempt to intercept Michael.","Unfortunately, she was too late. Michael had already arrived.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","His fist crashed directly into the old man's chest. The old man's ribs shattered instantly. His entire body folded inward before being blasted thousands of meters through the void. Blood exploded from his mouth. The force of the punch continued traveling through him, rupturing organs and tearing apart muscles.","The old man felt his vision darken. Too fast. The attack had come too fast.","Before he could even stabilize himself, Michael appeared again. The old man's eyes widened.","\"No!\"","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The second attack landed. This time Michael's fist smashed directly into his face. Half the old man's skull collapsed. His body spun uncontrollably through the void while blood and shattered teeth scattered everywhere. The surrounding space distorted violently.","The old man had already reached the brink of death. His aura plummeted. His soul fluctuated violently.","The woman finally arrived. Her expression was filled with fury. \"STOP!\"","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","A gigantic tidal wave descended from above. Water dragons. Water spears. Water blades. Everything she could summon crashed toward Michael simultaneously.","Michael ignored all of it. A water spear pierced through his shoulder. A water blade sliced across his back. One dragon slammed into him hard enough to crack several bones.","Yet Michael did not stop. His eyes remained fixed on the old man.","The old man's face finally showed fear. At that moment he could sense death approaching closer than it had ever been. For the first time since becoming a Legendary being, he felt it truly near.","\"Save me!\"","He screamed toward the woman.","Unfortunately, Michael was already there. The third attack arrived.","KRAAAAAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The entire void shook. Michael's fist punched directly through the old man's chest.","The old man froze. His eyes widened. His mouth opened. Yet no words came out.","A moment later, cracks began spreading across his body. Then everything shattered simultaneously.","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The old man's body exploded into pieces. Michael's hand twisted at an unnatural angle, but a moment later it instantly healed.","Silence descended.","The woman froze. For a brief moment, she could not believe what she was seeing.","A Legendary being. Dead just like that.","Michael slowly withdrew his arm. Blood dripped from his fist. Several wounds covered his body. His breathing was slightly heavy. Yet his eyes remained bright.","The moment the old man died, a notification panel appeared before him. At the same time, a sensation of strength filled him. Though minor, it was enough to heal him slightly.","Michael had levelled up.","More importantly, he had levelled to Level 75, which was the maximum level for Rank 3. This meant his rank advancement task had finally generated.","The moment the old man exploded apart, the woman finally reacted. The shock and disbelief vanished from her face. What replaced it was pure killing intent.","If Michael had paid more attention to his earlier suspicion, he would have noticed something. These two were definitely monster-kin, meaning a human had mated with their mother. Or perhaps their father. But there were two of them. Had that human mated with the monster twice, or were the two likely twins?","\"You bastard!\"","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","The surrounding void instantly transformed into a raging ocean. Countless rivers appeared from nowhere. Water dragons roared. Thousands of water spears condensed around her. Every attack she could unleash descended toward Michael simultaneously. The sheer fury behind the assault was enough to distort the surrounding void.","Unfortunately for her, Michael had already seen it coming.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","His figure vanished. Several hundred water spears pierced through the place he had occupied moments earlier. The void exploded.","The woman did not stop. She had already realized something. Michael was exhausted. His mana reserves were low. His body was injured. His strongest treasure had consumed an absurd amount of energy. If there was ever a chance to kill him, it was now.","\"Die!\"","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","A colossal water dragon lunged toward Michael. At the same time, dozens of tidal blades cut through space from every direction.","Michael dodged the dragon. Unfortunately, he could not avoid everything. A water blade sliced across his chest. Another pierced through his thigh. A third exploded against his shoulder. Fresh blood sprayed into the void.","Yet Michael did not retreat. Instead, his eyes became colder. If she wanted his life, then he would exchange injuries for hers.","Without hesitation, Michael activated his Law Skill once more.","\"Brutal Rebirth. First State.\"","KRAAAAAACK!!!","His heartbeat exploded like thunder. The strain that had only just begun fading immediately returned. His muscles tightened. His bones creaked. His lifeforce began burning once more. The familiar surge of power flooded his body.","The woman's expression changed.","KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","Michael disappeared. The woman immediately retreated. Water surged around her. Defensive barriers appeared one after another. Water dragons moved to intercept him.","Unfortunately, she was slower. Much slower.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","Michael's fist smashed through the first barrier.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The second shattered.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","The third exploded apart.","The woman's eyes widened. She immediately condensed a spear of abyssal water and thrust it forward.","Michael ignored it. The spear pierced directly through his abdomen. Blood exploded from his mouth. Yet his speed did not decrease.","The woman's heart sank. This madman. He was not even trying to defend. He was only trying to kill her.","Before she could retreat further, Michael arrived.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","His fist smashed into her shoulder. The entire arm exploded. The woman screamed. Her body spun backward through the void.","Unfortunately, Michael was already following. The second attack arrived almost instantly.","KRAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","His knee collided with her ribs. Bones shattered. Several organs ruptured. Blood poured from her mouth. Her aura immediately weakened.","Yet she was still alive. After all, she was a Legendary being. Not someone who could be killed so easily.","Unfortunately, Michael had no intention of giving her time to recover.","The woman finally panicked. For the first time since becoming a Rank 4 being, she felt genuine terror.","\"No!\"","She unleashed everything she had. Thousands of water blades erupted outward. Water dragons exploded. Tidal waves swallowed the surrounding void. Michael endured everything.","One blade nearly severed his left arm. A dragon shattered several ribs. Another attack tore through his back. His injuries rapidly accumulated. Yet every wound only brought him closer, and at the same time filled him with strength.","The woman's face became increasingly pale.","The third attack arrived.","KRAAAAAAAAAABOOOOOM!!!","Michael's fist smashed directly into her chest. The woman's eyes widened. Time seemed to freeze.","Then cracks began spreading across her body. Her soul. Her Law. Her origin. Everything began collapsing simultaneously.","\"N... no...\"","Those were her final words.","KRAAAAABOOOOOOOOM!!!","Her body exploded into countless fragments."]},{"number":1023,"title":"Chapter 1023 Poor Eunuch","paragraphs":["As Michael fought his opponents, the battles between the other Legendary beings had also reached their peak.","However, among all the battlefields, two in particular had taken an unexpectedly strange turn. One belonged to Beginning. The other belonged to Lily.","Once again, Michael's troublesome undead proved they could do more than create problems for their master.","The one who had chosen to fight Lily was the Emperor's closest confidant. Eunuch Liang.","In terms of pure combat ability, Eunuch Liang was actually stronger than Lily. After all, he was a genuine Legendary being who had spent centuries perfecting his Law. His combat experience vastly surpassed Lily's. His understanding of battle surpassed Lily's.","Yet at this moment, Eunuch Liang's expression was incomparably ugly. Hidden beneath it was something else entirely.","Dread. And disbelief. Never in his entire life had he encountered such an absurd opponent.","The battlefield they occupied existed within a hidden world inside the second layer of the void. It was a world of mountains. Nothing else. Endless mountains stretched toward the horizon. Gigantic peaks rose tens of thousands of meters into the sky. The air was thin. The earth was heavy. Gravity itself seemed several times stronger than normal.","At the center of this mountainous world stood Lily.","Unlike her usual appearance, she had already expanded her body. A forty-meter-tall giant stood atop a shattered mountain. Her pale skin resembled marble. Her long black hair danced wildly behind her.","In comparison, Eunuch Liang appeared tiny. The old man floated several hundred meters away, his robes fluttering in the wind.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A mountain exploded apart. Thousands of stone spears erupted from beneath Lily's feet. The countless stone spears transformed into golden chains before wrapping around Lily from every direction.","Any ordinary Legendary being would have dodged or destroyed the attack. Lily did neither.","Instead, she opened her mouth.","CHOMP.","The nearest chain vanished.","Eunuch Liang blinked.","CHOMP. A second chain disappeared. CHOMP. CHOMP. CHOMP.","Within seconds, thousands of meters worth of Law-infused chains had vanished into Lily's mouth.","Eunuch Liang stared. His eyelid twitched.","He still remembered the first time it happened. At first he thought it was some kind of illusion. Then he thought it was a defensive skill.","Unfortunately, the truth was much worse. She was literally eating his attacks. Not redirecting. Not neutralizing. Eating. As if his carefully crafted Law attacks were nothing more than snacks.","Eunuch Liang unleashed another attack. Golden mountains descended from the sky. Each one contained enough force to flatten entire regions.","Lily looked upward. Then smiled. She had actually learned this from Spartan. He always smiled when he saw something good. Food was good enough to smile at, right? Unfortunately, as an undead, even with high intelligence to mimic emotions, she was still miles away from undead like Spartan and Jester.","A mountain-sized mouth opened and swallowed Eunuch Liang's attack whole.","CRUNCH. CRUNCH. CRUNCH.","The sound echoed throughout the world. Eunuch Liang nearly coughed blood at the sight, especially when he noticed that not only had the attack disappeared entirely, but Lily's injuries were healing. The cuts on her body closed. Even her aura grew slightly stronger.","Lily suddenly appeared before him. Despite her massive size, her speed was absurd.","Her fist descended. Eunuch Liang immediately raised several layers of defense.","The first shattered. The second shattered. The third exploded apart.","The old man's face changed. A moment later, the giant fist smashed into him.","His body shot through three mountains before finally stopping. Blood spilled from the corner of his mouth.","Far away, Lily charged again. Eunuch Liang's scalp went numb.","This was another problem. Lily was not only difficult to kill. She was physically powerful. Ridiculously powerful. Every attack carried terrifying force. Every strike could shatter mountains. Every punch forced him to waste enormous amounts of energy defending.","And every time he managed to injure her, she ate something and healed.","At this moment, Eunuch Liang genuinely felt wronged. For decades he had fought countless enemies. Sword experts. Beast tamers. Elemental supernaturals. Assassins. Necromancers. Yet never once had he fought something like this.","\"Just what kind of monster is this?\"","Eunuch Liang could not help but curse. At this point, if he could not tell Lily was not normal, he might as well commit suicide.","Unfortunately, Lily did not care about his complaints.","Eunuch Liang launched another attack. Lily rushed forward with excitement as his face turned even uglier.","The giantess crossed dozens of kilometers in an instant. Her enormous foot landed on a mountain peak, causing the entire region to collapse beneath the force. Eunuch Liang immediately retreated. Golden chains erupted from behind him. Each chain carried traces of his Law and enough force to easily bind ordinary Legendary beings.","Lily's mouth widened as entire sections of the golden chains vanished.","CRUNCH. CRUNCH. CRUNCH.","The sound of metal being crushed echoed endlessly across the mountain world. Eunuch Liang nearly vomited blood.","This was not a battle. This was robbery. Every attack he launched became her nourishment. Every successful strike became healing. Every exchange strengthened her. Meanwhile, his own reserves continued falling.","\"Die already!\"","Golden light erupted from his body. Thousands of golden runes appeared throughout the sky. The mountains rose. Even the earth itself rose. Everything transformed into weapons.","A mountain several kilometers wide ripped free from the ground and smashed toward Lily. Another followed. Then another. And another. Within seconds, the sky was filled with falling mountains.","Lily finally stopped charging. She looked upward.","Then she opened her mouth even wider. She spoke out her Law name before doing so, though in truth she did not need to use her mouth to devour. It was simply the most efficient and direct method.","Eunuch Liang's eye twitched. \"Don't you dare.\"","Lily dared.","Her mouth expanded. Then expanded again. And again.","CHOMP!!! One mountain disappeared. CHOMP!!! A second vanished. CHOMP!!! A third followed.","The giantess happily continued eating while molten rock and shattered debris fell around her.","Eunuch Liang felt something crack inside his heart. This thing was unreasonable. Completely unreasonable.","Before Lily could finish her meal, dozens of golden chains erupted from beneath her feet. Unlike before, these chains wrapped around her arms, legs, waist, and neck simultaneously. The mountains themselves joined the suppression.","For the first time, Lily's movement stopped.","Eunuch Liang's eyes lit up. Finally. Finally he had managed to restrain her.","Without hesitation, he thrust both hands forward. \"Mountain Burial!\"","The entire world shook. Thousands of mountains descended simultaneously. The sheer weight distorted space. Lily disappeared beneath the attack.","Then came the impact.","BOOM!!!","The mountain world trembled violently. Shockwaves spread across the horizon. Entire peaks shattered. Even Eunuch Liang was forced backward by the resulting force.","For several seconds, silence descended.","Then a sound echoed from beneath the pile of mountains.","CRUNCH.","Eunuch Liang froze.","CRUNCH. CRUNCH. CRUNCH.","\"No.\"","The sound grew louder. CRUNCH. CRUNCH. CRUNCH.","Then the mountains exploded apart.","Lily burst free. Chunks of mountains were still in her mouth. She was literally chewing them. Not only that, the injuries she had accumulated throughout the entire battle were gone. Completely gone.","Eunuch Liang stared blankly.","His attention shifted for only a fraction of a second. Against ordinary opponents it would not matter. Against Lily, it was fatal.","The giantess vanished. Eunuch Liang's heart sank, but it was already too late.","A colossal hand appeared around him. The old man barely raised a defense before the impact crushed it apart. Lily had caught him.","Her gigantic hand enclosed him completely. The old man's face turned pale.","It was then that he realized something, seeing as the giantess had not killed him even though she clearly could. From the very start, Lily had not been trying particularly hard to kill him.","She had been trying to eat him.","Slowly. Very slowly. The giantess brought her hand toward her face.","Eunuch Liang struggled frantically. Golden chains erupted. Golden mountains formed. Law power exploded. Everything smashed against Lily's fingers. Nothing worked.","The hand continued moving. Closer. Closer. Closer.","Until Eunuch Liang found himself staring directly at a gigantic mouth. A mouth large enough to swallow mountains.","Soon his vision darkened amidst his screams."]},{"number":1024,"title":"Chapter 1024 Beginning","paragraphs":["Meanwhile, in another hidden region of the second layer of the void, a completely different battle was taking place.","Unlike Eunuch Liang's mountain world, this domain was bizarre.","It was a world of scrolls. The sky was covered in endless burning scrolls stretching beyond sight. Rivers made entirely from parchment flowed across the land. Mountains of ancient documents rose toward the heavens.","Some scrolls were golden. Some were black. Some burned with crimson flames. Others floated silently through the air as though possessing minds of their own. Countless words and runes drifted throughout the world. Every second, thousands of flaming scrolls opened and closed by themselves, releasing waves of Law power into the surroundings.","This was the domain of one of the empire's Legendary beings. The Scroll Sovereign.","Among the seven Legendary beings, three belonged to the royal family. This included the emperor and his two ancestors. The fourth was Eunuch Liang, who belonged to one of the empire's eunuch forces. Among the remaining three, one belonged to a powerful noble family, one was the empire's military general, and the last was said to be an invited force.","Or at least, this was the understanding of the two empire ancestors.","They were of course very mistaken, as even they had no idea of the true identity of the other two. Most likely only the emperor and the first ancestor who had died to Shojo knew their true identities. The reason the first ancestor knew and not the other two was simple. He was their father.","Yes, the figure who had fought against Shojo had also mated with a Legendary stage monster, who had birthed two children for him.","As for why the two ancestors still did not know about this, and why even someone like Michael could find out, it was partly because of the decades-long seclusion where only the emperor could meet them personally, and partly because the emperor had deliberately ensured both sides never crossed paths.","As for the outside world remaining unaware, on any normal day the two bloodlines were sealed. Only when fighting at full strength would their true identity be revealed.","This was also why the two ancestors had noticed nothing when they briefly encountered them outside the void. They had only spared the two a glance before the emperor answered their questions through voice transmission, offering a half-truth that concealed their real nature.","Like the emperor and Eunuch Liang, these two also hid their true power, though in the eyes of the outside world they openly appeared to be at the peak of Rank 3.","The Scroll Sovereign, on the other hand, was genuinely from a noble family, though he too had hidden his true strength from the world. Only a select few knew how powerful he truly was.","At the center of the Scroll Sovereign's domain stood Beginning.","A giant standing over sixty meters tall amidst the endless sea of burning scrolls. His grey skin resembled ancient stone.","Countless wounds covered his body. Deep cuts. Missing chunks of flesh. Burning scars. Broken bones protruding from several locations. Yet his expression remained completely calm, as though none of it mattered in the slightest.","Meanwhile, in one enormous hand, Beginning was holding a man.","The Scroll Sovereign.","At this moment the man was desperately struggling to escape. His face was pale, his breathing heavy, and a look of pure terror was painted across his entire expression.","A gigantic flaming scroll descended from the sky. The scroll opened. Thousands of glowing runes erupted outward. The surrounding world immediately shook.","\"Law Skill!\"","The old man roared desperately. \"World Scripture Annihilation!\"","The countless runes condensed together, then transformed into a gigantic spear of blazing scripture hundreds of meters long. The attack descended directly toward Beginning.","The spear struck. A massive explosion illuminated the entire domain. The surrounding scrolls burned away instantly as the resulting shockwave spread thousands of kilometers.","When the light finally faded, what the Scroll Sovereign saw only deepened the dread in his heart.","Beginning had not been stopped by the attack. The spear had pierced directly through his chest, creating a gigantic hole in the center of his body. One could see completely through him. His left arm had been torn off entirely. Half his ribs were gone. His internal organs had practically been vaporized.","Even for a Legendary being, such injuries were horrifying.","And yet Beginning simply looked down at the hole in his chest, then returned his gaze to the old man. His expression never changed.","Meanwhile, his aura seemed to climb even higher.","The Scroll Sovereign's face lost all color. \"No...\" His voice trembled. \"No. No. No.\"","This was not the first time something like this had happened. The series of injuries covering Beginning's body was proof of that.","However, knowing how Beginning's Law functioned, should all of those injuries not have disappeared already? Should his body not have healed completely and become even stronger?","If nothing was wrong with his Law, the answer was simple.","Beginning was suppressing his own healing.","At the start of their battle, Beginning had fought normally, or rather, as normally as Beginning ever fought. He had intentionally allowed the Scroll Sovereign to injure him, since every brush with death increased the power of his Brutal Rebirth.","Initially, that had been his entire plan.","Then a thought occurred to him, and his entire approach changed.","It was also the reason he had willingly entered the Scroll Sovereign's domain, and the reason he had tolerated injury after injury instead of ending the battle immediately.","Beginning wanted the greatest possible benefit from this fight. And the way to achieve that was through his own Law Domain.","Back in Hell, during his battle against the Rank 4 Amazari, Beginning had already attempted something similar. At the time, Rank 4 beings were heavily suppressed and his Law had not been complete. What he created back then could only be described as a partial manifestation. A prototype.","But things were different now.","Beginning had advanced. He was a genuine Rank 4 existence. And his Law had evolved alongside him."]},{"number":1025,"title":"Chapter 1025 Poor Scroll Sovereign","paragraphs":["The Law of Brutal Rebirth was not merely a Law of healing. Its deepest concept was transformation through adversity. The closer one approached destruction, the greater the rebirth. The closer one approached death, the greater the return.","Eventually, that understanding gave birth to Beginning's Domain which also happened to be a very rare type of Domain. A Trial Domain.","Unlike most domains, Beginning's did not necessarily require a hidden layer in the second layer of the void to manifest. It could become a world, but it did not have to. More importantly, it did not care about physical bodies. What mattered were souls and essence.","As long as Beginning possessed even the slightest advantage over an opponent, he could forcibly drag their soul and essence into his Trial Domain.","The Trial Domain was essentially a death battle. A brutal contest between two souls. The winner devoured. The loser was devoured. Simple. Cruel. Absolute.","If Beginning won, the opponent's soul and essence would become nourishment for his rebirth. If Beginning lost, he would become nourishment instead. The victor would inherit everything. Strength. Potential. Essence. It was direct and brutal strengthening.","This was the rebirth Beginning had discovered within his Law back in Hell.","It was also precisely because of this new plan that he had allowed the Scroll Sovereign to injure him so heavily.","Back in Hell, using this Law Domain had carried somewhat less risk since Rank 4 beings had been suppressed there. Here, things were different. One mistake could kill him. If the gap between him and his opponent was too small, activating the Trial Domain would be gambling with his own existence.","A slight advantage was not enough. Beginning wanted certainty. He wanted overwhelming superiority.","So he endured. And endured. And endured.","Every wound increased his strength. That was why he had not healed. Everything had been deliberate preparation. Everything had been leading to this moment.","The Scroll Sovereign, however, knew none of this. All he knew was that the monster before him continued growing stronger. The more damage he dealt, the stronger Beginning became.","Beginning stared silently at the struggling old man in his palm, then lowered his gaze toward the countless injuries covering his own body. For the first time, Beginning seemed satisfied.","There was no point continuing. The Scroll Sovereign had already reached his limit.","More importantly, Beginning had reached the limit of what he was willing to risk. The Law of Brutal Rebirth was powerful, extremely powerful, but there was a limit. The closer he approached death, the stronger the return. However, if he truly died before that return arrived, then everything would become meaningless.","Even Beginning understood that.","A moment later, he stopped suppressing his healing.","The entire domain shook violently. The Scroll Sovereign's eyes widened.","Beginning's wounds began healing with terrifying speed. The flesh around the gigantic hole in his chest grew visibly before the eye. Broken bones twisted back into place. Missing organs regenerated. Cracks throughout his body disappeared one after another. The arm that had been completely torn off rapidly reformed.","At the same time, his aura exploded upward. A terrifying shockwave swept across the scroll world. Countless burning scrolls were torn apart. The rivers of parchment below erupted into the sky.","The Scroll Sovereign's face turned even paler. He wanted to escape. Unfortunately, he could not. Beginning was still holding him. The old man could feel his bones creaking.","\"What... what are you?\"","The Scroll Sovereign's voice trembled. Beginning did not answer. He simply continued healing and growing stronger.","If Michael had been present, he would have immediately noticed something shocking. Before the High Drake's recent evolution, the current Beginning was no weaker than the High Drake had been. In fact, he might have been stronger.","Then the Scroll Sovereign felt a chill spread throughout his soul. A chill unlike anything he had experienced before.","A dark aura began spreading from Beginning and quickly covered him entirely.","This was Beginning's domain, and yes, it could be activated even within another's domain. This was not entirely unheard of. Cultivators with great control and understanding over their domain could create partial manifestations, like certain half-step Rank 4 experts, and use some of their domain abilities inside another's territory.","The only difference between that and Beginning was that for him it was entirely natural.","The Trial Domain did not require territory. It did not require a world of space, because its battlefield had never been physical to begin with. Its battlefield was the soul and essence of the parties involved.","The moment the dark aura completely covered him, the Scroll Sovereign suddenly lost control of his body. Everything froze. Even Beginning himself. Everything became motionless.","The old man looked around in confusion. Then he noticed something horrifying. His body had become translucent.","Was this his soul? No. Something even deeper than that. It was a mixture of his soul and essence condensed together, a representation of his very existence.","Before he could fully comprehend what was happening, another figure appeared in the darkness opposite him.","Beginning.","The giant no longer possessed a physical body. Yet his presence felt infinitely heavier. The countless injuries that had covered him earlier were gone. Though only essence mattered here, Beginning's essence was terrifying.","The Scroll Sovereign immediately tried to retreat. Unfortunately, he was too slow.","Putting aside whether he could even escape this domain, Beginning was no longer the weakened opponent from the start of their battle.","The darkness exploded. Beginning appeared before him instantly.","The Scroll Sovereign's eyes widened. \"No!\"","The old man unleashed every technique he possessed. Countless scripture runes erupted around him. Golden scrolls appeared. Thousands of symbols flooded the darkness.","Unfortunately, nothing happened. Or rather, everything happened too slowly.","Beginning simply reached forward. His gigantic hand closed around the old man's soul.","The Scroll Sovereign screamed. \"Wait! WAIT! I surrender!\"","Unfortunately, Beginning did not understand mercy. Nor did his Domain possess such a concept. The Trial Domain had only two outcomes. Victory or defeat. Devour or be devoured. Nothing else.","Before the Scroll Sovereign could react further, Beginning pulled him closer. The giant opened his mouth.","The Scroll Sovereign struggled desperately, but Beginning's hand remained unmoving. He was brought closer and closer to the giant's mouth.","\"No...\"","His voice became weaker. \"No...\"","Regret appeared in his eyes. It was unclear whether it was for personal reasons or whether he simply hated that he was dying for something like the empire.","Amidst his thoughts and screams, Beginning swallowed him.","GULP."]},{"number":1026,"title":"Chapter 1026 Worry","paragraphs":["Michael breathed heavily. His body was covered in injuries and his mana reserves were low, yet despite all that, his mood was excellent.","Not only had he finally reached Level 75, the maximum level of Rank 3, but his advancement task had also finally been generated. After waiting for so long, he was finally about to see what stood between him and Rank 4.","Well, in truth, this could count as his fastest Advancement speed outside when he wanted to advance to rank 1.","Michael immediately focused on the system.","However, before he could check the newly generated task, another notification suddenly appeared.","[Ding!]","[Your Undead: Lily has leveled up.]","[Current Level: 86]","Michael froze. \"...What?\"","For a moment, he thought he had misread it. Level 86? Lily?","Michael blinked several times. Then his expression became strange.","His first thought was simple. Had the opponent Lily fought been a monster? After all, only monsters granted experience points. If Lily had killed a powerful monster, then reaching Level 86 might not be impossible.","But Michael immediately dismissed the idea. It made no sense. If Lily had killed a monster, he would have received a kill notification as her master and shared a portion of the experience gained. Yet he had received nothing, which meant Lily had not killed a monster.","Michael's brows furrowed. Then realization slowly appeared in his eyes.","\"Lily...\"","A complicated expression crossed his face. The details of Lily's Law flashed through his mind. Lily could devour the essence of whatever she wanted for personal benefit. Not only could she use it to absorb the traits of what she devoured, she could also use it to grow.","Michael had known about the latter for a long time. After all, he had personally fed her many corpses. Yet until today, despite all that feeding, Lily had never directly gained a level from it. He had assumed it had something to do with the quality and quantity of what she consumed.","In any case, for her to level up now, knowing Lily, there was a high probability she had eaten something. And that something was most likely her opponent.","A silence fell over Michael. His expression became even more complicated.","On one hand, he was pleased. His undead becoming stronger was naturally a good thing, especially an undead as terrifying as Lily. On the other hand, the person Lily had eaten had been human. An intelligent being, not a monster or some mindless creature.","Michael stared at the notification panel for a few moments. Then he sighed.","He was not yet at the stage where he could willingly feed a human to his undead, even knowing it would benefit them and even himself since his talent could also devour their corpses for evolution points. But since he had not been there to make that call, he had no grounds to dwell on it.","Before Michael could think any further, another notification suddenly appeared.","[Ding!]","[Your Undead: Beginning has leveled up to Level 89!]","Michael's eyes widened. What was this nonsense?!","Normally his undead levelling up was great news, but when it came from Beginning and Lily it was strange in many ways. Did Beginning levelling up mean his opponent had also been a monster in disguise? Even Michael did not believe such a coincidence was possible. So how had Beginning levelled up from killing a human as well?","Lily was understandable given her Law, but Beginning would not grow simply from eating someone.","\"Ohh...\"","It was then that Michael recalled the ability of Beginning's Trial Domain, and understanding washed over him. Though both undead were technically doing the same thing in a broad sense, Beginning's method of devouring was far more acceptable to Michael than Lily's. Perhaps it was simply a matter of aesthetics.","In any case, his undead levelling up was good news. It also meant that in addition to the two he had killed himself, plus the two the undead had accounted for, the empire only had three Legendary beings remaining out of their original seven.","The emperor was currently fighting the Rank 4 Demonic Supernatural, while the empire's two strongest protectors were battling the High Drake.","Though he wanted to focus on his rank advancement quest now, Michael knew what his priority currently was.","Aside from Beginning, none of his current available forces could realistically assist the High Drake, and might even get themselves killed trying. That meant the only viable target left was the emperor. With him gone, only those two serpent ancestors would remain, and with everything Michael could bring together, this battle with the empire would soon be over.","Thinking this, Michael took a deep breath and immediately made his way toward the emperor's location in the void while reaching out to Lily and Beginning through their bond.","Far away from Michael's battlefield, another battle was reaching a critical point.","Purple flames and black water collided once more. The resulting explosion tore apart massive sections of the void as shockwaves spread in every direction.","The Emperor's enormous serpent body twisted through the darkness. His obsidian scales were cracked in several places. Purple blood dripped into the void while flames burned between the gaps in his armor-like scales.","Opposite him, the Rank 4 Demonic Supernatural stood silently. Dark water flowed endlessly around its body. Its expression remained as calm and emotionless as ever.","A gigantic serpent tail descended. The Demonic Supernatural raised a hand. An ocean condensed around its fist.","The two attacks collided. Space shattered. The Emperor was forced backward several hundred meters.","Normally, such an exchange would not have affected his composure. Unfortunately, he could not calm down. Something felt wrong. Very wrong.","The Emperor's eyes flickered across the surrounding void. Where were they?","The battle had been going on for a long time. His side had possessed seven Legendary beings. The enemy had only five. Even accounting for the terrifying strength Michael's forces had displayed, numerical superiority still existed. By now, at least one battlefield should have been resolved and someone should have appeared to reinforce him.","Yet there was nothing. Only silence.","The Emperor's heart gradually sank. A terrible possibility surfaced within his mind, one he immediately suppressed.","_Drakon"]},{"number":1027,"title":"Chapter 1027 Running Away","paragraphs":["These were Legendary beings. People who had dominated entire eras and could destroy kingdoms easily. Even if they lost, they should have been able to retreat.","Yet still no one had appeared, and even the Emperor could not enjoy his own confidence now.","The Emperor's expression became increasingly ugly. His instincts screamed that something terrible had happened.","\"Huh?\"","The Demonic Supernatural suddenly appeared before him. The Emperor reacted a fraction too slowly.","A fist wrapped in endless black water smashed directly into his jaw. In the eyes of others it might have looked like nothing more than a large sphere of water surrounding the combatants, but the Emperor knew it carried the weight of an ocean.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The gigantic serpent's head snapped sideways. Several scales exploded. Purple blood scattered across the void.","The Emperor immediately recovered. Unfortunately, the Demonic Supernatural had already launched another attack. A sea condensed around its arm once more.","\"Demonic Abyss Crushing Tide.\"","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The fist landed squarely against the Emperor's chest. This time dozens of scales shattered. The Emperor's enormous body shot backward like a meteor.","Visible anger immediately appeared on his face.","The Demonic Supernatural watched him silently. Then it spoke. \"You are distracted.\"","The Emperor's eyes narrowed. He did not answer, but the other party was correct. He was distracted. Very distracted. The silence from the other battlefields was becoming increasingly difficult to ignore.","\"Shut it and fight!\"","The Emperor exploded forward again. This time his attacks became noticeably fiercer. Purple flames flooded the void. The Demonic Supernatural met every attack head-on. The two exchanged dozens of blows in seconds. Each collision shattered space.","Yet despite fighting at full strength, the Emperor's unease only continued growing.","Then suddenly, a strange fluctuation spread through the void.","The Emperor froze as he watched three figures rapidly making their way toward him through the darkness. Each figure looked like they had been through a war, yet each also carried a terrifying aura.","Though he did not know any of them individually, he recognized what they represented. And it was precisely because he recognized them that his heart shook.","If these three were here, then what had happened to their opponents?","The three figures were, of course, Michael and the two undead who had gathered together to deal with the Emperor. What Michael did not expect was that the moment they appeared, the Emperor would immediately retreat.","The gigantic serpent did not hesitate. Purple flames exploded throughout the void as the Emperor forcibly broke away from the Demonic Supernatural and shot toward the edge of the battlefield. The Demonic Supernatural immediately attempted to pursue.","Unfortunately, the Emperor was willing to pay any price. Several scales exploded from his body. His aura weakened slightly. Yet his speed increased dramatically. In a few breaths, he vanished into the distance.","Michael was stunned. \"...He ran?\"","Even Beginning paused briefly.","The current Beginning was no weaker than the two serpent ancestors fighting the High Drake. After absorbing the Scroll Sovereign and completing his rebirth, the aura he radiated had become terrifying. Even Michael had been surprised when they regrouped.","Facing a Demonic Supernatural, Michael, Lily, and the current Beginning simultaneously was enough to make any sane Legendary being reconsider their life choices. The Emperor had simply chosen the most practical option.","However, Michael's expression soon changed as he recalled his undead outside.","The Emperor froze as he watched three figures rapidly making their way toward him through the darkness. Each figure looked like they had been through a war, yet each also carried a terrifying aura.","The moment that thought appeared, anxiety rose in his heart. Aside from the undead he had been able to unsummon to the Netherworld through Undead Summoning, many others had forced their way out of the void after the battle began. If the Emperor targeted them, the result would be disastrous. A Rank 4 being could easily massacre many Rank 3 creatures. Even extraordinary undead would not last long.","Unfortunately, the void trap only seemed effective against outsiders. The Emperor himself appeared capable of leaving freely, which explained why he had escaped so quickly.","However, Michael was not particularly worried about leaving himself. With Beginning, Lily, and the Demonic Supernatural assisting him, breaking out of the void would not take long. The real concern was whether the Emperor would decide to vent his anger on the undead army before they could arrive.","\"Move!\"","Michael shot forward. Beginning followed immediately. Lily's gigantic figure tore through the void behind them while the Demonic Supernatural silently joined the pursuit.","The group crossed the second layer of the void at astonishing speed. A few seconds later, they burst out into the outside world.","Michael's eyes immediately swept across the battlefield. Then he froze.","\"Huh?\"","The sight before him completely caught him off guard. His undead were fine. Not only were they alive, they appeared completely untouched. The massive undead army still filled the skies and surrounding regions.","Instead, something else had happened. The capital was glowing. More specifically, it was the Imperial Palace. A gigantic dome of golden light had appeared over the entire palace grounds. Runes flowed across its surface. The light was so bright it illuminated half the capital.","Michael immediately recognized what it was. \"A protection formation...\"","His expression became strange. Then finally he spoke.","\"...Did the Emperor just lock himself inside his own palace?\"","Even he found it difficult to believe. This was the ruler of the Black Serpent Empire. A Rank 4 existence. A being feared throughout the entire region. And now he was hiding behind a formation.","Michael's gaze shifted toward the glowing barrier. His eyes slowly narrowed.","If the Emperor was willing to retreat to this extent, then there were only a few possibilities. Either the formation possessed enough power to stop all of them, or the Emperor himself had already lost confidence in winning, or he was planning something.","Michael strongly suspected it was the second or third.","Far below, countless cultivators, soldiers, and nobles stared at the glowing palace. Many of them were equally stunned.","Meanwhile, high above the city, Michael slowly smiled.","If the Emperor thought hiding inside a formation would end this battle, then he was about to be very disappointed."]},{"number":1028,"title":"Chapter 1028 Blood Sacrifice [1]","paragraphs":["With a thought, the Sovereign Pipa appeared in Michael's hand. The Three-Star Epic treasure radiated a faint pressure that seemed to stir the surrounding air.","Michael did not hesitate. He immediately tossed it toward the Rank 4 Demonic Supernatural.","\"Use it.\"","The Demonic Supernatural caught the instrument without question. Unlike Michael, who was relatively weakened and running on depleted mana reserves, the Demonic Supernatural still possessed enough power to fully utilize the treasure.","Michael's eyes remained fixed on the glowing palace. The Emperor had clearly prepared something. The man did not strike him as a coward, so Michael did not dare underestimate him, nor was he currently qualified to.","The problem was that Michael did not know the Emperor's plans.","Fortunately, or unfortunately, he did not need to wait long to find out.","AAAAARRRRGGGHHHHHH!!!","A horrifying scream suddenly erupted from within the palace. The sound echoed throughout the entire capital. Everyone froze. Cultivators. Soldiers. Nobles. Even Michael's undead.","The scream did not sound like a single person. It sounded like close to a thousand. Countless voices merged together into a single terrifying cry.","Michael's expression changed instantly.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The next moment, a pillar of bloody light erupted from the center of the palace. The protective formation trembled violently. Crimson energy flooded the heavens.","At the same time, an aura began rising. Growing stronger and stronger. The pressure rapidly climbed toward a terrifying level.","Michael's eyes remained narrowed. The aura felt familiar. Very familiar.","\"It's the Emperor.\"","Meanwhile, feeling the aura coming from the palace, blood drained from the faces of countless spectators.","Michael remained focused on the Emperor's aura. It carried the Emperor's presence, yet it was also different. More violent. More chaotic. Very unstable. It was as though countless presences had been mixed together into a single existence.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The bloody pillar expanded again. The aura continued rising. Soon it approached Beginning's current level.","Michael immediately understood he could no longer keep waiting. Whatever the Emperor was doing, it could not be allowed to continue.","\"Attack! Break it now!\"","His voice thundered across the capital.","The moment the command left his mouth, Beginning moved. The giant's body rapidly expanded. Sixty meters. Seventy. Eighty. The surrounding air exploded as his terrifying physique loomed above the capital. Countless people looked up in horror.","The giant raised his fist.","Meanwhile, the Demonic Supernatural had already raised the Sovereign Pipa. The amount of mana entering it was far greater than anything Michael had previously supplied.","The strings immediately began trembling violently. The Demonic Supernatural's finger landed on the first string.","Shattering Pluck.","TWAAAAAAAAANG!!!","The sound exploded across the heavens. Unlike Michael's previous attacks, this was a Rank 4 existence wielding the treasure. The difference was immediately obvious. A concentrated sonic burst shot forward, appearing almost invisible. Only a thin line distorting reality itself marked its passage.","Then it struck.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The golden barrier shook violently. Countless runes exploded apart. Cracks instantly spread across the surface.","Far below, screams erupted throughout the capital while the bloody aura inside the palace fluctuated.","\"Again!\"","Michael roared. The Demonic Supernatural plucked the string a second time.","TWAAAAAAAAANG!!!","Another sonic burst erupted, even stronger than the first. The protective formation trembled violently. Entire sections of the barrier caved inward. The golden light dimmed.","At the same moment, Beginning attacked. His gigantic fist descended from the heavens. The world seemed to go silent for a fraction of a second.","Then, KRAAAAAAAAAAAAAABOOOOOOOOM!!!","The fist smashed directly into the weakened formation. The capital shook. Buildings collapsed. Shockwaves flattened entire districts. The protective barrier distorted dramatically. Thousands of cracks spread across its surface.","Inside the palace, the bloody aura suddenly surged again. Michael's expression immediately darkened. Not only had the attack failed to stop whatever ritual was occurring, it seemed to have accelerated it.","\"Faster!\"","Beginning attacked again. The Demonic Supernatural plucked another string.","TWAAAAANG!!! KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","TWAAAAANG!!! KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The barrier trembled continuously. Chunks of golden light exploded away. Runes shattered as formation nodes collapsed. The entire capital watched in horror as the protection formation of the palace was slowly torn apart.","Yet despite the terrifying attacks raining down upon it, the bloody aura within the palace only continued rising. The pressure spreading from within was becoming increasingly suffocating.","Michael's expression darkened. This could not continue.","\"Together!\"","His voice echoed throughout the sky. Beginning moved immediately. The giant drew back his fist while the Demonic Supernatural simultaneously placed its fingers upon the first string of the Sovereign Pipa once more.","The heavens shook. The concentrated sonic burst tore through space itself. At the exact same moment, Beginning's fist descended. The two attacks landed simultaneously.","This time the protective formation could no longer endure. The already damaged runes shattered one after another. Entire sections of the barrier collapsed. Golden light exploded outward.","Then, KRAAAAAAAAAACK!!!","A gigantic crack spread from the center of the formation. For a brief moment, everything seemed to freeze.","Then the entire defensive barrier exploded.","KRAAAAAAAABOOOOOOOOM!!!","A storm of golden fragments swept across the capital. The palace grounds were finally exposed.","What everyone saw caused countless faces to pale. Michael's expression immediately changed.","The palace, or rather what remained of it, was devastation. The majority of the palace complex had already collapsed. Spread throughout the entire area were bodies. Hundreds of bodies. Men. Women. Children. Servants. Guards. The dead were everywhere. Blood covered the ground. It flowed through the ruins like rivers.","Even many of the empire's surviving experts outside the palace who had remained loyal until now stared in disbelief. The scene resembled a sacrifice. A massive sacrifice.","At the center of it all stood eleven figures. Or rather, eleven corpses. Their bodies remained standing despite being completely drained. Their skin had shrunk tightly against their bones. Their eyes were hollow. Their expressions were frozen in pain.","And standing amongst them was the Emperor.","He had returned to his human form. Blood-red veins covered his entire body. His black robes had long since disappeared. Crimson energy continuously flowed from the eleven corpses into him.","The surrounding space distorted from the pressure. The emperor's rising aura had now stabilized, though even then it seemed marginally stronger than Beginning beside him."]},{"number":1029,"title":"Chapter 1029 Blood Sacrifice [2]","paragraphs":["Michael's frown deepened.","Even from thousands of meters away, his eyesight remained terrifying. After absorbing so many memories recently, he immediately recognized eight among the standing figures.","Eight of them were direct descendants of the Emperor. The remaining three were unfamiliar, but judging from their position and aura, they were clearly not ordinary individuals either. Most likely direct descendants of the Emperor as well.","The moment Michael saw them, realization immediately struck him. \"So that's what you did...\"","A rare trace of disgust appeared on his face.","The Emperor had sacrificed them. Their blood. Their vitality. Their essence. Everything. All of it had been fed into himself.","The bloody aura flooding the heavens suddenly made sense. The instability. The violent fluctuations. The mixture of countless presences. Michael finally understood why the aura had felt so strange earlier. It was because it was no longer entirely the Emperor's. It was a fusion. A forced amalgamation created through sacrifice.","Far below, many of the empire's experts reached the same conclusion.","At the center of the ruins, the Emperor slowly raised his head. His eyes had become completely crimson. The bloody aura around him surged violently. Then his gaze locked onto Michael.","A vicious smile slowly spread across his face. \"You forced me to this point.\"","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The eleven corpses instantly collapsed into dust. The Emperor's aura surged once more.","Michael felt his heart sink slightly. \"Beginning!!!\"","He had only just shouted the giant's name when a figure suddenly appeared barely ten meters away from him. The speed was so absurd that Michael's pupils contracted instantly.","Too fast. Far too fast.","The Emperor's crimson eyes locked onto him. A vicious grin stretched across his face. Michael felt death descend upon him. Every instinct screamed. Even his soul seemed to freeze.","This attack would kill him.","Just as the Emperor's claw-like hand was about to reach him, TWAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAANG!!!","The heavens exploded with sound. The Demonic Supernatural reacted first. The first string of the Sovereign Pipa vibrated violently. A concentrated sonic burst erupted forward. The attack struck the Emperor's side.","KRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABOOOOOOOOM!!!","The Emperor was blasted sideways. The sonic wave distorted space itself.","Unfortunately, Michael was just as close. The shockwave swept over him as well.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","Michael felt as though an entire mountain had smashed into him. His body spun uncontrollably through the air. Several of his ribs cracked. Fresh blood sprayed from his mouth. A cold sweat covered his back.","Fortunately, he was still alive. If not for the Demonic Supernatural's intervention, he would already be dead.","Meanwhile, Beginning had already reacted. The giant's eyes locked onto the Emperor. Without hesitation, he threw a punch.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A fist larger than buildings descended toward the Emperor. Yet this time the Emperor did not run. Instead, the bloody aura around him erupted and his body suddenly began changing. His human form rapidly distorted as he entered his bloodline state.","Beginning's punch landed.","Just as the Emperor's claw-like hand was about to reach him, TWAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAAANG!!!","KRAAAAAAAAAAAAAAABOOOOOOOOM!!!","The Emperor crossed his claws. The collision shook the entire capital. Shockwaves flattened countless buildings. Space shattered.","However, seeing the Emperor's transformation, not only were the empire's experts shocked, even Michael's eyes widened.","The creature standing before him no longer resembled the two-hundred-meter serpent from before. No. It looked frighteningly familiar. Massive wings. Draconic claws. A scaled body. A long tail. A powerful neck. And a head that carried both serpentine and draconic characteristics.","It looked eerily similar to his undead High Drake. Not identical, but close enough that Michael immediately recognized the connection.","The Emperor slowly lowered his claws. Purple flames dripped from his mouth. His crimson eyes glowed with madness. The aura rolling from his body became increasingly unstable, yet it was undeniably powerful.","Realization struck Michael.","Just as he had done with his Rank 4 undead High Drake, the Emperor had also used the Black Serpent bloodline to push the purity of his bloodline further.","The Emperor looked toward Michael and laughed. The sound was completely unhinged.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","His wings expanded. A pressure even greater than before swept across the capital. Countless people collapsed to their knees. Even many Rank 3 experts turned pale.","Before Michael could fully process the Emperor's transformation, Beginning had already moved. Unlike everyone else present, Beginning did not care about bloodlines. He cared about one thing.","The Emperor's face.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The giant vanished. The Emperor's newly transformed eyes narrowed slightly.","Fast.","Beginning appeared directly before him and threw a punch. The Emperor immediately counterattacked. His claw descended. The collision shattered the surrounding sky.","For a brief moment, both figures froze. Then the Emperor's claw tore straight through Beginning's shoulder. Purple flames erupted. Half the giant's upper body exploded apart. Blood rained from the sky. The surrounding spectators gasped as many dodged or sought shelter.","Even Michael's expression changed. That attack had been devastating.","However, the Emperor's expression suddenly became strange. Unlike others who had fought Beginning, he sensed that the attack could have been blocked, yet seemed to have been taken deliberately.","And as expected, KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","The Law of Brutal Rebirth activated. The flesh around Beginning's injury immediately began regenerating. And as the healing completed, Beginning's aura rose significantly.","The Emperor frowned. \"What?\"","Beginning answered with another punch. This time the Emperor was forced backward. The capital grounds shook.","The Emperor's expression changed. The previous attack had not possessed this level of force. Yet before he could think further, Beginning attacked again. The Emperor met him head-on.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A claw pierced through Beginning's abdomen.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","A flame blade sliced across his chest.","KRAAAAABOOOOM!!!","Purple flames exploded throughout his body.","Any one of those attacks would have severely injured an ordinary Rank 4 being. Beginning endured all of them.","Then once again, KRAAAAABOOOOOOM!!!","His injuries healed. The gigantic holes disappeared. The severed flesh regenerated. The burns vanished. And his aura climbed again.","The Emperor's confusion deepened. The stronger he injured Beginning, the stronger Beginning became.","\"What kind of monster are you?\"","Uncertainty appeared in the Emperor's voice. Beginning remained silent. The giant merely looked at him. A strange light flickered within his eyes.","The Emperor felt like Beginning seemed almost satisfied.","Michael suddenly realized what Beginning was doing. His expression immediately changed.","\"Wait...\"","Unfortunately, he was too late.","The Emperor suddenly felt a chill spread through his body. A very familiar one. The same chill the Scroll Sovereign had felt before his death.","Beginning slowly raised a hand. Darkness spread outward. The surrounding air became heavy. The Emperor's pupils contracted.","\"What is this?\"","The darkness continued spreading. Beginning's voice finally sounded. Calm and emotionless.","\"Trial.\"","_Drakon"]},{"number":1030,"title":"Chapter 1030 Unfavourable Situation","paragraphs":["The moment the word fell from Beginning's mouth, alarm appeared in the Emperor's eyes.","\"What are you doing?\"","Beginning did not answer. He simply extended his hand, letting the darkness spread outward to touch the Emperor, who tried to dodge but could not.","Above the capital, countless supernaturals felt their souls tremble simply from staring at the sea of darkness overhead.","Even Michael felt goosebumps spread across his body.","The physical bodies of Beginning and the Emperor stopped moving. Both figures remained suspended in midair. It was as though time itself had stopped for them.","\"What happened?\"","\"Why did they stop?\"","\"What's going on?!\"","Panic spread throughout the capital. Most of it came from the citizens who had at some point emerged from their hiding places for reasons known only to themselves.","A gigantic sea of darkness had appeared overhead, and within it stood two colossal figures.","Together with the physical representations of the Emperor's and Beginning's essence, it felt as though four gigantic creatures loomed above the capital sky, creating a dreadful feeling that hell itself was about to descend.","The Emperor's soul form resembled an enormous draconic serpent. Bloody energy flowed endlessly through its body. Countless screaming faces could be seen beneath its scales, obviously the remnants of the sacrifices he had consumed.","Meanwhile, opposite him stood Beginning. A gigantic humanoid titan. His body appeared forged from stone.","Michael stared upward silently, worry etched into his expression.","He knew this was probably the same method Beginning had used to level up moments ago, but it was a different story when the undead used his domain while Michael was not close by versus when he was present and aware. Michael would have preferred Beginning's domain be used on creatures far weaker than him, where the outcome was far more stable and certain.","Now it might seem as though Beginning had the advantage since he had forcefully dragged the other party into his domain, but when the gap in strength was not sufficiently large, anything could happen. Michael himself was proof of that, which was precisely why he disliked this sort of reckless behavior.","Unfortunately, through his connection with Beginning, he could tell that his undead had grown quite greedy. It most likely stemmed from the significant increase in strength Beginning had only just undergone. It did not matter whether it was an undead or a living creature. The instinctive desire for more strength was universal.","Far above, inside the sea of darkness, the Emperor finally understood what had happened. His expression changed drastically.","\"You dragged me into your domain?\"","His voice thundered across the darkness. The Emperor immediately tried to retreat.","Unfortunately, nothing happened. The sea of darkness possessed no exit.","At the same time, foreign information about the domain drilled into his mind. The Emperor's expression finally became ugly. What he hated most was a battle with life and death as the stakes, and this creature had just forced him into exactly that.","Thinking this, the soul of the Emperor turned to glare at Michael outside. At this point, he had already realized that these creatures were not mindless beasts. Though he did not believe they belonged to Michael, or even think in that direction, the Emperor had concluded that Michael was an important figure within the group that wished to destroy his empire.","Feeling the Emperor's gaze on him, Michael angrily returned the glare.","After all, if it was not for this man, he would not be worrying about the life and death of his undead. Well, it was technically already a dead being, but that was beside the point.","Clearly, Michael was feeling a mixture of justifiable and entirely unreasonable anger.","The battle unfolded almost exactly as Michael had feared.","Beginning was stronger. That much was undeniable. However, strength and victory were not the same thing. The Emperor had lived for decades. Beginning had not even existed for a full year. The difference in combat experience was significant. Whether in terms of practical experience or simply years of existence, Beginning was ultimately a newborn. An extraordinarily powerful newborn, but a newborn nonetheless.","Inside the Sea of Darkness, the two colossal soul forms collided repeatedly.","BOOOOM!!!","Beginning's fist crashed into the Emperor's jaw. Then a moment later, the Emperor twisted his body unnaturally and tore three massive chunks of essence from Beginning's shoulder.","The giant staggered. For the first time since the battle began, Beginning's aura dropped slightly.","Below, Michael's expression changed.","The Emperor's eyes widened in surprise as realization struck him.","\"So that's how it works...\"","The foreign information granted by the Trial Domain had already explained the rules. Victory or defeat. Devour or be devoured.","With the rules of Beginning's domain, among roughly equal opponents, the first one to successfully consume the essence of the other would strengthen themselves while weakening their opponent.","The Emperor looked down at his body. The fragments of Beginning's essence were already dissolving into him. A moment later, his aura rose. At the same time, Beginning's aura fell by an equal amount. The two were now almost perfectly equal.","The Emperor froze. Then a smile slowly spread across his face. A genuine smile mixed with pure joy.","\"Hahahaha...\"","His laughter echoed throughout the Sea of Darkness. The bloody draconic serpent raised its head.","The benefits were far greater than he had imagined. The domain's information had told him what the rewards would be, but understanding something and experiencing it were entirely different matters. The strengthening was immediate, direct, and perfect. There was no refinement process. No bottleneck. No waste. Everything became his.","The Emperor felt power flooding through every part of his soul. His eyes brightened. The fear he had initially felt rapidly disappeared, replaced entirely by greed.","His gaze locked onto Beginning. The giant no longer looked like a threat. He looked like an opportunity. A heaven-sent opportunity.","\"If I kill you...\"","The Emperor's excitement deepened as his thoughts began to race. \"If I completely devour you...\" The current increase alone was already significant. What if he won completely? What if he absorbed everything? Wouldn't he emerge from this domain as a completely different existence? Wouldn't he stand equal to or even surpass his two ancestors?","The more he thought, the more the Emperor began to see a path opening before him.","The Black Serpent Empire? Suddenly it seemed too small. Far too small. Why stop there? Why remain confined to a single empire? Why continue bowing before his ancient ancestors? Why not set his eyes on the neighboring empires?","Ambition ignited in the Emperor's heart.","His laughter echoed once more. \"Hahahahaha!\"","Outside the domain, Michael's expression darkened. He could not hear the Emperor's thoughts, but through his connection with Beginning he could feel something changing. The Emperor was becoming more dangerous. He also seemed to have grown considerably more confident.","This was not a good sign.","Inside the Sea of Darkness, the Emperor spread his wings. Bloody energy flooded the horizon. His eyes locked onto Beginning.","\"Thank you.\" The Emperor smiled. It was a strange sight on a serpent's face, but a smile it was nonetheless. \"I was worried this would be a life-and-death trap.\"","His expression shifted. A vicious grin stretched across his face. \"But now? This looks more like an opportunity.\"","BOOOOOOM!!!","The draconic serpent shot forward. Beginning charged at the exact same moment. Two gigantic soul forms collided once more."]},{"number":1031,"title":"Chapter 1031 Conflicting Thought","paragraphs":["If Beginning could not defeat the Emperor while possessing a clear advantage in power, then there was even less chance of overwhelming him now that both stood at nearly the same level.","That was the cruel reality of combat. Strength mattered. Experience mattered too. And in that regard, the Emperor possessed decades of advantage.","BOOOOM!!!","The Sea of Darkness exploded once more. Beginning's gigantic fist smashed toward the Emperor's head. The draconic serpent twisted its body with impossible flexibility. The attack brushed past his scales before he counterattacked instantly. His claw swept across Beginning's ribs.","BOOOOM!!!","A massive section of the giant's side exploded apart. Before Beginning could recover, the Emperor's tail struck.","BOOOOM!!!","The titan was blasted backward through the darkness. The Emperor pursued relentlessly.","For the first time since entering the Trial Domain, he had completely abandoned caution. Why would he be cautious? The more he fought, the more benefits he obtained. The more Beginning weakened, the stronger he became.","BOOOOM!!!","The Emperor appeared above Beginning. A claw descended. Beginning blocked. The collision shook the darkness. Then another claw followed. Then another. Then another. The Emperor attacked like a storm. His mountain of combat experience was finally being displayed in full.","Beginning fought back fiercely. His fists shattered scales. His kicks fractured bones. Several times he even forced the Emperor backward. Though they were only in their soul states, what they felt was just as real as what their physical bodies would have experienced.","Yet unlike before, the Emperor no longer feared exchanging injuries. He welcomed them.","BOOOOM!!!","Beginning's fist smashed into the Emperor's neck. Several scales shattered. At the same moment, however, the Emperor's jaws snapped shut around Beginning's forearm.","The darkness trembled.","Below, Michael's expression hardened further. \"No...\"","Inside the Trial Domain, excitement lit up the Emperor's eyes.","CHOMP!!!","A massive chunk of Beginning's essence disappeared. The giant staggered. His aura immediately dropped.","Meanwhile, the Emperor's body shook. Then, BOOOOM!!!","His aura surged upward once more. The strengthening was immediate.","The Emperor's laughter echoed throughout the darkness. \"Hahahahaha! It really works!\"","He released Beginning's arm and retreated several hundred meters, his gaze sweeping across his own body. He could feel it. Every bite made him stronger. Every bite made Beginning weaker.","Beginning's expression remained unchanged, seemingly unbothered. But Michael could clearly feel the difference through their connection. Beginning was losing, and if something did not change soon, he would die. At that point there would be no use worrying about Beginning either, as they would all have to worry about their own lives.","The Emperor was simply too skilled.","BOOOOM!!!","The battle resumed. The giant's attacks remained terrifying, yet whenever the two exchanged injuries, it was almost always the Emperor who emerged with the greater gain.","Minutes passed.","Then the Emperor intentionally allowed Beginning's fist to strike his shoulder. At the same time, however, his claws pierced directly into Beginning's chest.","The giant froze.","The Emperor smiled. Then pulled.","RIIIIIIIP!!!","Another enormous chunk of Beginning's essence was torn free. For a moment, the entire Sea of Darkness seemed to freeze.","The Emperor immediately swallowed it. GULP.","BOOOOM!!!","His aura exploded upward again. Meanwhile, Beginning's aura visibly weakened.","The Emperor spread his wings. Bloody energy flooded the darkness. His eyes gleamed with greed.","More. He wanted more. He could already see the future. Defeat this giant. Devour everything. Leave this domain. Surpass the ancestors. Conquer neighboring empires. Become the true ruler of the region.","The Emperor's gaze locked onto Michael outside the domain. He flashed him a smile before charging at Beginning again. At this point he believed he was going to win.","He was not alone in that belief. Michael, as Beginning's master, felt the same way.","Michael's expression darkened further. He felt helpless.","He wanted to help, but unfortunately he dared not. The moment he tried to interfere with the Trial Domain, the domain itself would react. He had already witnessed this once before, back in Hell.","A Rank 4 Amazari had nearly suppressed Beginning during an earlier use of the domain. At the time, one of the surrounding allies had attempted to assist. The result was immediate. The Trial Domain had forcefully dragged them inside as a participant. The moment one interfered, they became part of the trial, and once inside there was only one way out. Victory or death.","Even if some miracle occurred and Michael entered the domain and helped Beginning kill the Emperor, there would still be a problem. The Trial Domain only released participants when a single victor remained. That meant if both he and Beginning survived, one of them would still have to die. The winner would devour. The loser would be devoured. That was the absolute rule governing Beginning's Law.","Michael had no intention of gambling his life on that. Nor did he intend to gamble Beginning's.","Above him, the Sea of Darkness shook violently. Another portion of Beginning's essence disappeared. The Emperor's laughter followed shortly afterward.","Michael clenched his fists. \"Damn it...\"","For the first time in a long while, he felt powerless.","Then suddenly, his eyes narrowed as a memory surfaced.","Back in Hell, the ally that had been dragged into the Trial Domain had been eaten by Beginning almost immediately. At the time, Michael had not paid much attention. After all, the situation then was chaotic and the important thing was that Beginning had survived.","But now Michael could not help but start recalling everything carefully.","Though it was tragic that the helper had died, they had also strengthened Beginning in the process.","Michael slowly raised his head. His gaze returned toward the Sea of Darkness.","\"If interference drags someone into the domain, and if that person dies...\"","Beginning would devour them for greater strength and perhaps even reverse the situation entirely.","BOOOOM!!!","Above the capital, Beginning was thrown backward again. Another portion of his essence vanished. The Emperor's advantage continued growing.","Michael's mind raced. The more he thought about it, the more possible it seemed.","The Trial Domain only cared about participants. It did not care whose side they were on. It only cared about winners and losers. Meaning, if enough participants entered and Beginning could devour them to strengthen himself, it could theoretically reverse the battle entirely.","Unfortunately, there was a problem.","Who exactly was he supposed to sacrifice?"]},{"number":1032,"title":"Chapter 1032 Sacrifice","paragraphs":["Michael immediately rejected several possibilities. He first thought of the Emperor's subjects, but unfortunately he still was not cruel enough for that.","Michael's expression became conflicted as he started battling with his sense of morals.","Then subconsciously, his eyes drifted downward toward the hundreds upon hundreds of undead spread across the capital. All were Rank 3. None of them individually mattered much compared to Beginning.","Michael froze. Then he looked again. His breathing slowly stopped.","A thought appeared inside his mind. A thought so ruthless that even he instinctively recoiled from it.","If a few dozen, even hundreds. Yes. The number was more than enough, Michael thought. If even a fraction of them were dragged into the Trial Domain and Beginning devoured them, they would become fuel for his victory.","Michael stared at the undead below. The undead stared back with empty eyes.","For a long moment, he said nothing. The battle above continued. Beginning kept losing while the Emperor kept growing stronger.","A dangerous light appeared in Michael's eyes. He could see a possible way to turn the tables. The only question remaining was whether he was willing to pay the price.","It did not take long for Michael to make a decision.","\"Come.\"","His voice echoed through the battlefield. Soon, one hundred Rank 3 undead stood before him. Various undead of different forms and strengths, all waiting silently.","The surrounding experts were confused by Michael's actions. Nobody understood what he was doing, but nobody dared to interrupt either.","Michael stared at the undead before him. A strange feeling appeared inside his chest.","Truthfully speaking, Michael was not particularly close to most of them. How could he be? He possessed thousands of undead. Building meaningful relationships with every single one was impossible, especially when he had only been a Necromancer for less than a year.","The undead closest to him were only a few, and most of the time they were either the strongest, the most unique of his legion, or the ones that had stayed with him the longest.","These hundred? Some of them Michael did not even know by race from memory alone.","Yet despite that, his expression remained complicated. After all, they still belonged to him and were loyal to him as their master.","And now he was about to send them to their deaths.","For a brief moment, Michael wondered if something was wrong with him. Perhaps only Michael would think something like this. If an orthodox Necromancer were to hear his thoughts, they would not just laugh. They would spit on him with disgust and mock him. Call him immature, naive, and weak-hearted.","To most Necromancers, only special undead mattered. The strongest. The rarest. The most useful. Everything else was simply resources, consumables, and expendable assets.","If sacrificing a hundred ordinary undead could save a powerful one, there was nothing worth considering. If sacrificing a thousand weak undead could strengthen a Rank 4 servant, most Necromancers would do it without blinking. In fact, many would celebrate. A profitable transaction. That was all it would be. Nothing more. Nothing less.","Michael also understood that logic. Objectively speaking, it was only right.","Beginning alone was worth far more than these hundred undead combined. A thousand times more. Perhaps ten thousand times more. The giant was one of the foundations supporting his entire future.","Without Beginning, his current Law would not exist as it did, and he would likely have turned to bones somewhere in Hell.","Meanwhile, these undead could be replaced.","Yet despite understanding all of that, Michael still felt uncomfortable.","Unfortunately, reality rarely cared about feelings.","Above the capital, the Sea of Darkness shook violently again. Another portion of Beginning's essence disappeared. The Emperor's triumphant laughter followed immediately afterward.","Michael's expression hardened. The conflict in his eyes vanished.","\"...Sorry.\"","The word escaped his mouth quietly. The undead naturally gave no response. They merely continued waiting for orders.","The first thing Michael did was sever his connection to the hundred undead. His body trembled slightly. A small backlash traveled through his soul. Yet compared to the pain he would experience if a hundred contracted undead died simultaneously while still connected to him, this was insignificant. A slight headache. Nothing more.","Michael immediately stabilized himself.","He had done this for two reasons.","The first was that he had absolutely no idea whether undead participating in the Trial Domain while still bound to him would cause the domain to classify him as a participant as well. If that happened, everything would be over.","The second reason was even simpler. Pain. Back in Hell, the death of multiple undead had almost crippled him from soul backlash. His soul was stronger now, but pain was still pain.","So he cut the connections.","For a brief moment, the hundred undead became ownerless. But Michael was not worried. Even after severing the contracts, the undead still stood obediently before him.","The reason was simply his class, Death's Heir. The class itself granted him near-absolute dominance over dead creatures. These undead were no longer his servants, yet they still obeyed him just as naturally as before.","Michael slowly looked over them.","Above the capital, the Sea of Darkness shook again. Through his connection with Beginning, Michael felt another loss. The Emperor was slowly winning.","Michael's expression hardened. A command traveled outward.","The hundred undead immediately rose into the sky.","Whoosh! Whoosh! Whoosh!","Like arrows released from a bow, they shot upward toward the Sea of Darkness. Many of the surviving experts immediately noticed.","\"What are they doing?\"","\"Where are they going?\"","Some began to realize something. Their faces changed.","Even the Emperor, who was currently tearing chunks from Beginning's essence, noticed the approaching figures. His eyes narrowed.","\"What is he doing now?\"","Meanwhile, Michael reached through his connection with Beginning and sent it a simple message.","Eat.","The hundred undead had already approached the edge of the Sea of Darkness. The domain reacted immediately.","*","A/N: Thank you for the continued support!! Update rate is back to normal!"]},{"number":1033,"title":"Chapter 1033 Two Hundred Replacement","paragraphs":["The moment the Trial Domain classified the hundred undead as participants, their essence forms were dragged from their bodies one after another.","Above the capital, a strange sight appeared. A hundred translucent figures emerged from the physical bodies of the undead. Some were wolves. Some were insects. Some were humanoid undead. Others possessed bizarre forms entirely their own.","Inside the domain, the Emperor's eyes widened. \"What?\"","A hundred new participants had suddenly appeared inside the domain. The newcomers were insignificant individually. Compared to him and Beginning, they were little more than ants, yet their sudden arrival immediately disrupted the flow of battle.","The Emperor's gaze shifted toward Michael outside the domain. Then realization appeared. \"You...\"","His expression darkened.","Meanwhile, the moment the hundred undead appeared, Beginning immediately acted.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","A devastating punch forced the Emperor backward. The attack was not particularly powerful, at least not powerful enough to seriously injure him. But that had never been the objective.","Taking advantage of the opening created, Beginning retreated toward the hundred undead who were already rushing toward him.","The Emperor's expression changed. \"No!\"","At that moment he finally understood what was happening. Unfortunately, he was too late.","The hundred undead possessed no intention of fighting. The giant opened his mouth wide.","Unlike the Emperor, who had to overpower his prey and tear away chunks of essence through combat, Beginning faced no resistance. The undead willingly entered. The entire process was instantaneous. One after another, their essence forms dissolved into streams of energy before disappearing into Beginning.","The Sea of Darkness shook violently. The surrounding darkness surged like an endless storm.","The Emperor's face became increasingly ugly. \"Stop!\"","He exploded forward. Unfortunately, he was too far away. Everything happened too quickly.","The giant's aura exploded. A terrifying shockwave swept through the Sea of Darkness. Beginning's previously weakened essence body immediately stabilized. The portions torn away by the Emperor rapidly recovered. His fading aura surged upward once more.","Not enough to completely surpass the Emperor. But more than enough that the Emperor could no longer do anything decisive to him in a short period of time.","The Emperor's expression became distorted. The advantage he had painstakingly accumulated throughout the battle instantly disappeared. Beginning was still weaker, yet the difference was no longer significant. More importantly, the Emperor could no longer rapidly snowball his advantage. The giant now possessed enough strength that every exchange would become dangerous again.","\"Damn you!\"","The Emperor roared. His draconic body erupted forward.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The two colossal figures collided once more.","Far outside the domain, Michael released a slow breath. The gamble had worked.","Beginning was still losing. But now the Emperor could no longer devour him to death within a short period of time. The battle had been dragged back into uncertainty.","Michael pulled his attention away from the battle overhead. His eyes swept across the ruined capital.","Aside from the collapsed buildings and broken streets, what caught his attention was something he had noticed since coming out of the void. The remains of the empire's forces that had refused to surrender before being cut down by Spartan.","It was unknown whether some with the intention to surrender had died before they could act, but that detail did not matter now.","Among the corpses, many had been torn apart beyond recognition. Yet among the dead were still hundreds of relatively intact bodies. Three hundred at least, perhaps more. Of those, just over two hundred remained largely complete.","Michael's mana spread outward. A vast invisible force descended over the battlefield.","The nearest spectators immediately noticed. \"Huh?\" \"What is he doing now?\"","The surviving imperial experts suddenly felt a very bad premonition. Under their gaze, more than two hundred corpses slowly rose into the air. The sight was horrifying.","Soon the bodies had gathered around Michael. The scene looked bizarre. The young necromancer stood calmly at the center. Around him floated hundreds of corpses. Behind him stood Lily, the Demonic Supernatural, and countless undead. Above him, the Sea of Darkness continued churning.","The image was so terrifying that many citizens subconsciously lowered their heads. The surviving imperial experts felt their faces turn pale.","Michael paid no attention to the empire's subjects below. Summoning the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten, he placed all the corpses inside the coffin space.","Was it easier to sacrifice his undead or to sacrifice the empire's subjects?","To Michael, even without being close to those hundred undead, sacrificing them had been difficult. But he had done it anyway, and for clear reasons.","Before being dragged into the void, he had told the people below that if they surrendered they would live.","Though young and lacking experience compared to his opponents, Michael was not a saint. Many times, he knew how to gauge what was beneficial to him.","If none of the surviving experts had surrendered and were still actively fighting his undead when he came out of the void just to find Beginning in a death battle with the Emperor, using them instead of his undead would have been the obvious choice without a second thought.","However, if he used them even after they had surrendered, every action he had taken and not taken for moral reasons before would become proof of hypocrisy.","After all, if he had no problem sacrificing people who were technically only opponents due to differences they themselves were not directly involved in, then he should have no problem feeding anyone to undead like Lily to accelerate their growth, or even devouring a few humans himself with his talent to gain Evolution Points.","Of course, Michael was still not a saint.","If it were not for the fact that two hundred Rank 3 materials could be immediately converted into another hundred Rank 3 undead, effectively maxing out his contract slots again, and if he had actually been close to the hundred undead he had sacrificed, his choice might have looked very different. At that point, morals might not have entered his thinking at all.","Fortunately, the loss here was also one that could not quite be called a loss.","The surviving experts, unaware of any of this, did not realize how narrowly they had escaped death.","*","A/N: A lot of readers disagreed with Michael's choice of action here. Someone even called him a cat. This chapter was written to show his thought process more clearly. Please read the rest in author's note and thank you for the continued support!"]},{"number":1034,"title":"Chapter 1034 The End","paragraphs":["Unfortunately, buying Beginning a little more time and restoring some of his lost essence did not change the reality of the situation.","Beginning was still losing.","The giant had recovered enough strength to prevent the Emperor from overwhelming him immediately, but that was all. The Emperor remained the superior fighter.","Inside the Sea of Darkness, the battle continued. The darkness trembled continuously. Neither side could gain a decisive advantage anymore, but Michael could tell through his connection what was truly happening. The giant was still being pushed back, little by little.","Michael slowly exhaled. \"This still isn't enough.\"","He had expected this, so he was not surprised. His gaze shifted away from the Sea of Darkness as he summoned the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten. The lid opened, and within moments, a hundred corpses floated around him.","Michael's eyes swept across the floating bodies. Reviving undead was as easy as breathing for him now. Unfortunately, properly reviving one hundred Rank 3 existences simultaneously in a short amount of time was not currently possible.","However, this was only the case if he wanted to revive them properly.","Fortunately, he had his class.","Many of the class's greatest strengths were not reflected on his status panel. Thanks to the authority over death his class granted him, all he needed was a thought and mana.","Michael extended his hand. His mana spread outward. Immediately, the lingering spirits sleeping inside the hundred corpses began to stir, and soon they all awakened.","The process looked almost effortless. Yet Michael knew the truth. This was not proper revival. At most, it was closer to a temporary awakening. A crude use of his authority. The lingering spirit would serve as an anchor while his mana served as fuel. The corpse could move and fight and perform many other functions like any other undead, but only temporarily.","Once the spirit was exhausted, it would disappear completely. At that point, even properly converting the corpse into an undead later would become difficult, as it would be little more than an empty shell.","The process was inherently wasteful.","This was not because of the Death's Heir class itself, but because of Michael. If a true master of death stood in his place, they could likely achieve the same result without such drawbacks. Unfortunately, Michael was not yet that person. His understanding was insufficient and his mastery over the class was incomplete. He had never even fully mastered his previous class, so expecting him to have already mastered this newer and obviously more uniquely powerful one was asking too much.","Michael did not hesitate. The moment the hundred temporary undead stabilized, he sent the command.","\"Go.\"","The newly awakened undead immediately shot toward the Sea of Darkness.","Unlike the previous hundred, these undead were inferior in several respects. Their essence was weaker and their spirits were unstable.","If one of the previous undead had been worth a full unit of essence, then one of these improvised creations was perhaps worth half that amount. Maybe less. Two of them together might barely equal one of the original sacrifices.","Still, quantity had a quality of its own. One hundred remained one hundred.","Above the capital, the Trial Domain reacted once more. The moment the undead touched the edge of the Sea of Darkness, their essence forms were dragged inside.","The Emperor's face immediately darkened. Again.","Inside the domain, Beginning received Michael's intention. The giant launched himself forward. A devastating exchange forced the Emperor backward.","\"No!\"","The draconic serpent had already realized what was happening, but was ultimately helpless to stop it. The newly arrived undead rushed toward Beginning.","Just like before, they offered no resistance. The giant opened his mouth. Streams of essence poured into him. The process completed almost instantly.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","Beginning's body erupted with power. His aura surged upward once more. Though the increase was smaller than before due to the lower quality of the sacrifices, the effect was still obvious. This time, Beginning stood on equal footing with the Emperor once again.","Outside the domain, Michael released a long breath.","The price he had paid just to prolong the fight had been two hundred undead. If Beginning had entered the Trial Domain with this much additional essence from the start, he might have won already. Unfortunately, the giant had been greedy and challenged an opponent he should not have challenged.","Fortunately, the situation had finally stabilized.","Inside the Sea of Darkness, the Emperor's expression became increasingly ugly. The easy victory he had envisioned no longer existed.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The two colossal figures collided again. The battle became increasingly violent. Minutes passed.","Michael continued observing from below. Part of him was already wondering whether he should prepare another hundred corpses when a sudden change occurred.","\"Hm?\"","Michael's eyes narrowed.","Inside the Sea of Darkness, the Emperor's aura fluctuated. The bloody energy flowing beneath his scales suddenly became chaotic. Countless distorted faces appeared briefly across his body. The same faces Michael had seen earlier, the remnants of the Emperor's sacrificed descendants and kin.","Realization struck Michael. \"Oh.\"","A strange expression appeared on his face.","The power the Emperor had gained through sacrifice had come back to haunt him. Perhaps it was not that the sacrifice itself was inherently flawed, but that it had been performed too hastily.","When it came to the fusion of supernatural materials to increase one's foundation, Michael could be considered a minor expert. For the power the Emperor had gained, the time taken had been far too short. It was not surprising that problems would surface later.","Seeing the faces appearing across the Emperor's essence, Michael could make a reasonable guess. When the Emperor had devoured his kin, it had most likely been done without properly separating their bloodlines, simply consuming everything whole. That was obviously going to become a problem eventually.","At first, the enormous increase in strength had hidden the flaws. But now that the battle had dragged on within the Trial Domain, the instability was beginning to surface. The Emperor felt it as well. His movements became less fluid.","Beginning immediately seized every opening.","Below, Michael slowly lowered the hand he had been raising toward the coffin. Perhaps he would not need another hundred after all.","In the end, Michael never needed to sacrifice another hundred. The battle continued for another two hours. At some point, many of the capital's residents had emerged from their hiding places to watch the battle that would decide their fate.","The clash had long surpassed their level of understanding. All they could see were two colossal figures repeatedly colliding inside the darkness above.","Inside the domain, the Emperor's situation grew increasingly worse. His original advantage had vanished the moment Michael restored the giant's strength, and the instability within his essence continued growing.","There was also the matter of Beginning himself.","The giant was a terrifyingly quick learner. He lacked experience, but he possessed something equally frightening. Adaptation. The Emperor gradually discovered that tricks which worked once no longer worked twice. Methods that had succeeded ten minutes ago suddenly failed. Openings that had previously existed disappeared. Mistakes were never repeated.","Beginning was learning throughout the entire battle. Learning. Adapting. Improving. Again and again with every exchange.","At first the Emperor could still rely on superior technique and experience, but the gap slowly closed due to his deteriorating condition until it finally disappeared entirely.","\"Damn monster...\"","The Emperor cursed with undisguised hatred. His essence remained unstable and the screaming faces beneath his scales appeared more and more frequently, steadily weakening him even without Beginning actively devouring portions of his strength.","Meanwhile, Beginning only grew stronger. The more they fought, the more the Emperor also understood this creature had been born for battle.","The battle became one-sided. The Emperor's confidence, greed, and ambition all vanished one after another. Now only survival remained. The emperor no longer thought about surpassing his ancestors. He no longer thought about conquering neighboring empires. He no longer thought about ruling the region.","He only wanted to leave.","Unfortunately, the Trial Domain possessed no exit.","Time passed, and the end finally arrived.","The Emperor's draconic body was barely holding together. Large sections of his essence had already been devoured. His aura had fallen dramatically. Meanwhile, Beginning stood before him like an unmovable mountain.","The Emperor let out a bitter laugh. \"Heh...\"","\"What a terrifying monster...\"","Beginning moved. The giant's hand closed around the Emperor's enormous neck. The draconic serpent struggled weakly.","\"No...\"","His resistance amounted to nothing. The giant opened his mouth and devoured him completely. The Emperor's screams echoed throughout the Sea of Darkness, then disappeared entirely.","The ruler of the Black Serpent Empire was gone.","Outside the domain, his body turned to ash alongside two hundred others. At the same time, a panel appeared before Michael.","[Your Undead 'Beginning' has levelled up to Level 96!]","A seven-level increase.","At the same time, under the shocked eyes of everyone present, a roar sounded and shook the entire imperial capital. Michael's undead High Drake emerged from the void. It too had already finished its battle.","With this, Michael had finally defeated the most powerful enemy he had faced until now.","It was finally time to deal with the aftermath."]},{"number":1035,"title":"Chapter 1035 Rank Advancement Quest [1]","paragraphs":["The first thing Michael did after confirming the Emperor was dead had nothing to do with the surviving citizens, the surrendered experts, or even the countless rewards he had yet to examine.","Without hesitation, Michael stepped directly into the void. The surrounding experts were confused but none of them could have guessed his true objective.","Corpses. Rank 4 corpses.","The moment Michael entered the void, his eyes immediately swept across the shattered battlefield left behind by the High Drake and the two serpent ancestors. The battle had been unimaginably destructive.","Fortunately, Michael found what he was looking for quickly.","The first and second ancestors. The enormous serpent corpses floated silently within the void. Neither possessed any signs of life. Their heads had both been separated from their bodies, but both remained relatively complete.","Michael's breathing became slightly heavier.","Rank 4 corpses. Two complete Rank 4 corpses.","Without wasting time, he immediately summoned the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten. The gigantic corpses disappeared inside, making the already tight space even tighter. Only after both had been secured did Michael finally relax. A smile slowly appeared on his face.","Together with Shojo's corpse, which he had yet to revive, that made three. Three future Rank 4 undead.","The number might seem small, but Michael knew exactly how terrifying it truly was. Once all three were successfully revived, that would give him seven Rank 4 combatants, excluding himself.","Seven.","Even Michael felt slightly dazed thinking about it. Just a year ago he had been struggling to kill slimes. Now, even many established powers throughout the universe could not match the strength he commanded. Some entire realms would struggle to gather seven Rank 4 combatants.","The thought caused Michael to chuckle softly.","For a moment, he simply stood there in the void. The endless darkness stretched in every direction.","At this point, Michael realized that like many other powerful beings, it was time to consider ascending into the third layer of the void in search of opportunities.","After all, his current problem was no longer strength. At least not directly. It was resources. Items capable of accelerating his growth and the growth of his undead. The most direct form of resources for him remained the corpses of supernatural beings.","The Land of Origin provided many opportunities, but it was far from the only source. The void itself was filled with them. Many powerful experts had spent significant portions of their lives wandering through the void. Michael had never truly understood the appeal before. Now he did.","Somewhere out there existed ownerless realms. If he were lucky enough to find one populated only by monsters, aside from evolving all his undead and advancing them to Rank 4, he might even accumulate enough for a Rank 5. He could also use such a realm to conceal the advancement phenomenon of his undead. If he discovered a realm rich enough in resources, it could support his growth for years. And even if it could not, the academy or Federation would pay handsomely to purchase the information. Any sufficiently valuable realm possessed tremendous strategic value, and selling information alone could earn unimaginable wealth.","The more Michael thought about it, the more attractive the idea became. Perhaps it truly was time to step beyond the boundaries of ordinary exploration.","Of course, not immediately. He still needed to revive the new Rank 4 corpses and deal with the Black Serpent Empire.","The only reason the urge to enter the void had grown so strong right now had everything to do with his Advancement Quest.","Thinking of what he had seen a few hours ago, Michael could not help but give a bitter smile.","[Rank Advancement Quest]","Comprehend A Domain [0% Progress]","A Death's Heir is the future sovereign. Even young, every supreme has been stated to be special. Be Renowned.","[Influence Levels: Realmic, Multi-Realmic, Sectoric, Grand Sectoric, Galactic, Multi-Galactic, Cluster Sovereign, Supercluster Sovereign, Cosmic, Universal]","[Current Influence Level: Multi-Realmic]","[Progress: Complete]","Own an entity on the level of your Personal Influence. Not less than three levels below. [0% Progress]","Have Five Hundred Rank 4 Subjects [Progress: 4/500]","Time Limit: 5 Years.","Rewards: 15 Level Ups, 400 Attribute Points, 500 Attribute Points in all stats, Three Random Epic Grade Treasures, One Random Gift, A Title, A Random Trait, and One Random Legendary Grade Item.","Failure: Cannot attempt Advancement for 10 years.","Just as Michael had suspected when the Origin Will first informed him that every future advancement would be tied to the highest possible limit-break path, it had truly meant what it said. At least, that was his conclusion after seeing the requirements.","None of them were simple. Not even one.","Compared to his previous advancement quests, where the requirements had largely revolved around obtaining stronger undead and completing specific milestones, things had become far more technical, far more troublesome, and far more ridiculous.","\"...You have got to be kidding me.\"","The first requirement was not too bad, but that was only in relation to the others.","Comprehend a Domain.","At first glance it looked reasonable. But one had to understand that for most supernaturals, advancing to Rank 4 did not require possessing a complete Domain. In fact, the overwhelming majority of Rank 3 existences advanced with nothing more than a prototype for their domain. After advancing, they would spend time gradually perfecting it until it matured into a true Domain. That was the normal path. The common path.","Michael had personally encountered numerous Rank 4 existences already, and he believed not one of them had needed to fully comprehend a Domain before advancing.","Yet there it was. Comprehend A Domain: 0%. No mention of a prototype. The Origin Will wanted a complete Domain.","Michael's eyelid twitched. \"What kind of nonsense is this?\"","Finally having a moment to himself, Michael could not help but vent a little. Unfortunately, he had no one to blame but himself and his past actions. He was simply paying the price now.","Like the first, the second requirement was also strange. But at least it was already complete.","Truthfully speaking, Michael had encountered similar requirements before, though not personally. He had read about them through other classes. Classes like the Merchant or the Chef, for example. Many unusual professions required fame, reputation, influence, or recognition. He had even read about a Rank 4 Advancement Quest belonging to a chef, the requirement being to create an entirely new supernatural dish.","With examples like those, seeing a renown requirement attached to Death's Heir was not completely shocking. After all, according to the Origin Will, a Death's Heir was supposed to be a future sovereign.","What surprised him was the level. Realmic made sense. Multi-Realmic did not.","Michael could understand reaching the first level. Months ago, his college entrance examination had been broadcast across Aurora. That alone had given him a ridiculous amount of attention. Currently, one of his social media accounts had ten million followers. The number still felt unreal. The strangest part was that he had not posted anything in a very long time, yet the number continued growing. Michael still did not fully understand why. Perhaps people simply enjoyed following someone who never spoke. Or perhaps they were merely curious. Either way, he had stopped paying attention long ago.","Realmic influence? He could accept that. But Multi-Realmic? That was where things became confusing.","Michael frowned. \"How exactly did I reach that?\"","His best guess was that it had something to do with his time in Hell. After all, he had fought alongside multiple races against a common enemy, and afterward had traveled to the Elven Realm and fought their princess as well.","If these counted as having influence in other realms, then reaching the Multi-Realmic level made sense.","As for the other levels listed after Multi-Realmic, the system had provided a brief explanation on each.","Realmic meant one's name and deeds were known within their home realm. Multi-Realmic extended that further, meaning recognition had spread across at least two realms. Sectoric referred to influence spanning an entire sector, a collection of hundreds of realms sharing proximity. Grand Sectoric was simply that, but across multiple sectors simultaneously. Galactic and Multi-Galactic were self-explanatory, influence measured against the scale of one or several galaxies respectively. Cluster Sovereign and Supercluster Sovereign represented influence over groupings of galaxies, the former covering a single cluster and the latter spanning multiple. Cosmic meant recognition felt across the universe.","Universal was the final level. The system offered no elaboration.","Michael was not entirely sure, but he suspected that reaching the Universal level would require standing among the top figures of the strongest races in the universe. Perhaps being at the levels of their leaders to be specific. In other words, completely unreachable by any normal standard.","Michael was only nineteen. He had been a supernatural for less than a year. The Origin Will truly had no concept of moderation.","*","A/N: Sorry for the bad update rate dear readers. Exams have started but don't worry. I'll try my best to keep up!!!"]},{"number":1036,"title":"Chapter 1036 Rank Advancement Quest [2]","paragraphs":["Fortunately, the second requirement counted as complete.","Michael figured it was because the requirement only demanded that he reach one of the listed influence levels. It did not require him to continuously increase it afterward.","Otherwise, he suspected the Origin Will would have forced him to climb all the way to Universal before allowing him to advance. And considering how unreasonable the thing already was, Michael was not entirely convinced it would not do exactly that one day.","Still, compared to the first requirement, the influence requirement was practically a gift.","Unfortunately, the third requirement was just as complicated.","Michael's gaze slowly shifted downward.","[Own an Entity on the Level of your Personal Influence. Not Less Than Three Levels Below.]","\"...\"","The more he looked at it, the more confused he became. \"What exactly does that even mean?\"","Entity. The word was extremely broad. Did it mean to create an organization? Or was it a guild? Or maybe a kingdom? All of them could technically be classified as entities.","Michael rubbed his forehead.","The requirement became even stranger when paired with the influence levels. His current influence level was Multi-Realmic. The requirement stated that the entity could not be more than three levels below his personal influence. That meant the requirement was effectively demanding he possess an entity operating at either Realmic or Multi-Realmic level.","\"Is it because of the word Heir in my title?\"","Michael suspected it was. Unfortunately, due to the nature of this requirement, it meant he could only realistically achieve it in the real world, and even that would not be easy. The Land of Origin was not particularly helpful here either. At least from what he knew, the concept of the third layer of the void did not exist there. The Land of Origin was simply an extraordinarily large world, possibly as wide as the universe itself, but contained within a single world.","After the third came the final requirement.","[Have Five Hundred Rank 4 Subjects (4/500)]","It was a familiar sight. Before this advancement, this type of requirement had been the only kind he had faced from Rank 1 to Rank 3, and it was the reason he had achieved so many limit breaks.","Of everything listed, it was arguably the easiest, second only to the already completed influence requirement.","If Michael excluded the second and fourth requirements, the only things standing between him and advancement were the first and third. Creating a complete Domain before advancing, and establishing an entity of sufficient scale.","The latter was confusing and would require time to properly understand. The former was simply troublesome.","And he only had five years to finish all of it.","With his comprehension, Michael felt that creating a Domain before advancing might not be impossible. But suddenly, he who had initially been so impatient to advance found himself feeling that five years was too little. He was not confident enough, but he could not blame anyone but himself for the situation he was now in.","Fortunately, the rewards made everything seem worth it. And the penalty for failure was clear enough to keep him motivated. If he failed to advance within five years, he would be unable to attempt advancement again for another ten. That meant at least fifteen years of stagnation at the very worst.","Though the urgency made him anxious, it also made him want to act immediately.","He truly did not have much time to waste.","Fortunately, the rewards were genuinely worth the pain.","Putting aside the Epic Grade treasures, attribute points, and Legendary item, just the Gift and fifteen level ups alone made five years of suffering look worthwhile.","The Gift was the reason he was an awakener in the first place. Aside from the Mark of Origin, he possessed another Gift, the Eye of Truth, and each was unique and extraordinarily powerful in its own right. A third Gift at that level would be an overall boost to everything he was capable of.","The fifteen level ups were self-explanatory. Even if his peers ascended before him in five years, the moment he advanced to Rank 4 he would emerge as a Level 90 awakener. Only ten levels from Level 100.","Alongside the other rewards, this task could truly be said to represent the highest possible grade advancement the Origin Will had promised him. Michael could imagine that if he had not been in his current situation, a standard first limit-break task might have looked something like this instead.","[Rank Advancement Quest]","Achieve full comprehension of your Law and begin touching the realm of Domain.","A Death's Heir is the future sovereign. Even young, every supreme has been stated to be special. Be Renowned.","[Achieve Realmic Influence Level]","Have Five Rank 4 Subjects.","Perhaps it truly might have been something as simple as that.","Unfortunately, there were no shortcuts.","Closing his panel, Michael turned to exit the void, where outside the people of the Black Serpent Empire waited to learn their fate.","Meanwhile, back in Aurora, inside the purple world, another important matter was approaching its conclusion.","At the center of a vast clearing stood a beautiful naked woman. Or rather, a body. The clone vessel Michael had prepared for Arianne. Grass and flowering vines covered the important parts of her form, concealing her nudity while simultaneously feeding life essence into the newly created vessel.","Not far away stood a coffin formed entirely from cold blue ice. Within it rested Arianne's original body. Her eyes remained closed. The entire coffin radiated chilling mist as layer after layer of preservation formations continuously maintained her condition.","Several dozen meters away, Michael and Jester stood side by side. Both looked exhausted. Their faces were slightly pale and traces of dried blood could still be seen around the enormous formation beneath their feet. The formation itself stretched for hundreds of meters. Countless runes overlapped one another.","Michael stared at it with narrowed eyes.","Truthfully speaking, he did not understand half of what Jester had done. The former Golden Core cultivator possessed centuries of accumulated knowledge while Michael had been a supernatural for less than a year. Many times he had considered inheriting the full knowledge directly, but had always settled for only having Jester vet specific methods for him. Now that decision was even more important given how many strong individuals' memories he had already absorbed. If he was not careful, he could create serious problems for himself.","Yet despite not fully understanding the ritual below, Michael felt increasingly reassured the longer he observed. Several portions of the formation looked strangely familiar. He could clearly recognize traces of his own Undead Revival skill hidden within the larger structure.","The discovery significantly increased his confidence in the process.","\"The preparation is complete,\" Jester stated, his gaze shifting toward the clone body. \"The difficult part starts now.\"","Michael nodded.","After everything they had invested, there was no turning back.","Soon they would discover whether Jester's method truly worked, and whether it was truly possible to bring someone back from the dead as a living creature."]},{"number":1037,"title":"Chapter 1037 Heaven’s Gaze","paragraphs":["The magic formation possessed two central nodes.","The first was occupied by Arianne's original body, still resting peacefully within the coffin of blue ice. The second was occupied by the clone vessel.","Countless lines of crimson light connected the two positions. Different energies flowed through the formation like rivers.","Jester slowly stepped backward. \"Your turn now, Master.\"","Michael nodded.","At this point, everything that could be prepared had already been prepared. The memories had been extracted. The fragments of Arianne's spirit had been gathered. The damaged portions had been repaired as much as possible.","What remained was the most important step. Transfer.","The ghost-like spirit containing Arianne's memories and sense of self needed to be implanted into the clone vessel. If successful, she would awaken. If unsuccessful, Michael did not want to think about that possibility.","\"Let's begin, Master,\" Jester said.","Michael immediately activated the formation.","BOOOOOOM!!!","The entire clearing trembled as countless runes on the magic circle lit up simultaneously. Streams of crimson light surged between the two nodes. Inside the ice coffin, Arianne's original body slowly began glowing.","At the same time, the clone vessel opened its eyes. She was not truly awake. Her body was simply reacting to the ritual. But the sight alone was enough to make Michael tense.","A faint translucent figure slowly emerged from the original body. This was her soul, or more accurately, the reconstructed spiritual imprint they had painstakingly pieced together. The moment Michael saw it, his eyes brightened slightly, though he remained silent. The difficult part had only just begun.","The translucent figure slowly drifted toward the clone body.","Then suddenly, both Michael and Jester froze.","An inexplicable chill spread across the clearing. A strange pressure descended as the two felt a gaze settle on them.","Jester might not have recognized it, but Michael did. It was the gaze of the Origin Will. However, though he was certain it was the Origin Will, her gaze this time felt odd. Cold, flat, and indifferent, while carrying a trace of majesty.","\"Why are the heavens gazing at us?\" Spartan muttered nearby.","Michael heard it and immediately became enlightened.","Yes. The heavens.","Just as the realm of Aurora had a will, Michael had long suspected the universe possessed one as well, a suspicion supported by the studies of others. If Aurora's will could be called the lower heavens, then the universal will could be called the higher heavens. Michael had always wondered whether the universal will and the Origin Will were one and the same.","However, feeling the gaze on him now, though it resembled the Origin Will, it also felt distinctly different for reasons he could not fully explain.","Michael was confused.","Meanwhile, Jester seemed to have realized something.","\"...Master.\" His voice was unusually serious. \"I think we should stop.\"","Michael slowly turned toward him.","Stop? After everything they had done?","Michael was not willing to stop. Even now, he still carried guilt regarding Arianne's death. Though he had avenged her and destroyed those responsible, it did not change the fact that he had been a cause. Now that a chance existed to bring her back, why would he abandon it?","However, Michael also knew Jester was not the type to speak without reason. Jester was very intelligent. Extremely intelligent. If he was saying this, there had to be a reason.","So Michael waited.","As expected, Jester immediately understood his master's thoughts. \"...You have no intention of stopping.\"","Michael remained silent.","Jester did not continue arguing. Instead, he looked back toward the heavens. \"It is related to the gaze.\"","As expected, Michael thought, his expression becoming slightly more serious. \"Explain.\"","Jester nodded. \"It took me a moment to realize it. I only noticed after recalculating the ritual.\"","His gaze remained fixed on the sky. \"Master, what we are doing is a taboo.\"","The clearing fell silent.","Jester continued. \"The dead are supposed to remain dead. When a living being dies, their spirit disperses. Their fate ends. Their existence enters the cycle of life to be reborn again. That is one of the fundamental laws of the world.\"","\"What we are attempting is not ordinary resurrection. Not something like undead conversion or spirit preservation.\"","His eyes shifted toward Arianne's clone body. \"We are attempting perfect resurrection. A true return. Essentially removing a name from the heavens' book of death.\"","The moment those words left his mouth, Michael finally understood. His gaze slowly rose toward the heavens. The pressure remained. Cold. Indifferent. Majestic.","\"So that's what this is.\"","Jester nodded. \"The heavens have noticed our actions and sent a warning.\"","Michael remained silent for several moments before asking the question he truly cared about. \"If we continue, will something happen?\"","Jester was briefly silent. Then he answered honestly. \"Not immediately.\"","Michael frowned.","Jester continued. \"Every action has consequences. In cultivation, we call it Karma. The greater the violation, the greater the karmic debt. And returning the dead to life creates an enormous debt.\"","\"And?\" Michael pressed.","\"And when Master attempts to advance in the future...\" For the first time since the conversation began, uncertainty appeared in Jester's voice. \"The difficulty will increase. There are many forms such debt can take.\"","Jester finally looked directly at Michael. His expression remained calm, but his meaning was obvious. \"I believe Master should reconsider. It is not worth it.\"","Michael was not offended. Not even slightly, because he understood exactly why Jester was saying it.","Among everything Jester cared about, Michael stood above all else. This was a natural consequence of his identity as his master.","To Jester, Michael's safety and wellbeing mattered more than almost anything. It was not that he disliked Arianne, nor that he wanted her to remain dead.","He likely felt nothing either way about her life or death. But if saving Arianne carried even a small possibility of harming Michael's future, then Jester would naturally oppose it.","Such a conclusion was obvious from his perspective.","Michael himself could understand the logic.","Unfortunately, logic was not always enough.","His gaze drifted toward the spirit slowly floating between the two bodies. Then toward the clone vessel. Then finally back toward the heavens.","The pressure remained unchanged.","Michael slowly exhaled. \"We've already come this far.\"","Jester closed his eyes. He had already expected that answer.","Michael's voice remained calm. \"Maybe this is a mistake. Maybe it isn't. But if I stop now...\"","His gaze settled on Arianne. \"...I'll regret it.\"","The formation beneath them suddenly glowed brighter. Streams of crimson light surged across the clearing. The spirit continued drifting toward the clone body.","And high above them, the heavens watched for a while longer before their gaze finally withdrew."]},{"number":1038,"title":"Chapter 1038 Truth","paragraphs":["The Royal Capital. The Moonlight Hall.","Even after the destruction that had swept through the capital, the hall still stood. It had not emerged completely unscathed though.","Cracks covered several pillars. Entire sections of the outer walls had collapsed. The magnificent gardens surrounding it had long since been reduced to rubble.","Had it been an ordinary structure, it would have been reduced to dust long ago.","Inside the enormous hall, silence reigned. The atmosphere was so oppressive that nobody dared breathe too loudly.","At the very center sat Michael. One hand supported his forehead while the other rubbed his temple slowly.","The recent battle, the advancement quest, Beginning's recklessness, Arianne's resurrection ritual, and the countless matters waiting for him afterward had all given him a headache.","For once, even Michael felt tired.","Behind him stood three Rank 4 undead. Beginning, Lily, and the High Drake, all in their human forms.","As for the Rank 4 Demonic Supernatural, Michael had sent it to search through the ruins of the empire palace alongside capable Rank 3 undead like Spartan, Ghost, Fade, and others, with orders to locate any hidden treasures.","Before the fight, Michael had not expected to lose, but he had wondered what he would do with the royal family after dealing with their leadership.","Though unfortunate, the Emperor's decision to wipe them out himself had removed that problem entirely and spared Michael from having to dirty his own hands.","Thanks to that, the palace was now essentially a treasure vault waiting to be looted.","Even though he had already sent several undead ahead to search on his behalf, Michael still planned to run a few additional sweeps himself to make sure nothing was missed.","After all, everything here represented potential resources that would likely yield a massive amount of Evolution Points, opening up possibilities that had previously been out of reach.","And this was only from the empire's own reserves. There were still many other places he could exploit, cough, earn from.","In front of Michael stood roughly two hundred surviving Rank 3 experts.","Alongside them were important officers of the empire, none of whom were weak in either personal strength or political influence.","These were the strongest remaining figures of the Black Serpent Empire. Even a tenth of this group would have been enough to make a powerful kingdom like Lionheart despair.","Yet right now, none of them dared move.","Many kept their heads lowered. Some had pale faces. Others were visibly trembling. No one dared meet Michael's eyes.","How could they?","The young man sitting before them had personally destroyed their empire. Their Emperor was dead. Their ancestors were dead.","Their strongest forces had been annihilated.","If Michael were to simply leave them alone, it was estimated that within a year at most, the surrounding powers would descend on them like a pack of wolves.","So even though Michael was the cause of their distress, he happened to be the only one they could lean on right now.","The silence in the hall stretched on and the pressure only continued to grow. Many of the Rank 3 experts felt sweat forming on their backs.","Finally, Michael lowered his hand from his temple.","When his gaze swept across the hall, every expert immediately stiffened. The room became even quieter.","Then Michael spoke.","\"Let's make one thing clear first.\" His calm voice echoed throughout the hall. \"I have no interest in slaughtering everyone here.\"","Several experts visibly relaxed. Only for Michael's next sentence to freeze them again.","\"That depends entirely on whether you give me a reason not to.\"","A heavy silence descended.","Michael looked at the two hundred experts before him and nodded slowly. His voice remained calm. \"At least none of you are stupid enough to test me.\"","To be honest, their reduced numbers were partly their own fault. If they had surrendered earlier, there would have been considerably more of them standing here now.","Of course, Michael understood it was unrealistic to expect them not to fight. As for those who had not surrendered in time and paid the price for it, he felt no particular guilt.","That was the nature of war.","If he had not been strong enough, putting aside the treasures and resources, it would have been his own life on the line instead.","Several experts lowered their heads further upon hearing his words.","Michael did not bother with their reactions and continued speaking. \"Truthfully speaking, I only called you here for one reason.\" His gaze swept across the hall. \"To decide how things move forward from here.\"","The experts immediately became attentive. This was the moment they had all been waiting for. The fate of the Black Serpent Empire was closely tied to their own.","Michael leaned back slightly. \"To begin with, I have no intention of ruling this empire.\"","The hall instantly fell into stunned silence. Many experts raised their heads in shock.","Michael ignored their reactions. \"I am still very young. I already have enough problems. I have no interest in spending the next several decades managing taxes, disputes, borders, trade agreements, noble conflicts, succession issues, and all the other nonsense that rulers deal with.\"","Several experts felt their eyelids twitch.","Young? The young monster sitting before them had destroyed an empire and killed multiple Rank 4 existences. Yet he was complaining about paperwork?","Unfortunately, nobody dared say a word. Just like many others before them, several in the room had already concluded that Michael was likely an old monster with a particular taste for youthful appearances.","Of course, they could use mana to scan his bone age but only suicidal people here would attempt that.","Michael continued. \"However, I also have no intention of simply letting go of the empire. After all, that would be stupid.\"","The empire's experts remained attentive and continued listening carefully.","\"Why should I spend all this effort destroying the Black Serpent Empire only for someone else to inherit the benefits? Why should I walk away from all the resources this place possesses?\""]},{"number":1039,"title":"Chapter 1039 Gains","paragraphs":["Many experts became speechless.","The bluntness of his words made them uncomfortable, and it did not help that nobody could find a flaw in his logic.","Michael was not even pretending. He simply said exactly what he was thinking.","\"I don't want to rule the empire. But I am certainly not abandoning it either.\"","The experts exchanged bitter looks. As expected. Things could never be that simple.","Michael tapped the armrest of his chair. \"It is almost dawn. Before the day ends, every family represented here will submit a complete inventory of their resources.\"","The atmosphere immediately became heavy.","\"Additionally, every family will surrender fifty percent of its current assets.\"","Many expressions changed. Half? That was painful. Very painful. Yet nobody dared object.","\"And one more thing.\" Michael's eyes narrowed. \"No one is allowed to touch the properties, territories, vaults, inheritances, or assets belonging to your deceased colleagues.\"","Several experts immediately became nervous. Clearly some had already begun considering exactly that.","Michael's voice became colder. \"If I discover anyone attempting it, I will personally visit your family.\"","Nobody doubted the threat. The hall became deathly silent.","Then Michael's expression eased slightly. \"Of course, there is good news.\"","The experts blinked. Good news? From him?","\"I only want everything documented. After I finish reviewing the assets and taking my share from the deceased families, anyone interested in acquiring those assets may come negotiate with me. I will offer fair prices. After all, I cannot be expected to manage so much myself.\"","Realization slowly spread through the room.","Ignoring the reactions of those before him, Michael pondered whether there was anything he had missed or forgotten to say.","What he wanted right now was complete information on the empire's wealth, territories, resources, industries, and everything else. After all, he was now at a stage where resources mattered more than ever.","Though he had no intention of claiming the emperor's throne, he had equally no intention of leaving such a rich opportunity to someone else.","This was an established empire. Michael did not believe an entity like this could not provide him with at least a few hundred thousand Evolution Points a year.","He had not forgotten that he had a target of fifty million Evolution Points to evolve all his undead to Rank 4.","Michael did not yet know how he would achieve it, but he still wanted to continue his old habits of building a stronger undead force before advancing.","As for whether he would trigger a limit break or even a unique rank advancement quest in the process, he was not certain.","However, if he succeeded, the rewards that came with it would surely be massive. Perhaps he might even reach Level 100 on the spot.","Of course, if Michael truly managed to achieve something like that, the Origin Will might actually ensure he never advanced again in his life.","He dismissed the thought almost immediately. It was fantasy. He did not genuinely believe he would achieve it. After all, he still lacked confidence in completing his current quest, let alone surpassing it.","Thanks to Michael's words, a bittersweet feeling spread through the hall. At least he was staying. That was a very important point. Without his presence, a power vacuum would have destroyed them far faster than Michael ever could.","Outside, the first rays of dawn slowly began appearing beyond the damaged capital.","After giving a few more commands, Michael sent them all on their way. Soon the hall was empty. After resting briefly, he left to inspect the ruined palace.","Not only were the empire's people going to be very busy in the days ahead. Michael was in the same position.","In the blink of an eye, three days passed.","In those three days, quite a few things happened.","For one, Arianne's resurrection was successful, though only partially. She appeared to be in a very deep sleep. Thanks to the strain of the ritual, Michael himself was very weak and needed rest.","In that state, let alone reviving the new Rank 4 corpses he had acquired, he could not even approach his oldest Rank 4 corpse without risking serious harm to himself.","Though weakened, Michael still paid attention to the Federation's attack on the demonic faction.","Since it had been planned as a swift strike, it was always going to end quickly one way or another.","Michael did not know the full details of how the battle unfolded, but based on his communications with his contacts at the academy, he was able to conclude that the Federation had come out victorious.","As for whether this would provide the realm with a few years of peace, only time would tell. In any case, the academy had requested his presence within a week.","At the same time, the Supernaturals Association tallied Michael's earnings from selling the corpses of the monsters that had attacked Brightgate City.","Though not entirely surprising, Michael had not genuinely expected the Federation to gift him a reward for his role in defending the city. Based on his current relationship with the Federation, he had half-expected to simply be ignored.","In any case, thanks to the Federation's gesture of appreciation combined with the corpse sales, Michael was now four hundred million dollars richer.","This was well past his previous estimate.","According to Jester, the figure should have been even higher, but understanding that the Federation had already shown him considerable face and also needed to turn a profit themselves, neither of them pursued the matter further.","Interesting things had also happened back in the Land of Origin.","Michael made a brief trip back to Thornvale to ease the anxiety of Arianne's father. Thanks to Michael's earlier arrangements and the supervision of Ace and Lia, the old man looked considerably healthier than before.","He became even more so after seeing his daughter's living body. Though she remained unconscious, Duke Evermoon was deeply grateful for Michael's efforts and visibly shaken by what Michael had managed to accomplish.","Before returning to the empire, Michael left behind a strong defensive arrangement to protect both father and daughter.","As for the Lionheart Kingdom, Michael had no business with them and left them alone.","If Michael's greatest gain in the real world was a profit approaching half a billion dollars, it could not compare to what he gained in the Land of Origin.","It truly could not compare.","[Evolution Points: 9,823,643]"]},{"number":1040,"title":"Chapter 1040 Changes In Talent","paragraphs":["It was noon on the third day after the fall of the Black Serpent royal family. It was also the last day Michael could feed his talent anything significant for a long time.","Right now, he stood inside a mine several miles away from the capital. The mine was enormous. Dark metallic ore covered the walls while faint traces of mana shimmered beneath the stone like buried starlight.","This place had originally belonged to one of the forces that had been wiped out during the battle.","Since Michael had already ordered the mine to be vacated beforehand, no one knew how much of its reserve had already disappeared. Of course, they would know later, but Michael simply did not care.","Before someone bought it from him or entered a cooperative arrangement with him, this place belonged to him. And since it belonged to him, he could do whatever he wanted with it.","After giving the hollowed-out mine one final glance, Michael quietly disappeared.","The next moment, he reappeared deep within a forest. Massive trees surrounded him on all sides.","Sunlight slipped through the leaves in thin golden lines, falling over his body as he sat cross-legged on the ground.","Michael closed his eyes. Most of his attention was fixed on one thing.","His accumulated Evolution Points.","[Evolution Points: 9,823,643]","Close to ten million.","Even Michael had not expected to come this close so soon. Three days ago, the number would have sounded ridiculous to him.","But after devouring a portion of the imperial reserves, the treasures hidden in the palace, several rare materials from destroyed noble forces, and part of the extraordinary materials stored across the empire's mines and vaults, his points had climbed at an almost absurd speed.","And this was not everything. Far from it.","Michael had only taken what he could justify taking immediately without destabilizing the entire empire too much.","The remaining resources still had value, but if he devoured everything blindly, he would gain a short burst of power while destroying one of the best long-term resource sources he had ever obtained. That would be foolish.","Michael exhaled slowly. \"Almost ten million...\"","The number was huge. Enough to evolve many of his undead and push several important ones forward. But still, compared to his true goal, it was not enough.","Fifty million.","That was the rough number Michael had estimated he would need if he wanted to push all his undead toward Rank 4. And that was only an estimate.","Michael rubbed his forehead. \"Resources...\"","Once again, everything returned to resources. Strength required resources. Undead required resources. Evolution required resources. His advancement quest required resources.","For a moment, Michael almost laughed. No wonder so many powerful beings spent their lives fighting, exploring, scheming, and occupying territories.","At the end of the day, power was expensive. Very expensive.","Looking at his accumulated Evolution Points, the desire to seek out surrounding powers as strong as the empire filled Michael. Eventually he quenched the urge with a sigh.","This time it was not because of morals, but basic reasoning. Even though he had a lot of Evolution Points now, it was his undead who were growing stronger, not him personally.","If multiple peak Rank 4 superpowers targeted him simultaneously, things would become troublesome very quickly.","But even that alone would not have worried Michael too much. What truly concerned him was the possibility of walking straight into the territory of a hidden Demigod-level supernatural without realizing it.","The Emperor's methods had left a deep impression on him. Such existences could hide their true power with frightening ease.","Shaking those thoughts from his mind, Michael turned his attention back to his talent.","As one would expect, with millions of Evolution Points accumulated, his talent had naturally revealed something new. A subtle but meaningful change.","With a contemplative look on his face, Michael retrieved a crystal from his storage space.","It was a transparent crystal that seemed to hold the dark ink of the void within it while simultaneously containing the stars of a galaxy.","[Evolution Essence Crystal {Common Grade}]","If used by a monster, can raise the grade of a Common Grade monster to Three-Star Common Grade, the peak of its racial rank.","If used by an intelligent race, can grant 3 to 5 attribute points randomly distributed across any stat below 20 points.","At some point after crossing the one million Evolution Points threshold, his talent had gained the ability to condense Evolution Points into physical form.","However, though it carried the same core effect as before and added extra benefits, it was an enormous waste of Evolution Points.","Each crystal cost one thousand Evolution Points to create.","Even evolving a Common Grade monster to Rare Grade normally required no more than twenty-five Evolution Points.","Not only could this crystal only be used on Common Grade monsters, but it was a thousand points per use. A thousand.","Of course, the second function of the crystal was more interesting. Michael suspected that was probably its true value, but even so, the cost remained steep.","However, this was only the Common Grade version his talent could produce. Higher grades were also possible.","[Evolution Essence Crystal {Rare Grade}]","If used by a monster, can raise the grade of a Rare Grade monster to Three-Star Rare Grade, the peak of its racial rank.","If used by an intelligent race, can grant 10 to 15 attribute points randomly distributed across any stat below 200 points.","To create this required 10,000 Evolution Points.","[Evolution Essence Crystal {Extraordinary Grade}]","If used by a monster, can raise the grade of an Extraordinary Grade monster to Three-Star Extraordinary Grade, the peak of its racial rank.","If used by an intelligent race, can grant 30 to 50 attribute points randomly distributed across any stat below 400 points.","Can be used in the crafting of an Epic Grade treasure to nurture an early item spirit.","To create this required 30,000 Evolution Points.","*","A/N: Thank you for reading today's chapters!"]},{"number":1041,"title":"Chapter 1041 Unexpected Visitor","paragraphs":["Were these crystals worth the price?","Michael's heart and mind gave the same answer almost instantly.","No. Absolutely not.","They were too expensive. Ridiculously expensive. The price difference made no sense to him.","Just the Extraordinary Grade Evolution Essence Crystal alone cost thirty thousand Evolution Points. Thirty thousand.","With that amount, Michael could evolve two suitable creatures to Epic Grade. Yet this crystal was only Extraordinary Grade.","The comparison made Michael's eyelid twitch. \"Is this thing robbing me?\"","The more he looked at it, the more speechless he became.","Of course, Michael understood that the crystal had advantages. For one, it could be given to others and could even be used in item crafting. From a broader perspective, it was far from useless.","In fact, if sold properly, it could become a terrifying resource that countless factions would fight over.","After all, an item capable of raising attributes or helping nurture an item spirit, a feature usually only seen in Legendary Grade items, was undeniably valuable.","But to Michael personally? The current value was very questionable.","He did not lack ways to strengthen monsters, and he had no reason to spend tens of thousands of Evolution Points on something he could accomplish far more cheaply through direct evolution.","As for using it on intelligent races to raise attributes, the cost still felt painful. It was not a good enough reason for him to throw points away casually.","Michael stared at the crystal for a long time before sighing. \"If a mere Extraordinary Grade crystal already costs this much, what about Epic Grade?\"","His expression became strange. \"Would it cost hundreds of thousands?\"","The thought alone made him uncomfortable. And if his talent became more powerful in the future, what then? Would a Legendary Grade crystal cost millions? Would a Divine Grade crystal require something truly obscene?","Michael suddenly felt that this function was not something meant for his current stage. Perhaps it was designed for situations where direct evolution was simply impossible.","That particular thought struck a chord somewhere in his mind, but he could not quite place what it was he had been enlightened on.","In any case, for now the crystals were inefficient. Because of that, Michael had only condensed a small number for research purposes. A few Common Grade crystals. A few Rare Grade crystals. And only one Extraordinary Grade crystal. Anything more would be wasteful.","Yes, he was rich now. He had nearly ten million Evolution Points. But being rich did not mean he could afford to spend stupidly. Especially when his target was still fifty million.","Michael closed his fingers around the crystal and stored it away. \"No more of these for now.\"","His decision was immediate. Until he fully understood their value, he would not waste large amounts of Evolution Points producing them.","Michael opened his status panel again. The number remained beautiful.","[Evolution Points: 9,823,643]","Beautiful, but not enough.","How great would it be if he has the treasury of another man's wealth.","He let out a long sigh before disappearing from the forest and reappearing back in the capital.","Though he had no intention of personally ruling the place, he still had to shoulder responsibility for certain matters until everything was stable to function without much intervention.","In the days that followed, life passed uneventfully until three days later when the Norman household received a surprising guest.","\"Teacher Brian, what are you doing here? It's a pleasure to see you. Please come in.\"","Since he was going to be staying indoors for a while, Michael had no reason to hide his presence from his family, especially since he needed Jester nearby as well. Explaining a long disappearance without that context would have been a headache.","Michael had not expected Teacher Brian to come and find him. The reason he was already at the door before the man even knocked was because he had sensed him through their connection.","\"Sorry to disturb you, but I just finished my business with the academy, and after so many days of your absence I thought I should come and see how you were doing. How have you been feel...\"","Teacher Brian's words trailed off.","Michael had just led him into the sitting room when the older man suddenly stopped walking. Confused, Michael turned to look at him.","\"Teacher?\"","Brian did not answer immediately. His gaze had shifted past Michael.","At that moment, Aunt Mia had just come downstairs. She was dressed simply, yet the moment she appeared, the atmosphere in the room seemed to soften slightly.","Her steps slowed when she noticed there was a guest, especially one whose aura clearly marked him as extraordinary.","Michael noticed Brian's brief distraction but thought nothing of it.","\"Oh, right.\" He stepped aside slightly. \"Teacher Brian, this is my aunt, Aunt Mia.\"","Then he looked toward Aunt Mia. \"Aunt Mia, this is Teacher Brian. He is one of my instructors and works directly with the Federation.\"","Aunt Mia's expression changed slightly. The Federation. For ordinary citizens, those two words carried enormous weight. Even knowing that Michael's current status was no longer ordinary, meeting someone connected directly to the Federation still made her feel a little nervous.","Still, Aunt Mia quickly composed herself. Her manners remained graceful.","\"It is a pleasure to meet you, Teacher Brian.\"","Brian seemed to recover only then. He cleared his throat lightly. \"The pleasure is mine, Madam Mia.\"","His voice remained calm and polite.","Inwardly, however, Brian could not help but feel slightly surprised.","Michael's aunt was beautiful.","Brian had met countless powerful women throughout his time with the Federation. Yet Mia Norman gave off a completely different feeling.","At first glance, the resemblance between her and Michael was obvious.","The shape of her eyes, the structure of her face, and even certain subtle expressions carried traces of the young necromancer.","If Michael represented a handsome male interpretation of the Norman bloodline, then Mia felt like a more refined and elegant expression of the same features."]},{"number":1042,"title":"Chapter 1042 Uncomfortable Nephew","paragraphs":["Her skin was exceptionally fair, almost flawless beneath the light. It possessed none of the artificial perfection that came from supernatural enhancement. Instead, it was the natural beauty of someone blessed with outstanding genes.","Her face was delicate yet mature. High cheekbones complemented a slender jawline while her nose was straight and elegant. Her lips possessed a natural softness that made her gentle smiles appear particularly warm.","Unlike many women who preferred long hair, Mia kept hers short. The dark hair ended just above her shoulders, framing her face perfectly and emphasizing her graceful neck.","The style suited her surprisingly well, making her appear both mature and sophisticated.","She was also tall. Not quite Michael's height, but still noticeably taller than most women. Her figure was elegantly curved, neither exaggerated nor lacking.","Every proportion seemed balanced, creating a sense of natural grace whenever she moved.","There was a quiet maturity to her appearance.","Countless women in the Federation were beautiful. Many were even objectively more stunning due to supernatural enhancement. Yet Mia possessed something rarer.","Warmth. The kind of beauty that made a house feel like a home.","For a brief moment, Brian found himself staring longer than was appropriate before quickly recovering his composure.","Aunt Mia, on the other hand, felt slightly flustered beneath Brian's polite gaze. Thankfully, she maintained her composure.","\"I hope Michael has not been causing you too much trouble.\"","Michael's eyelid twitched. \"Aunt.\"","Brian paused. Then, almost instinctively, a faint smile appeared on his face. \"Not at all.\"","Michael looked at him silently.","Brian continued with a perfectly calm expression. \"Michael is one of the most talented students I have ever taught.\"","That was true. Whether he was troublesome or not was a completely different matter. Though, since when had Teacher Brian started teaching him anything?","Aunt Mia smiled with visible pride. \"I am glad to hear that.\"","Michael felt the atmosphere heading in a direction he did not particularly like. So he coughed lightly. \"Let's sit first.\"","Aunt Mia nodded and turned toward the kitchen. \"I will get something for our guest.\"","\"There is no need to trouble yourself,\" Brian said quickly.","\"It is no trouble at all,\" Aunt Mia replied with a smile. Then she left.","Brian watched her leave for only half a second before looking away naturally.","Unfortunately for him, Michael had noticed.","The room became quiet. Michael slowly turned his gaze toward Brian. Brian looked back calmly. For a moment, neither spoke.","Then Michael's eyes narrowed slightly. \"Teacher.\"","Brian's expression did not change. \"Yes?\"","Michael stared at him. Brian stared back. The silence lasted for several seconds.","Then Michael finally sat down. \"...Nothing.\"","Brian also sat across from him.","Moments later, Aunt Mia returned carrying a tray. \"Sorry for the wait.\"","\"You really didn't have to,\" Brian said.","\"It is fine,\" Aunt Mia replied.","She set the cups down before taking a seat opposite them.","This was the first time she had been this close with one of Michael's instructors. She was very curious.","For a few moments, the conversation remained normal. At least it started that way.","\"So, Teacher Brian,\" Mia asked politely. \"What exactly do you teach?\"","Brian smiled. \"Combat.\"","Mia blinked. \"Just combat?\"","\"Mostly combat.\"","Michael lowered his head and quietly drank his tea.","\"That sounds dangerous,\" Mia said.","Brian nodded. \"It can be.\"","\"Do you get injured often?\"","\"Occasionally.\"","Aunt Mia frowned. \"That's unfortunate.\"","Brian's smile widened slightly. \"It comes with the job.\"","Michael suddenly had a strange feeling. A very strange feeling.","Then Aunt Mia asked another question. \"Are you married? Your line of work must make your family worry.\"","Michael nearly choked on his tea.","Brian remained calm. \"No, I am not married. Well, I was before, but she passed away.\"","\"I see.\" Aunt Mia nodded thoughtfully.","Michael slowly lowered his cup. Why was this conversation happening?","\"Any children?\"","\"...No.\"","\"Busy career?\"","\"Very.\"","\"I understand.\"","Michael looked from one adult to the other. Neither appeared embarrassed. In fact, both looked strangely comfortable. Meanwhile, he felt increasingly uncomfortable.","Brian politely returned the questioning. \"And you, Madam Mia?\"","Aunt Mia smiled. \"Also single.\"","Michael closed his eyes. Why? Why was he sitting here?","\"Life has been busy,\" Mia continued. \"Raising children leaves very little free time.\"","Brian nodded. \"I can imagine.\"","\"You don't have children though.\"","\"No.\"","\"Then how can you imagine?\"","Brian opened his mouth. Paused. Then laughed. Aunt Mia laughed as well.","Michael stared at the ceiling. What was this conversation?","Several minutes passed. The two adults somehow moved from discussing work to discussing cooking, then from cooking to gardening, then from gardening to travel. The strangest part was that they seemed to genuinely enjoy talking to each other.","At one point Brian mentioned visiting a coastal city. Aunt Mia immediately responded.","\"Oh, I have always wanted to visit one.\"","Brian smiled. \"Perhaps one day you should.\"","Michael immediately sat up. \"No.\"","Both adults turned toward him. Michael realized what he had just said.","\"...I mean.\" The room became silent. \"Nothing.\"","Aunt Mia looked confused. Brian's lips twitched. The older man suddenly seemed to be enjoying himself far too much.","Michael could already feel a headache forming.","Finally he stood. \"Teacher.\"","Brian looked up. \"Yes?\"","\"I just remembered why you came here.\"","Brian raised an eyebrow. \"You did?\"","\"Yes.\" Michael nodded firmly. \"Important academy business.\"","\"There is?\"","\"There is now.\"","Aunt Mia seemed to realize she had indeed gotten carried away. A faint smile appeared on her face before she excused herself.","Michael's headache immediately worsened.","After Aunt Mia excused herself, the atmosphere in the room finally returned to normal. At least for Michael. For Brian, that was debatable.","The moment Mia disappeared upstairs, Michael immediately looked at his teacher. Brian calmly sipped his tea.","\"...Teacher.\"","\"Yes?\"","Michael stared at him. Brian stared back.","Eventually, Michael gave up.","A few minutes later, the conversation finally shifted to more relevant matters.","\"The operation was a success,\" Brian said. There was visible satisfaction in his voice. \"We achieved far more than expected.\"","Michael became interested. \"Oh?\"","Brian nodded. \"Several demonic strongholds were destroyed. Multiple Rank 4 enemies were eliminated and a large amount of their infrastructure was wiped out.\"","For a moment, a cold light flashed through his eyes. \"They will recover eventually. They always do. But not anytime soon.\"","Michael understood immediately. \"How long?\"","Brian leaned back slightly. \"Based on current estimates, the Federation should enjoy close to two years of relative peace.\"","Michael raised an eyebrow. Two years was indeed a meaningful window.","Brian continued. \"The damage was not merely physical. Their manpower, resources, and influence networks all suffered heavily.\"","\"Good,\" Michael replied honestly. The fewer demonic supernaturals causing trouble, the better.","The two continued discussing a few academy matters afterward before the conversation finally came to a close.","Soon, Michael escorted Brian toward the front door. \"Thanks for visiting, Teacher.\"","Brian smiled. \"Try attending the academy before everyone starts thinking you have dropped out.\"","Michael coughed awkwardly. \"I will consider it.\"","Brian laughed.","As he stepped outside, his gaze unconsciously drifted toward one of the upstairs windows. Michael immediately noticed.","\"...Teacher.\"","Brian looked innocent. \"Yes?\"","\"Goodbye.\"","Brian smiled. \"Goodbye, Michael.\"","A few moments later, Michael watched the man disappear into the distance before slowly turning his gaze toward the second-floor window."]},{"number":1043,"title":"Chapter 1043 Epic Grade Evolution Essense Crystal","paragraphs":["While Michael in Aurora went about handling various matters, another Michael sat quietly in the Land of Origin.","The scenery around him was majestic. Towering mountain peaks stretched toward the sky in every direction. Clouds drifted lazily between them while cold winds swept across the rocky landscape.","Michael sat atop a massive boulder overlooking the mountains. His attention was focused on two items resting in his hands.","A palm-sized black coffin. And a silver ring.","These were currently his two storage treasures. The first was naturally the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten. The second was the spatial ring he had acquired later.","Both were invaluable Three-Star Epic Grade treasures, obtained as rewards from his rank advancement quest.","Yet at this moment, Michael was not admiring them.","As he stabilized the situation in the empire while his original body recovered from exhaustion, Michael had not been idle during the past week. He had continued accumulating Evolution Points steadily.","After three more days, though the rate of growth had slowed considerably, it had still managed to cross the ten million mark.","However, no significant change had come to his talent aside from gaining the ability to create an Epic Grade Evolution Essence Crystal.","Speaking of which, the crystal had impressive properties if one ignored the cost of seventy thousand Evolution Points per creation.","Each use could increase a stat by seventy to one hundred points, provided the stat in question was below a thousand. It could also be used in the creation of items and already possessed an item spirit embryo.","The difference between this and the Extraordinary Grade Evolution Essence Crystal was that the latter only offered a chance at producing an item spirit, while the former already contained one that simply needed to be activated.","Of course, like the other crystals, this one could also raise the racial limit of Epic Grade monsters to Three Stars.","Surprisingly, despite its cost, it was the only crystal Michael genuinely felt was worth its price for his own use.","To evolve a monster to Rank 4, Michael needed at least fifteen thousand Evolution Points. With his talent and sufficient points now at his disposal, he had also been able to determine that evolving a One-Star Epic Grade creature to Three Stars cost seventy-five thousand Evolution Points.","Though that was only five thousand less than evolving normally, spread across thousands of undead, using the Epic Grade Evolution Essence Crystal would save him an enormous amount of Evolution Points in total.","However, though tempted, Michael currently had no opportunity to evolve his undead during such a sensitive period.","It was only now, six days after the battle against the Black Serpent Empire, that he finally had time to himself.","With so many Evolution Points accumulated, it made little sense to simply save them. It would be far better to convert them into immediate strength. That was also the reason Michael was currently in this location.","The territory of the Black Serpent Empire was vast. Under its command were as many as thirty-three kingdoms. Even now, Michael only possessed a rough understanding of the empire's true prosperity.","The destruction of the palace had not helped matters. Many records had been lost while others remained buried beneath mountains of rubble, waiting to be excavated.","Restoring the empire to full functionality was not something that would happen anytime soon. Perhaps months. Perhaps years. Michael honestly did not know.","Fortunately, he had no intention of personally managing such matters.","Still, one advantage came from controlling the empire. Information.","Thanks to surviving officials and recovered records, Michael had gained access to numerous locations hidden throughout the empire. Aside from resource-rich territories, there were also extremely remote ones.","The location he currently occupied was one of them.","Compared to Evermoon Forest, where people occasionally passed through, this region was practically forgotten by civilization. Within two hundred thousand miles there were no surrounding territories.","In fact, Michael suspected that some areas here might not see a single visitor in ten years. It was simply a vast wilderness officially owned by the empire but unused by anyone, which made it perfect for his purposes.","If he wished, he could evolve dozens of undead to Rank 4 here without anyone discovering the phenomenon.","The thought was tempting, especially with over ten million Evolution Points sitting in his possession.","But Michael resisted. That was not why he had come.","His gaze lowered toward the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten and the storage ring resting in his hands. A thoughtful expression appeared on his face.","For weeks now, a particular idea had lingered at the back of his mind. An idea he had considered multiple times but never possessed the resources to test.","Now things were different. He had a safe location. And most importantly, he finally had enough Evolution Points to afford the attempt.","He wanted to merge the two items together.","Individually, both were exceptional treasures. The Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten in particular had functions like serving as a gateway to the Netherworld and reviving him if he ever died.","However, the function he relied on most for both the coffin and the storage ring was their internal space.","Even when he divided his forces between the two, things were becoming crowded. Though he could have his undead maintain their human forms to create more room, this was not good for their development.","Just like other intelligent races, Michael's undead needed to train their abilities. After all, they were not mindless beasts.","Like any intelligent creature, they had the capacity to think independently and develop themselves. But due to the limited space, many of his undead could only stand idle, wasting their potential.","For undead who could train indefinitely, not exhausting their energy to grow stronger or comprehend their own Laws was a waste of their talents.","Something needed to change.","The Michael of before could not have done anything about it. But the Michael of now could.","He was genuinely excited at the idea of fusing the two spatial items together. With both being Three-Star Epic Grade, he was eager to see what would emerge after the merge.","There was an extremely low chance they would remain at Epic Grade afterward. What that meant was that Michael was confident the merge would result in a higher grade treasure.","And above Epic Grade was Legendary.","Yes. Today, Michael had decided to create a Legendary Grade item."]},{"number":1044,"title":"Chapter 1044 One Million Evolution Points","paragraphs":["Michael had naturally checked the cost of evolving each item beforehand. The moment he learned the price, he had nearly abandoned the idea entirely.","One million Evolution Points.","That was the cost to evolve either the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten or the spatial ring into a Legendary Grade treasure. One million. Michael still felt it was pure madness.","But after calming down and thinking about it carefully, he could also understand why.","This was a Legendary Grade treasure. Not Epic. Legendary. The difference between the two was likely greater than the difference from Common to Epic combined.","From everything Michael had observed so far, not even all Rank 4 supernaturals possessed Epic Grade treasures. Many still used Three-Star Extraordinary Grade items.","Even a One-Star Epic Grade treasure was considered valuable enough to start conflicts between powerful figures.","If Rank 4 experts were already like this, Michael doubted Rank 5 existences would be much better. That was the realm of Demigods. Yet even among them, Michael suspected many would still be using Two-Star or Three-Star Epic Grade treasures.","From that perspective, the value of a Legendary Grade treasure became obvious. Honestly speaking, one million Evolution Points almost looked cheap.","Unfortunately, understanding the value and paying the price were two different things.","Michael looked at the coffin and the ring. If he evolved both separately, that would cost two million Evolution Points. He could afford it. But it felt extremely wasteful.","Two million Evolution Points could create an absurd amount of combat power, giving him dozens of Rank 4 undead. A Legendary Grade treasure was valuable, but not valuable enough to blind him.","Fortunately, there was another option.","With his talent, he could merge the two treasures together. Compared to direct evolution, merging was far cheaper. Only five hundred thousand Evolution Points. Compared to the original two million, this was practically robbery.","Of course, the process would consume one of the treasures. Some people might consider that a loss, but Michael disagreed.","After all, he was not destroying them. He was combining two similar treasures to create something stronger.","More importantly, these were not the only Three-Star Epic Grade treasures he possessed.","If he wanted, he could simply create more Three-Star Epic Grade treasures on his own. When he became richer, he could have as many Epic Grade treasures as he wanted, so there was no need to be too stubborn about it.","Michael's gaze settled on the black coffin and the ring. The wind howled across the mountain peaks.","For several moments, he simply stared at them. Then he finally opened his status panel.","[Evolution Points: 10,147,392]","Five hundred thousand points vanished instantly.","The next moment, both treasures alongside a small drop of his blood essence floated into the air. Michael's talent activated.","This was Michael's first time evolving something to the Legendary Grade, and he had known the process would not be simple. He was right.","After all, this was a Legendary Grade treasure. Even among Demigods, such an item would likely be considered a prized possession.","Yet even with all his preparations, he had not expected what happened next.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The instant the fusion began, the heavens shook.","Michael's pupils contracted.","The clear blue sky above him darkened at a visible speed. It was as if an invisible hand had grabbed the sky itself and smothered it with darkness.","Massive black clouds appeared from nowhere and immediately began expanding.","Ten thousand miles. Twenty thousand miles. Thirty thousand miles.","The clouds continued growing without slowing.","Forty thousand miles. Fifty thousand miles.","Only then did they finally stop.","Michael sucked in a cold breath. A chill ran down his spine. The scale alone was enough to make his scalp tingle.","The surrounding mana had also become chaotic. Violent currents swept across the mountains.","With his exceptional senses, Michael watched as countless beasts fled in terror. The world itself seemed to be warning all living creatures to stay away.","At some point, Michael too had already retreated dozens of miles from the fusion site. Even then, he still felt uneasy.","The two treasures floated at the center of the phenomenon. The black coffin and the storage ring had become enveloped within a cocoon of silver-black light.","The surrounding space continuously twisted and shattered before restoring itself.","Then everything became silent. Even the violent winds vanished.","CRAAAAAAACK!!!","A blinding bolt of lightning descended from the heavens. It tore through the dark clouds like a divine spear and struck directly toward the cocoon surrounding the treasures.","The scene felt very familiar to Michael. \"Heavenly Tribulation.\"","The words escaped his mouth unconsciously. It reminded him exactly of the tribulations faced by those advancing to Rank 4.","Michael had always wondered when he would personally witness something like this.","After all, he was no longer the same person he had been a year ago. He was considerably more knowledgeable now, thanks in no small part to his habit of having some of his undead read extensively and then implanting their accumulated knowledge into his memory.","He knew that starting from Epic Grade, items would face a heavenly tribulation.","The key difference between an item tribulation and one faced by an intelligent race was that the former was usually far faster.","After all, the heavens were simply testing whether the item deserved its rank. Epic grade items and above could only force their way through with their bodies.","As those thoughts flashed through his mind, Michael watched as the lightning crashed into the cocoon.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","The first tribulation lightning slammed into the cocoon with enough force to shatter mountains. Space rippled violently. The silver-black cocoon trembled. Yet it endured.","Then came the second bolt.","CRAAAAAAACK!!!","Then the third. The fourth. The fifth. Each strike was stronger than the last. The heavens seemed determined to destroy the treasure before it could even be born.","Entire mountain peaks collapsed under the residual shockwaves. Several nearby rivers changed course.","Hundreds of miles of land were reduced to wasteland."]},{"number":1045,"title":"Chapter 1045 Legendary Grade Treasure [1]","paragraphs":["Even from his distant position, Michael could feel his skin tingling from the excess lightning energy filling the air.","By the seventh bolt, small cracks had appeared across the cocoon. Michael's heart immediately tightened.","\"Come on...\"","The eighth bolt descended. The cracks multiplied. The cocoon dimmed.","Then came the final strike. The ninth tribulation lightning.","The clouds above churned violently as if gathering all remaining power. For a brief moment, the world became white.","CRAAAAAAAAAAAAACK!!!","The lightning pillar descended. It completely swallowed the cocoon.","Silence followed. Michael's fists unconsciously clenched.","Several seconds passed.","Then the cocoon remained. Though covered in cracks, it had survived. The heavenly tribulation was over.","As if acknowledging the result, the dark clouds rapidly dispersed. Sunlight returned. The surrounding mana erupted, and gathered energy from tens of thousands of miles rushed toward the cocoon like countless rivers returning to the sea.","The cracked shell shattered. A dazzling radiance burst forth. The newborn treasure greedily absorbed the gathered energy as its aura rose continuously, becoming stronger, denser, and more profound.","Michael stared without blinking.","An hour later the light slowly condensed and the object hidden within finally revealed itself.","It was no longer a coffin. Nor was it a ring.","It resembled a miniature black shrine carved from obsidian, covered in silver runes and ancient patterns. Countless stars seemed to flow across its surface while an endless darkness existed within. One glance made Michael feel as if he were looking at an entire world.","Before he could inspect it further, WHOOSH!","The treasure shot toward him. \"So fast!\"","Michael barely reacted before the object reached him. Then it entered directly into his soul through the center of his forehead.","BOOM!","A connection instantly formed. Immediately, Michael's mind cleared as though a layer of dust had been wiped away. His soul space also strengthened and expanded from the feedback received, marking yet another first for Michael.","At the same time, countless pieces of information flooded into his mind.","A moment later, an excited Michael stared at the panel now floating before him.","[Item]: Mausoleum of Endless Dominion","[Grade]: Legendary ★","Bound to Michael Norman","[Description]: A legendary treasure born from a strange fusion. It contains a vast self-sustaining inner world suspended between life and death.","[Effect 1]: Eternal Dominion","Contains a massive internal world capable of sustaining life, death, and spiritual existence simultaneously.","The domain possesses mountains, rivers, forests, plains, and naturally regenerating mana. The owner may freely shape terrain, climate, and environmental conditions within certain limits.","Undead residing inside receive accelerated growth, recovery, and comprehension speed. Living creatures may also inhabit the domain without restriction.","[Effect 2]: Nether Gate","The owner may open a gateway connecting the domain to the Netherworld. The gate can be used to travel, summon undead, or establish temporary links between both realms.","Summoned undead may be up to one rank above the owner's rank. Duration and energy consumption depend on the strength of the summoned entity.","[Effect 3]: Dominion Pulse","The treasure may release a spatial shockwave. The pulse disrupts formations, barriers, domains, spatial structures, and weaker treasures while inflicting spiritual damage upon living targets.","Power scales with the amount of energy supplied.","[Effect 4]: Tomb of Rebirth","If the owner is killed, their soul will be anchored within the Mausoleum. After a period of recovery, the owner may resurrect within the Netherworld.","Each resurrection permanently consumes a portion of the treasure's accumulated origin energy.","Currently, the treasure can perform this function twice before becoming dormant for one hundred years.","[Effect 5]: World Seed (Sealed)","The internal domain possesses the potential to evolve into a true independent world. Growth requires vast quantities of origin energy. Current Progress: 0.01%","Michael carefully read through the information several more times. The more he read, the more satisfied he became.","It was obvious that the treasure's abilities were not random. Rather, they were the result of a perfect fusion between the two treasures that had created it.","Eternal Dominion originated from the Veilring of Quiet Dominion's living space.","Nether Gate and Tomb of Rebirth were inherited from the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten.","Even Dominion Pulse was clearly an upgraded version of the Veilring's original attack.","Everything made sense. Everything except the last effect.","World Seed.","Michael's eyes lingered on the final line. A true independent world. Even someone with his limited knowledge understood the implications.","If this effect was real, then the treasure possessed the potential to become far more than a simple storage item. The possibilities were ridiculous.","Unfortunately, Michael had absolutely no idea what Origin Energy was, nor did he know where to find it. But one thing he was certain about was that anything capable of evolving a Legendary treasure into an independent world was definitely not cheap.","Still, that did nothing to diminish his excitement.","A smile appeared on his face. With a thought, Michael summoned the treasure, and the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion appeared above his palm.","It was only palm-sized now. The treasure no longer resembled a coffin or a ring. Instead, it looked like a miniature mausoleum carved from an unknown black metal.","The material seemed darker than obsidian, almost capable of swallowing light itself. Yet hidden within that darkness were faint streams of emerald-green radiance.","The green light flowed slowly through the surface like veins carrying life through a living organism. They could also be said to resemble roots spreading beneath soil.","The structure itself possessed several elegant layers, and at the center of the mausoleum rested a small circular emerald gem. The gem was not bright.","Instead, it emitted a gentle green glow filled with vitality. It stood in stark contrast to the surrounding darkness.","Deep within the treasure, Michael could sense a faint consciousness.","\"An item spirit?\"","As it was his first time dealing with something like this, his voice carried a hint of doubt. After sensing it a bit more, he confirmed it was truly an item spirit.","However, it was still very young and weak, like a newborn that had only just come into existence."]},{"number":1046,"title":"Chapter 1046 Legendary Grade Treasure [2]","paragraphs":["It was evident it would take a while to grow, though depending on the nourishment Michael's soul provided it, that process could be shorter or longer.","For several moments, Michael simply stared at the miniature mausoleum resting on his palm. Then he laughed softly.","\"Five hundred thousand points.\"","Michael shook his head. \"It was definitely worth it.\"","Though he was pleased, Michael also understood that this was a treasure that should not see the light of day.","There was a saying that a poor man carrying a great treasure invites his own ruin.","Putting aside everything else, Michael felt that the World Seed the treasure contained could potentially drive Demigods to chase him to the ends of the universe.","Unless absolutely necessary, the only visible function of this treasure would be to serve as a storage item.","Michael drew the treasure back into his soul and turned his senses inward.","After all, he had merged two of his strongest items to create something better. It was time to see the state of the world within.","\"Wow, it is so huge!\"","An hour later, after relocating the four thousand plus undead he left a hundred miles from where he evolved the Mausoleum into the Mausoleum's storage space, Michael stepped inside with his physical body for the first time.","Before entering physically, Michael had already learned several things through his connection with the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion. The first was the most important.","The inner space was vast. Not merely larger than the Damaged Coffin of the Forgotten and the spatial ring combined, but absurdly larger. .","According to the information transmitted to him, the internal domain was already comparable to a medium-sized country from his previous world.","Michael had no exact measurement, but judging from his perception, the space stretched across hundreds of thousands of square kilometers.","It also possessed everything a world would naturally have. Mountains. Rivers. Forests. Plains. Valleys. Lakes. Everything existed inside.","Sections of the domain were also divided into several special regions. Currently Michael only recognized the most obvious ones. For other special areas he would still need to conduct an extensive search, or leave the task to his undead.","The first was a vast land shrouded in grey mist. Death energy gathered there naturally, making it the most suitable place for undead to rest or recover.","The second was a mountain region filled with dense earth and death attributes.","Beginning immediately found this place suitable, and Michael suspected many physically powerful undead would benefit from training there.","The third was a region filled with rich vitality. Forests grew there naturally, and faint green light flowed through the soil.","The fourth stretched across thousands of miles and was dominated by volcanoes, rivers of magma, and black mountains constantly releasing heat.","Occasionally, flames would erupt from the ground without warning before dissolving back into pure energy.","For fire-attributed creatures, this place was a paradise.","Spartan immediately became interested in the region.","The undead mage could absorb the surrounding fire energy to strengthen his Abyssal Pyre abilities while also using the harsh environment to temper his understanding of fire-related laws.","The fifth was an enormous inland sea filled with crystal-clear water.","Countless rivers from across the domain eventually flowed into this region before being purified and redistributed throughout the world.","The water attribute mana here was incredibly dense. Gentle rain frequently fell over the sea while powerful currents moved beneath the surface.","Any creature possessing water affinity would benefit greatly from training here. Even Michael himself felt slightly refreshed standing near it.","The sixth was an elevated region constantly swept by powerful winds. Lightning occasionally danced between dark clouds overhead while violent air currents crossed the land.","The seventh was the Golden Sun Fields. Unlike the deathly atmosphere found in many other regions, this area was filled with pure light and life energy.","Golden grass stretched to the horizon while warm sunlight permanently illuminated the land.","Michael suspected this region had formed because the Mausoleum was no longer purely a death-attributed treasure.","It was most likely due to the mysterious World Seed. The World Seed had introduced balance, and now life and death coexisted within the same space.","The last core area was the true center of the Mausoleum. It was a black shrine standing on a floating island above a silent lake, and Michael could sense that the young item spirit slept there.","Aside from these special regions, most of the space was ordinary land.","For the first time, Michael's undead legion truly had a home.","When Michael entered with his physical body, the scene before him made him pause. The sky above was a dim silver, neither day nor night.","A pale green sun hung high above, radiating gentle vitality, while a black moon floated beside it, releasing faint death energy.","The two forces did not clash. Instead, they circulated together in strange harmony.","Scattered across this vast world were Michael's undead. For once, they did not look crowded. In fact, they looked few.","If people lived here, they would probably live their whole lives not meeting one of his undead.","Michael stood silently for several moments, communicating further with the treasure to deepen his understanding.","Compared to his two previous treasures, Michael did not need to summon the Mausoleum to enter it.","Instead, when his physical body was drawn inside, his soul would separate and hide in a concealed pocket within the second layer of the void, maintaining his position.","When he came back out, his soul would return and merge with him again. This was something Michael had figured out early through his connection with the Mausoleum.","Suddenly Michael's eyes opened wide and his body trembled slightly.","\"I can open a gate to this world that allows others to enter from anywhere in the universe? Is a Legendary Grade item truly this powerful?\"","*","A/N: I'm implementing more time skips and will continue in future chapters. Please let me know if the pace becomes an issue. Thank you for reading today's Chapters. 11|06|2026."]},{"number":1047,"title":"Chapter 1047 Surprise [1]","paragraphs":["\"I can open a gate to this world that allows others to enter from anywhere in the universe? Is a Legendary Grade item truly this powerful?\"","The more information he received, the more ridiculous the Mausoleum seemed.","Previously, entering and leaving had only been possible for him and those directly stored within the treasure.","Now things were different.","As long as he supplied sufficient energy and possessed a coordinate to lock onto, the Mausoleum could open temporary gates.","Michael took a deep breath. Then a thought suddenly appeared in his mind.","\"If that's the case...\"","His gaze became strange, and immediately he left the Mausoleum world.","Meanwhile, Michael's original body in Aurora suddenly opened its eyes.","Back in his room in Brightgate, Michael stood up from his bed. The room was empty and Jester was nowhere nearby.","In fact, he was the only one at home at the moment. Aunt Mia had gone to work while Jester and Lily had resumed school.","Knowing no one was home, Michael stretched out his hand. His consciousness connected with the miniature Mausoleum sleeping within his soul, then he activated the treasure.","Hum.","Mana flooded from his body. At the same time, the space before him distorted. Silver-black ripples spread through the air. Then a crack appeared.","The crack rapidly expanded. Soon, a circular portal over three meters tall formed in the middle of the room.","Beyond it was not darkness, nor was it empty space. Instead, Michael saw the familiar silver sky of the Mausoleum.","Michael's eyes lit up. \"It actually worked.\"","For several moments, he simply stared at the gate. Then he stepped forward. One foot entered. Then the other. The next moment, his body vanished from Aurora and appeared inside the Mausoleum.","There was no transfer delay, no discomfort, no instability. It was as smooth as walking through a doorway.","Michael immediately turned around. The portal still existed. And on the other side, he could clearly see his room in Aurora.","His heartbeat sped up. The implications of this were enormous. Though the cost of creating a portal was significant, Michael felt he could still manage two more before being completely drained.","With an ability like this, if the information the Legendary item had given him was accurate, it was potentially possible for him to travel from one continent to another within Aurora.","If nothing else, it could also serve as a means of escape should the need ever arise.","Though he had not tested it yet, he could already sense that linking two portals together was possible.","Thinking of even more possibilities, Michael felt a growing excitement.","Perhaps a day might come when an entire undead legion could walk through a gate and appear anywhere he desired.","Suddenly, Michael seemed to think of something. His eyes lit up.","Back in the Land of Origin, Michael sat atop a rocky outcrop within a remote forest. The moment the thought of his other body crossed his mind, he immediately stood up.","\"No way...\"","His heartbeat quickened. The body in the Land of Origin stretched out a hand.","Hum.","Silver-black mana gathered. Space distorted. Soon, another portal appeared before him.","Michael's eyes widened. \"It works.\"","Since this body was essentially a reflection of the original, it possessed access to many of the same functions, including the ability to open portals.","This body could also only create two more portals before exhausting itself completely. However, that was not what had excited Michael.","At that moment, both Michaels stared at each other through the portal. One stood in the Mausoleum world.","The other stood in the Land of Origin. Two different worlds. Two different universes. Connected by a single doorway.","Silence fell.","Then both Michaels spoke at the same time. \"...No way.\"","The next second, the Michael standing in the Land of Origin stepped forward. One foot crossed the threshold. The portal rippled. And suddenly, he appeared inside the Mausoleum world.","The two Michaels now stood face to face.","For several seconds, both simply stared at each other.","Then Michael slowly raised a hand. The other Michael raised a hand as well. Their palms met. It was Solid. It was Real.","A strange expression appeared on Michael's face.","Thanks to the mysterious Land of Origin, the body that had always been there was simply another version of himself.","However, it was only now that they stood side by side that he realized something. Though they were the same, they were also not entirely the same.","For a long moment, neither Michael spoke. They simply stood there, staring at one another.","The resemblance was perfect. The same face. The same height. The same eyes. The same soul. Yet the feeling they gave off was completely different.","It was only now, standing side by side, that Michael truly noticed it.","The Michael of Aurora looked younger. Not physically, but mentally. His posture was more relaxed. His expressions came easier. There was a casualness to the way he stood.","To the outside world, he was merely a student, an exceptionally talented student with a bright future. He still possessed traces of the old Michael.","The other Michael was different.","The Michael from the Land of Origin stood straighter. His movements were calmer, measured, and deliberate. There was a natural authority in the way he carried himself. His gaze seemed deeper and colder, not because he lacked emotions, but because he had spent considerable time being treated as someone of status.","Countless people bowed when they saw him. Officials addressed him with respect. Powerhouses treated him as an equal.","Whether he liked it or not, the Land of Origin had slowly transformed him. He was no longer merely Michael. He was Lord Mic Nor. Master of Thornvale. Controller of the Black Serpent Empire.","The difference was subtle. Yet impossible to ignore.","\"...Interesting.\"","The Aurora Michael spoke first.","The Origin Michael nodded. \"Very.\"","For a moment they circled each other.","The scene would have looked incredibly strange to an outsider. Two identical men studying one another as if meeting for the first time.","_Drakon"]},{"number":1048,"title":"Chapter 1048: Surprise [2]","paragraphs":["Then Michael suddenly laughed. The other Michael laughed as well. Even their timing was identical.","\"I guess this is what happens when someone lives two completely different lives.\"","The Origin Michael nodded. Though they shared memories, each body experienced things the other did not.","Over time, tiny differences accumulated. Those differences eventually became habits. Those habits became temperament. And temperament became presence.","The Aurora Michael crossed his arms. \"If someone met us separately, they probably would not even realize we are the same person.\"","\"Most likely.\"","The Origin Michael glanced down at his own somewhat elegant dark robes, then toward the simple t-shirt and jeans worn by his counterpart.","The contrast alone was enough to tell a story. It was almost amusing. Despite being the same individual, their auras had diverged so much that they felt like twins raised in entirely different worlds.","Which, in a sense, they were.","Then suddenly both Michaels froze. A realization struck them simultaneously. Their eyes widened.","\"...Wait.\"","\"...No way.\"","The two spoke at the same time.","If the Mausoleum could connect both worlds, and if both bodies could physically exist in the same location, then theoretically... The Aurora Michael slowly turned toward his counterpart. The Origin Michael slowly turned toward him. Neither spoke for several seconds.","As they shared the same mind, neither needed to explain what the other was thinking. The moment the thought appeared in one mind, the other already knew.","Without another word, both turned and walked toward the portal leading back to Aurora. A moment later, they stepped through. The transition was smooth.","Nothing exploded. Nothing collapsed. No mysterious cosmic force appeared to stop them. The Michael from the Land of Origin had successfully entered Aurora.","For several seconds both stood inside the room as the Origin Michael looked around. Then he smiled.","\"If this is possible...\" His gaze softened slightly. \"...then we do not need to worry about being away from Aunt Mia and Lily anymore.\"","The Aurora Michael smiled as well. \"That is true.\"","No matter how important things became in the Land of Origin, part of Michael always remained worried about the people back in Aurora, and the same was true for the Michael already in Aurora.","It was unknown whether this came from ordinary familial love or from the experience of having nearly lost his family within a month of becoming a supernatural turning protection to excessive cautiousness.","Now that problem had greatly diminished.","The Origin Michael could return whenever he wished. Likewise, the Aurora Michael could visit whenever necessary. The pressure weighing on him suddenly felt much lighter.","Then the Origin Michael looked around the room. His expression changed. A look of dissatisfaction appeared on his face.","\"...Michael.\"","\"What?\"","\"Do you ever clean your room?\"","The original Michael froze. He suddenly felt an intense wave of disdain coming from his other self. His eyelid twitched.","\"What are you talking about? It is not even dirty.\"","The Origin Michael glanced at the desk. Then the chair. Then the pile of books. Then the clothes. His expression became even more judgmental.","The Aurora Michael became speechless. For some reason, he felt like he was being inspected by a noble visiting a peasant's quarters.","Since they shared the same mind, the Origin Michael naturally knew exactly what the other was thinking. He immediately became embarrassed. He coughed awkwardly.","Ignoring his counterpart's reaction, the original Michael dragged him back into the Mausoleum world.","As time passed, both took the opportunity to learn more about the abilities of the Legendary Grade item and what applications were most beneficial to them.","Time passed, and soon it was the morning of the next day.","Today was also the day Michael was required to be present at the academy.","After having breakfast with his family, Michael took his leave immediately.","Using Wisdom's spatial abilities, it did not take long to arrive at the academy's secret realm, where he made his way directly to Director Lin's office.","Fortunately she was in, and Michael did not need to search for another director to report to.","Director Lin looked up from the documents on her desk the moment Michael entered. A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"You are finally back.\"","Michael nodded. \"Director.\"","She gestured toward a seat. \"Sit.\"","Michael obeyed. For a moment, Director Lin studied him before speaking. \"How was your emergency?\"","Michael naturally understood what she was referring to. More than a week ago, he had abruptly left the anti-demonic operation after learning about Arianne's death.","Of course, there was no way he could explain the real reason.","\"It has been resolved,\" Michael replied calmly. \"Thank you for your understanding back then.\"","Director Lin shook her head. \"I did not help you. I simply gave you permission to do what you already intended to do.\"","Michael did not reply. Technically speaking, she was right. His thanks had mostly been intended to ease the atmosphere. So Michael simply smiled and let the matter drop.","Director Lin did not dwell on it either. Instead, her expression became serious. \"Now then. Let us talk about the operation. After all, that is the reason you were called back to the academy.\"","Michael straightened slightly.","Over the next several minutes, Director Lin summarized the aftermath of the Federation's widespread assault against the demonic supernaturals.","Most of what she said was information Teacher Brian had already shared during his visit, but there were also a few details Michael had not heard before.","Several neutral factions had apparently also secretly assisted once they realized how badly the demonic faction had been weakened.","To many forces throughout Aurora, the demonic faction had long been a dangerous pest that harmed everyone around them while benefiting only themselves.","In short, the demonic supernaturals had suffered heavily.","At one point, Director Lin looked directly at him. \"Although you did not personally participate in the operation, you were one of its largest contributors to its success.\"","Michael remained silent but listened attentively.","\"The information you provided regarding the hidden locations of the demonic faction saved countless lives. The operation would have looked very different without it.\"","Michael smiled modestly. \"I merely got lucky.\"","Director Lin snorted. \"Luck is also a form of strength.\"","Michael wisely decided not to argue.","Then finally, the words he had been waiting to hear arrived.","Director Lin opened a drawer and pulled out a document. \"We have finished processing your request.\"","Michael's eyes immediately sharpened. By request, he knew she was referring to his compensation.","Back when he had surrendered information regarding multiple hidden locations of the demonic faction, Michael had specifically requested payment in the form of access rights to as many dimensional cracks as could reasonably be opened to him.","Director Lin placed the document on the desk. \"Your request has been approved.\"","Michael's heartbeat sped up slightly.","Director Lin's smile widened. \"Not only approved.\" She slid the document toward him. \"The higher-ups were surprisingly generous this time.\"","Michael immediately picked it up."]},{"number":1049,"title":"Chapter 1049: Three Months Later, Changes [1]","paragraphs":["Michael immediately picked up the document.","The moment his eyes began scanning through the contents, his expression changed. Even Michael was genuinely surprised.","He had expected access to dimensional cracks before coming here, but what he had not expected was this level of generosity.","For one thing, Michael had completely overlooked the involvement of the other academies. When he originally negotiated compensation, he had only considered two parties.","The Federation and his own academy.","After all, he was not a student of the other academies. Why would they reward him?","From Michael's perspective, his relationship with the Federation was also somewhat awkward. It was not bad, but it definitely was not good enough for him to expect special treatment.","In fact, before arriving, Michael had mentally prepared himself to receive a handful of weak dimensional cracks as a symbolic payment. Perhaps five. At most ten.","As for the academy, he had expected better treatment from them, but they were still only a single organization. No matter how wealthy they were, their resources could not compare to the Federation that governed the entire Aurora Realm.","Yet reality completely exceeded his expectations.","As it turned out, the Federation had not handled the rewards alone. The ten great academies had also participated. Including his own academy, all ten top academies had contributed portions of their dimensional crack resources.","Naturally, the amount each academy contributed varied. The determining factor was how much Michael's intelligence had benefited them during the operation.","Some academies had received only limited benefit from his information while others had gained significantly.","Unsurprisingly, the four major awakening academies located within his own country contributed the most, given that the Rank 4 demonic supernatural had also been primarily stationed there.","Michael continued reading. The further he read, the brighter his eyes became.","Thirty-five. A total of thirty-five dimensional cracks.","Michael nearly laughed. Thirty-five!","More than half contained monsters below Rank 1. Around half of the remainder primarily contained Rank 1 creatures.","Only two dimensional cracks regularly produced Rank 2 monsters.","This distribution might have looked disappointing to some. After all, stronger dimensional cracks meant stronger resources, or more accurately in Michael's case, stronger monsters. But Michael's lips still curved upward.","What he needed was quantity. Evolution Points were all he cared about. A Rank 2 and above monster corpse was indeed valuable.","A single corpse could provide a large amount of Evolution Points. However, stronger dimensional cracks had a major weakness. Their regeneration speed was slow.","The weaker dimensional cracks were different. Their monster populations replenished at absurd rates.","To Michael, they were practically Evolution Point farms. In the long run, these weaker dimensional cracks were significantly more profitable.","Of course, that did not mean he disliked stronger dimensional cracks. In any case, the thirty-three weaker dimensional cracks alone were enough to make Michael extremely happy.","However, what the ten academies provided was not actually the largest portion of his reward. That honor belonged to the Federation itself.","When Michael reached the second section of the document, even he could not hide his surprise. His eyebrows rose.","Director Lin smiled when she saw his reaction. \"It seems you have reached the Federation's contribution.\"","Michael looked up. \"They gave this much?\"","Director Lin nodded. \"The Federation council personally approved it.\"","Michael lowered his gaze back to the document.","If the ten academies had jointly provided thirty-five dimensional cracks, then the Federation alone had contributed seventy more. Twice the amount. Seventy dimensional cracks.","Michael suddenly found the Federation looking much more pleasant than usual.","Like the academies, the majority were lower-ranked dimensional cracks. Most contained monsters below Rank 1. A significant portion contained Rank 1 monsters.","Several possessed Rank 2 monsters, and unlike the academies, the Federation had even included a handful capable of regularly producing Rank 3 creatures.","That alone made Michael's heart beat faster. Even if their numbers were small, their value was immense.","With a sufficient supply of Rank 3 monster corpses, he would be able to fill more than half his contract slots with stronger creatures, saving a considerable amount of Evolution Points.","One had to remember that Michael had swept the entire Everlong Forest clean of monsters.","Even the lowest level creatures that could be converted into undead had been cleared out, all so he could maximize his contract slots and increase his daily Evolution Point income.","Though it could not compare to his gains from the Black Serpent Empire, four thousand Evolution Points daily across three hundred and sixty-five days amounted to at least one million four hundred thousand points per year.","It was a modest amount relative to his needs, but the Federation and the ten academies had arrived just in time to solve that problem.","Adding everything together, thirty-five from the academies and seventy from the Federation gave a total of one hundred and five dimensional cracks.","Though it appeared everyone had agreed to lease him access for only three years, what Michael stood to gain from them within that period was well worth it.","As for the issue of distance, since many of these cracks were spread across different continents, this might have been a serious concern before he acquired his Legendary Grade item.","Now it was merely a minor inconvenience.","It seemed like the next few months were going to be extremely busy.","Michael continued reading through the document. The more he read, the more satisfied he became. One hundred and five dimensional cracks.","Even after confirming the total, Michael found himself repeatedly going over the list to make sure he had not missed anything.","Director Lin observed his expression and chuckled. \"It seems you are satisfied.\"","Michael nodded honestly. \"Very.\"","That was putting it mildly. This reward was several times better than anything he had originally expected.","Director Lin leaned back in her chair. \"Good. Then let us move on to the second matter.\"","Michael immediately looked up. The second matter?","Director Lin tapped a finger lightly against the desk. \"As discussed previously, after your advancement, the academy planned to send you outside Aurora for a mission.\"","Michael immediately remembered. Back then, Director Lin and the other academy leaders had decided that allowing him to remain in Aurora indefinitely was not a good idea.","Part of it was for training. Part of it was for experience. And another part was simply to let him disappear from everyone's sight for a while. After all, he had attracted far too much attention recently.","Michael nodded. \"I remember.\"","Director Lin smiled slightly. The smile told Michael she had never expected him to forget. The question had merely been part of the conversation.","\"Good.\" Her expression gradually became serious. \"The academy believes you should leave soon.\"","Michael raised an eyebrow. \"Soon?\"","Director Lin nodded. \"The sooner the better.\" She folded her hands together. \"Originally, we were willing to wait a little longer. However, several recent developments have changed our assessment.\"","Michael immediately became attentive.","Director Lin continued. \"Your advancement speed is too fast.\" Michael remained silent. Unfortunately, he could not argue against that.","\"At first, only a handful of people were paying attention to you. Now?\" Director Lin sighed. \"Far too many people know your name, even if you have kept to yourself for a while now.\"","She continued. \"Normally, this would not be a major problem. But recently, various factions have begun making questionable movements. We suspect some most likely have dealings with hostile realms and the demonic supernatural faction.\"","Director Lin did not dwell on that point and moved on. \"Fortunately, your contribution during the operation has given you considerable protection. It is invisible, but sometimes having more eyes on you can also act as a form of protection. Unfortunately, it has also made you even more visible. At this point I am simply repeating myself, but you should have understood this by now.\"","Michael sighed.","\"Therefore, the academy's recommendation remains unchanged. In fact, it has become stronger.\"","Director Lin's gaze settled on him. \"We believe you should leave Aurora as soon as possible. The longer you stay, the more difficult things may become.\"","Michael slowly nodded. That assessment actually matched his own thoughts.","Before obtaining the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, leaving Aurora had been somewhat inconvenient.","Now things were different. With the portal abilities of the Mausoleum and his connection to the Land of Origin, distance had become far less meaningful than before.","Director Lin naturally had no idea what Michael was thinking.","For the next hour the two continued speaking before coming to a conclusion that three months later Michael would leave aurora.","In fact, Director Lin had wanted him to leave earlier, a sentiment shared by the other directors as well. But to their surprise, Michael was stubborn on the matter.","Perhaps they would not understand him. All of them were old, and Michael, who still had genuine attachments to the material world and the people in it, could not simply depart on such a journey in haste.","Michael wanted to use the remaining time to properly set up bases on the continents where he would be operating, and at the same time he wanted to wait for his cousin's first awakening ceremony.","Though the Mausoleum gave him the ability to return at any time, not knowing what could happen once he was outside the realm, he saw no reason to rush."]},{"number":1050,"title":"Chapter 1050: Three months later, Changes [2]","paragraphs":["In the blink of an eye, three months passed.","In those three months, a great deal could be said to have happened, both in the real world and in Aurora.","For ordinary people, three months was not a particularly long period of time. For Michael, it was enough time to completely reshape an empire.","After the meeting with Director Lin, Michael had immediately thrown himself into preparations for his eventual departure from Aurora.","The academy had assumed his attention was primarily focused on the one hundred and five dimensional cracks. And to some extent, that was true, given that he had also taken visible action in relation to them.","However, the cracks were far from the only thing occupying Michael's attention. The Black Serpent Empire demanded his time as well.","Now, three months later, Michael could finally say something with confidence.","He had completely taken over the Black Serpent Empire.","Not just the imperial capital or the territories surrounding it. The entire empire and all thirty-three kingdoms beneath it now stood under his control.","The achievement was honestly absurd. If someone had told Michael a year ago that he would one day control an empire spanning thirty-three kingdoms, he would have assumed they were insane.","Even after taking over the imperial capital, the notion had seemed far-fetched. Something like that would not happen so quickly.","Historically, conquering an empire was one thing. Controlling it was something else entirely. Many powerful conquerors throughout history had managed the first while failing the second.","Yet somehow, in only three months, Michael had accomplished what should have taken years.","And the reason for that was surprisingly simple.","Jester.","As the most intelligent creature under his command, Jester had always occupied a special position. Whenever Michael encountered a difficult problem, he occasionally consulted the undead if it was nearby.","If it was not, then Spartan would be his next option, though the latter was mostly for magic-related questions thanks to that undead's unique inclinations.","Usually Jester would simply provide a precise answer. Straightforward. Efficient. Cold. It rarely involved itself beyond that.","It would provide a solution and then quietly return to whatever it had been doing before, unless told otherwise or specifically needed.","This time had been different. For the first time since becoming undead, Jester had actively requested involvement.","Michael had found the request strange, but over time he had learned to trust Jester's judgment.","Michael was a fairly self-aware person. In terms of combat ability, he could confidently say he was stronger than Jester.","But when it came to pure thinking, pure calculation, and pure strategy, Michael knew he was nowhere close.","Why this was the case, he did not fully know. The only explanation he could think of was Jester's nature. Even before becoming undead, the creature's intelligence had been terrifying.","Perhaps that was part of why the System had once described it as a Taboo. Months had passed since then, and Jester had grown even more formidable in that regard.","Exposure to humanity's accumulated knowledge had transformed Jester's already terrifying mind.","In those past months, Jester had been exposed to a vast library of information. With a simple search, it could find almost anything on the internet.","Thanks to this, Jester had somehow become even more terrifying, to the point where managing an empire no longer seemed impossible.","At the time of their first discussion on the matter, Michael had expected almost nothing. After all, what did he know about governing an empire?","In his previous life, he had not even reached his mid-twenties, and during most of that life, illness had restricted what he could do.","His current life was not much different in that regard. Though he possessed extraordinary power, that did not magically grant him centuries of political experience.","Running Thornvale had been manageable. It was small. The problems were limited. The scale was understandable.","The Black Serpent Empire was different. An empire spanning thirty-three kingdoms was not something one could manage through instinct alone. At least not successfully.","Yet Jester had somehow made it possible.","The undead had created administrative structures. Reorganized supply chains. Identified corrupt officials. Mapped influence networks.","Created methods to monitor governors. Predicted rebellions before they happened. Calculated tax reforms. Optimized military deployment.","The terrifying part was that the undead never needed rest, working day and night without pause.","It had not even asked for Michael's direct assistance, only requesting the loan of a thousand undead and two Rank 4 undead to support its operations.","The results spoke for themselves. Several kingdoms that had originally opposed imperial authority voluntarily submitted after realizing resistance no longer benefited them.","Even the imperial treasury had grown healthier. When Michael reviewed the weekly reports, he occasionally felt as though he was reading fiction. Yet every number was real and every improvement could be verified.","Three months later, the Black Serpent Empire was stronger than it had been at the time of its conquest.","Michael knew exactly who deserved most of the credit.","Though he understood this was only possible thanks to a degree of bloodshed, Michael accepted it. As he had done in the capital, he gave everyone the chance to live if they surrendered, and those who did not could expect no mercy.","Of course, so he could sleep at night, Michael had made sure Jester understood this clearly and could not twist the words to find a loophole.","However, knowing that excessive kindness could read as weakness, he also gave Jester the freedom to read the minds of anyone troublesome among those who had resisted.","If it found them to be genuinely dangerous, it had permission to make an example of them.","For an action like that, Michael felt no guilt. He might have been kind-hearted by nature, but when his interests were touched, he knew what actions to take.","Thanks to Jester effectively managing things in the Land of Origin on his behalf, Michael's accumulated Evolution Points reached a new height.","In three months, from the kingdoms alone, he was able to increase his Evolution Points by another eight million."]},{"number":1051,"title":"Chapter 1051: Three Months later, Changes [3]","paragraphs":["Truly, plunder was the quickest path to wealth.","Only after indulging, cough, having no choice but to do it did Michael fully understand that saying.","As for where this profit came from, it naturally came from the thirty-three kingdoms under the empire's control, each contributing twenty percent of their resources to their new ruler, an arrangement that would continue for years to come.","At first, Michael had not wanted to become that sort of ruler. Twenty percent of the resources produced by thirty-three kingdoms was not a small amount by any standard.","Even after taking control of the Black Serpent Empire, he had felt uncomfortable with the idea. In his mind, the kingdoms had already suffered enough through the war and the sudden change in leadership.","However, Jester's reasoning had been extremely simple.","The empire had only been conquered three months ago. That was not enough time for genuine loyalty to form. At present, the kingdoms obeyed because they had no choice.","Given the opportunity, many would immediately begin rebuilding their strength. That was simply how conquered territories behaved.","According to Jester, the most dangerous period for any new ruler was not during the invasion itself. It was the years immediately afterward. History had proven this countless times.","New conquering powers almost always followed the same pattern.","First came conquest, the violent seizure of land and the breaking of existing power structures.","Then came consolidation, the elimination of remaining resistance and the installation of loyal figures in key positions.","Then came control, the gradual tightening of administrative, economic, and military authority over the occupied territory.","Only after enough years passed, and enough generations grew up knowing nothing different, did true stability finally emerge.","The kingdoms currently possessed their own armies, noble families, influence networks, wealth, and administrative structures.","If allowed to retain all of that strength, they would inevitably begin viewing themselves as separate powers. The result would be future rebellions, future wars, or future instability.","Therefore, before stability could be achieved, control needed to be established first.","The twenty percent resource contribution was not primarily about wealth. The imperial treasury certainly benefited from it, but that was not its main purpose. Its true purpose was control.","By drawing resources toward the imperial center, the growth of the kingdoms slowed while the growth of the empire accelerated. The difference might seem small in a single year.","Over several years, however, it became enormous. The kingdoms would gradually become weaker relative to the imperial capital. Meanwhile, the imperial capital would become stronger relative to the kingdoms.","Eventually, a point would be reached where resisting the empire would no longer be realistic. Once that happened, separation became increasingly difficult.","A kingdom could not simply rebel without damaging its own economy, security, and political stability.","According to Jester, this was how nearly every successful conquering power throughout history had operated.","The difference was that most people only remembered the final result. They remembered the prosperous empire decades later. They forgot the years of harsh control that came before it.","Ironically, becoming a tyrant was easiest at the beginning.","Immediately after conquest, fear still existed. Military superiority still existed.","As time passed, however, that window disappeared. New generations were born. Memories faded. Local powers recovered. Influence shifted. By then, attempting to impose the same level of control would become far more difficult.","That was why Jester had insisted the current period was unique. The empire possessed a window of opportunity. A temporary period where it could reshape the foundation of all thirty-three kingdoms.","If that opportunity was missed, the cost of achieving the same result later would multiply many times over.","Three months later, Michael could already see signs of the process working. The kingdoms were becoming increasingly tied to the empire. And while some might call the policy harsh, the results were undeniable.","For the first time in decades, the Black Serpent Empire was beginning to function as a single entity rather than thirty-three kingdoms loosely gathered beneath a crown.","Like before, Michael had no intention of ruling the empire personally as some grand emperor. That had never been his goal.","Even now, after completely taking over the Black Serpent Empire, his interest in governance remained limited at best.","However, not wanting to rule and not wanting to control were two completely different things.","Michael had no intention whatsoever of relinquishing his control over the empire. After all, this was currently his greatest source of Evolution Points.","The one hundred and five dimensional cracks in Aurora were valuable, but their access rights only lasted three years. Three years later, they would return to their original owners.","The empire was different. As long as he wished, it would remain under his control indefinitely.","One was temporary. The other was long-term. One generated profits for a few years. The other could continue generating profits for decades. The difference was obvious.","Because of this, Michael was willing to tolerate certain things he normally disliked.","The empire was an investment.","An investment capable of continuously generating resources, wealth, influence, manpower, intelligence, and Evolution Points.","The returns were simply too great to ignore.","Naturally, Jester understood this as well. In fact, the undead had gone a step further.","According to Jester, if the empire was truly going to become Michael's long-term foundation, then it needed to stop being associated with the previous ruling family.","The Black Serpent Empire represented the old regime. Its history. Its loyalties. Its symbols. Its identity. Leaving those things untouched would only encourage people to continue viewing the empire through the lens of the past.","That was undesirable.","Therefore, one of Jester's earliest recommendations had been a complete rebranding of the empire itself.","The proposal was simple. Erase the old symbol. Create a new one. Replace the identity people served. Over time, memories of the Black Serpent Empire would fade.","In its place, a new state would emerge. One built around Michael's authority rather than the authority of the previous dynasty.","The proposal had eventually been approved.","Three months later, the Black Serpent Empire had ceased to exist.","In its place stood a new power.","The Eternal Crown Empire."]},{"number":1052,"title":"Chapter 1052: Three Months Later, Changes [4]","paragraphs":["Unfortunately for Michael, even after controlling the empire there was no progress on his rank advancement quest. He had expected this, but it did not stop him from feeling disappointed.","However, since it had only been three months since his quest started, though anxious, Michael could only keep his calm.","At least compared to his other ongoing tasks, his goal of having thousands of Rank 4 undead was drawing closer.","The Eternal Crown Empire was not Michael's only source of growth during those three months. The one hundred and five dimensional cracks in Aurora had also begun producing results.","When Michael first received access to them, he had performed several rough calculations. The final number had honestly shocked even him.","If he completely sacrificed every monster killed across all one hundred and five dimensional cracks and converted every corpse into Evolution Points, the amount he could obtain each month would easily exceed ten million Evolution Points.","Just thinking about it felt absurd. Only a few months ago, fifty million Evolution Points had been one of Michael's greatest concerns. Now he could earn that amount in less than five months.","Unfortunately, reality was not quite that simple. Michael quickly realized there was a problem.","Attention.","Going by his initial plan would draw attention. Being a Necromancer meant needing corpses was normal. Nobody would find that suspicious.","A few thousand corpses? Normal. A few tens of thousands? Still understandable. Hundreds of thousands? Questions would begin appearing. Millions? People would inevitably start investigating.","Michael reached that conclusion shortly after his meeting with Director Lin three months ago. The issue was not merely the corpses themselves. It was the scale. At some point, the number became abnormal even for a Necromancer.","More importantly, pursuing his original plan also carried another risk of exposing the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion.","The more dimensional cracks he personally managed, the more frequently he would need to move resources across continents, and the greater the chance of revealing abilities he had no intention of exposing.","After careful consideration, Michael altered his plans. He did not abandon the dimensional cracks. Instead, he changed his priorities.","Rather than pursuing one hundred percent Evolution Point profit, he shifted toward a seventy-thirty split. Seventy percent wealth. Thirty percent Evolution Points.","Even with this adjustment, the results remained incredible. He was still capable of generating over one million Evolution Points every month.","Out of the one hundred and five dimensional cracks, Michael only retained direct control over roughly twenty-five. The remaining eighty were returned to their original organizations. Of course, not for free.","Instead, Michael negotiated profit-sharing agreements. The academies and various organizations regained operational control while Michael retained a percentage of the benefits generated from those dimensional cracks.","The arrangement worked perfectly for both sides. The organizations recovered valuable resources. Michael avoided attracting excessive attention. And everyone made money.","In fact, several powers seemed almost relieved when Michael proposed the arrangement.","They had already suspected he would not personally manage all one hundred and five dimensional cracks forever. The logistical burden alone would have been ridiculous.","As a result, negotiations proceeded far more smoothly than expected. Using the academy as an intermediary, Michael spent weeks meeting representatives from various organizations. The final agreements were surprisingly generous.","By the time everything concluded, Michael had secured a massive advance payment covering the next three years of projected profits. The amount was enough to leave even him speechless.","Twenty billion dollars. Raw liquid assets. Not resources. Not land. Not investments. Actual money.","Of course, this was after a thirty percent tax, something that still made his teeth ache every other night.","In any case, not only had Michael become wealthy in the Land of Origin. Now he was just as wealthy in Aurora.","Of course, wealth itself was not what interested him most. What truly mattered was what that wealth could become. Everything ultimately led back to strength.","Using the massive amount of Evolution Points he had accumulated over those few months, Michael finally accomplished part of the all-strong undead goal he had set for himself.","Right now, Michael had a thousand Rank 4 undead.","As for the rest of his legion, none remained below Rank 3. Every single contracted undead under Michael's command had reached at least Rank 3.","The resources consumed during the process were enough to make him feel genuine pain. Yet Michael never regretted it.","After all, every advancement generated feedback, and a thousand Rank 4 undead produced an amount of feedback that could only be described as monstrous.","Of course, the more undead that advanced, the less significant the individual gains became. That was simply how the system worked.","Otherwise Michael would have become invincible long ago. Even so, the accumulated benefits from a thousand Rank 4 undead were still enormous.","His physical strength increased. His vitality increased. His soul strengthened, granting him even a few more contract slots. His mana reserves expanded. His perception sharpened. Every aspect of him experienced meaningful growth.","The result left Michael with rather mixed feelings.","Objectively speaking, he was strong. Without using magic, he was now capable of suppressing Lily in direct combat. Unfortunately, though he was powerful, he was ultimately not a true Rank 4.","Rank 4 was the realm where one's understanding of existence began affecting reality itself. Every true Rank 4 possessed a Law Domain, which Michael lacked.","Without one, Michael often felt like a counterfeit. A fake Rank 4. A brute carrying enough power to challenge genuine Rank 4 existences while lacking the foundation that made them truly terrifying.","It was similar to a child carrying a legendary sword. The weapon was real. The power was real. But the person wielding it had not fully grown into it.","Of course, this was only Michael's own assessment. If a normal Rank 4 heard him describe himself that way, they would probably spit blood from anger.","After all, most Rank 4 existences spent decades accumulating power. Michael had accomplished what many of them could not in only a year.","These three months could be said to be the most progressive in Michael's career.","Aside from his gains, there were also a few changes in his interpersonal life.","For one, Arianne had woken up a month ago, but there was a problem.","A problem appearing was not something that surprised Michael. It was the kind of problem that appeared that caught him off guard.","Following her awakening was something Michael had not expected to see. A status panel.","Yes. Arianne somehow had a status panel, something that only awakeners or things directly related to them could possess.","Though taken aback, Michael immediately understood what had happened.","It was simple. It was because Arianne now resided in a body that had once been his clone.","In reality it was technically still his clone, and Arianne could be said to be an external consciousness of his.","Because of this complex yet intimate connection to his existence, she who was tagged as his clone now had a status panel.","Knock knock.","Michael, who was currently in one of the villas he owned in the royal capital that had belonged to the previous royal family, heard a knock on the office door.","With his senses he immediately knew who it was, making him draw a quiet breath.","\"Come in.\"","A second later, the door opened with a soft click and a figure entered the room.","The person who stepped inside appeared to be a young woman in her late teens or perhaps early twenties. Seeing her, the first thing most people would notice was her hair.","Golden. Not merely blonde, but a rich golden color that seemed to shimmer beneath the light. Yet scattered throughout those golden strands were streaks of black.","The black was not overwhelming. It appeared only in certain places, weaving naturally through the golden hair and creating a strange beauty that made it difficult to look away.","The next thing that attracted attention were her eyes. Bright emerald-green eyes. They seemed almost luminous, as though faint light existed within them.","Combined with her pale skin and delicate features, the result was breathtaking.","She was also surprisingly tall. Not as tall as Michael, but taller than most women.","And unlike before, Michael's gaze unconsciously drifted downward for a brief moment. Then he immediately coughed.","\"Ahem.\"","A faint trace of embarrassment appeared on his face. This was something the previous Arianne had lacked before he reconstructed her body.","Every single time he noticed it, Michael silently swore to himself that he was not some kind of pervert. Absolutely not. Unfortunately, his conscience seemed unconvinced.","The young woman stopped before his desk. Her glowing green eyes landed on him.","\"...\"","\"...\"","For several seconds neither spoke. Then Arianne's gaze slowly shifted downward. Toward the documents in front of him. Then toward the tea beside him. Then toward the half-finished reports stacked on another table.","Finally, she looked back at him.","\"Busy?\"","Michael immediately felt a slight headache.","Ever since waking up a month ago, Arianne had changed. Not dramatically. She was still Arianne. Yet there was something different about her now.","Perhaps it was because of her unusual circumstances. Perhaps it was because she had literally died once. Or perhaps it was because she now possessed a status panel.","Whatever the reason, she seemed...clingy.","It was only noon and this was the sixth time since daybreak that she had come to his office."]},{"number":1053,"title":"Chapter 1053: Three Months Later, Changes [5]","paragraphs":["As for why this was the case, Michael did not have a firm answer. It was not like he could just ask Arianne directly.","He had a few guesses, however.","One of them was that it was probably related to her recent death. During the time when Michael and Jester had been sorting through her memories, even without deliberate intention on his part, Michael had still come to know fragments of Arianne's memory, with her last memory, the memory of her death, being the most recent and vivid.","Though he could not feel her pain, Michael had seen it clearly. Her head had been slowly cut off while she was still alive.","It did not matter how strong one was. Michael dared to say that even a true divine being would hate such a death, let alone a relatively gentle girl like Arianne.","As for why the manner of her death would be a reason for her clinginess toward him, Michael figured it had to do with him being the reason she was alive again. Perhaps he provided her with a powerful sense of security, making her want to be close to him most of the time.","Another reason he had in mind was probably the more intimate connection they now shared through one body.","Thanks to her identity as a distinct consciousness, Michael could not see her as family in the traditional sense, yet the bond of blood was still there in its own way.","Perhaps combined with the former reason, it caused Arianne to feel a need for a certain level of closeness in order to feel at ease.","Did Michael hate this? At first it could not be said he was fully comfortable with it, but after several days of adjusting, Michael found himself even.... liking it.","Knowing what was about to come, Michael straightened slightly and directed his gaze toward Arianne's shadow.","\"Fade.\"","The moment his voice sounded, the shadow beneath Arianne's feet rippled. Arianne did not react. She was already used to it.","The darkness stretched outward before slowly rising from the floor. Then a figure stepped out.","The newcomer appeared to be a man in his late twenties. Extremely handsome. Even Michael had to admit that if looks alone were considered, Fade could probably make a living doing absolutely nothing.","His features were sharp and refined. His black hair was neatly combed. His posture was perfect. Dressed in a dark suit tailored to fit his body, he looked less like an undead assassin and more like the personal secretary of some wealthy noble.","The moment he emerged, he bowed respectfully. \"My Lord.\"","Three months ago, Fade had still been a Rank 3 undead. Now, thanks to Michael's abundance of Evolution Points and his increasingly formidable resources, the undead assassin had successfully entered Rank 4.","Not that Fade was unique in this regard anymore. Among Michael's legion, Rank 4 undead had become increasingly common.","Still, Fade remained one of the undead Michael trusted most. His stealth abilities were terrifying. His assassination capabilities were even more so.","Even among Michael's thousand Rank 4 undead, Fade was unquestionably near the top.","As for why such an undead was currently hiding inside Arianne's shadow, the answer was simple. Michael had too many powerful undead.","Even after assigning duties throughout the Eternal Crown Empire, countless powerful undead remained with little to do.","Occasionally, Michael assigned tasks based entirely on mood.","Fade had simply been unlucky enough to be selected this week, or perhaps lucky, depending on one's perspective, to be assigned as Arianne's personal guard.","Fade straightened. His expression remained perfectly calm. \"My Lord called for me?\"","Michael nodded. \"Please excuse us for a moment.\"","The undead bowed and obeyed without hesitation. As for why this particular order had been given six times today, an undead like Jester might have been curious, but Fade saw nothing unusual in it. It was simply an order.","The moment Fade received the command, he bowed once more. \"As you command, my Lord.\"","His body dissolved into darkness. A second later, the office became quiet.","The silence lingered for several moments. Arianne stood where she was, her fingers nervously clasped together behind her back. Without Fade present, the confidence she had displayed earlier seemed to disappear almost immediately.","Michael felt a familiar sense of helplessness.","What was about to happen was another strange development that had emerged over the past two months.","The young woman slowly approached his desk. Step. Step. Step.","Michael watched her draw closer. Then, without a word, he pushed his chair slightly backward. The movement was so natural that even Michael did not realize when it had become a habit.","Arianne's eyes brightened slightly. Moments later she reached him. There was a brief pause. Then she carefully sat down.","Not on another chair. Not across from him. Directly on his lap.","Michael maintained an expressionless face. At least outwardly. Internally was a completely different matter. His heart immediately became somewhat restless.","Arianne, meanwhile, seemed completely satisfied. She adjusted herself slightly before leaning forward and resting her head against his shoulder. The familiar scent of flowers reached him.","For a few moments neither spoke. The office fell into silence once more.","Surprisingly, it was not an uncomfortable silence. In fact, it had become increasingly common over the past month.","When Arianne first woke up, Michael had been awkward. Extremely awkward. After all, before her death, their relationship had been relatively ambiguous, but now it was increasingly approaching a clear direction, largely thanks to the girl's own active choices.","•","As I watched the prince of the empire slowly cut off my head while rage and satisfaction filled his face, I fell into darkness.","For some reason, I knew exactly what had happened. I was dead. There was no confusion or denial. There was no desperate attempt to convince myself otherwise. I simply knew.","The strange thing was that I could still think. I could not feel my body. I could not move. I could not see. I could not hear. Yet my thoughts remained.","At first, I wondered if this was what death felt like. An endless darkness where only the mind remained. It was not painful. It was not peaceful either.","In that darkness, there were only two people I found myself thinking about.","The first was my father.","I wondered what he would do after learning I was dead. Would he be angry? Would he be sad? Would he blame himself?","I did not know. For all his flaws, he had always cared for me. Perhaps too much. Perhaps not enough. I honestly did not know anymore.","I only hoped my death would calm things down. I hoped the old man would survive. He had already sacrificed enough. There was no reason for him to throw away his life because of me.","The second person I thought of was Michael.","Even now, thinking back, I find it somewhat embarrassing.","In my eighteen years of life, I had never truly believed in love. Not really. As a noble daughter, reality had been made very clear to me from a young age. Love stories existed in books and plays. Reality was different.","It was filled with contracts, alliances, and family interests. Reality gave me the prospect of marriage between noble houses. I had always assumed my future would follow the same path.","Perhaps I would marry some noble heir. Perhaps we would eventually grow to care for each other. Perhaps not. That was simply how things worked.","Then Michael appeared.","Looking back now, I still do not know exactly when it started. Maybe it was the first time we spoke. Maybe it was later. Maybe it happened so gradually that I never noticed.","He was handsome. That much was obvious. He was also young and strong. Ridiculously strong. Yet despite all that, what I remembered most was something else.","He was awkward. Sometimes unbelievably awkward. There were moments when speaking to him felt like speaking to someone who had never learned how normal conversations worked.","And somehow, I liked that.","He made me laugh. He made me curious. He made me want to know more. For the first time in my life, I found myself genuinely interested in someone.","But the realization that came after had been frightening. Because the more I learned about him, the more I felt I did not deserve him.","Michael always seemed to be moving forward. Always growing stronger. Compared to him, I felt ordinary. Small. Insignificant.","Even so, I still found myself wanting to stay near him.","In those final moments before darkness completely consumed me, my thoughts drifted toward him again. I hoped he escaped. I hoped he survived. I hoped he ran as far away from the empire as possible.","I knew he was strong. Stronger than most people could imagine. But the empire was the empire. One person could not fight an entire nation. At least that was what I believed back then.","So I prayed. Not for myself. Not for my future. Not even for revenge.","I simply hoped he would live.","With that final thought, my consciousness slowly sank deeper into the darkness. And eventually, even my thoughts disappeared. The world became silent.","And I slept.","What I did not expect was i would see the light of day again."]},{"number":1054,"title":"Chapter 1054: Confession [1]","paragraphs":["At first, I thought I was dreaming. After all, dead people were supposed to stay dead. That was common sense.","Yet after what felt like an eternity of darkness, I suddenly became aware of my surroundings. What came first was sensation. I felt weak, numb, strange, as though my body did not belong to me and I could only think.","The process was painfully slow, but eventually, I managed to open my eyes. My thoughts felt sluggish. The first thing that greeted me was an unfamiliar ceiling, unfamiliar yet strangely familiar at the same time.","I had never been here before. I was certain of that much, since most ceilings in the capital were very high up, and this one was much lower than any I was used to. However, the style reminded me of someone. It reminded me of Sir Mic... Click. Suddenly, the sound of a door opening echoed. I tried turning my head, but the effort felt enormous.","Footsteps entered the room. I wondered who it could be. A servant, or someone from the empire? The thought made my heart tighten.","Then the figure stepped into view, and I froze.","\"...Father?\"","The words barely escaped my lips.","For a moment, he simply stood there, staring. His eyes widened, and his body trembled. The expression on his face was one I had never seen before, shock, disbelief, hope, and fear, all mixed together.","Then suddenly, tears appeared, and my father rushed forward. The powerful man who had faced countless dangers throughout his life grabbed my hand tightly.","\"Arianne.\" His voice cracked. \"Arianne...\"","He kept repeating my name, over and over again, as though afraid I would disappear if he stopped.","\"You're awake.\" His grip tightened. \"You're finally awake. I'm glad. I'm so glad.\"","Seeing him like that made something inside me break. I had never seen my father cry before, yet now he sat beside me crying like a child. Somehow, that made me want to cry too.","I could not understand anything. I was confused, terrified, overwhelmed.","Was I not supposed to be dead?","The memory of my execution was still clear. I remembered all of it.","So why was I here? Why was I alive?","For a long time, neither of us spoke properly. My father seemed unable to stop looking at me, as though he was worried that if he blinked, I would disappear again.","Eventually, after calming down slightly, he began explaining things, and the more he spoke, the more unbelievable everything became.","Sir Mic had not only killed members of the royal family related to my death, but he had dared to even touch an imperial prince, and succeeded to the extent that the empire itself no longer existed. The Black Serpent Empire had fallen.","At first, I thought I was still dreaming, because none of it made sense. However, as days passed, I came to accept my new reality, even though so many things had changed.","Thanks to Sir Mic, my death was avenged, and not only was I brought back to life, I was even given a stronger body. Damn, I don't even have a bit of my foundation yet, but I can cast spells better than I could before.","Also, what was this \"status\" thing that appeared after I followed my father on a hunt a few days ago? Unfortunately, just like me, my old man had no idea, but fortunately, the only man who could answer all my questions soon appeared.","It had been only a few months since I last spoke with him, though for me, it felt like only a few days had passed. But seeing how he seemed to have grown even stronger, I realized it truly had been a while since we'd last seen each other.","When I saw him again after so long, I saw an intense look of emotion flash across Sir Mic's expression. It was so brief that I thought it might have been an illusion, but I knew I wasn't wrong.","Seeing how he looked at me with a different gaze than before, I remembered the words my father had told me days ago on our short hunt.","Yes, Sir Mic was incredibly powerful and very unique. Normally, I didn't deserve to stand at his side, but even though he didn't need to, he still brought me back to life.","I might be ignorant of high tier magic, but I knew the cost of my revival couldn't have been cheap, yet Sir Mic had sacrificed for me anyway.","Could it be he saw me as more than just a friend? Maybe not in the same way I viewed him, but surely a little more special, right?","I don't know if it's because I died once, or because I owe him my life, but whatever the reason, it made my emotions even more intense, and I got bolder. That night when he arrived, I kissed him.","I can still remember the look of surprise and shock on his face. *Given how awkward the kiss had been, was it possible this was his first kiss too?* I don't know why, but the thought of that made me want more. I wanted to be more of his firsts.","I really didn't know where my audacity came from, but I got bolder each day that passed without him stopping me. *Was it that I needed to die for Sir Mic to like me?* In any case, after spending a while in Thorbvale and telling my father goodbye, I followed Sir Mic to the empire.","Though I could see some traces of damage around, it didn't stop me from seeing the prosperity of the empire city. It was really memorable.","Since then, it's been more than a month since Sir Mic and I got here. As I lay on his chest, listening to his powerful heartbeat and breathing in his strong scent that almost made me moan in comfort, I heard his youthful deep voice echo near my ear.","\"Arianne, I have something to say to you. Something to show you.\"","*","Feeling the soft warmth of the young woman resting against him, Michael found himself enjoying the moment.","However, as the days passed and moments like this became increasingly common, another feeling began growing within him.","Guilt.","At first it had been small, easy to ignore and push aside. But now it had become impossible to escape, a quiet weight that pressed harder with every passing day.","Arianne seemed blissfully unaware of it, but Michael felt as though he was standing at the edge of a cliff. Every day that passed like this felt like another step closer to the fall, and he had no idea how to stop walking.","All of this stemmed from a question he could not answer.","Did Arianne like Michael?","Or did she like Mic Nor?","The question haunted him, returning every time her gaze met his, every time she smiled at him.","Mic Nor was the person she knew. The one she had developed feelings for, the one she trusted enough to fall asleep against. The problem was that Mic Nor was not entirely him. Or perhaps the problem was that Mic Nor was him but his profile here wasn't.","Michael no longer knew.","All he knew was that even though he remained the same person beneath it all, despite the minor differences, when Arianne looked at him, who exactly was she seeing?","Michael?","Or Lord Mic Nor?","And if she ever learned the truth, would anything of what they had remain standing? Or would it all collapse the moment the mask came off?","The thought made his chest tighten.","Michael felt genuinely afraid, and he didn't fully understand why this particular fear cut so deep each time it surfaced. He didn't like the possibility that the feelings currently directed toward him might vanish the instant she learned the truth.","It felt selfish. Pathetic, even.","Yet Michael could not deny it.","He enjoyed this.","He enjoyed her presence.","He enjoyed her smile.","He enjoyed the quiet trust she placed in him without hesitation.","Most importantly, he enjoyed being loved.","Was it because this was a first for him, in both lives? He didn't know.","But a problem remained, and it was that he selfishly wanted that love directed toward Michael. Not the mask. Him.","He wanted her to choose that version of him.","The real one.","As these thoughts ran through his mind, he felt Arianne shift slightly against him. Her head remained resting against his chest, steady and unguarded. The familiar scent of flowers drifted into the air between them, soft and warm and achingly normal.","For a few moments he remained silent, gathering whatever courage he had.","Then he finally made a decision.","A difficult one. But necessary.","If he continued avoiding it, things would only grow worse later","\"Arianne.\"","His voice was soft.","\"Hm?\"","She tilted her head slightly, eyes still half lidded with comfort.","\"Arianne... I have something to tell you.\""]},{"number":1055,"title":"Chapter 1055: Confession [2]","paragraphs":["\"I think it might be better to show you.\"","Arianne blinked in confusion.","Show her? What exactly needed to be shown instead of explained?","Still, the look on Sir Mic's face made her swallow the questions that immediately rose to her lips. For the first time since she had met him, she saw a deep conflict in his eyes.","\"Sir Mic?\"","She reached out and touched his arm.","\"Are you okay?\"","No reply came immediately. Instead, he slowly stood up and helped her to her feet.","The entire time, his expression remained unusually serious, causing Arianne's heart to beat faster. Did something happen? Was it because of her?","A hundred thoughts flashed through her mind.","Without answering, Michael guided her toward the open section of the office. Then he raised a hand.","Space distorted.","A circular gate appeared before them. It rapidly expanded until it became large enough for a person to walk through.","Beyond it lay a forest. Not one Arianne recognized. Towering trees stretched toward the heavens while faint green mist drifted between their trunks.","\"Go inside,\" Michael said.","Arianne turned toward him.","\"What?\"","\"Walk straight ahead.\" His voice remained calm. \"It's safe.\"","Honestly, safety was not what worried her. What worried her was him. Something was clearly bothering him.","Still, after a brief hesitation, she nodded. If he wanted to show her something, then she would trust him.","Arianne stepped through the portal.","The moment she crossed over, the first thing she noticed was the air. It felt different. Cleaner. Fresher. Every breath felt strangely refreshing.","Then she looked upward.","Her steps faltered.","The sky.","The sky was unlike anything she had ever seen. Green. Purple. Countless colors blended together above her.","Beautiful. Yet slightly eerie. It felt like standing beneath the heavens of another world.","For several moments, Arianne simply stared. Then she remembered Michael's instructions.","Walk straight ahead.","So she did.","The forest was quiet. Only the sound of her footsteps accompanied her. Occasionally, strange lights drifted between the trees like wandering spirits.","Eventually, the forest began to thin. A few minutes later, she arrived at a cliff.","And there, standing near the edge, was a figure. His back faced her. For some reason, the silhouette looked familiar. Very familiar.","Arianne frowned.","Why? The height. The posture. The build. Something about him reminded her of someone.","As though sensing her presence, the figure slowly turned around.","The moment he did, Arianne froze. Her eyes widened. Her thoughts stopped.","Because standing there was Sir Mic.","But that made no sense. Michael was supposed to be back in the office. So why was he standing here?","Arianne stared at the young man in disbelief. At first glance, there was no mistake. The face was the same. The eyes were the same.","Yet the longer she looked, the more she noticed things that felt different.","The most obvious difference was his clothing. Arianne had never seen anything like it before. Gone were the elegant robes and noble attire that Sir Mic usually wore. There were no embroidered patterns.","Instead, he wore a simple black shirt that fit closely against his upper body and a pair of dark blue trousers made from a material she could not identify.","The outfit looked incredibly plain. Yet somehow, it wasn't.","The strange clothes seemed designed with a completely different philosophy from anything she knew. There was no attempt to display wealth, authority, or power. Yet the more she looked at them, the more refined they seemed.","It was a simplicity that somehow felt elegant.","Arianne found herself unable to look away. If the nobles of the empire saw such clothing, they would probably dismiss it as commoner's attire. Yet she somehow felt they would all be wrong.","The style possessed a strange beauty. A beauty she could not explain.","It felt free.","Then there was the second difference.","Youth.","Sir Mic had always appeared young. But standing before her now, that youthful appearance seemed even more obvious. He suddenly looked closer to his actual age. Like a young man. Not some noble lord. Just a young man.","It made him seem more approachable, as the aura of mystery that constantly surrounded Sir Mic felt thinner here.","Arianne's confusion only deepened. This was undoubtedly Sir Mic. She could feel it. Yet at the same time, they felt different.","For several moments, neither of them spoke. The silence stretched between them.","Arianne looked at the young man standing before her while Michael looked back with an expression she had never seen before. There was nervousness. There was hesitation. And there was fear.","The last one surprised her the most.","Fear? On Sir Mic? The same man who had challenged an empire and won? The same man who could casually command legendary existences?","\"Miss Arianne.\"","His voice broke the silence.","\"Yes?\"","Michael hesitated for a moment before asking a question that completely caught her off guard.","\"Have you ever heard the term Otherworlder before?\"","Arianne blinked in confusion. Then she slowly shook her head.","\"No.\"","Michael nodded as though he had expected that answer. For several seconds he remained silent again.","Then he asked another question.","\"Have you ever wondered where I came from?\"","This time Arianne paused.","Of course she had. Who wouldn't? Sir Mic had appeared almost out of nowhere. He possessed strength that defied common sense. Even his behavior was occasionally strange.","Naturally she had been curious.","Arianne nodded in response. Then immediately shook her head.","\"I am curious. But it's okay.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"If Sir Mic isn't ready to tell me, then you don't have to.\" Arianne smiled softly. \"I can wait.\"","\"Whether it's now or later.\" Her voice became quieter. \"I'll wait until you're ready.\"","For a moment Michael simply stared at her. Then a bitter smile appeared on his face.","The sight made Arianne's heart tighten. For some reason, that smile looked sad.","\"Miss Arianne.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"The truth is...\"","Michael looked toward the strange sky above them.","\"I don't come from this world.\"","Arianne blinked. For a moment she thought she had misheard.","\"What?\"","Michael looked back at her.","\"I come from a place called Aurora.\"","Aurora.","The name sounded beautiful. Yet completely unfamiliar.","\"Aurora?\" she repeated.","Michael nodded. Then he began speaking.","\"In Aurora, there are no kings.\"","Arianne frowned.","\"No kings?\"","\"No.\"","\"No emperors?\"","\"No.\"","\"No nobles?\"","\"No.\"","The more answers she received, the more unbelievable everything sounded.","Arianne stared at him. Then stared harder. Then narrowed her eyes.","Michael noticed immediately.","\"Why are you looking at me like that?\"","Arianne crossed her arms.","\"Are you sure you're not joking?\"","\"Miss Arianne.\"","\"Sir Mic.\"","\"Call me Michael.\"","\"Why?\"","\"Call me Michael.\"","\"...Michael.\"","\"Thank you.\"","Arianne felt a bit strange about Michael's behavior but went on to voice her confusion anyway.","\"You expect me to believe there's a place without nobles, kings, or emperors?\"","\"But it's true, though.\"","\"Then who rules?\"","Michael opened his mouth. Then paused. Then opened it again.","Honestly, explaining modern governments to someone born in a feudal empire suddenly felt impossible.","\"It's complicated.\"","Arianne immediately looked victorious.","\"I knew it.\"","Michael sighed. Then continued.","\"In Aurora, there are also supernatural people.\"","\"Like knights and mages?\"","\"Yes and no.\"","Arianne tilted her head.","\"No?\"","\"There are two major groups.\" Michael raised two fingers. \"Cultivators and Awakeners.\"","Arianne felt like she was drowning in confusion. The first term sounded somewhat familiar, but the second didn't.","\"What are cultivators?\"","\"Basically everyone you're familiar with.\"","\"What?\"","\"Knights. Mages. Necromancers. Elementalists. Healers.\" \"They all fall under the broad category of cultivators.\"","\"Oh.\"","That part made sense. Then she remembered the second group.","\"What about Awakeners?\"","This time Michael became noticeably more serious.","\"They're different.\"","\"How?\"","\"They grow stronger much faster.\"","Arianne's eyes widened slightly.","\"Faster than geniuses?\"","\"Much faster.\"","That was absurd.","Michael continued.","\"They possess status panels.\"","Arianne froze. She recalled this was what Sir Mic had once called that blue glass that appeared in her eyes when she had called that deer more than a month ago. Unfortunately he hadn't seemed willing to explain further at the time.","Now she was even more interested, and her attention sharpened.","Michael looked directly into her eyes.","\"The most important thing is, every Awakener has access to another world.\"","Another world?","Arianne frowned.","\"What does that mean?\"","Michael took a slow breath. Then continued.","\"They can enter another world using a body similar to their real one. There, they have another identity. And can live another life.\"","Arianne's heartbeat slowly accelerated. Something about this conversation suddenly felt strange. She wasn't sure why.","Michael continued regardless. Since he had started, he had to continue.","\"The body they use isn't exactly fake. The original body in my world experiences everything the other body experiences as well.\"","Arianne felt her heartbeat speed up again. For some reason, she suddenly had a bad feeling.","With his gaze fixed on Arianne, Michael took a deep breath.","\"Miss Arianne. What if...\"","Michael hesitated for only a second. Then finally forced the words out.","\"What if I told you that Sir Mic Nor is one of those identities?\""]},{"number":1056,"title":"Chapter 1056: New World [1]","paragraphs":["Arianne wasn't dumb.","The moment those words left Michael's mouth, countless things that had once seemed strange suddenly began connecting together inside her mind.","It all started making sense.","Yet somehow, it was too much. The entire situation was so absurd that part of her instinctively refused to believe it.","Michael immediately noticed the look on her face and took several steps toward her.","Feeling his presence, Arianne subconsciously took a step backward. It was an instinctive reaction born from shock rather than fear, but she failed to notice how it made Michael's expression change.","For a brief second, something flashed across his face.","\"Miss Arianne.\"","Michael forced himself to remain calm.","\"That's why I said I wanted to show you. Because if I only explained it, you wouldn't believe me.\"","Arianne opened her mouth. Then closed it again. Because she honestly wasn't sure she believed him now either.","Michael raised a hand.","Space distorted once more. Another portal appeared.","Without saying anything further, Michael stepped through first. Then he turned around and looked back at her. His expression remained serious. Yet there was also something else there.","Nervousness. As though he was worried about what would happen next.","Since she was technically inside a part of him, Michael felt she should be able to enter Aurora. If not, he would have no choice but to wipe her memory clean of everything he had just said.","In fact, if Arianne proved to be a problem after all this, that was exactly what he planned to do. If things turned out differently from what he wanted, they would simply have to end their relationship afterward.","\"Come.\" Michael said.","Arianne hesitated, took a steadying breath, then stepped through the portal.","The moment she crossed over, she froze. Her eyes widened as she looked at her surroundings in shock.","She had appeared inside a room unlike anything she had ever seen before. At first glance it seemed simple. Yet the longer she looked, the stranger it became.","The walls were smooth and painted a soft brown. Clean. Neat. Orderly.","The room was spacious, and a large bed occupied one side of it. Unlike the beds she was familiar with, there were no carved wooden decorations. The sheets were spotless. The blanket looked unbelievably soft.","Everything appeared comfortable.","Arianne slowly turned around, her gaze sweeping across the room again. There was a wardrobe with perfectly smooth white doors. Shelves holding books and strange objects she could not identify. A desk unlike any she had ever seen. A large window covered by elegant gray curtains.","Everything looked strange and foreign.","For several moments she simply stood there. Then curiosity won.","The first thing Arianne approached was the bed. Slowly, she reached out. Her fingers touched the mattress, then immediately sank slightly into it.","Arianne blinked in surprise and pressed harder. The mattress yielded beneath her hand.","So soft. Very soft.","She pressed again. Then again. Then she used both hands.","Arianne looked genuinely shocked. Compared to this, even the beds in the empire's capital felt lacking.","\"What is this?\"","Michael glanced over.","\"A bed.\"","Arianne immediately looked at him.","\"No.\"","Michael blinked.","\"No?\"","\"It literally is.\"","Arianne stared at the mattress. Then back at Michael. Then back at the mattress. Finally she pointed at it.","\"It must be so expensive, right? At least a few hundred gold coins?\"","For the first time since the conversation began, Michael nearly laughed.","Meanwhile, Arianne reluctantly pulled herself away before becoming distracted by something else. She walked toward the curtains, carefully grasped the fabric, then pulled them aside. She froze when she saw the window.","The window itself looked strange. More importantly, it was completely transparent. Arianne instinctively touched it.","Unfortunately, all she could see was a fence made from strange material. The room sat close to a wall outside. However she could hear strange noises, horns and conversations in an unfamiliar language drifting in from beyond it.","For several moments she simply stood there listening. At this point, she didn't even have enough mental energy left to be shocked that Michael could casually move between worlds.","Soon her attention was stolen by Michael's desk. Dropping the curtains, Arianne slowly approached it and stared in admiration. The entire setup looked incredibly luxurious.","A large black screen sat on the desk. Beside it was another, smaller screen. A strange board covered in symbols. Several sleek devices she could not identify.","Everything looked expensive and impossibly fragile.","Arianne immediately clasped her hands behind her back. She didn't dare touch anything. What if she broke it? For all she knew, these could be priceless treasures.","Meanwhile, Michael simply watched from behind. Under normal circumstances, the sight would have amused him. Arianne looked like a child who had wandered into a treasure vault by accident.","Unfortunately, Michael's attention was elsewhere. His thoughts remained fixed on the conversation they had left unfinished.","Before he could decide how to continue, Arianne's attention was stolen by something else. Her gaze slowly drifted upward, toward the glowing object attached to the ceiling.","Arianne blinked. The object looked like a small glass fruit hanging above her. Yet unlike any crystal lamp she had ever seen, there was no flame or visible source of energy. Still, it emitted a steady white light that illuminated the entire room.","\"Amazing...\"","Arianne murmured. Then her eyes moved lower, toward the wall. There, near the doorway, was a small object protruding from the surface.","Arianne frowned.","\"What is that?\"","Michael followed her gaze.","\"Oh. That's a light switch.\"","\"A what?\"","Before Michael could explain, curiosity had already won. Arianne walked over, stared at the small switch for a second, then reached out when she saw that Michael didn't stop her.","Click.","The room instantly sank into darkness.","\"Ah!\"","Arianne jumped in shock, instinctively taking a step backward. Unfortunately, she forgot Michael was standing directly behind her. Her back collided with his chest.","Strong arms immediately steadied her before she could lose her balance.","\"It's fine.\" Michael's calm voice sounded beside her ear. \"It's just the light.\""]},{"number":1057,"title":"Chapter 1057: New World [2]","paragraphs":["Arianne's heart pounded. The sudden darkness had genuinely startled her. For several moments she remained frozen.","Then she realized something. Michael's arms were still around her, but she didn't point that out. And for some reason, Michael didn't seem eager to let go either.","The room remained dim, illuminated only by faint light filtering through the curtains from outside.","Eventually Michael cleared his throat.","\"The switch controls the bulb.\"","\"The what?\"","\"The glowing thing on the ceiling.\"","\"Oh.\"","Arianne looked upward, even though she could barely see it now.","Slowly, Michael guided her hand back toward the wall.","\"Press it again.\"","Arianne obeyed.","Click. The room instantly brightened.","Her eyes widened.","Click. Darkness.","Click. Light.","Click. Darkness.","Click. Light.","Arianne stared. Then looked at the switch. Then at the ceiling. Then back at the switch. A sparkle appeared in her eyes.","Click. Darkness.","Click. Light.","Click. Darkness.","Click. Light.","Michael watched in silence.","Ten seconds later.","Click. Darkness.","Click. Light.","Twenty seconds later.","Click. Darkness.","Click. Light.","Michael rubbed his forehead.","\"Miss Arianne.\"","\"Mm?\"","Click. Darkness. Click. Light.","\"What are you doing?\"","Arianne looked genuinely confused.","\"I'm testing it.\"","\"Testing what?\"","\"The magic.\"","\"It's not magic.\"","Click. Darkness. Click. Light.","Arianne gasped.","\"It worked again.\"","Michael stared at her.","The young woman stared at the switch for a few more seconds before finally asking the question she had been holding back.","\"What exactly is this thing?\"","Michael looked at the switch but didn't speak. Before even starting, he could already tell that explaining electricity to someone from a medieval fantasy world might actually be harder than explaining that he came from another world entirely.","He honestly wasn't sure where to start.","Finally, he gave up.","\"I'll explain later.\"","Arianne immediately looked dissatisfied.","\"But—\"","\"Later.\"","\"But—\"","\"Definitely later.\"","Arianne puffed her cheeks slightly. Michael pretended not to notice. Instead, he reached forward and grabbed her hand.","For some reason, Michael felt he should be bolder, braver. More confident. Come on. Why was he fearing rejection and acting so weak? Surely Arianne wasn't that scary, right?","\"Come on.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"I'll show you something cooler.\"","Without waiting for a response, Michael gently pulled her toward the door.","A few moments later, they stepped outside, and Arianne's world shattered all over again.","She stood completely frozen. The view before her was unlike anything she had ever imagined.","People. Dozens of people. Perhaps hundreds. Everywhere she looked, people moved through the streets. None of them wore robes, carried swords, or rode horses. Their clothing came in countless strange styles and colors.","Some wore black jackets. Others wore colorful shirts. Some exposed their arms. She even saw a few women in extremely short clothing. Sheesh. If she dared wear that outside, her father would kill her.","The buildings were equally absurd. Towering structures stretched high into the sky. Many were made almost entirely from glass. Others displayed enormous glowing signs across their walls. Moving pictures flashed across giant boards suspended above the streets. Words appeared and disappeared. Images changed constantly.","Arianne's mouth slowly opened, then she froze again.","Something large flew past on the road. It was not an animal but a large metal block. Then another. And another. Dozens of them, moving unbelievably fast.","Arianne instinctively took a step backward.","\"Si— Michael!\" Her voice carried alarm. \"What are those?\"","\"Cars.\"","\"What?\"","\"Cars.\"","\"That explains nothing!\"","Before she could ask another question, a loud horn sounded from the street. Arianne nearly jumped.","\"What attacked us?\"","\"Nothing attacked us.\"","\"Then why is it screaming?\"","\"It isn't screaming.\"","\"It definitely screamed.\"","Michael rubbed his forehead. Meanwhile Arianne continued staring around in complete shock. At this point she had forgotten almost everything else. The city itself was overwhelming.","Soon Michael pulled a black nose mask from his pocket and put it on.","Arianne immediately noticed.","\"What is that?\"","\"A mask.\"","\"Why?\"","Michael paused.","\"Privacy.\"","\"Why are you hiding?\"","\"I am not. My identity is just a bit troublesome.\"","\"That sounds like hiding.\"","Michael decided not to continue that argument. Instead, he led her through the streets.","The entire journey was a battle. Every few seconds Arianne stopped walking. Every few seconds she found something new to stare at.","A giant screen. A motorcycle. A traffic light. An elevator visible through a glass building. A child holding a glowing tablet.","Everything seemed capable of breaking her understanding of reality.","Eventually Michael guided her toward a nearby bakery. The moment they entered, Arianne was drawn in by a rich aroma that filled the air. The scent alone nearly made her dizzy with hunger.","Rows upon rows of bread lined the displays. Cakes. Pastries. Donuts. Croissants. Countless foods she had never seen before, though a few looked vaguely familiar.","Meanwhile, the employee behind the counter looked equally fascinated. The young man glanced at Arianne. Then at Michael.","The cashier leaned forward.","\"Bro.\"","Michael sighed.","\"What?\"","The man's grin widened.","\"Your girlfriend is gorgeous.\" His eyes remained fixed on Arianne. \"Seriously though, where'd you meet her?\"","Michael remained silent, but the young man didn't seem to mind. The grin on his face only widened further.","\"That cosplay is insane.\"","\"Cosplay?\"","\"Yeah.\" The cashier gestured toward Arianne's dress. \"The hair. The eyes. The outfit. The whole fantasy princess look. It's perfect.\" He lowered his voice. \"Natural too.\"","Michael felt completely helpless.","Across from him, Arianne understood absolutely none of the conversation. The language being spoken was entirely foreign. Still, she could tell something was happening.","The employee kept looking at her, then at Michael, then back at her, and every time he did, that strange smile on his face grew wider.","Arianne narrowed her eyes suspiciously, then quietly moved closer to Michael, almost unconsciously. The movement caused the cashier's grin to widen even further.","Michael was starting to wonder if he should leave. Unfortunately, the cashier wasn't finished.","\"Bro.\"","\"What?\"","\"You better marry her.\"","Michael nearly choked.","Meanwhile Arianne tilted her head. She had no idea what was being said. But judging by Michael's expression, it was probably something embarrassing."]},{"number":1058,"title":"Chapter 1058: New World [3]","paragraphs":["Michael was starting to feel that perhaps going to a clothing store first would have been better. It wasn't that he hadn't thought of it, but he had figured that in an era where anyone could wear literally anything, a woman in ordinary clothes wouldn't catch much attention.","This much was true. Unfortunately, the person working in the store just happened to be someone who liked this kind of thing, or rather seemed deeply into it in more ways than one.","Michael could only endure it.","The young man had been polite so far, and there was no reason to suddenly leave. Besides, they weren't planning to stay long.","\"Anyway,\" Michael said, deciding to change the topic, \"please give me a chocolate ball pack.\"","The cashier immediately nodded.","\"What kind? The usual?\"","Michael paused.","That was actually a good question. The chocolates he had previously given Arianne had been fairly ordinary. Since she had liked those so much, he hadn't bothered looking into other options.","Now that he thought about it, maybe there were better choices.","The cashier leaned forward.","\"We've got milk chocolate. Dark chocolate. White chocolate. Chocolate-filled pastries. Chocolate cake. Chocolate croissants.\" He pointed toward another display. \"Candies too.\"","The young man lowered his voice.","\"First date?\"","\"No.\"","The cashier looked unconvinced.","\"Uh huh.\"","Michael sighed.","\"Just give me recommendations.\"","The young man's eyes immediately lit up. Now this was a subject he understood.","\"If you're introducing sweets to a date, milk chocolate is usually safest.\" He pointed toward several products. \"Those are popular.\" Then he pointed elsewhere. \"And that's our specialty.\"","Michael followed his finger. Inside the display sat several freshly baked pastries coated in chocolate and drizzled with something glossy. Even from where he stood, the smell was incredible.","Michael thought for a moment. If he only bought chocolate, Arianne would probably enjoy it. But this was her first time in Aurora. Perhaps letting her try more things wouldn't be a bad idea.","\"Alright.\" The cashier straightened. \"I'll take both. The chocolates and the specialty pastries.\"","\"Good choice.\"","The young man immediately began packing everything.","Meanwhile, Arianne continued examining the displays. She had no idea what most of the items were. However, she had reached one firm conclusion: Aurora really had enough food. There was simply too much of it.","Eventually, Michael paid and quickly escaped before the cashier could continue the conversation.","The moment they stepped outside, Arianne finally asked the question she had been holding back.","\"What was he saying?\"","Michael immediately answered.","\"Nothing.\"","\"You are lying.\"","\"I am not.\"","\"You are.\"","\"It wasn't something important. Don't bother about it.\"","\"It was.\"","\"It wasn't.\"","\"It was.\"","\"It wasn't.\"","\"It was.\"","Eventually Michael surrendered.","\"Fine. He was talking about your clothes.\"","Arianne blinked in surprise.","\"My clothes?\"","Michael nodded.","\"You dress differently from everyone here.\"","That answer immediately made sense to Arianne. In fact, she had already noticed it. Since arriving in Aurora, not a single person she had seen dressed remotely like her. Compared to the flowing dress she wore, everyone else looked completely different.","Arianne looked around. She deliberately began studying the people passing by. More specifically, the women.","At first she merely observed out of curiosity. Then her pace gradually slowed until she completely stopped walking.","Michael had only taken a step before realizing she was no longer beside him. When he turned around, he found Arianne staring at a group of women walking down the street.","One wore a fitted black jacket. Another wore a long cream-colored coat. A third wore a simple white blouse and jeans.","The clothing looked incredibly simple. Yet strangely elegant.","More importantly, there was variety. An unbelievable amount of variety. Some outfits looked practical. Others looked beautiful. Others somehow managed to be both.","Arianne's eyes slowly lit up. She looked at one outfit. Then another. Then another. The more she looked, the more fascinated she became. Though deep within her she still felt overwhelmed by this strange world, and a little fearful of it, its beauty wasn't something any capital she had visited or heard of could match.","\"You like the clothes?\" Michael suddenly asked.","Arianne remained silent. Which was answer enough.","Fortunately for Arianne, the trip had already changed from its original purpose. At first, Michael had only intended to show her something memorable. Something that would help her understand that Aurora truly existed and that this wasn't some elaborate illusion.","However, after the incident at the bakery, he had come to realize the importance of another problem.","Clothes.","Arianne attracted attention far more easily than he had expected. At first Michael hadn't considered it important, and indeed he could still choose to walk around with her looking like this. But there was no need for them to draw so much attention if they could help it.","Now he was reconsidering.","Arianne remained completely unaware of the thoughts running through Michael's head, still busy observing the women around them. The sheer variety fascinated her. She had never imagined a world where fashion could possess so much freedom.","Without realizing it, she found herself wondering how she would look in some of those outfits. The thought embarrassed her slightly, so she kept it to herself.","Several minutes later, Arianne suddenly realized they had changed directions.","\"Hm?\"","She looked around. This wasn't the road they had been following earlier.","Before she could ask, Michael stopped in front of a large glass storefront. Behind the transparent wall stood countless outfits.","Arianne's eyes widened.","\"Come on.\"","Michael entered first. Arianne followed after only a second of hesitation.","The moment she stepped inside, she was overwhelmed. There were clothes everywhere.","Before Arianne knew what was happening, she had been surrounded by several enthusiastic employees. Then things became chaotic.","An hour later, Michael sat silently on a nearby chair. His expression had long since gone blank.","Meanwhile, several store employees seemed more energetic than ever.","\"No, no, no.\" A woman shook her head. \"Try the blue one.\"","\"But—\"","\"The blue one.\"","Five minutes later.","\"No, the white one is even better.\""]},{"number":1059,"title":"Chapter 1059: Final Answer","paragraphs":["Ten minutes later.","\"Actually, let's try both.\"","Michael had long since given up resisting.","Eventually, the dressing room curtain opened once more. The store became noticeably quieter.","Arianne slowly stepped out. For several seconds neither she nor Michael spoke. Even Arianne seemed stunned by her own reflection.","The flowing noble dress she had worn earlier was gone. In its place was a cream-colored long coat layered over a soft black turtleneck sweater and a fitted dark skirt that reached just below her knees.","Simple. Modern. Elegant.","The outfit somehow emphasized her emerald eyes and golden hair even more than her noble attire had.","Arianne stared at the mirror. The woman looking back at her felt familiar. Yet unfamiliar. Like herself. But also not herself.","A middle-aged woman immediately clapped her hands.","\"I knew it!\" She pointed dramatically at the mirror. \"Look at her!\"","The woman turned toward Michael.","\"Young man, your friend is beautiful.\"","Arianne blinked. Though she couldn't understand the language, she could tell the woman was praising her.","The older woman walked around her, then nodded in complete satisfaction.","\"Perfect.\"","Arianne looked at her reflection again. For the first time since arriving in Aurora, she felt something unexpected.","She belonged. At least a little.","And somehow, that realization made the overwhelming strangeness of this new world feel just a bit less frightening.","Soon, Michael and Arianne returned home. Or rather, they returned to Michael's home.","Even now, Arianne still felt somewhat dazed. The trip through Aurora had overwhelmed her far more than she cared to admit. Every street. Every building. Every person. Every object. Everything challenged what she believed the world should be.","After entering the apartment, Michael led her back to his room. The moment they entered, Arianne instinctively glanced toward the light switch.","Michael immediately noticed.","\"...No.\"","Arianne looked somewhat disappointed and looked away.","Michael walked toward his desk and placed several bags down. Then he picked up a small package before turning around.","\"Here.\"","Arianne's eyes fell onto the object in his hand, and her expression immediately changed at the familiar shape beneath the wrapping.","\"This is...\"","Michael nodded.","\"Chocolates.\"","Arianne accepted it carefully. The moment she held it, memories surfaced. This wasn't the first time Michael had given her one of these. At the time, Michael had simply told her they came from back home, and Arianne had believed him.","Now she realized he hadn't lied. The problem was that his \"back home\" wasn't another city, but an entirely different world.","The thought made her stare at the chocolate for several seconds. How strange. A simple snack she had eaten before suddenly felt completely different.","Slowly, she unwrapped it. Then took a bite.","Crunch.","The familiar sweetness spread across her tongue. Arianne's eyes brightened slightly.","\"...\"","Another bite followed. The rich sweetness melted inside her mouth.","It was still delicious. Perhaps even more delicious now that she knew where it came from.","Michael watched from nearby. A faint smile appeared on his face.","Meanwhile, Arianne examined the half-eaten chocolate in her hand. Then she looked around the room, and at the clothes she was currently wearing.","Everything felt surreal. A few hours ago she had thought Sir Mic was simply a mysterious genius with a strange background. Now she knew the truth was far more ridiculous.","The thought made her glance toward him again. This time, her gaze lingered.","The Michael standing before her looked younger than the Sir Mic she knew. More relaxed. Less distant. The aura of an untouchable lord was gone. In its place stood a young man.","Arianne's lips slowly curved upward. Then she took another bite of chocolate.","For some reason, the confusion and fear she had felt earlier seemed much smaller now. Perhaps it was because Aurora truly existed. Or perhaps it was because despite all the impossible truths she had learned today, one thing remained unchanged.","Whether he was Sir Mic. Or Michael. The person standing before her was still the same person who had crossed an empire for her. The same person who had brought her back from death. The same person who looked absurdly nervous whenever she got too close.","That thought comforted her more than she expected.","Crunch.","Arianne took another bite of chocolate when she suddenly heard Michael speak.","\"So...\"","His voice carried an unusual hesitation.","Arianne looked up. Michael was standing a short distance away. His hands were in his pockets. His posture appeared relaxed.","Yet somehow his nervousness was still visible to Arianne.","\"So?\" Arianne repeated.","Michael was silent for several seconds. Then he finally asked.","\"What do you think?\"","The room became quiet.","At first Arianne didn't answer. Instead, she simply looked at him and saw the uncertainty in his eyes. The tension in his shoulders.","Seeing that expression unexpectedly made the unease inside her relax a little. A lot of her earlier confusion remained. But somehow seeing Michael look this uneasy reassured her.","Arianne slowly lowered the chocolate. Then a small smile appeared on her face.","\"Sir... Michael.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Were you worried?\"","\"About what?\"","Arianne tilted her head.","\"That I would stop liking you.\"","The words landed like a hammer. Michael immediately froze.","Arianne's smile widened slightly, because for a brief moment she had actually seen a flicker of panic flash across his face.","Unfortunately for Michael, his silence answered her question better than any words could.","The room became quiet again.","Eventually Michael let out a slow breath. He rubbed his forehead before speaking again.","\"Miss Arianne.\"","His voice became more serious.","\"A relationship shouldn't be built on falsehoods.\"","The smile on Arianne's face softened.","Michael continued.","\"You deserved to know.\"","\"I know.\"","\"You only knew Mic Nor.\"","Arianne remained silent.","\"You didn't know Michael.\" His gaze lowered slightly. \"I kept wondering whether your feelings were directed at me, or at the person you thought I was.\"","For several moments neither spoke. Then unexpectedly Arianne asked a question.","\"Can I ask something?\"","Michael nodded.","\"Of course.\"","Arianne stared directly into his eyes."]},{"number":1060,"title":"Chapter 1060: In All My Lives, You’re The First","paragraphs":["\"Do you think Mic Nor and Michael are different people?\"","Michael opened his mouth. Then paused. Because he didn't actually know.","Arianne continued before he could answer.","\"When you spoke to me. Was it Michael speaking?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"When you saved me?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"When you carried me?\"","Michael's ears immediately turned slightly red.","\"Yes.\"","\"When you crossed an empire for me?\"","Michael sighed.","\"Yes.\"","\"When you brought me back to life?\"","\"Yes.\"","\"Then where exactly is this different person?\"","Michael froze.","Arianne watched his expression. Then shook her head.","\"You keep talking as though there are two people.\" Her voice became gentler. \"But every memory I have belongs to the same person.\"","Michael fell silent. Because for the first time since this entire conversation began, he realized she might have been looking at the situation very differently from him.","Arianne slowly took another bite of chocolate.","Crunch.","Then she swallowed. And asked another question. A much more dangerous one.","\"S... Michael.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Do you like me?\"","Michael choked violently and coughed several times.","\"Where did that come from?\"","\"You didn't answer.\"","\"Miss Arianne.\"","\"You didn't answer.\"","Michael looked away.","Arianne immediately narrowed her eyes.","\"...Michael.\"","\"No.\"","\"No?\"","\"I mean yes. Yes, I really like you. You're the first person I've ever liked in all my lives!\"","The room froze.","Arianne stared at him as he closed his eyes after the words left him, then slowly smiled. It was a very beautiful smile.","Michael slowly opened his eyes, and the first thing he saw was that smile.","The fear he had been carrying all day suddenly felt ridiculous. And perhaps because of that, for the first time that day, he stopped overthinking. Stopped worrying. Stopped doubting.","Instead, he took a step forward, until only a short distance remained between them.","The smile on Arianne's face gradually faded into confusion.","\"Michael?\"","This time, Michael didn't retreat. Instead, he looked directly into her emerald eyes. Then asked quietly.","\"You asked me a question.\"","Arianne tilted her head.","\"I did.\"","\"Now it's my turn.\"","For some reason, Arianne suddenly became nervous.","\"What is it?\"","Michael inhaled slowly. Then asked the question that had been haunting him for months.","\"Arianne.\"","\"Hm?\"","\"Do you like me?\"","The room fell silent.","Arianne's eyes widened slightly. The confidence she had displayed moments ago immediately weakened.","Michael almost laughed. So she could become nervous too. Interesting.","Several seconds passed. Arianne stared at him. Then sighed.","\"You already know the answer.\"","Michael did. But hearing it and knowing it were different things.","Arianne seemed to realize that as well. Slowly, she met his eyes again. And this time she didn't look away.","\"I like you.\" Her voice was soft. Yet firm. \"I liked you before I knew about Aurora.\"","She took a small step forward.","\"I liked you before I knew your real name.\"","Another step.","\"And I still like you now.\"","Michael felt his heartbeat accelerate.","Arianne smiled softly.","\"Whether you're Michael. Or Sir Mic. You're still you.\"","Silence followed. Neither moved. Neither looked away.","For a brief moment, the room seemed strangely quiet.","Then Michael made a decision. A simple one. Instead of thinking. Instead of doubting. Instead of worrying.","He stepped forward.","Arianne's breath caught. Michael slowly raised a hand and gently brushed a strand of golden hair behind her ear. His fingers lingered for a moment.","Neither spoke.","Then, before Arianne could understand what he intended to do, Michael leaned forward.","And kissed her.","Arianne froze. Completely froze. Her eyes widened. The chocolate in her hand nearly slipped from her fingers.","For a brief moment, her body instinctively stiffened, and she resisted. Not because she disliked it, or wanted him to stop. Though she had accepted the reality of things, it was still too much for her to immediately reconcile kissing Michael's other body.","The shock left her completely motionless.","Even Michael felt it. For a brief second, doubt surged through him. Had he moved too quickly? Had he made a mistake?","The thought flashed through his mind.","Then Arianne's fingers slowly tightened around his shirt. The tension in her body began to fade as the familiar sensation only Michael could cause coursed through her.","Arianne closed her eyes. And leaned into him.","The last traces of resistance vanished.","Relief flooded through Michael. One of his hands settled gently against her waist while the other moved to her cheek. Neither spoke, nor wanted to.","The distance that had existed between them for months finally disappeared. The kiss deepened naturally, as though both were trying to memorize the moment.","The room became silent. Arianne could feel her heart pounding inside her chest. Michael's wasn't much better.","The young man who commanded legendary creatures now felt nervous because of her. The realization made Arianne very happy. This wasn't Lord Mic Nor, or some untouchable genius. This was simply Michael. A young man who liked her.","Time seemed to lose meaning.","Eventually, a phone notification ringtone forced them apart.","A bit embarrassed, neither spoke as Michael checked his notification, a text from his aunt asking if he wanted her to bring anything for him. She seemed to be clocking out early today.","Thinking of something, Michael turned to look at Arianne and asked a question.","\"Do you want to stay with me here for a few days, or should we go back?\"","\"Is that okay?\"","\"Yes.\"","Of course it was fine. Michael's household was already numb to him bringing things out of nowhere. First it had been undead creatures. Then it was Jester, who looked no different from the living and even attended school. Arianne would be novel, but hardly surprising.","After receiving Michael's confirmation, though still worried, she decided to trust him.","Just like that, the household gained an additional member.","Just like that, a week passed quickly.","Knowing he didn't have to wipe her memories, Michael, much more relaxed with Arianne now, took her around his dimension cracks while feeding her his evolution crystals and arming her to the teeth with precious treasures as well.","However, today Michael took a break.","Something important was happening today.","It was Lily's first awakening ceremony."]},{"number":1061,"title":"Chapter 1061: Methods","paragraphs":["The Federation had always tried to ensure that the Awakening Ceremony occurred at roughly the same time throughout the realm.","Of course, that was easier said than done.","Aurora alone possessed countless cities, different time zones, varying levels of development, and regions separated by enormous distances. Making every ceremony occur on the exact same day was practically impossible.","Still, with enough planning and preparation, the Federation had managed to reduce the overall Awakening Period to only three days. For an event involving an entire realm, that was already considered extremely efficient.","Aurora wasn't unique in this regard. In fact, many realms throughout the universe did something similar, and were even more coordinated, since the gap between awakening periods among many realms was surprisingly small.","Generally speaking, most conducted their ceremonies within a one-to-two-month window of each other.","This level of coordination was, of course, impossible to be mere coincidence.","Though the number of ordinary supernaturals in any established realm would always be greater than awakeners, Awakeners were simply too important to dismiss thanks to their unique nature.","No civilization was willing to ignore even the slightest possibility of increasing their numbers. The problem remained that Awakening was one of the greatest mysteries known to the universe.","No one could force it. No one could guarantee it.","Two powerful awakeners could give birth to an ordinary child, and two completely normal people could produce an Awakener. Countless civilizations had spent thousands of years researching the phenomenon, and none had truly succeeded.","Yes, ordinary supernaturals existed in enormous numbers. Yet despite that, Awakeners remained extraordinarily valuable.","If it took a thousand years for an ordinary supernatural to reach a supreme level, an awakener could cut that time significantly. And if both sides started with a hundred people, where ten from the ordinary side might succeed, thirty could succeed on the awakener side.","As one's power grew, the advantages awakeners held did decrease, but they never completely disappeared.","Thanks to this, as a result of wanting more awakeners, civilizations had experimented with every method imaginable to increase Awakener births.","Some focused on bloodlines. Some focused on resources. Others focused on environmental factors. Among the countless theories was one particularly widespread belief.","Synchronization.","The theory proposed that if enough civilizations conducted their Awakening Ceremonies during roughly the same period, the odds of producing Awakeners might increase.","No one knew if it actually worked. No one had ever managed to prove it, but nobody had disproved it either.","More importantly, it cost absolutely nothing.","As a result, over countless years it had evolved from a theory into a universal tradition. Whether in a beginner realm or an ancient realm that had existed for millions of years, many civilizations still attempted to synchronize their ceremonies.","These past three days had been Aurora's turn, with today being the last day, and the one on which Michael's home country conducted theirs.","At the dining table in Michael's home sat four figures. Michael. Aunt Mia. Jester. And Lily.","Among them, only Lily was dressed in a school uniform. Unfortunately, the young lady currently looked nervous. Her fingers tapped repeatedly against the table as she stared at the breakfast in front of her.","Today was her Awakening Ceremony.","Even knowing that this was only her first try, and that she still had two more attempts after this, Lily couldn't stop herself from feeling anxious.","\"Jester.\"","\"Hm?\"","Jester looked up from his food and turned to look at Lily. Though his true body was an undead, the body he controlled was truly living. Through it, Jester lived a more fulfilling life than his brothers and sisters.","Lily frowned.","\"Why aren't you getting ready?\"","\"I'm not going with you to school today.\"","Hearing this, Lily became even more anxious.","Over the past several months, Lily and Jester had become very close and got along fairly well. To Lily, Jester's absence from today's ceremony felt strange, especially because nobody had informed her beforehand.","The realization only increased her anxiety. It felt like losing moral support before an important battle.","Michael swallowed his food before answering in Jester's place.","\"He can't go with you because it's not suitable. If anyone asks, tell them he's conducting his Awakening Ceremony somewhere else.\"","Lily looked toward Jester. The undead continued eating breakfast as though the conversation had nothing to do with him.","Seeing that neither of them seemed interested in elaborating, Lily could only keep her thoughts to herself. Though she wanted an answer, she wasn't stupid. In fact, she already had a rough guess.","Jester looked human. But only looked human. Inside, he was probably more than human. The more Lily thought about it, the more obvious the answer became.","Jester attending an Awakening Ceremony never made much sense to begin with.","As it happened, Lily's conclusion was almost entirely correct.","Michael had no intention of having Jester follow Lily to school. Not because it would cause trouble, but because it might create unnecessary questions.","Normally, every Awakening Ceremony involved at least a small number of newly awakened students, if Lily's school wasn't simply unlucky.","All awakeners could use the detect skill, and if one of those students used such an ability on Jester, they might notice something.","It wouldn't cause an issue, since even the school's higher-ups knew Jester wasn't an ordinary student, but Michael preferred avoiding such situations altogether. To everyone else, Jester was simply another youth, and Michael intended to keep it that way.","After several seconds, Lily finally nodded.","\"...Fine.\"","Though she still looked disappointed.","Jester finally looked up. His green eyes met hers.","\"Good luck.\"","The simple words caused Lily to smile, and a little of her nervousness disappeared.","\"Thanks.\"","Jester nodded and returned to eating.","Aunt Mia finally set down her cup.","\"Enough chit-chat. Lily, you need to be in school soon.\"","Lily immediately looked up.","\"There's no rush. The ceremony won't start until afternoon anyway.\"","Aunt Mia immediately threw a glare at her daughter. She might be unable to do much to Michael anymore, as he grew stronger and took on more responsibility, but Lily was still under her roof.","Lily immediately lowered her head and returned to eating.","\"...Okay.\""]},{"number":1062,"title":"Chapter 1062: Worries","paragraphs":["Satisfied, Aunt Mia nodded.","Michael watched the scene silently and wisely chose not to interfere. Even if Lily could subdue a hundred men with one hand, in this house, Aunt Mia's glare still held authority.","After dealing with Lily, Aunt Mia's gaze naturally moved toward Michael.","\"Where is Arianne?\"","Michael's hand holding his spoon stopped for half a second before continuing normally.","\"She has something to do, so she won't be around for a while.\"","\"Oh.\"","Aunt Mia's tone carried a trace of disappointment.","Lily also looked up.","\"She's not coming today?\"","\"No.\"","Lily's expression fell slightly. Over the past few days, Arianne's presence had made the house strangely lively.","She couldn't speak their language properly, and most conversations required Michael to translate, but that somehow made things more interesting rather than awkward.","Aunt Mia had also grown curious about her. How could she not? The girl was beautiful, polite, strangely innocent, and carried an air that was clearly not ordinary.","More importantly, there was the atmosphere between her and Michael. Aunt Mia was not blind. Neither was Lily. Even if neither of them asked directly, both had noticed the subtle changes.","Only Jester seemed to want nothing to do with the matter. Or rather, Jester seemed to deliberately ignore it.","\"Will she be back?\" Lily asked.","Michael nodded.","\"Eventually.\"","Aunt Mia smiled lightly.","\"She's a sweet girl.\"","Michael coughed.","\"She is.\"","Aunt Mia looked at him for a moment longer, her smile gaining a faintly meaningful edge. Michael immediately lowered his gaze to his food. Seeing his reaction, Aunt Mia's smile widened slightly, but she did not press further.","Truthfully, Michael would have liked to spend more time with Arianne in Aurora as well. However, he understood that a visitor should not overstay their welcome.","Three days had already been enough to introduce her to his family and allow them to grow familiar with her presence.","Arianne's situation was different from Jester's. Jester could pass as a family relative, but Arianne was different. Her lack of understanding of Aurora made her stand out even more. So, for now, it was better to let her return to the Land of Origin.","Michael took another bite of food. Across the table, Lily continued eating with visible reluctance.","Aunt Mia glanced at the clock.","\"Five more minutes.\"","Lily froze.","\"But—\"","Aunt Mia looked at her. Lily immediately swallowed the rest of her complaint.","\"Yes, ma.\"","Michael nearly laughed. Jester remained expressionless.","A few minutes later, Lily finally stood up with her school bag. Compared to her usual energy, she looked unusually stiff.","Aunt Mia walked over and adjusted her collar.","\"Don't be nervous.\" Aunt Mia smiled gently.","Lily lowered her head slightly.","Michael stood as well.","\"I'll go with you.\"","Lily immediately looked at him.","\"You will?\"","Michael raised an eyebrow.","\"Of course. Taking you to school is much faster with me, no?\"","Some of the tension on Lily's face disappeared. Then she glanced at Jester.","Jester looked back at her. After a moment, he said calmly, \"Do well.\"","Lily smiled again.","\"I will.\"","Michael looked toward Aunt Mia.","\"We'll be back later.\"","Aunt Mia nodded.","\"Take care of her.\"","Michael smiled.","\"I will.\"","Soon after, Michael and Lily left the house together. The moment the door closed behind them, Lily took a deep breath.","Michael glanced at her.","\"Nervous?\"","\"...Yes.\"","Michael laughed softly.","\"Just accept whatever comes to you, and you'll be fine as long as you're open to any possibility. For hundreds of years everyone in Aurora has gone through this, and regardless of the results, life continued. Right?\"","Lily was silent for a moment before nodding. The two continued walking.","Outside, the city was already unusually lively. Students in uniforms could be seen everywhere, each heading toward their respective schools.","Some looked excited. Others looked terrified. Some moved in groups, loudly discussing what class they hoped to awaken. Parents stood at gates, roadsides, and bus stops, offering advice even when their children clearly did not want to hear it.","The entire city seemed to be holding its breath. Today, countless lives would change. Some for the better. Some for worse. And some would remain exactly the same.","Lily looked at the streets. Then at Michael.","\"What if I don't awaken?\"","Michael's answer came immediately.","\"Then nothing changes.\" He continued walking. \"You'll still be Lily.\"","Lily smiled faintly.","\"Mm.\"","The two walked a few more steps until they reached a dark alley, where Michael immediately used his spatial powers.","After dropping Lily off at her school and saying goodbye, Michael did not immediately leave. Instead he went to settle in a nearby establishment and waited until noon.","Regardless of the result from Lily's awakening, he needed to leave Aurora soon. A little anxious, and not wanting to spend the rest of his day at home or do anything else, he figured he'd just wait to see the result of his cousin's awakening himself.","Inside school, Lily behaved no differently than usual. At least on the surface. She chatted with her classmates when they spoke to her. To anyone watching, she appeared completely normal.","Only Lily knew that her thoughts had barely stayed inside the classroom all morning. Every few minutes, her eyes drifted toward the clock. Every few minutes, she found herself wondering the same thing.","Would she awaken?","The question repeated itself endlessly. Fortunately, she wasn't alone. Today, almost the entire class was distracted. Even students who normally slept through lessons were paying attention to the time.","Every once in a while, whispers broke out.","\"What class do you think you'll get?\"","\"I just want to awaken.\"","The discussions never stopped. As the hours passed, the atmosphere gradually grew more tense.","Even the teachers seemed distracted. After all, an Awakening Ceremony wasn't only important for students. Teachers felt nervous too. Every awakened student improved a school's reputation.","By the time noon finally arrived, almost nobody could focus anymore.","Then the classroom door opened. Instantly, every conversation stopped.","The homeroom teacher entered. Floating beside her was a small anti-gravity platform. Resting atop it was an orb roughly the size of a human head."]},{"number":1063,"title":"Chapter 1063: Failure","paragraphs":["The moment students saw the orb, the entire classroom went silent. Nobody needed an explanation. Everyone recognized it immediately.","The Awakening Orb. The artifact responsible for awakening countless lives every year.","Lily unconsciously straightened in her seat. Even her breathing slowed.","The teacher guided the floating platform to the front of the classroom before turning around. For a moment, she simply looked at the students. A faint smile appeared on her face.","\"Everyone, today is your awakening ceremony. If you fail to awaken, do not worry, as this is only your first time. You'll have another chance next year, and the year after that. Of course, it would be great to awaken on your first try, haha.\"","Thanks to the Federation's deliberate timing, before university, the average age range in a middle-school-to-high-school class stayed very similar.","One could only be older, never younger. In Lily's class, the youngest was sixteen and the oldest was seventeen.","At this age they should already be in their first year of high school, but until the awakening ceremony passed, they remained middle school students even if they had technically graduated.","Only after the ceremony would a new chapter in their life begin. The same was true for those who were eighteen and having their last awakening ceremony.","Though the visible changes between failing and succeeding weren't always obvious, the significance remained.","The homeroom teacher finished her brief explanation before glancing down at the attendance sheet in her hand. Then she frowned.","\"Hm?\"","The teacher counted the students again. Her frown deepened.","\"There should be thirty-five students here.\"","The classroom went quiet. Several students looked around as well. Only then did some of them realize a particular seat was empty.","The teacher's gaze slowly moved through the classroom before eventually landing on Lily. She tapped the attendance sheet.","\"Where is Jester?\"","Several students immediately turned toward Lily. After all, Jester was a somewhat unusual presence in the class. They wondered where he'd gone on such an important day.","Lily remembered Michael's instructions and answered honestly.","\"He's conducting his Awakening Ceremony elsewhere.\"","The teacher's eyebrows twitched.","\"Elsewhere?\"","\"Yes.\"","The teacher stared at Lily for several seconds. Clearly, she wasn't satisfied with the answer. An Awakening Ceremony wasn't something students simply skipped.","Normally she would have immediately demanded an explanation, but unfortunately, Lily wasn't a normal student.","The teacher silently swallowed the words that had nearly left her mouth. Putting aside everything else, Lily herself was already an officially registered Knight at sixteen.","That achievement alone placed her ahead of the overwhelming majority of adults. Even if she never awakened, her future was already brighter than most people's. And if she did awaken, things would become even more ridiculous.","An official cultivator who awakened would most likely receive dual classes. One from her cultivation path. Another from the Awakener system. Such individuals were rare and highly valued.","Then there was the other issue: her cousin.","Michael Norman.","The teacher wasn't ignorant. She knew exactly who Lily's older cousin was. At this point, there were very few people in the city who hadn't heard of Michael.","Truthfully speaking, one of the reasons she was standing in this classroom today was because of him.","Thinking this far, the teacher finally let out a small sigh. Regardless of her personal dissatisfaction, she decided to close one eye.","If Jester truly wasn't here, then there was little she could do. More importantly, she figured everyone was old enough to know exactly what they were doing.","At least she hoped so.","\"Very well.\" The teacher put away the attendance sheet. \"We'll proceed.\"","The topic immediately disappeared.","The teacher's gaze swept across the classroom.","\"Awakening order will follow the class register.\"","Nobody complained or cared. They simply wanted their turn to arrive.","The teacher glanced at the first name. Then spoke.","\"Adrian Walker.\"","A boy stood up promptly. His legs looked slightly stiff. Several classmates chuckled. Unfortunately, none of them looked much better.","Adrian slowly walked toward the front of the classroom. The closer he got to the orb, the quieter the room became.","Finally, he stopped directly before it. The creamy-white sphere reflected his nervous face.","The teacher spoke calmly.","\"Place both hands on the orb.\"","Adrian swallowed and obeyed. The moment his palms touched the surface, several students immediately leaned forward in their seats.","For a few seconds, nothing happened.","Then the light began to change. Thin streams of silver energy appeared inside the orb.","The teacher's eyes immediately sharpened.","The silver streams inside the orb grew brighter and brighter. Then they exploded outward.","A collective gasp swept through the classroom.","Behind the boy's body, a translucent image slowly formed. A sword and a shield. The two floated behind him in a crossed position, radiating a faint silver glow.","The teacher smiled.","\"Congratulations. You awakened the Knight class.\"","The young man and the entire class froze. For a brief moment nobody reacted. Then the realization hit.","\"He awakened!\"","\"Seriously?!\"","\"First try?!\"","The classroom erupted.","The boy himself stared blankly at the sword and shield behind him. A moment later, several translucent blue panels appeared before his eyes. His body trembled.","He had succeeded. He had really awakened.","The teacher raised a hand.","\"Quiet.\"","The classroom immediately calmed down.","The teacher nodded.","\"Stand to the side.\"","Still dazed, Adrian Walker obeyed.","The teacher looked at the next name.","\"Sarah Mitchell.\"","A girl nervously walked forward. Her hands touched the orb. The classroom watched. Several seconds passed. Nothing happened.","The teacher sighed inwardly.","\"No awakening.\"","Sarah's shoulders fell. She quietly returned to her seat.","The third student. Failure.","The fourth. Failure.","The fifth. Failure.","The sixth. Failure.","The excitement created by Adrian's success gradually faded. Reality was beginning to show itself. Awakening was difficult.","One after another, students stepped forward. One after another, they returned disappointed.","Dylan Parks. Failure.","Emma Watson. Failure.","Ryan Clarke. Failure.","Sophia Johansson. Failure.","Lucas Smith. Failure.","Mira Johnson. Failure.","Nathan Reeds. Failure.","Olivia Browne. Failure.","Kevin Taylor. Failure.","The atmosphere inside the classroom gradually grew heavier. The students waiting their turn became increasingly nervous. Even Adrian's excitement had dimmed somewhat as he watched classmate after classmate fail.","Then another name was called.","\"Ethan Brooke.\""]},{"number":1064,"title":"Chapter 1064: Success","paragraphs":["A tall boy stood up. Compared to the others, he appeared unusually calm. The moment his hands touched the orb, silver light erupted again.","The classroom instantly straightened.","\"It happened again!\"","Inside the orb, silver currents swirled rapidly. Then an image appeared. A long wand, floating above Ethan's right hand. Several water orbs revolved around it.","The teacher's eyes brightened.","\"Water Mage class.\"","The classroom exploded once more.","A second awakener. Ethan himself looked stunned. Unlike Adrian, who had appeared overjoyed, Ethan simply stared blankly at the floating wand.","The teacher smiled.","\"Congratulations.\"","The young man nodded mechanically before moving to stand beside Adrian.","Two awakeners. Out of twenty students. The ratio wasn't terrible. But it wasn't good either.","Unfortunately for everyone else, luck seemed to run out immediately afterward. The next student failed. Then another. And another. The classroom became increasingly silent. The pressure continued to build.","Eventually the teacher glanced down at her list again. Then called the next name.","\"Lily...\"","The moment the words left her mouth, every eye in the classroom turned toward Lily. Including Adrian, Ethan, and the teacher herself. After all, whether they admitted it or not, everyone was curious.","This was Lily. Michael Norman's cousin. The sixteen-year-old Knight. Many wondered if she'd awaken a class.","Lily slowly stood. Her heartbeat thundered inside her chest.","Thump. Thump. Thump.","Taking a deep breath, Lily walked toward the Awakening Orb. The entire classroom watched her approach. Soon she stopped before the sphere. The orb reflected her face.","For a brief moment, silence completely consumed the room.","Then Lily slowly raised both hands. And placed them against the orb.","Outside the school grounds, Michael, who had also been paying attention, swept away his lazy expression and grew more alert.","However, before he could continue, a sharp pain flared across the surface of his palm, and the mark of origin appeared before vanishing again.","If not for the pain, it would have seemed like an illusion.","Michael didn't seem particularly surprised, though. This situation was strange, but it wasn't the first time it had happened.","The earliest instance had been two months ago. Michael hadn't expected a second occurrence to show up today.","\"What's actually happening? Should I just ask the Origin Will?\"","Remembering the effect of a certain title of his, Michael was tempted, but soon shook the idea from his mind.","Not only had this strange thing happened to him, but for some reason it had appeared to a large number of fellow awakeners as well.","When the signs had first appeared, since they were tied to the mark of origin, Michael had immediately logged into his Supers Association forum account to see if he could find anything, only to realize the signs had already been appearing on others a few days before his own.","Unfortunately, no one had any explanation to give.","Still worried, Michael had sought out the directors at his academy, only to discover that some of them had experienced the same signs. Unfortunately, like him, they had no explanation either.","It had been a troubling issue at first, but it was soon forgotten and pushed to the back of many people's minds once the situation didn't repeat itself and everything seemed fine again.","\"For something that's probably affecting all awakeners, I doubt the Origin Will would even answer me. Since I only have a chance of being answered in the first place, not a guarantee, there's no reason to waste it.\"","Michael thought, when suddenly something caught his attention.","\"Huh?!\"","Back in the classroom, Lily remained completely still. Both hands rested against the surface of the Awakening Orb.","The entire classroom watched.","One second passed. Then two. Then five.","Nothing happened.","The orb remained completely silent. A few students subconsciously relaxed. Some looked disappointed. Others weren't surprised. After all, this was the reality of awakening.","Even with Lily's reputation, there was no guarantee she would succeed.","The teacher's expression remained calm. She had conducted enough ceremonies to know that expectations of personal power meant very little before the orb.","Thirty seconds passed. Still nothing.","Lily's heart slowly sank. Had she failed? Though Michael's words echoed in her mind, disappointment still began creeping into her chest.","The classroom grew increasingly quiet. Even Adrian and Ethan exchanged glances.","The teacher finally sighed inwardly. It seemed this was the result.","\"Alright, Lily. You can ret—\"","She never finished her sentence.","The Awakening Orb suddenly trembled. A faint pulse spread through the room. Everyone froze.","The teacher's eyes widened.","Then the orb erupted.","A brilliant emerald light exploded from its surface.","\"W-What?!\"","The classroom instantly erupted into chaos. Unlike the previous awakenings, the light did not remain confined to the orb. Instead, countless green particles spread outward like fireflies.","Leaves began materializing from thin air. Vines. Flowers. Tiny motes of life energy. The entire classroom was suddenly filled with the scent of forests and fresh rain.","Several students stared in disbelief. Some of the flowers even bloomed before their eyes.","At the center of everything stood Lily. The emerald light gathered behind her. Slowly. Gradually. A translucent image began taking shape.","First came roots. Then branches. Then a massive ancient tree appeared behind her, its canopy stretching toward the ceiling.","At the same time, countless vines wrapped around Lily's arms and shoulders like living ornaments. Several glowing butterflies landed upon the branches.","The scene looked beautiful. Almost sacred.","The teacher completely forgot her professional composure.","\"Druid...\"","Her voice barely escaped her lips.","The image behind Lily became clearer. The ancient tree radiated vitality. The butterflies danced. The flowers bloomed. Life energy filled every corner of the room.","Then blue panels appeared before Lily's eyes.","[Awakening Successful.] [Class Obtained: Druid] [Skills Acquired.] [Nature Sense Lv1] [Spirit Bond Lv1] [Taming Lv1] [Minor Healing Lv1] For a moment, Lily simply stared.","She had awakened. She had really awakened.","The realization struck her like lightning.","The next second the classroom exploded.","\"So cool!!!!\"","\"She awakened!\"","\"I knew it!\"","\"Oh my god!\"","The reactions were even louder than when Adrian and Ethan had awakened. After all, Knight and Mage classes appeared somewhat often.","The teacher took a deep breath before forcing herself to calm down.","\"Silence!\"","The classroom gradually quieted, though excitement still remained visible on every face.","The teacher looked at Lily. For the first time that day, genuine envy appeared in her eyes.","\"Congratulations, Lily.\"","Only then did Lily finally recover from her shock. A smile slowly appeared on her face.","\"Thank you.\"","The teacher pointed toward Adrian and Ethan.","\"You may stand with the other awakened students.\"","Still feeling slightly dazed, Lily obeyed. As she walked over, many students looked at her with admiration. Others looked jealous. A few looked depressed.","Such was the nature of awakening ceremonies. Some lives changed in a single moment. Others remained exactly the same.","However, Lily wasn't focused on any of this. Her attention stayed fixed on the panel that had appeared before her eyes.","[ Name: Lily Cole ]","[ Race: High Human ]","[ Class: Druid, Magic Knight ]","[Title: Watched By The Will]","[ Level: 1 ]","[ EXP: 0/100 ]","[ Strength: 7.3 ]","[ Agility: 9.4 ]","[ Constitution: 10.2 ]","[ Intelligence: 14.5 ]","[ Attribute Points: 0 ]","[ Skills: ...... ]"]},{"number":1065,"title":"Chapter 1065: Conclusion and Future Plans [1]","paragraphs":["A smile immediately appeared on Michael's face as he sensed Lily's awakening.","The seriousness that had occupied his expression vanished almost instantly. His shoulders relaxed, and he leaned back into his chair once more.","It would be a lie to say he didn't care whether Lily awakened or not. Of course he cared. She was family.","Though even if Lily never awakened, Michael possessed more than enough resources to forcefully push her to incredible heights and turn her into a powerhouse regardless.","Still, he considered that external help. Who didn't want the people close to them to achieve great things through their own efforts and talents?","Now Lily possessed both. Her own path. And his support.","Thinking about it made Michael's mood improve considerably. The future suddenly looked much more interesting.","With his mind at ease now, Michael's thoughts naturally drifted toward Lily's class.","Among awakeners, there were hundreds upon hundreds of classes. Possibly thousands. No one truly knew the exact number. Unless it was someone's primary area of research, it was impossible to know every class that existed.","Awakeners had existed for an absurdly long time, long enough for entirely new classes to emerge and become permanent parts of the system. For example, the Gunner class.","Originally, it hadn't existed. It had evolved from the Hunter class after generations of awakeners adapted their abilities toward firearms.","Eventually the Origin Will recognized the path. After that, Gunner became a legitimate class capable of being awakened naturally.","Countless similar examples existed. Classes created by civilization. Classes created by accidents. Classes born from evolution. Classes born from entirely new paths. The longer history progressed, the larger the list became.","Michael naturally didn't know everything. However, he did know quite a bit, and Druid happened to be one of the classes he was somewhat familiar with, because it shared similarities with two classes Michael understood very well.","Beast Tamers and Necromancers.","Yes, the Druid class also possessed contract slots, and unlike the Beast Tamer and Necromancer classes, it was classified as a Special Grade Class.","However, while all three classes shared the concept of contracts, the way those contracts functioned was very different.","Among the three, Necromancers possessed the greatest number of contract slots. As they grew stronger, their available slots increased at an astonishing rate.","Beast Tamers came second. Though the gap between them and Necromancers was significant, Beast Tamers still possessed far more contract capacity than most other classes.","Druids, meanwhile, were different. Unlike the first two classes, whose contract capacity continued expanding throughout their growth, Druids possessed a fixed number of slots per rank.","The exact amount depended on the individual's talent and potential. Some Druids started with as little as one slot per rank, indicating limited talent in that regard, while others started with far more.","Yet regardless of the starting number, the growth pattern remained relatively stable.","In that regard, their contracts functioned more like a support system than a primary source of strength, at least when compared to Beast Tamers and Necromancers.","However, that didn't make them weaker. Far from it.","Michael wasn't just happy that Lily had awakened. The class she had awakened added much to his excitement.","This was because the Druid class was arguably one of the most complete classes in existence. A true hybrid. A class that borrowed strengths from multiple paths while avoiding many of their weaknesses.","They possessed decent physical combat ability. Strong magical affinity. Excellent support capabilities. Powerful healing. Natural affinity with beasts. Natural affinity with plants. High adaptability. And respectable contract abilities.","There were very few situations where a Druid became completely useless.","Against undead? They had life energy.","Against beasts? They could communicate with and influence them.","Against warriors? They possessed crowd control and support magic, and they could hold their own in close combat too.","Because of this versatility, Druids could be described as a class without obvious weaknesses. Of course, that description wasn't entirely accurate.","Every class had weaknesses. But compared to specialized classes, Druids had very few glaring flaws. They might not surpass specialists in their own fields. A pure healer would heal better. But their versatility alone made them dangerous.","Michael's gaze suddenly turned thoughtful, and he muttered to himself.","\"I wonder how many classes she awakened.\"","Awakening wasn't always limited to a single class. Individuals who already possessed an established profession before awakening often had a high chance of receiving that profession as an additional class.","Such people were commonly referred to as Dual Awakeners. They were uncommon but far from unheard of.","Triple Awakeners also existed. However, those individuals were genuinely rare.","Some people became unlucky enough to awaken a class identical to their existing profession. Instead of gaining something new, their awakening merely strengthened what they already possessed.","Others were even more unlucky, as despite possessing a profession beforehand, they wouldn't awaken a second class at all. No one truly understood why. The process remained one of the universe's countless mysteries.","Fortunately, Michael wasn't worried about the first possibility. Lily had never been a Druid before awakening. The real question was whether her previous professions had become secondary classes.","Months ago, Lily had already stepped onto the path of a Knight. Though her energy reserves remained limited, her talent had allowed her to enter the cultivation path through her spirit root as well. In theory, both paths had the potential to be recognized by the Origin Will.","If she was lucky, she might possess three classes. Druid. Knight. And whatever class her cultivation path evolved into.","If she was less fortunate, she might only possess the Druid class. Or perhaps Druid and Knight. There were simply too many possibilities.","Michael rubbed his chin.","\"I'll find out soon enough.\"","Initially, he had planned to return home immediately after confirming Lily's awakening. Now he changed his mind. There was no hurry.","After awakening, every successful student was required to register with the Supers Association. The entire process was mandatory. That meant Lily would be leaving the school before long. All he had to do was wait.","Thinking this, Michael leaned back in his chair and relaxed. A smile still lingered on his face. No matter how calm he appeared, he couldn't completely hide his satisfaction.","Lily had awakened. Not only that, she had awakened an excellent class. The Druid class was among the strongest hybrid classes in existence.","A class capable of healing, supporting, fighting, controlling beasts, controlling plants, and forming contracts. Its versatility was indeed an advantage.","More importantly, it suited Lily surprisingly well. Michael had always felt Lily lacked a clear direction, partly because of him. She possessed talent in many areas but didn't overwhelmingly dominate any single path.","The more he thought about it, the more satisfied he became.","Back inside the classroom, the Awakening Ceremony continued. Unfortunately, Lily's success marked the end of the class's good fortune. The orb remained silent again and again.","The excitement that had erupted when Lily awakened gradually faded, replaced by a much heavier atmosphere.","By the time the final student finished, the results had become clear.","Out of thirty-plus students, only three had successfully awakened.","Adrian Walker. Ethan Brooke. And Lily. That was all.","Three awakeners.","The ratio wasn't unusual. If anything, it was considered relatively normal. Yet knowing that fact did little to comfort the students sitting in the classroom.","Many of them stared at the floor. Others stared blankly at their desks. Some looked as though they had expected this outcome. Others looked devastated.","The homeroom teacher silently observed the scene before letting out an inward sigh. She had seen it countless times before. Still, there were things she was required to say.","\"The ceremony isn't over for you.\"","Several students looked up.","\"This is only your first attempt.\" Her voice remained calm. \"You will have another chance next year.\" Then she paused. \"And another the year after that.\"","No one responded. The classroom remained quiet. The students weren't stupid. Everyone knew the truth. The first awakening attempt possessed the highest success rate.","The second year was lower. The third year was lower still. After that, there were no more chances. In fact, rather than saying one had three chances to awaken, one could say that for most people, it was really only one.","From this one could see how unusual Michael's awakening last year had been, and why the principal had been so happy.","The teacher knew what she was saying was mostly sweet nonsense. The students knew it as well. Still, tradition demanded she offer encouragement.","\"As long as you haven't given up, there is still a possibility.\"","A few students nodded weakly. Most simply remained silent.","Truthfully, the teacher wasn't particularly optimistic. Based on experience, if even one of the failed students awakened next year, it would already be considered excellent news. If none awakened, nobody would be surprised. That was simply the difficulty of awakening.","Eventually, seeing there was nothing more she could say, the teacher closed her notebook.","\"Awakened students, follow me.\"","Immediately, countless envious gazes landed on Lily, Adrian, and Ethan. The difference between them and everyone else had already begun.","The teacher led them from the classroom with the awakening orb by her side. As they moved through the school corridors, Lily noticed groups of students from other classes doing the same.","Teachers escorted awakened students toward the administrative building while the unsuccessful students were dismissed for the day.","Curious, Lily began counting. Including her class, the entire school had only produced five awakeners this year.","Five.","The realization weighed on Lily. She had always known awakening was difficult. Seeing the actual numbers made it feel much more real.","\"Only five?\" Ethan quietly muttered beside her.","The teacher overheard him and nodded.","\"Five is already a good result.\"","The three students immediately looked surprised.","The teacher smiled bitterly.","\"You'd be amazed how many schools finish with one or two.\"","Nobody spoke after hearing that.","Soon they arrived at the principal's office. Several teachers were already gathered there. Beside them stood the other newly awakened students from the remaining classes."]},{"number":1066,"title":"Chapter 1066: Conclusion and Future Plans [2]","paragraphs":["What happened next was something the teachers present had already experienced countless times.","The principal first gathered the five awakened students together and offered his congratulations.","\"First of all, congratulations.\" His smile was genuine. \"You have successfully awakened and taken your first step onto a path many people spend their entire lives hoping to enter.\"","The five students immediately straightened.","The principal continued speaking.","\"Talent is important. Luck is important. Opportunity is important. However, awakening is only the beginning. Whether you become powerful or ordinary from this point onward depends on your own efforts.\"","The students nodded.","The principal then spent several minutes giving the standard advice every awakened student in Aurora received.","\"Your awakening has already been recorded by the school,\" the principal continued. \"However, official registration must still be completed. Delaying it can create unnecessary complications later.\"","Everyone nodded again.","Only after finishing his speech did the principal dismiss the group.","\"You may leave now. The school has no further obligations today.\"","The awakened students immediately thanked him before turning to leave.","\"Lily, stay behind for a moment.\"","The room became quiet.","Adrian, Ethan, and the other two awakeners glanced at Lily before leaving. Soon only three people remained.","The principal. Lily. And the homeroom teacher.","The principal waited until the door closed before looking toward Lily. For a moment, he seemed hesitant. Then he smiled.","\"How did your awakening go?\"","At first glance, the question seemed normal, but Lily immediately understood what the principal was actually asking. He wanted to know her real situation.","After a brief moment of thought, Lily answered.","\"It went well. I awakened two classes.\"","The room immediately went silent. Then a smile slowly spread across the principal's face.","\"Dual Awakener?\"","Lily nodded.","\"Yes.\"","The principal's smile widened even further. He didn't ask for the names of the classes, at least not immediately. In reality, Lily's answer had not exceeded his expectations.","Before today, both he and several teachers had privately speculated that if Lily awakened, there was a high chance she would become a Dual Awakener.","After all, she was already a Knight. Unlike ordinary students, she already possessed a profession before awakening.","Among awakeners, it was common knowledge that established professions often transformed into secondary classes after awakening. It wasn't guaranteed, but the probability was very high.","In fact, among cultivators who successfully awakened, becoming a Dual Awakener was more common than remaining a single-class awakener.","It was because of this that, even before her awakening, Jester had advised Lily that if she ever did awaken, there was no need to hide a dual class. Sometimes transparency was better.","Trying to hide something would only make others suspicious.","A triple class, however, was different. That was something worth concealing. But that wasn't the situation Lily currently found herself in.","The principal nodded repeatedly.","\"Excellent.\" His voice carried genuine satisfaction.","As a cultivator himself, he wasn't ignorant regarding awakeners. Though he had never awakened, he possessed enough knowledge to understand the significance of dual classes.","A Dual Awakener often possessed greater potential than ordinary awakeners.","After calming down slightly, the principal spoke once more.","\"I could offer you advice. But honestly, anything I say would probably be less useful than whatever your cousin tells you.\" He laughed.","Lily remained silent. She neither confirmed nor denied the statement. What she was more amazed by was how cautiously and respectfully the principal addressed her older cousin.","Lily found the change slightly strange. Only a year ago, Michael had still been an ordinary student. Now even someone like the principal, who was said to be a step away from the master stage, equivalent to a rank 2 awakener, spoke about him with obvious respect.","A thought appeared in her mind.","Could she become like that someday? Now that she was an awakener, could she also reach a point where people looked at her the way they looked at Michael?","The thought filled her with intense motivation.","The principal naturally didn't know what she was thinking.","\"Well, regardless of what happens next, remember that this will always be your school.\"","Lily nodded.","\"Thank you, Principal.\"","\"Register with the Supers Association as soon as possible,\" he reminded her. \"And listen carefully to whatever plans your cousin has prepared. Someone like him sees things much further ahead than people like us.\"","Lily nodded obediently.","\"I understand, sir.\"","\"Good.\"","The principal stood to see her off.","\"You may go.\"","Lily thanked both him and her teacher before leaving the office. The moment she stepped outside, sunlight greeted her. She looked down at the panel floating before her eyes.","A smile slowly appeared on her face. She couldn't wait to see her family and tell them about her awakening.","However, Lily had only taken a few steps out of the principal's office when suddenly her vision darkened.","When the darkness faded, she found herself standing inside an unfamiliar room. A large table occupied the center, filled with food.","Roasted meat. Fruit. Desserts. Several other dishes. At the left side of the table sat Michael.","The young man looked completely relaxed. One arm rested against the chair while the other held a glass of juice. As though sensing her arrival, he turned his head. A smile appeared on his face as he casually took a sip of his drink.","After three months of cultivation, Michael's understanding of his own prowess only grew stronger. Dragging an ordinary person through the void wasn't particularly difficult.","Though doing the same to a rank 3 supernatural would prove difficult, in his wisdom state, they would only be able to resist for a moment at most.","\"You're finally done.\"","Lily stared blankly as she noticed another chair already prepared for her.","Michael pointed toward it.","\"Sit.\"","\"...\"","\"Why are you looking at me like that?\"","Lily opened her mouth. Then closed it again. All the excitement she had been carrying moments ago suddenly vanished.","For some reason, seeing Michael calmly drinking juice while waiting for her made everything feel normal again."]},{"number":1067,"title":"Chapter 1067: Origin Milestone Achieved!","paragraphs":["Michael raised an eyebrow in confusion.","Lily immediately glared at him.","\"I awakened!\"","\"Good.\"","Michael nodded seriously. Then immediately returned to drinking his juice.","Lily nearly laughed. That was it? She had become an awakener. A Dual Awakener.","The principal had practically treated her like a future celebrity. Yet Michael's reaction was somehow calmer than Aunt Mia asking whether she had eaten breakfast.","The absurdity of it made her shoulders relax. Without realizing it, she sat down.","Only then did Michael place his cup on the table.","\"So?\"","Lily immediately straightened. A smile appeared on her face.","\"I awakened two classes.\"","Michael nodded.","\"I know.\"","Lily's excitement instantly dropped several levels.","Michael almost laughed seeing her expression.","\"What?\"","\"I suddenly don't feel very impressive anymore.\"","Michael leaned back.","\"Why?\"","Lily paused.","Michael pointed at her.","\"You awakened on your first attempt.\" Then he pointed toward the city outside. \"Do you know how many people would trade places with you right now?\"","Lily became quiet.","Michael continued with a smile.","\"You awakened two classes. So yes. You're impressive.\"","For a moment, Lily felt happy hearing those words from him. Then she remembered the thought that had appeared after leaving the principal's office.","Could she become someone like Michael one day? Could she reach the same height? Could people look at her the same way they looked at him?","The thought had filled her with motivation. Now, however—","Lily looked at Michael and lowered her head.","\"...Never mind.\"","Michael frowned.","\"What?\"","\"Nothing.\"","Lily picked up a piece of fruit. A few seconds later she muttered quietly, \"I was wondering if maybe I could catch up to you someday.\"","Michael nearly choked on his juice.","\"Cough!\"","Lily watched him. Michael stared back. Then he burst out laughing.","\"Hahahaha!\"","Lily immediately became annoyed.","\"Why are you laughing?!\"","Michael wiped the corner of his mouth.","\"That's a good goal. I believe you can do it.\"","Lily's eyes brightened slightly.","Then Michael continued.","\"But you'll probably need several miracles, a few divine inheritances, an ancient treasure, and perhaps the universe itself helping you.\"","\"...\"","\"...\"","\"...You're impossible.\"","Michael grinned. Lily rolled her eyes.","In actuality, Michael wasn't lying. To surpass him, Lily would indeed need the help of the universe, much like he himself did, given that even the Origin Will seemed to want to slow his growth.","Michael picked up another piece of fruit and tossed it toward her.","\"Eat first. You just awakened on your first trial. Let's celebrate first. After that, tell me everything.\"","Lily caught the piece of fruit automatically and started eating obediently.","After the meal, Lily finally began recounting everything that had happened during the Awakening Ceremony.","Strictly speaking, Michael already knew most of it. He had been paying attention from outside the school, and with his current senses and abilities, following what happened inside the classroom had not been difficult.","Even so, he did not interrupt her.","Lily spoke with visible excitement. From the moment the homeroom teacher entered with the Awakening Orb, to the first student awakening as a Knight, then the second as a Water Mage, then the failures that followed one after another.","Michael listened quietly the entire time.","Only after Lily finished did he fall into thought.","To be honest, he had originally expected Lily to awaken an ordinary Knight class.","Whether as part of a dual class or triple class awakening, he had thought her existing Knight profession would naturally become a Knight class. He had not expected it to become Magic Knight.","As for the fact that she had not awakened three classes, Michael was slightly disappointed. But only slightly. His greed had limits.","Lily had already awakened successfully on her first attempt. Not only that, she had awakened a Special Grade Class and a Rare Grade Class at the same time.","If he still complained after that, even the heavens might strike him with lightning out of disgust.","Even if Lily had fallen into the unlucky category where her previous profession failed to become a class, awakening itself would have been enough. In that sense, Magic Knight was already an additional reward.","Thanks to his previous advancement rewards and the amount of information he had gained over time, Michael was fairly clear on the details of the Magic Knight class.","As a class that provided four attribute points per level, it could be considered Rare Grade. It was also a hybrid class. It combined martial combat and magic, allowing the user to fight with weapons while enhancing their body and attacks through mana. If needed, they could also fight like mages.","Among Rare Grade Classes, Magic Knight was considered one of the stronger ones.","Thinking this far, Michael could not help but give Lily an odd look.","Lily immediately noticed.","\"What?\"","Michael stared at her for another second. Then he shook his head.","\"Nothing. I just think your luck is strange.\"","\"My luck?\"","Michael quickly explained the concept of rare and special classes.","Though with the Federation finally releasing supernatural knowledge to the public, Lily wasn't as clueless as Michael had been this time last year, Michael still shed more light on the topic.","\"More importantly, both your classes are hybrid classes.\"","Lily slowly lowered the fruit in her hand.","\"Is that good?\"","\"It is very good.\"","Lily's eyes brightened.","Michael leaned back slightly.","\"Druid gives you healing, plant control, beast affinity, spirit contracts, nature magic, and support abilities. Magic Knight gives you close combat, mana reinforcement, weapon skills, and offensive magic.\"","\"Separately, both classes are already strong. Together, they support each other extremely well.\"","Lily listened with growing excitement.","Michael continued.","\"A normal Druid might lack enough direct combat power at the beginning. A normal Magic Knight might lack healing, control, and long-term support. You have both.\"","He pointed at her.","\"That means you can fight directly, heal yourself, restrain enemies, support allies, contract beasts or spirits, and still grow as a Knight.\"","Lily's mouth slowly opened.","Michael smiled faintly at her reaction. Coming this far, he was very pleased. Thanks to his talent, Lily might not be able to surpass him in the future, but it was very possible she could dominate a lot of awakeners in her own rank.","Speaking of talent, though Lily was lucky to awaken a class, her luck still fell short when it came to awakening a talent.","After discussing her classes for a while, Michael was about to bring up her plans for entering the Land of Origin.","Compared to his own start, Michael, who could almost be considered an elder awakener by now, naturally intended to give Lily second-generation privileges.","However, he had only just opened his mouth to speak when suddenly a look of pain appeared on both his face and Lily's.","Immediately, the invisible mark of origin on the surface of their hands appeared without their permission, emitting a subtle heat that caused them both pain.","It wasn't only them. Michael immediately extended his senses across a large part of Brightgate City and checked on the few new awakeners he could spot, only to realize they were all experiencing the same thing.","\"What's happening?\" Lily asked, fear evident in her voice.","Before Michael could reply, a panel suddenly appeared in their vision.","[Universal Milestone Achieved!]","[Five percent of the universe has successfully integrated with the Origin Will] [Opening access to the Origin Battlefield!]"]},{"number":1068,"title":"Chapter 1068: Forced Entry?","paragraphs":["Aside from methods that could increase the possibility of more awakeners, there was another thought most awakeners had entertained at least once.","What would happen if everyone became an awakener?","But was such a reality even possible? Unless every existing awakener decided to kill every non-awakener in existence, it clearly wasn't.","Awakeners had always been treated as a minority. No one had seriously considered what it would mean for their numbers across the universe to reach a truly terrifying scale. After all, the universe was too vast.","But now, every awakener in the universe stared at the same panel.","[Universal Milestone Achieved!]","[Five percent of the universe has successfully integrated with the Origin Will.]","[Opening access to the Origin Battlefield.]","What did five percent of the universe actually mean?","Michael didn't have an accurate grasp of it, but he could tell it was a terrifying number.","A realm with a billion people didn't mean a hundred million of them would be awakeners. The same held true even at ten million, or a million.","The mortality rate for supernaturals, even awakeners, was high. Even in his short time as an awakener, Michael had already come face to face with death several times.","Was it his first encounter with Jester? Or the attack on Woodstone City by demonic supernaturals, barely a week after his awakening?","It was only because of his talent that he had survived those ordeals. But what about those who weren't as lucky?","They were dead.","Michael's time as an awakener was still brief, and because he was so strong, even his own brushes with death hadn't fully shown him how the majority actually lived.","After all, unless someone had no desire for strength at all, every supernatural eventually had to fight for resources.","Even powerful figures like the dean and vice dean of his academy had to spend long stretches in the lower levels of hell just to keep growing, where a single mistake could cost them their life.","Given all this, wasn't it inevitable that awakeners would always remain a cold, small number?","And yet now they made up five percent of the universe's population.","It was a difficult idea to grasp at first, before it slowly became understandable.","Yes, awakeners were rare. But what was the one thing they had that ordinary people didn't?","A long lifespan.","Even an untalented awakener, given enough time, could grind their way up to the peak of rank 2, which represented the highest average tier of awakeners across the universe.","Though that level wasn't particularly strong in the grand scheme of things, even people at that stage could live up to five hundred years.","The mortality rate among supernaturals was high, but not as high as among ordinary people. At least supernaturals could defend themselves. Ordinary people could not.","Every year, new realms containing billions of lives were devoured by supernaturals. Even in the early days of Aurora's apocalypse, demonic supernaturals had casually sacrificed hundreds of thousands of people for their own gain.","Put together with the long lifespans of awakeners, the accumulated total of those who survived long enough could indeed reach a terrifying scale.","What no one had expected, though, was for it to become a milestone the Origin Will itself would acknowledge.","\"What's this, cousin?\" Lily asked, a hint of fear in her voice.","\"I don't know, but it's best if you don't attempt to communicate with your mark of origin. Just remain still,\" Michael's deep voice echoed, a grave expression settling on his face.","Origin battlefield?","Did this have any relation to the Land of Origin? Was it another alternate space that only awakeners could enter?","And given that it was called a battlefield, did that mean only awakeners would exist there, and that they would be forced to fight?","For some reason, none of Michael's thoughts were optimistic.","As several possibilities flashed through his mind, beads of sweat began forming on his forehead.","He was just about to reach for his phone, intending to log into the Supers Association forum to search for anything related to this phenomenon, when several panels appeared before him again.","[The Origin Battlefield is a space catering exclusively to awakeners and serves as their primary intended cultivation ground.] [Each rank possesses its own layer within the Origin Battlefield, governed by its own rules.]","[Awakener Michael Norman detected as a Rank 3 Awakener. Your dedicated battlefield is the Origin Battlefield, Third Layer. Please enter as soon as possible and fulfill your required time quota.] [Required Time Quota:]","Zeroth Layer: 480 hours every 30 days (calculated at 24 hours a day).","First Layer: 240 hours every 30 days.","Second Layer: 7 days every 60 days.","Third Layer: one month every 90 days.","Fourth Layer: one month every 180 days.","Fifth Layer: one month every 365 days.","[Failure to fulfill the required time will result in forced entry. Please make adequate preparations for true body descent.] [Time remaining for awakener to enter: 23:57:56]","\"The Origin Will is forcing me to enter?\"","\"Cousin! Another panel appeared!\" Lily called out in alarm.","Michael first calmed her down before asking for the details of what had appeared in her vision.","Like him, she had received a similar message.","Unlike him, her dedicated location was the Zeroth Layer, but this didn't exempt her from the same forced entry.","Thanks to the information provided by the panels, Michael could understand his situation a bit better, but it didn't make his expression any less grim.","For now, he could tell that, like the Land of Origin, the Origin Battlefield was a space only awakeners could enter. But unlike the Land of Origin, where natives existed, whoever he encountered in this new space would undoubtedly be an awakener.","And worse still, they had to use their true bodies to enter!","One should know that, except in a few rare cases, death in the Land of Origin wasn't true death. An awakener would only lose ten percent of their stats and a clone, and would simply be barred from re-entering the Land of Origin for a while.","But if their true body died, it was true death. And according to the panels, they had to use their actual bodies to enter!","The danger of the situation had just escalated by several levels!"]},{"number":1069,"title":"Chapter 1069: Explosive Growth, Armed to the Teeth, First Entry [1] Lily’s face turned pale.","paragraphs":["\"C-Cousin...\"","For the first time since awakening, fear appeared in her eyes.","\"I'm scared.\"","Michael turned toward her. Seeing the fear on Lily's face, he couldn't help but feel a complicated emotion rise within him.","Just moments ago he had been genuinely happy that his cousin had awakened. She was even a rare Dual Awakener, with two excellent classes.","He had already started thinking about her future and how much stronger she could become.","Now all those thoughts felt far away.","The panel before him remained unchanged.","[Failure to fulfill the required time will result in forced entry.] [Time remaining for awakener to enter: 23:57:21] Michael's expression darkened.","Origin Battlefield. The name alone sounded dangerous. What was worse was that the Origin Will wasn't giving awakeners a choice.","They had one day, then they would be dragged inside.","Michael wasn't afraid for himself. If it truly came down to it, he was confident in his ability to survive.","But Lily?","She had awakened less than an hour ago. She didn't even fully understand her classes yet. Yet now the Origin Will was telling her she would be thrown into a battlefield alongside awakeners from across the universe.","The situation was absurd.","For perhaps the first time since his awakening, Michael felt a trace of anger toward the Origin Will.","No, this was actually the second or third time. The Origin Will had truly put him through a lot already.","Also everyone was getting equally messed up. He didn't have the right to cry out unfair. The timing was simply too ridiculous.","Michael closed his eyes briefly. When he opened them again, his expression had returned to normal.","\"Calm down.\" His voice was steady.","Lily immediately looked toward him.","Michael reached forward and grabbed her wrist.","\"Don't panic.\"","The next moment, space distorted and the two disappeared. A moment later they reappeared inside Michael's house, specifically the living room.","Michael released Lily's hand and sat down on the sofa. Lily immediately sat beside him. Neither spoke for several seconds. The atmosphere was unusually heavy.","Michael stared at the panel floating before him as his mind rapidly processed every piece of information available.","Lily nervously looked at him.","\"Will we die?\"","Michael didn't answer immediately. After a long moment, he finally spoke.","\"Yes. People will definitely die. But not you. If awakeners from the entire universe are being gathered into a place called a battlefield, then people are going to die.\"","His voice remained steady as he rubbed his chin, starting to wonder if he had been too overprotective. Now that he had finally calmed down, he began to realize that his little cousin was just like him.","Perhaps she might not be able to dominate her peers, but if it came down to it, and she made no major mistakes, surviving shouldn't be an issue.","\"Lily, tell me your stats after awakening.\"","[ Name: Lily Cole ]","[ Race: High Human ]","[ Class: Druid, Magic Knight ]","[ Title: Watched By The Will ]","[ Level: 1 ]","[ EXP: 0/100 ]","[ Strength: 7.3 ]","[ Agility: 9.4 ]","[ Constitution: 10.2 ]","[ Intelligence: 14.5 ]","[ Attribute Points: 0 ]","[ Skills: Detect, Nature Sense {Beginner}, Spirit Bond {Beginner}, Taming {Beginner}, Minor Healing {Beginner}, Basic Swordsmanship {Intermediate}, Basic Spearsmanship {Intermediate}, Knight Aura Burst {Beginner} ] [ Traits: Life Seed ]","[ Gifts: Mark of Origin ]","Upon hearing his cousin's stats, Michael couldn't help but let out a series of tsks. He could still remember his own stats when he first awakened.","His highest stat back then hadn't even matched his cousin's lowest stat now, and that was without accounting for the fact that, compared to him at the time, she was already a High Human.","With the same numbers, that made her far stronger than an ordinary human would be.","Then there was her skill set. Putting aside the abilities she'd gained after awakening, the ones she already had from her Knight training were all at an impressive level.","Not only did this mark her as exceptionally skilled, but as an awakener, she would only grow more formidable from here.","\"Hmmm. Now that I think of it, Lily is quite strong. With the right preparation she could probably handle an early-stage Rank 1 monster easily.\" Michael muttered to himself with a smile as he brought out a crystal from his storage space.","\"Here, take it.\" Michael turned to Lily and handed her the crystal.","\"What's this?\" she asked, curious, as she subconsciously used {Detect} on it.","Though she was only a new awakener, this innate skill had come to her naturally, and she had already used it a few times since awakening.","The first person she had used it on had been her cousin, but the information she'd gotten back had only confused her.","[Death Heir ??]","She had wondered what that meant, but unfortunately never gotten the chance to ask.","[Evolution Essence Crystal {Common Grade}]","If used by a monster, can raise the grade of a Common Grade monster to Three-Star Common Grade, the peak of its racial rank.","If used by an intelligent race, can grant 3 to 5 attribute points randomly distributed across any stat below 20 points.","\"Hmm? What's this?!\"","Lily was shocked by the information {Detect} gave her. Though there were quite a few things she didn't understand, she understood the part about stats.","What a precious thing.","\"Try to focus your mind on it and absorb it,\" she immediately heard her cousin's voice beside her.","\"Cousin, isn't this thing precious?\"","Looking at how delicately Lily held the crystal he'd given her, Michael couldn't help but wear an odd expression.","\"You're not wrong in saying they're precious. They really are, but...\"","As he spoke, Michael spread out his hand, and several more crystals appeared from the void and fell to the floor.","\".....\"","[ Name: Lily Cole ]","[ Race: High Human ]","[ Class: Druid, Magic Knight ]","[ Title: Watched By The Will ]","[ Level: 1 ]","[ EXP: 0/100 ]","[ Strength: 20 ]","[ Agility: 20 ]","[ Constitution: 20 ]","[ Intelligence: 20 ]","[ Attribute Points: 0 ]","[ Skills: ... ]","[ Traits: Life Seed ]","[ Gifts: Mark of Origin ]"]},{"number":1070,"title":"Chapter 1070: Explosive Growth, Armed to the Teeth, First Entry [2]","paragraphs":["Michael couldn't help but click his tongue several times.","The more he thought about Lily's stats, the stranger his expression became.","Twenty. Twenty. Twenty. Twenty.","Every single basic attribute had reached exactly twenty points. At level one.","He wasn't sure if such a ridiculous level one awakener existed anywhere else in the universe. Perhaps there were.","After all, the universe was simply too vast for him to confidently claim otherwise. But if they did exist, any level one who could match Lily in pure foundational strength was almost certainly a member of one of those terrifying pure-blood races, like Dragons, Titans, Phoenixes, and so on.","Thanks to her intelligence stat also crossing the twenty-point threshold, Lily had been lucky enough to gain a skill.","Unfortunately, it was just a messy Earth Spike skill, not a core skill. Had it been a core skill, it might have immediately boosted her strength further, since such skills also started at intermediate mastery.","In any case, the current growth was already drastic. One had to consider that, intelligence stat aside, the current Lily was almost as strong as Michael had been at level 20.","At that stage, Michael had already started handling Rank 2 monsters, so one could imagine just how ridiculous the current Lily truly was.","What was crazier still was that she could grow even stronger thanks to the trait she'd gained when her Knight profession evolved into a class.","[ Trait: Life Seed ]","[ Type: Active ]","[ Mastery Level: Beginner ]","When activated, can boost stats by 20%.","The description alone made clear the trait's effect wasn't something to underestimate. It bore some similarity to the Aura Burst skill used by Knights, but since it was a trait capable of growing stronger over time, it was definitely not a simple one.","Michael was also pleased with the trait's existence for another reason beyond its effect. Though it wasn't technically a talent, it could function as one, once again setting Lily apart from her peers.","At her current stage, as long as Lily wasn't suicidal, Michael felt she should do just fine in the Zeroth Layer of the Origin Battlefield.","However, since the day was still young, and there were still more than twenty hours left before they would be forced to enter, Michael felt there was room for more preparation.","\"Cousin... could you please put me down.\"","Michael heard Lily say. Currently they were in the spatial world of his legendary-grade treasure, and Lily was slung over Michael's shoulder like a sack of rice.","\"Can't do. With the sudden boost in strength, it's not just possible you'd hurt yourself, you'd destroy the environment for no reason.\"","\"But we're not at home anymore! You can drop me now!\"","Since Michael had never made an effort to hide the portals leading into the spatial world of his legendary-grade treasure, Lily, Jester, and even Aunt Mia during her initial curious phase were all aware of them and could enter at any time, aside from helping maintain the structure by infusing mana into the gate.","However, to prevent accidents, the area the three of them could access within the spatial world was kept far from most other entrances and maintained a higher concentration of his undead.","Michael ignored the struggling Lily on his shoulder and led her into a cave set into a hill. After walking a few steps, he emerged into a large clearing.","It was also Lily's first time here.","\"Woooooowwww.\"","All around her she could see screen-like portals similar to the ones in her cousin's room. She couldn't help but wonder why they seemed to lead to different places across Aurora. Was that exactly what they were?","Also at the center of the cave was Jester, who had a large sheet of paper spread across the rocky ground and was studying something on it.","Upon seeing Michael, it stood to greet him, casting a curious glance toward Lily, who remained slung over its master's shoulder like a sack of rice.","At this point, Michael finally set Lily down.","\"Lily successfully awakened, but she's still a bit weak, and I need her to level up a few more times, though not too many. Take her to a few low-tier dimensional cracks, but only let her kill a handful of monsters. Her control over her own strength should reach a satisfactory level before tomorrow noon. Please handle this.\"","\"Yes, master.\"","Yes, after stabilizing the empire back in the Land of Origin, Jester, whose workload had significantly decreased, had taken over managing the rest of Michael's dimensional cracks.","Thanks to Michael having previously sold off his rights to the other cracks, Jester's control over the remaining ones was absolute, and he could do as he pleased with them.","Lily didn't quite understand what the two of them were discussing, but she was happy to see Jester.","After the two identical figures, one looking older, one looking younger, finished their exchange, she finally took a step forward to greet him.","Unfortunately, she had only taken a single step when, due to her immense strength and lack of control, her foot sank straight into the ground, leaving her stuck and stunned.","Michael couldn't bear to keep watching and left Jester to handle it. As for himself, he returned to the Supers Association and purchased several necessities for Lily.","Thanks to his inventory, she wouldn't lack for weapons or armor, but items like potions, guns, or bombs could only be acquired in Aurora. Potions existed in the Land of Origin as well, but Aurora's versions were simply of better quality, thanks to its technology.","Several hours passed this way.","A new day arrived, and only two hours remained until the Origin Will would force them into the Origin Battlefield.","Right now, Lily and Michael were back in the spatial world of his legendary-grade item, reviewing Lily's growth over the past day.","[ Name: Lily Cole ]","[ Race: High Human ]","[ Primary Class: Druid, Level 5 ]","[ EXP: 13/**** ]","[ Sub Class: Magic Knight, Level 3 ]","[ EXP: 36/**** ]","[ Title: Watched By The Will ]","Thanks to a strange presence surrounding you, you have attracted the gaze of the Origin Will.","Effect: Gain 1.5 times more experience points.","[ Strength: 40.3 ]","[ Agility: 50.5 ]","[ Constitution: 60.7 ]","[ Intelligence: 70.6 ]","[ Attribute Points: 10 ]","[ Skills: ... ]","[ Traits: Life Seed ]","[ Contract Slots: 2 / 5 ]","[ Gifts: Mark of Origin ]","Thanks to Michael's dimensional cracks, Lily had been able to level up a few times.","Of course, she could have reached max level in both classes given the sheer abundance of monsters, but Michael had deliberately stopped her before she advanced too far.","Too much sudden strength wasn't necessarily a good thing.","As for why her classes sat at different levels, that came down to her identity as a Dual Awakener. Although both classes accumulated experience simultaneously, they didn't necessarily gain levels at the same speed.","This was because awakeners with multiple classes could designate one class as their Primary Class and the others as Secondary Classes.","Doing so didn't weaken the secondary classes or the awakener in any way. Instead, it simply changed how experience points were distributed.","The Primary Class received the larger share. The remaining classes received proportionally less.","The designation wasn't permanent either. At any time, an awakener could freely switch which class was primary. It simply depended on the individual's circumstances.","For Lily, Michael had temporarily made the Druid class her primary class.","In any case, thanks to leveling up, Lily's attributes had received another sweeping upgrade.","Every level granted awakeners attribute points. The amount depended on their race and classes. Ordinary Humans received two points per level from their race.","High Humans received six. Rare Grade classes granted four attribute points. Though Druid was a Special Grade class, it also granted four.","As a High Human possessing both a Rare Grade and a Special Grade class, Lily received an astonishing fourteen attribute points every time she leveled up. Six from her race. Four from the Druid class.","Four from the Magic Knight class. Fourteen points, per level.","That alone had granted her one hundred and twelve attribute points across a combined level of 8.","After distributing them carefully, on top of the natural increases from leveling, Lily's foundation underwent yet another astonishing transformation.","Even Michael had to admit the number was absurd. It was only now that he truly realized Dual Awakeners weren't nearly as simple as he'd assumed.","If one thought about it properly, didn't this mean a rank 0 Dual Awakener with two maxed classes was effectively the equivalent of a level 20 human, or a level 10 undead?","Michael turned to look at Lily's appearance.","Setting aside her battle gear, she also now had two creatures by her side.","One was a familiar forest wolf, and the other was a bull-like creature.","These were the monsters Lily had decided to tame the previous day, which had also revealed her contract slots, capped at five per rank.","It wasn't a low number for a Druid at all.","As the deadline on the timer drew closer, Michael offered a few last pieces of advice and made sure they were both in top condition.","The moment the timer hit zero, the two figures vanished from where they stood."]},{"number":1071,"title":"Chapter 1071: Earth","paragraphs":["After the flash of darkness disappeared, Lily found herself standing inside a forest.","The first thing she noticed was the absence of sunlight. There was a sky above her, but no sun. No moon either. Only a dull gray canopy of clouds stretching endlessly overhead, casting the entire forest in dim, gloomy light.","The trees around her were tall and twisted, their bark dark and rough. Strange moss covered their roots, and faint mist drifted between the trunks.","Before Lily could properly examine her surroundings, a panel appeared before her eyes.","[You have entered the Origin Battlefield]","[Current Location: Zeroth Layer]","[Region: Level 1 Mistwood Forest]","That was all. No detailed explanation, no guide, not even a warning.","Lily frowned.","\"That's it?\"","She waited for another panel to appear, but nothing happened. After several seconds, she dismissed the panel and carefully looked around. The forest was quiet, and no sound could be heard.","Lily's grip tightened around the sword at her waist. Only when she felt two familiar presences beside her did the tension in her shoulders ease slightly.","A low growl sounded from her left. The Forest Wolf stood there, its light green fur blending into its surroundings, sharp eyes scanning the area.","On her right stood the bull-like creature she had tamed the previous day, its body bulky and covered in dark brown hide, two curved horns extending from its head.","Fortunately, they had followed her in. This was one of the things Michael had worried about before she entered. He hadn't been sure whether the Origin Battlefield would allow contracted creatures to follow their masters inside.","After all, this place seemed different from the Land of Origin. If the connection between her and her tamed beasts hadn't been recognized, she would have been forced to enter alone.","Thankfully, it worked. The two contract slots hadn't been wasted.","Lily slowly placed a hand on the wolf's head.","\"Good. You're here.\"","The wolf gave a soft sound in response. The bull-like beast snorted and scraped one hoof against the ground.","Seeing them both made Lily's nervous heart calm down a little. She wasn't afraid, thanks in part to the mental training Jester had put her through over the past months, and her training and tests besides.","Of course, the virtual reality games she had played growing up had also played their part in her composure.","After calming down a bit more, Lily checked her storage space and saw that everything placed inside still remained there. Looking over the sheer quantity, though, her lips twisted slightly.","Aside from the familiar crystals meant to boost her stats, there were several items that, had the Federation caught her carrying them before her awakening, would have gotten her charged with arms trafficking.","After checking everything once more, Lily couldn't help but mutter under her breath.","\"Cousin really is an overthinker...\"","She looked around the quiet forest again. There were still many things she didn't understand about awakeners. In fact, she had only become one yesterday. She wasn't even officially registered yet.","Even so, she wasn't completely ignorant anymore. After everything Michael and Jester had taught her over the past day, she could already tell that her current strength simply didn't make sense for someone at her level.","Lily lowered her gaze to her own hand.","\"...I think I'd still be fine with just a sword and armor.\"","Of course, she was still grateful for everything Michael had prepared. None of the items inside her storage space were ordinary. Take the Evolution Essence Crystals, for example.","Initially, she had assumed their greatest use was as treasures for increasing an awakener's attributes. Only after Michael explained them properly did she realize that wasn't even their primary purpose. Using them to raise stats was actually the wasteful application.","They were evolution resources meant for monsters. According to him, monsters could use them to evolve their race and increase their racial grade.","Naturally, the two beasts standing beside her had benefited from them as well. Lily couldn't help glancing toward the wolf and the bull. Before yesterday, both had only been Common Grade, Two-Star monsters.","At the time, Lily had honestly felt that was already pretty good. She had only just awakened. Being able to tame two Common Grade monsters had already felt like enough.","Then Michael had casually handed her two Evolution Essence Crystals.","Thanks to those, both monsters had successfully advanced from Two-Star Common Grade to the peak of the Common Grade. Three-Star Common Grade.","Thanks to the excess energy, they had also leveled up a few times. The Forest Wolf was now level 7, and the Horned Bull had reached level 8, matching Lily's combined level.","According to Michael, races, equipment, treasures, and even many natural resources all possessed grades. From lowest to highest, they were divided into seven major grades.","Common. Rare. Extraordinary. Epic. Legendary. Mythical. Demigod.","Within each major grade were three smaller quality tiers. One Star. Two Stars. Three Stars. Three Stars represented the peak of that grade. Only after reaching Three Stars could something evolve into the next major grade.","Of course, successfully crossing that boundary was an entirely different matter.","Lily reached over and rubbed the Forest Wolf's neck. Its fur was noticeably glossier than before, carrying a faint emerald sheen beneath the gray light of the forest. Its body had grown larger too.","She subconsciously used Detect.","Forest Wolf","Grade: Three-Star Common","Level: 7 Skills: Bite, Plant Control","Then she looked toward the horned bull.","Horned Bull","Grade: Three-Star Common","Level: 8 Skills: Fierce Charge","As for why she had extra crystals on hand, her cousin had given them to her in case she came across other tameable beasts of lower quality along the way.","According to him, rarity mattered, but she was free to tame whatever she liked, even if it was a rabbit. Though her cousin hadn't exactly agreed with the idea of her taming a rabbit, she knew it was possible, and allowed.","\"Okay, that's enough waiting. Let's explore this place and see what it's for. You two, pay attention!\"","Awwooo!","Moooo!!","\"Be quiet!\"","After wandering through the Mistwood Forest for several minutes, Lily suddenly came to an abrupt stop. The Forest Wolf and Horned Bull halted immediately as well.","Lily's eyes narrowed.","\"...Come out.\"","Silence. Only the gentle rustling of leaves answered her.","Lily slowly shifted her stance, her right hand tightening around the hilt of her sword.","\"I know you're there.\"","Her heartbeat sped up. For a while now she had sensed a presence following her without revealing itself.","\"I'll count to three.\"","\"One...\"","\"Two...\"","Before she reached three, a soft laugh echoed through the forest.","\"Hehe...\"","A graceful figure stepped out from behind one of the enormous trees.","Lily froze.","The girl looked no older than her. She possessed long silver hair that reached her waist and skin the color of polished obsidian. Two long, pointed ears protruded through her hair, immediately identifying her race.","She wore clothing that exposed far more skin than Lily felt was practical for combat.","Dark leather wrapped around her slender body while several silver ornaments decorated her waist and thighs. Despite the revealing attire, not a single one of her movements seemed wasted.","The Forest Wolf immediately bared its fangs.","\"Grrrr...\"","The Horned Bull pawed at the ground.","Lily instinctively activated Detect, and a panel appeared.","[Assassin Level 10]","Realm: Umbra Grove","\"A Dark Elf?\"","Lily muttered unconsciously.","The moment Detect finished, the elf raised an eyebrow.","\"Oh?\"","A surprised smile appeared on her beautiful face.","\"Interesting.\" She tilted her head slightly. \"How did a level five human notice me while I was using Shadow Veil?\"","Lily didn't answer. Michael had repeatedly warned her not to casually reveal information. Instead, she simply tightened her grip on her sword.","The Dark Elf smiled even wider.","\"I suppose it doesn't matter.\"","She slowly drew two curved daggers. Silver light reflected off their blades.","Lily's expression immediately turned vigilant.","\"You should leave.\"","The Dark Elf laughed softly.","\"And why would I do that?\"","\"I don't want to fight.\"","\"Neither do I.\" The elf's smile turned strangely charming. \"I simply want everything you're carrying.\"","Her gaze swept casually over Lily. \"The armor. The sword. They look very expensive. Are you from some noble family out there, perhaps?\"","Lily's face turned cold.","\"I suggest you don't get any ideas.\"","The Dark Elf giggled.","\"What an adorable threat.\"","The next instant, she disappeared.","Lily didn't panic.","Yet before either side could collide, a calm voice echoed through the forest.","\"Attacking someone on our first day.\" \"...How low.\"","The Dark Elf's expression changed.","Someone else?","The shadows several meters away suddenly twisted. A tall figure calmly stepped out from within them.","Lily's heart skipped a beat. She hadn't sensed this person. Not even once. Unlike the Dark Elf, whose presence she had picked up on immediately, this newcomer had been standing nearby the entire time without her noticing in the slightest.","The newcomer wore rags and shared a similar complexion to the elf, though darker.","The two girls immediately activated Detect on the new arrival.","[Dark Knight Level 10]","Realm: Earth"]},{"number":1072,"title":"Chapter 1072: Powerful Youth","paragraphs":["Earth.","The name sounded unbelievably ordinary, yet for some reason it lingered in the minds of both girls. That brief distraction lasted only an instant before their attention returned to the young man standing between them.","He appeared to be around their age, perhaps a year older at most. His black hair was messy, reaching just past his ears as though it hadn't been cut in months.","His clothes were even worse. The dark tunic he wore had been patched together so many times that it was difficult to tell what its original color had been. Several tears remained unrepaired, exposing parts of his arms and shoulders.","His trousers weren't much better. One leg had been stitched together using coarse thread, while the other had a long tear running from the knee downward.","Even his boots looked ready to fall apart.","The only thing on his body that appeared properly maintained was the sword resting in his right hand, but even that wasn't an impressive weapon. It was simply an ordinary longsword.","Despite its plain appearance, the blade had been polished so carefully that one could almost see their reflection upon its surface. It was obvious someone took meticulous care of it.","If one ignored the fact that he had silently approached the two of them without either girl sensing him, no one would ever associate him with the word \"danger.\" He looked more like a wandering refugee than an awakener.","If someone without any knowledge were asked who among the three looked strongest, almost everyone would point toward the Dark Elf or Lily first. The young man would undoubtedly be ranked last.","Yet neither girl dared underestimate him.","The Dark Elf slowly narrowed her crimson eyes.","\"...Who are you?\"","The young man looked at her quietly. After a brief pause, he answered.","\"...A human.\"","The Dark Elf's eyebrow twitched.","\"I can see that.\" She tightened her grip on her daggers. \"I asked who you are.\"","The young man remained silent for another moment. Then he shrugged.","\"...Just another survivor. But let me ask my own question now. Are your worlds, or based on the system's 'term' for it, also facing an apocalypse?\"","The question caught both girls off guard.","\"...Apocalypse?\"","Lily unconsciously repeated the emphasis in his words. The Dark Elf also frowned. For a brief moment, neither of them answered.","The young man quietly observed their expressions before speaking again.","\"...So your worlds weren't?\"","The Dark Elf clicked her tongue.","\"What kind of stupid question is that?\"","The next instant, she vanished. A blur of darkness flashed across the forest. Her twin daggers aimed directly for the young man's throat and heart.","Clang!","Sparks erupted. The ordinary-looking longsword somehow appeared exactly where it needed to be, knocking both daggers away with frightening precision.","The Dark Elf's pupils shrank.","Fast.","Before she could retreat, the young man stepped forward. His left hand caught her wrist. His shoulder crashed into her center of gravity. His foot hooked behind her ankle.","In a single flowing motion, the Dark Elf found herself slammed against the trunk of a nearby tree.","Bang!","Before she could react further, the young man's sword rested against her neck while one arm pinned both of her wrists above her head.","The entire exchange had lasted barely two seconds.","Lily's eyes widened.","\"So fast...\"","The Forest Wolf lowered itself instinctively. Even the Horned Bull took several uneasy steps backward.","The Dark Elf struggled violently.","\"You bastard!\"","She tried twisting her body. Her knees. Her elbows. Even her head. Every movement was instantly neutralized before it could build any momentum.","\"...Impossible.\" She grit her teeth. \"We're both Level Ten.\"","The young man remained expressionless.","\"...Yes.\"","His grip never tightened. Nor did it loosen. He wasn't even hurting her. He was merely preventing her from moving.","\"You...\" The Dark Elf glared at him. \"...Who exactly are you?\"","The young man ignored the question. Instead, he calmly spoke.","\"If you move again...\" For the first time since appearing, his voice became slightly colder. \"...I'll assume you wish to die.\"","The forest suddenly went silent. The Dark Elf instinctively stopped struggling. For just a fraction of a second, she had felt it.","Killing intent.","The young man slowly continued.","\"...The only reason you're still alive...\" His eyes met hers. \"...is because you're the first Dark Elf I've ever seen.\"","\"...\"","\"So I'm curious.\"","\"...\"","\"Don't mistake curiosity for kindness.\"","The Dark Elf's breathing unconsciously slowed. Every instinct she possessed screamed at her not to provoke this human any further.","Only after several long seconds did the young man slowly release her wrists and take two steps backward. He even lowered his sword, but the Dark Elf didn't dare attack again.","Lily quietly watched everything unfold. A solemn expression appeared on her face.","According to Cousin Michael, High Humans possessed physical foundations vastly superior to ordinary Humans.","Even if their stats were identical, a High Human should easily overpower a normal Human because of the difference in racial quality. That was one of the greatest advantages of possessing a superior race.","And yet, why did she feel threatened? It was as though the young man standing before her possessed something that made him extraordinarily dangerous. It wasn't his level, and it surely wasn't his equipment.","His clothes were practically rags, and his sword was completely ordinary. Even Detect hadn't shown any extraordinary title, race, or equipment.","Yet Lily couldn't shake the feeling.","Right now, every instinct she possessed was telling her the same thing.","This young man was not normal.","The young man seemed to notice the way both girls were looking at him. He sighed softly.","\"...Now.\" His gaze swept over Lily before shifting toward where the Dark Elf had stood. \"Can someone answer my question?\" He paused. \"Were your worlds already ending before you entered this battlefield?\"","The Dark Elf remained where she stood for several more seconds. Her crimson eyes shifted between Lily and the ragged young man. She clicked her tongue in annoyance.","\"Tch.\"","There was no fear left on her face. Only frustration. The beautiful human girl clearly wasn't easy prey. As for this strange young man, she had absolutely no confidence in defeating him."]},{"number":1073,"title":"Chapter 1073: New World","paragraphs":["After another brief silence, the dark elf snorted.","\"...You're both weird.\"","Without another word, darkness gathered beneath her feet. Her figure melted into the surrounding shadows before disappearing into the forest at high speed. Within moments, even her presence could no longer be sensed.","Silence returned. Only Lily, the young man, the Forest Wolf, and the Horned Bull remained.","Lily studied him quietly. Compared to how calmly he had subdued the Dark Elf, his attitude toward her seemed strangely different. He wasn't relaxed. If anything, he appeared wary.","She subconsciously shifted her body to adjust her posture.","Crunch.","The young man's reaction was immediate. He took one equally measured step backward. At the same time, he instinctively raised his ordinary-looking sword into a guarded stance.","Lily blinked.","\"...Huh?\"","She hadn't expected that.","The young man spoke before she could ask anything.","\"I know you're powerful.\" His eyes remained fixed on her every movement. \"But I bear no malice toward you.\"","\"...\"","\"I don't want to fight. I only wanted to ask a few questions.\"","Lily looked down at the sword he continued holding between them. Though her cousin and Jester had warned her to be very wary of strangers, since this young man seemed to bear no malice and could only give her a slight sense of threat, Lily wasn't in any hurry to leave.","For one thing, this was the second person she had seen in this unfamiliar space, and the only one who was at least willing to talk.","\"What do you want to know?\" she asked.","\"Are you an awakener as well? The system, before dragging me here, seemed to have called me that, so I'm assuming you're the same as me.\"","\"Yes. I'm an awakener.\"","Lily was a bit confused by the youth. Though he spoke intelligently, he seemed severely ignorant compared to her, for some reason. Seeing that Lily was willing to answer his question, the youth had a brief look of excitement cross his face before he forcefully calmed his emotions down.","\"This realm thing, is it like another term for planets?\"","\"Planets?\"","Lily was stunned. To think someone would mention such an old-era term. According to history, this had once been the name for a world, back when humans could use machines to reach space.","But after the apocalypse descended, people started calling planets realms, and only the strong, or those with technology far superior to what had existed in the olden age, could reach space again.","Though confused, Lily still answered the young man.","\"Yes, realms are like planets, but nobody uses that term anymore.\"","\"Nobody uses that term anymore?\"","The young man was visibly confused for a moment before he seemed to understand something. But before he could ask another question, Lily beat him to it.","\"At first I was confused, and I'm still not sure, but hearing apocalypse and planet from you, I can't help but have some assumptions. Is it possible that...\"","At this point Lily seemed to hesitate.","\"Is it possible that your world is a newly initiated realm?\"","Upon hearing her question, the youth in front of her was visibly taken aback.","The young man remained silent for several seconds. His grip around the sword unconsciously tightened.","\"...Newly initiated realm?\"","He repeated the unfamiliar phrase slowly, as though tasting each word.","Lily nodded.","\"It means a realm where the Origin Will has only recently descended.\"","This was something Lily had learned after borrowing Michael's account on the Supers Association forum that morning.","The young man lowered his head slightly.","Lily looked at him carefully. The more she observed him, the stranger he seemed.","Finally, the youth raised his head again.","\"...Answer one more question for me.\"","Lily nodded cautiously.","\"What?\"","He looked directly into her eyes.","\"So... your world really isn't facing an apocalypse?\"","\"No.\" Lily answered honestly. \"It isn't.\"","The young man frowned.","\"No monsters appearing everywhere?\"","\"No.\"","\"No cities collapsing?\"","\"No.\"","\"No people dying from monsters that appeared out of strange cracks?\"","\"...No.\"","His expression grew even more complicated.","Lily couldn't help asking, \"When did the Origin Will descend in your world?\"","The young man blinked.","\"The Origin Will?\"","Lily pointed upward.","Understanding immediately appeared on his face.","\"...Ah. So that's what it's called. I've always called it the system. It just made so much sense to follow the terms in novels.\"","He thought for a moment before answering.","\"About two months ago.\"","\"...Two months?\"","Lily froze. Her eyes widened.","\"Only... two months?\"","The young man nodded.","\"Yes. My world changed a year ago, but this system, no, the Origin Will, only appeared two months ago. I got mine five days ago.\"","He spoke calmly.","Lily remained speechless.","Two months. Only two months.","Seeing Lily's stunned expression, the young man asked another question.","\"...Why are you surprised?\"","Lily slowly answered.","\"Because...\" She hesitated before continuing. \"...our world has had the Origin Will for almost three hundred years.\"","Silence.","The forest itself seemed to freeze.","\"...Three...\" The young man's lips moved slightly. \"...hundred?\"","Lily nodded.","\"Yes. The apocalypse happened centuries ago. Our ancestors survived it. The Federation was established afterward. The world gradually recovered, and if you're powerful enough, you can even visit other realms, or planets, as you call them.\"","The young man stood completely still.","Three hundred years.","His mind instinctively began calculating. He slowly let out a long breath.","\"...I understand now.\"","Lily tilted her head.","\"What?\"","He looked at her before speaking quietly. Then, for the first time since they had met, a faint smile appeared on his face.","\"...Thank you.\"","Lily blinked.","\"...For what?\"","\"For answering. I've been wondering whether Earth was simply unlucky.\" His eyes drifted toward the gray sky. \"Now I know we're truly just unlucky.\"","Lily remained silent. Despite the calm expression on his face, she could hear the exhaustion hidden beneath those words.","At this point she could understand what was going on.","This Earth. This Earth seemed to be in the same situation Aurora had faced more than three hundred years ago, and this youth was from there."]},{"number":1074,"title":"Chapter 1074: Outlier","paragraphs":["Compared to Lily, whose situation remained relatively stable, Michael ran into a problem the instant he arrived in the Origin Battlefield.","Unlike the gloomy forest Lily had entered, Michael found himself standing atop an enormous mountain range.","Jagged peaks stretched beyond the horizon like countless swords piercing the heavens. The sky above was completely clear. Yet there was no sun. Even so, one could somehow tell it was daytime.","The strange light illuminating the world seemed to come from the sky itself rather than any celestial body.","Ordinarily, Michael would have immediately begun studying his surroundings. Instead, his entire attention remained fixed on the panels floating before him.","[Awakener 'Michael Norman' has been detected to be too powerful for the Third Layer]","[Awakener 'Michael Norman' has been detected to possess the Outlier Status]","[Outlier detected]","[Current combat capability exceeds the extreme threshold of the Third Layer]","[Searching for countermeasures...]","Michael's eyelid twitched.","\"...Again?\"","He couldn't help muttering under his breath. Then, with no one around to hear him, he spent the next several seconds silently cursing the Origin Will, along with its ancestors, assuming something like an ancestor even existed.","\"This thing really has a personal grudge against me.\"","This wasn't the first time the Origin Will had attempted to make his life difficult. Nor the second. Nor even the third.","Compared to his worries for Lily, Michael had entered the Origin Battlefield with complete confidence.","If his suspicions were right, the Third Layer should only contain Rank Three awakeners. Even ignoring his undead legion, his own strength was already sufficient to dominate most, if not all, Rank Three opponents.","Once his undead were factored in, Michael genuinely couldn't imagine losing. Surely there wasn't another Rank Three awakener walking around with over two thousand Rank Four undead at their command.","Even if such a monster somehow existed, Michael was convinced that person's forces still couldn't compare to his own.","That was the confidence he had built over months of growth.","Unfortunately, the Origin Will clearly had different ideas.","Michael quietly waited, knowing there was nothing he could do. The Origin Will wasn't something he could negotiate with, fight, or threaten. Knowing this, he simply stood atop the mountain and waited for the verdict.","\"...Just don't erase me from existence.\"","That was honestly his greatest concern. If the Origin Will truly considered him an error, who knew what ridiculous punishment it might choose?","Fortunately, the waiting didn't last long. Several new panels appeared.","[Countermeasure found]","[Awakener 'Michael Norman' possesses combat capability matching a higher battlefield layer]","[Reassigning battlefield layer...]","[Promotion complete]","[Awakener 'Michael Norman' will be transferred to the Fourth Layer of the Origin Battlefield]","Michael stared blankly for several seconds.","\"...That's it?\"","He blinked in surprise.","\"I've been promoted...\"","Relief spread through him almost immediately. At the very least, he hadn't been erased, sealed, or forcibly weakened. From that perspective, this was probably the best outcome possible.","Even so, Michael's expression gradually turned unpleasant.","\"...How annoying.\"","He clicked his tongue. Originally, his situation had been absolutely safe. Now it had merely become safe. There was a difference. A very significant one.","If his suspicions were correct, then every battlefield layer corresponded to a specific rank. The Third Layer should mainly contain Rank Three awakeners. Likewise, the Fourth Layer should primarily belong to Rank Four awakeners. More importantly, it should belong to peak Rank Four awakeners.","Michael slowly rubbed his forehead.","\"I'm not even Rank Four yet...\"","This alone wasn't what worried him, though. After all, he possessed over two thousand Rank Four undead. Michael was fairly certain very few people would be capable of confronting such a force head-on.","His real problem was much simpler. He was only one man. No matter how strong his undead were, no matter how terrifying his legion appeared, the number of Rank Four awakeners throughout the universe had to vastly exceed the number of Rank Four undead under his command.","Tens of thousands. Perhaps hundreds of thousands. He had no way of knowing. But he was certain that among such an enormous population, there had to be at least a few monsters capable of fighting above their rank.","Michael refused to believe otherwise. He himself was proof such people existed. If he could fight beyond his realm, others certainly could as well.","Perhaps there were awakeners capable of slaying ordinary Rank Five opponents while still remaining at Rank Four.","Perhaps there were legendary geniuses out there with Mythical races, Divine inheritances, Legendary talents, Special constitutions, or treasures even he had never heard of.","The universe was simply too vast for him to be the only one of his kind.","Unfortunately, whether Michael was willing or not did not matter. The Origin Will had already made its decision. More panels appeared before him.","[Transfer preparations complete]","[Balance restored]","[Outlier adjustment successful.]","Then, after a brief pause, another panel appeared.","[As compensation for the inconvenience caused by the forced reassignment...]","[Suitable compensation is being evaluated...]","[Compensation package currently under preparation]","Michael raised an eyebrow.","\"...Compensation?\"","He hadn't expected that. Knowing the Origin Will, he had assumed it would simply throw him into the Fourth Layer and call it a day. The fact that it was actually preparing compensation surprised him a little.","\"...At least you still have a conscience.\"","Of course, he didn't lower his guard. For all he knew, the compensation might simply be an Epic Grade weapon, handed over as a formality.","Before Michael could think any further, the space around him distorted. His surroundings blurred, and the mountain range disappeared. The next moment, his feet landed firmly on solid ground once more.","Michael immediately looked around. The scenery had completely changed.","He was still standing within a mountain range, but unlike before, these mountains were far taller and far more rugged.","Dark cliffs stretched toward the heavens like gigantic walls. Ancient trees clung stubbornly to impossible slopes, while rivers of silver water flowed through the valleys below.","The sky remained perfectly clear. This time, however, it was night. Unlike the Third Layer, there was no strange daylight without a sun. Instead, countless unfamiliar stars covered the heavens.","Three enormous moons hung in the distance, each emitting a different color. One pale white. One deep blue. One faint crimson. The entire world was illuminated beneath their combined glow.","Michael only spared them a brief glance, because the very next instant, his eyes widened.","\"...This mana...\"","His breathing unconsciously slowed. Every breath he took caused mana to pour into his body at an astonishing rate. The surrounding mana wasn't merely abundant. It was incredibly dense.","\"Such dense mana...\"","Michael closed his eyes for a brief moment. He could feel mana naturally flowing into every cell of his body, even without actively cultivating. When he opened his eyes again, surprise crossed his face.","\"...It's even richer than the Land of Origin.\"","That conclusion shocked him.","The Land of Origin was already widely recognized as the greatest cultivation ground in existence. Yet compared to the Fourth Layer, it was actually a few levels inferior. Not by an overwhelming margin, but inferior nonetheless. At least in terms of mana density.","A thoughtful expression crossed Michael's face.","Starting from Rank Three onward, cultivation gradually shifted. Mana refinement remained important, but the soul became the true focus. Of course, that didn't mean the body had been abandoned.","Many powerful supernaturals still spent countless years cultivating their physique while meditating to accumulate mana. After all, no matter how advanced one's soul became, a weak body remained a weakness. Most experts still advanced traditionally.","Michael was simply abnormal. His growth had skipped countless intermediate steps thanks to his talent, which repeatedly allowed him to leap over years, sometimes decades, of ordinary cultivation.","Rather than slowly refining his body over countless meditation sessions, he would occasionally receive an instantaneous increase in strength. A single evolution could accomplish what might take another awakener years of cultivation.","Because of that, Michael had never truly appreciated environments meant for cultivation. Until now.","Feeling the astonishing mana density surrounding him, he suddenly understood why so many ancient experts secluded themselves for centuries. If someone cultivated here continuously, their progress would undoubtedly be terrifying.","\"...This place really is meant for the powerful.\"","Michael slowly exhaled. Then another thought crossed his mind.","\"If even the Fourth Layer has mana density like this...\" He slowly lifted his gaze toward the three moons overhead. \"...then what kind of environment exists in the Fifth Layer?\"","For the first time since arriving in the Origin Battlefield, Michael found himself genuinely curious.","Just then, another familiar panel appeared before him.","[You have entered the Origin Battlefield]","[Current Location: Fourth Layer]","[Region: Level 1 Earthly Peak]","\"Level 1? I wonder what that means.\"","This wasn't the first time he'd seen a panel like this. The same had appeared just when he entered the Third Layer. He simply hadn't been able to focus on it before the Origin Battlefield decided to cast him out almost immediately afterward.","Unfortunately, Michael still wasn't cut out for a break. Just as he decided to take things slow, the night sky suddenly brightened.","Anyone within a reasonable distance, except blind or not, should have been able to see the light, caused by what appeared to be several falling objects.","However, much to Michael's surprise, the brightest of the objects that had appeared out of nowhere, scattering off in different directions, seemed to be heading straight toward him.","Along with it were multiple extremely powerful presences making their way towards him."]},{"number":1075,"title":"Chapter 1075: Special Treasure","paragraphs":["After three months, Michael had grown considerably more powerful than he had been during the battle against the Black Serpent Empire.","For one, all twenty of his engravings, granted by his class, were now filled with either his most powerful undead or his most unique.","Since they just happened to be the most powerful undead he possessed, when his engravings were in their passive state, Michael was at his absolute strongest.","A few months ago he could barely handle an opponent in their level eighties. Now the current Michael was confident that if he were to face Shojo again, as long as the other party didn't use their domain, he could desperately exchange a few moves before having to flee.","This was why Michael hadn't been particularly surprised by the Origin Battlefield forcing him into a higher layer.","If the Origin Will was operating it directly, then it surely knew Michael possessed more than one undead close to the peak of Rank Four, along with thousands of others at Rank Four.","It was no wonder it had stated that Michael had surpassed its \"extreme threshold,\" showing that even though the Origin Battlefield had made preparations for anomalies, it still couldn't contain him.","This was also why Michael didn't feel too bad about it. He was almost certain there would be a few other unfortunate souls in the same situation.","After all, compared to him, there were bound to be centuries-old awakeners scattered across the universe. Only the heavens knew how many tricks they'd accumulated over that time.","None of that mattered now, however.","Even with Michael's prowess, within the range his senses could stretch, there were hundreds of blazing presences rushing toward him. Among them were three moving fastest, radiating the brightest light.","One had to understand that each of these presences burned brighter than even his highest-level undead.","Michael's pupils contracted.","\"...Shit.\"","Without another thought, he kicked off the ground.","BOOM!","The mountain beneath his feet exploded as his figure shot into the sky like a cannonball. His target wasn't the approaching presences, but the brilliant purple object descending directly toward him.","\"If that's really my compensation, no one else is taking it.\"","The purple light seemed almost alive. It descended at incredible speed, leaving a long violet trail across the night sky. Michael reached it in only a few breaths. Without hesitation, he stretched out his hand.","The instant his fingers touched it, the purple radiance condensed. The light vanished, and a single object appeared in his palm. It resembled neither a weapon nor any artifact he recognized.","It was...","\"...A candle?\"","No. Looking more carefully, it resembled a stick of incense carved from translucent violet crystal. Golden patterns flowed through its surface like liquid stars. A rich fragrance escaped from it despite not being lit.","Without wasting another second, Michael activated Detect. A panel immediately appeared.","Heavenly Enlightenment Incense","Grade: Epic ★★★","Description: A supreme treasure born naturally within regions blessed by the Origin Will.","Once ignited, the incense releases Heavenly Enlightenment Mist.","Depending on the quantity burned and the intensity of the flame, the user's comprehension may increase by up to ten times.","Duration and effectiveness depend upon the amount consumed.","Michael's breathing stopped. His heartbeat accelerated.","\"Ten...\"","\"...times?\"","His grip tightened around the incense. His expression instantly shifted from surprise to excitement.","\"No...\"","\"This is exactly what I need!\"","His heart pounded violently. Someone else might simply value this treasure. Michael, on the other hand, needed it desperately.","His greatest obstacle now was no longer resources, but comprehension, thanks to his advancement requirement demanding that he develop his own Domain before reaching Rank Four.","A Domain. A power that, under normal circumstances, only genuine Rank Four existences possessed. Even with all his advantages, Michael still wasn't confident. Five years was the limit the Origin Will had given him.","\"...If I can get more...\"","Michael's eyes shone, but just as quickly, his smile slowly faded.","\"...Hmm?\"","He instinctively attempted to place the incense into his storage space. Nothing happened. The treasure remained firmly in his hand.","Michael frowned and tried again. This time he attempted to use the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion. The legendary spatial treasure immediately responded. Yet the incense still refused to enter.","\"...Rejected?\"","Michael narrowed his eyes. A faint invisible resistance surrounded the incense. It wasn't refusing absolutely. It was resisting. And more strangely, Michael could clearly feel that the resistance was weakening. Very slowly.","His eyes drifted toward the faint purple glow still lingering around the incense.","\"...The light.\"","The brighter the purple radiance, the stronger the rejection. As the light gradually dimmed, the resistance weakened accordingly.","Michael's expression immediately darkened.","\"...So that's how it is.\"","This wasn't a reward he could casually hide away. At least, not yet. As long as the incense continued shining, it couldn't be stored. Which also meant it was effectively broadcasting its own location.","Michael slowly lifted his head. Hundreds of blazing presences were still rushing toward him.","\"...Origin Will.\"","Michael couldn't help but laugh bitterly.","\"You really don't know how to give gifts normally.\"","A treasure capable of increasing comprehension by up to tenfold. A Three-Star Epic treasure. Something countless Rank Four experts would undoubtedly kill for.","Of course, he wasn't entirely certain this was his compensation, since the panel from before hadn't updated to confirm that a reward had been delivered, and still remained in its previous state.","If that was the case, then the Origin Will hadn't targeted him specifically. This was simply how such objects worked.","Suddenly, Michael felt he understood a little more about the Origin Battlefield.","\"...This thing is a hot potato.\"","He tightened his grip around the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","\"Looks like my welcome to the Fourth Layer is going to be far more exciting than I hoped.\"","Without hesitation, Michael immediately chose a direction with fewer presences and weaker signatures and started running.","Ohh, was he expected to stand his ground and fight?","Setting aside the three brightest presences, which radiated power even stronger than his High Drake undead, there were at least a hundred others at Shojo's level.","Yes, he had two thousand Rank Four undead, but a wise man was one who could retreat to fight another day.","Unfortunately for Michael, it seemed easier to stand still than to run away."]},{"number":1076,"title":"Chapter 1076: Confrontation [1]","paragraphs":["Immediately switching to Wisdom State, Michael's power over the void dramatically increased by several levels, his body becoming a blur, appearing for only the briefest moment before flickering to another location.","Unfortunately, his speed of escape only made the three presences behind him push their pace even further.","Seeing the distance he had just created instantly close again, Michael's heart grew a bit heavy.","For these three to carry presences more powerful than even his highest-level undead meant they too were at level 100.","What he didn't know was whether they were old and powerful thanks to time, or whether they were simply geniuses on top of everything else.","If it was the former, then if worst came to worst, he could fight it out with them. But if they happened to be geniuses who might even sit within the extreme threshold of the Origin Battlefield, then unless he was willing to risk a loss, all he could do was run obediently.","As for dropping the treasure, that wasn't an option at all.","At this point, Michael had already avoided confrontation several times.","Several awakeners had attempted to block his path. Unfortunately for them, Michael was not merely someone who could use spatial movement. In his Wisdom State, his understanding and control over the void rose to a terrifying level.","Their interceptions were useless. The moment they thought they had surrounded him, he would vanish. The moment they sealed one direction, he would slip through another.","Sometimes he didn't even appear where they expected him to.","To most of the Rank Four awakeners chasing him, Michael was like a ghost flickering through space itself.","However, the pursuers were not fools. After several failed attempts, they quickly realized what he intended to do. He was trying to break the encirclement entirely.","Soon, several groups stopped chasing blindly. Instead, they began coordinating. Powerful auras gathered ahead of him. One by one, figures appeared in the air, forming a loose net across the sky.","Michael's eyes narrowed.","\"Troublesome.\"","The next instant, his body blurred again. Space folded. He vanished from his original position and reappeared several miles away.","Just one more teleportation and he would break through the encirclement entirely.","But at that moment, Michael's expression changed. His movement locked. For the briefest instant, the surrounding space hardened like solid iron.","Then an external force seized him.","It didn't injure him, nor did it intend to. It simply interfered with the space around him and forcefully dragged him elsewhere.","Michael's vision shifted. A heartbeat later, he appeared above a wide valley. Dozens of figures floated in the air around him. Some looked human. Others clearly were not.","There were horned races, winged races, scaled races, giants with stone-like skin, spirits with transparent bodies, and several beings Michael couldn't immediately identify.","Each radiated the aura of a Rank Four supernatural, and thanks to the age of some, their auras were even stronger still.","None of them looked weak.","Michael's gaze instantly landed on one figure standing farther back. It was a thin man with pale gray skin and six eyes arranged vertically across his face.","In his hand was a bronze compass covered in silver runes. The compass was still trembling faintly.","Michael's senses locked onto it.","\"...Epic Grade.\"","His expression turned slightly colder. Sure enough, the Origin Battlefield was not simple. Treasures that would be considered rare and valuable outside were clearly not as uncommon here, at least not among powerful awakeners who had survived long enough.","An Epic Grade spatial treasure. Outside, something like that would make countless factions go to war. Here, someone had casually used it to drag him into an ambush.","Michael exhaled softly. Unfortunately, he had no time to waste. The purple glow around the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense hadn't faded completely yet.","As long as it continued shining, more awakeners would keep coming.","The thin six-eyed man spoke first.","\"Hand over the treasure and we can—\"","He never finished.","The moment Michael understood the situation, his thoughts accelerated. At the same time, one of the engravings belonging to his undead griffin shone faintly.","Among Michael's undead, Gale was one of the strongest, holding dominion over wind and storm. Its trait was copied instantly.","Michael's eyes turned cold.","\"Move.\"","His voice was quiet.","Then the sky screamed.","A terrifying storm erupted around him without warning. Wind compressed into countless blades, each one nearly invisible and sharp enough to tear through enchanted metal.","The valley vanished beneath a hurricane of cutting light.","The awakeners surrounding him reacted immediately, but Michael's spell had been too sudden.","A dozen figures were caught before they could fully defend. Blood sprayed into the air. Several screams rang out.","One winged awakener had half his feathers shredded apart. A scaled giant raised both arms to block, only for dozens of wind blades to carve deep marks across his skin.","The six-eyed man's expression changed sharply as the bronze compass in his hand trembled violently.","\"He's not ordinary!\"","Michael didn't care. The storm wasn't meant to kill them all. It was meant to create space. The instant the wind blades tore open a gap in the encirclement, Michael stepped forward.","Space twisted around him again. However, this time, before anyone could activate another treasure, Michael's figure split into several afterimages.","Each one moved in a different direction.","The awakeners hesitated for less than half a second.","But half a second was enough.","Michael's real body appeared at the edge of the valley, the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense still clenched tightly in his hand.","His expression remained calm, but his eyes were colder than before.","\"I really don't have time to play with you people.\"","The next moment, the storm behind him exploded outward, and Michael vanished again.","A few seconds after he disappeared, three powerful presences arrived at his previous location."]},{"number":1077,"title":"Chapter 1077: Confrontation [2]","paragraphs":["A few seconds after Michael disappeared, three terrifying presences arrived where the battle had just taken place. They stopped in midair.","The lingering storm of wind blades was still carving deep scars into the surrounding mountains, while wounded awakeners slowly regained their bearings.","None of the three newcomers paid any attention to those around them.","The first was a man. Or rather, he looked human. Towering well over seven feet in height, his physique possessed proportions no ordinary human could ever achieve.","Every muscle appeared perfectly sculpted, giving him the imposing build of a miniature titan rather than a mortal man.","Behind his back spread four pairs of enormous white wings. Each feather shimmered with a faint silver radiance. Golden hair flowed to his shoulders, while a pair of sapphire-blue eyes calmly observed the battlefield beneath him.","He wore white armor engraved with countless holy runes that seemed to pulse with living light. Simply standing there caused a gentle pressure to descend upon the surroundings. He gave off an indescribable sense of dignity.","An Angel. A genuine member of one of the universe's higher races.","Beside him floated a much younger-looking woman. She appeared to be in her early twenties. Unlike the male angel, she possessed only three pairs of wings. Her silver-white hair reached her waist, while her emerald eyes remained emotionless.","She too possessed the same inhumanly perfect physique, hidden beneath elegant white armor. Although considerably smaller than the man beside her, her aura wasn't weaker than many of the other awakeners around.","Anyone foolish enough to judge her by appearance alone would undoubtedly regret it.","Neither angel spoke. Their expressions remained cold from beginning to end.","Not far away stood another figure. She was a middle-aged woman dressed in flowing azure robes embroidered with clouds and mountains. Her black hair was tied into a simple bun using nothing more than a wooden hairpin.","Beneath her feet floated a jade-colored sword. Its blade emitted faint ripples through space every few seconds, as though the sword itself breathed. Her hands remained folded behind her back.","The surrounding spiritual energy instinctively gathered around her without needing conscious control.","Every movement she made carried the natural elegance unique to a profession belonging to one of the universe's high civilizations.","Even before she spoke, one could immediately recognize her as a sword cultivator.","Finally, several dozen meters away floated a broad-shouldered man with burning crimson hair.","Unlike the other three, he wore no armor whatsoever.","His upper body remained bare, revealing skin covered in fiery red patterns resembling flowing magma. The air around him continuously distorted. Heat poured from his body in visible waves.","Every breath he exhaled raised the surrounding temperature.","Even the lingering storm left behind by Michael gradually weakened under the scorching heat surrounding him.","Without another word after failing to see their target, all four immediately disappeared.","They had only stopped because Michael aura had briefly halted here. Now that it was moving again, there was no reason to remain.","Within moments, all four terrifying presences vanished completely.","...","Only after they had disappeared did the dozens of awakeners trapped within the valley slowly release the breaths they had been unconsciously holding.","\"...They're finally gone.\"","A stone-skinned giant wiped blood from his shoulder before sitting down heavily on a broken cliff. Another awakener laughed bitterly.","\"I thought we were dead.\"","Several people nodded in agreement.","No one doubted it. If Michael had thrown away the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense during that brief confrontation, those four monsters would have descended directly into the middle of everyone present.","At that point, whether they survived or not would have depended entirely upon luck.","The six-eyed awakener carefully stored away his bronze compass before sighing.","\"It's a shame though.\"","Silence followed.","A beastkin suddenly frowned.","\"...Wait.\"","He looked toward the direction the four had disappeared.","\"Wasn't that...\" He hesitated before continuing. \"...Fairy Sword Immortal Qing Yue?\"","Several people immediately turned toward him.","\"The cultivator?\"","\"Yes.\"","A bird-winged awakener slowly nodded.","\"...I'm fairly certain it was her.\"","Another person looked toward where the angels had vanished.","\"And wasn't that...\" He swallowed unconsciously. \"...Lord Seraphiel?\"","The atmosphere immediately became strange. Even those who had remained relatively calm until now couldn't hide their surprise anymore.","\"...Those two?\"","\"But...\"","A horned giant frowned.","\"Aren't the Celestial Dominion and the Azure Sword Realm supposed to be at each other's throats?\"","One would normally assume supernaturals, or in this case awakeners, originating from different realms would remain strangers to one another. Reality, however, was very different. After all, not everyone was like Michael.","Among the Rank Four awakeners gathered here, many had lived for several centuries. Some were already approaching a thousand years of age, and others had long surpassed that milestone.","Over such vast stretches of time, countless awakeners had traveled between realms, explored special dimensions like hell, participated in inter-realm tournaments, joined large organizations, or simply wandered the universe in search of opportunities.","They had met countless races, and countless civilizations had interacted with one another across the ages.","Naturally, the truly famous figures among those civilizations were known far beyond the borders of their own realms.","The male angel was one such existence. Likewise, the sword cultivator's reputation had spread throughout numerous star regions.","Neither had reached the Demigod Realm. Yet both had long been acknowledged as standing only a single step away from it.","A burly beastkin suddenly burst into laughter.","\"Hahaha! So what if their realms are at odds?\"","Several people looked toward him. The beastkin shrugged.","\"Don't tell me you've lived this long and still think a civilization is the same thing as the people living in it.\" He scratched one horn casually.","\"The Celestial Dominion and the Azure Sword Realm may dislike one another, but Lord Seraphiel isn't the Celestial Dominion. And Fairy Sword Immortal Qing Yue isn't the Azure Sword Realm. They're individuals. Watch your mouth and be careful what you say. The two of them may not care. But if someone hears you speaking so casually about existences like them...\""]},{"number":1078,"title":"Chapter 1078: Confrontation [3]","paragraphs":["The beast kin didn't finish the sentence. He didn't need to.","Everyone present understood. People at that level weren't merely famous. They represented the absolute pinnacle below the Demigod Realm.","Offending one of them over careless words wasn't something any ordinary Rank Four awakener wished to experience.","The horned giant laughed awkwardly before raising both hands.","\"Fine, fine. I'll keep my mouth shut.\"","Another awakener suddenly spoke.","\"...Forget those two.\" He gestured toward the direction the crimson-haired man had vanished. \"Who was the third one?\"","Several nearby awakeners exchanged glances. After a moment, an elderly man with crystal-like skin slowly spoke.","\"If I'm not mistaken, he should be from the Phoenix Race.\"","\"The Phoenix Race?\"","Quite a few people revealed surprised expressions. The old man nodded. Several awakeners followed suit.","\"That makes sense.\"","\"No wonder his presence felt so oppressive.\"","\"The Phoenix Race has always been among the highest races.\"","Someone quietly added,","\"If he really is a Phoenix...\" \"...then he should also be one of those monsters standing just beneath the Demigod Realm.\"","Silence followed once again.","Eventually, another person looked in the direction where the younger female angel had disappeared.","\"...What about her? The younger angel. She only had three pairs of wings.\"","Several expressions immediately became strange.","\"That's true.\"","\"I noticed that too.\"","\"Three pairs...\"","\"Shouldn't that only correspond to Rank Three?\"","Another person slowly nodded.","\"It should. Yet she entered the Fourth Layer.\"","Though no one spoke after that, they all knew the implication. If she had been placed here despite only possessing three pairs of wings, then she possessed some other qualification they weren't aware of.","Though they hadn't been in the Origin Battlefield for long, for something connected to the Origin Will and involving five percent of the universe's population, it shouldn't be a place where loopholes appeared casually.","If someone like her had been placed here, there was almost certainly a reason.","Still, compared to the other three, the female angel simply wasn't nearly as eye-catching.","Lord Seraphiel's reputation had echoed throughout countless realms for centuries.","Fairy Sword Immortal Qing Yue had once challenged seven peak Rank Four cultivators in succession without suffering defeat.","Even the suspected Phoenix expert possessed an overwhelming aura that naturally commanded attention. Standing beside those three, the young female angel inevitably faded into the background.","If they had known that the youth who had just pushed them all back by himself was also Rank Three, only the heavens knew what their reaction would be.","*","Michael's expression darkened as he sensed the presences behind him. The three brightest were still chasing.","There was also a smaller presence among them now, for some reason. Its aura was weaker than the other three, but it followed closely behind.","\"Persistent bastards...\"","Michael cursed under his breath.","His figure flickered again, vanishing through folded space before reappearing dozens of miles away. Yet almost immediately, those terrifying presences adjusted their direction and continued closing in.","The Heavenly Enlightenment Incense in his hand still glowed with a faint purple light. Michael glanced down at it.","From what he had observed so far, the radiance was indeed weakening, but the process was far too slow. At this rate, it would probably take around twenty minutes before the glow faded enough for him to place it into his storage space.","Twenty minutes. Under normal circumstances, that was nothing. Now, it felt absurdly long.","Michael wasn't sure whether the other treasures that had fallen from the sky followed the same rule. Perhaps they did. Perhaps they didn't. However, this incense had been the brightest among all the lights that descended.","It was probably the highest grade treasure among them. In that case, its restriction being stronger made sense.","Unfortunately, understanding the reason did nothing to improve Michael's mood. He could only deal with it.","Putting aside the thought of dropping it entirely, if this continued, he might actually have to stop and defend the treasure directly.","Michael wasn't exactly afraid. But he also wasn't fully confident. Those three were not ordinary Rank Four awakeners. Their presences alone proved that much.","If he truly fought them, victory was uncertain. What Michael wanted to avoid was loss. Perhaps victory was still possible if he exposed enough of his cards, but the price would be unknown.","In fact, he did possess a method to launch a terrifying counterattack right now. The Mausoleum of Endless Dominion's third effect.","After accumulating energy for so long, the legendary-grade treasure could unleash a spiritual attack powerful enough to threaten even peak Rank Four existences.","If Michael had been stronger himself and could supply more energy to the Mausoleum, killing one of them might not have been impossible.","But Michael rejected the thought almost instantly. He was unwilling to reveal more about the Mausoleum unless absolutely necessary.","Even now, aside from when he had first obtained the treasure, Michael had never summoned its true body from his soul. The fewer people who understood the nature of his legendary-grade item, the better.","If its true ability were exposed here, Michael dared to say the entire Fourth Layer would be drawn to him like moths to flame.","Michael's gaze flickered coldly.","\"This incense is already troublesome enough.\"","In fact, Michael also had a feeling this would be the last time in a long while that obtaining a treasure like this would go so smoothly.","If these falling lights were not one-time rewards, then once everyone understood what could be gained from them, the next battle would become far bloodier.","Treasures capable of aiding comprehension were too attractive, especially to these centuries-old peak Rank Four superpowers. Many of them had probably been stuck before the Demigod threshold for years.","To such people, an object that could increase comprehension represented hope, and hope was often enough to drive people to madness.","Just look at him. He was still young. He had only cultivated for a little over a year. Yet even he couldn't bear to throw away the incense despite being chased by several level 100 monsters."]},{"number":1079,"title":"Chapter 1079: Confrontation [4]","paragraphs":["How much more desperate must those ancient beings feel, having been trapped at the same bottleneck for centuries?","Even if it weren't always a comprehension treasure and was simply a consistent Epic Grade item, Michael was sure that alone would be enough to cause a bloodbath. After all, one could never have enough Epic Grade items.","Michael tightened his grip around the incense. The purple glow reflected in his eyes as he pushed his speed higher.","Unfortunately, only ten minutes later, Michael could already see the figures chasing him with his own eyes.","Knowing he couldn't run aimlessly, lest more peak Rank Four awakeners join the pursuit out of curiosity or knowledge of what he carried, he had circled back near his previous locations more than once. He was fairly sure the awakeners he had passed by were long accustomed to it by now.","However, though he hadn't given much thought to who exactly was chasing him, he was genuinely shocked when he finally made out their appearances.","\"Fuck!\"","Was that a four-winged angel?","And was that a sword cultivator?","As for the third figure, why was his presence literally burning the space around him as he moved through the void?","Setting aside the third figure, Michael was no stranger to angels or cultivators. One belonged to a top race that could be ranked in the top ten of the universe, and the other belonged to a civilization that could also be ranked in the top ten thanks to the mysteries of their profession.","He just didn't know if the woman was merely a cultivator in appearance with a different class, but the angel was definitely real.","Michael could also tell they were angry.","Even across such an enormous distance, the fluctuations in their auras were becoming increasingly obvious. Michael's own expression darkened.","\"...As if I'm enjoying this.\"","He couldn't help feeling irritated. He understood their frustration. From their perspective, they had spent a significant amount of time chasing someone who refused to fight, constantly slipping through the void before they could catch him.","Every time they thought they had cornered him, he disappeared. Every time they shortened the distance, he folded space and escaped again.","Anyone would become annoyed after being led around in circles for so long. Michael understood that perfectly.","But the same applied to him.","Did they honestly think he wanted this? He had been forced into the Fourth Layer the moment he entered the Origin Battlefield.","He had barely had time to look at his surroundings before a treasure literally landed in his hands.","Then, before he could even examine it properly, hundreds of Rank Four awakeners had started chasing him.","Michael clicked his tongue.","\"If you're irritated...then what about me?\"","He hadn't provoked them. He hadn't robbed them. He hadn't attacked them first.","The Origin Battlefield itself had practically thrown the treasure into his hands. Yet somehow, he was the one forced to spend the last ten minutes fleeing across mountains, valleys, rivers, and forests.","Even worse, he couldn't even hide the damned thing. Every second the purple light continued shining was another second broadcasting his exact location to everyone nearby.","Michael glanced down at the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","\"Ahhh, since it's come to this, let's go all out!\"","Knowing that he could now make them out with his own eyes, even if only as blurs as everyone flickered in and out of the void with each teleportation, meant they would catch up before long.","Rather than wait until that moment and be left with little time to prepare, it was better to make a stand now while he still had room to set things up.","Without hesitation, Michael activated one of the engravings.","Ash-gray lines spread across his skin before countless black ashes poured from the engraving like smoke escaping from a volcano. The ashes gathered rapidly behind him.","Within moments, they condensed into the figure of a rugged middle-aged man. His weathered face remained expressionless, before his body suddenly began expanding.","The transformation lasted only a heartbeat. A colossal drake over three hundred meters in length now occupied the sky behind Michael.","Its wings stretched so wide they cast a shadow across the plains below, while cold green eyes stared toward the four approaching figures.","The undead High Drake. Michael's strongest undead.","The drake slowly drew in a breath. Its chest expanded.","\"ROOOOAAAAARRRRRRRRR!!!!\"","The roar exploded from its throat. The air itself shattered. Visible rings of compressed atmosphere expanded outward at terrifying speed. Trees thousands of meters below were forcefully uprooted and sent flying in every direction.","Clouds stretching across the horizon were instantly blown apart. The sound wave continued expanding. Every Rank Four awakener within hundreds of miles subconsciously looked toward the source.","Michael wasn't done yet.","Over the past three months, it wasn't only his body, soul, and undead that had grown stronger. His understanding of the Law of Echoed Existence had also deepened tremendously.","Back when he had first stepped into Rank Three, he had only begun scratching the surface of what his law truly represented.","Now he had finally managed to derive his own Law Skill from it.","Michael's eyes became strangely ethereal. The drake behind him let out another low growl, as if responding to his will.","Michael slowly raised one hand.","\"Law Skill...\"","\"...Echoed Bestowal.\"","The instant the words left his mouth, a terrifying aura erupted from the High Drake's body.","The Law of Echoed Existence recognized everything connected to him as part of a single echo.","Every creature whose existence had become intertwined with his was, to the law, no longer an entirely separate individual. They were echoes within the same existence.","Echoed Bestowal embodied that concept. Rather than copying traits only for himself, it allowed any creature connected to Michael to temporarily receive the traits of another creature connected to him.","It was, in essence, an extension of the sharing ability his law had always possessed.","Before ascending to Rank Three, Michael himself had only been capable of copying a single trait at any given time.","After reaching Rank Three, that limit had increased to two. Now, thanks to Echoed Bestowal, a creature connected to Michael could also be bestowed two traits from two other connected creatures simultaneously.","The recipient did not have to be Michael himself. As long as both parties were connected to him, the transfer could occur. The possibilities that emerged from this ability were nearly endless.","Naturally, the stronger the trait and the greater the difference between the two creatures involved, the more energy the Law Skill consumed.","Even for Michael, using it recklessly with powerful creatures over prolonged battles would quickly become impossible.","But right now, he had no intention of conserving energy.","His eyes remained fixed upon the four terrifying figures approaching from the distance.","A faint smile slowly appeared on his face as he confirmed the two traits he would bestow upon the High Drake.","The first was from Beginning. The second was from Spartan."]},{"number":1080,"title":"Chapter 1080: Mutation","paragraphs":["The Law of Brutal Rebirth and the Law of Abyssal Pyre.","These were the laws of Beginning and Spartan respectively.","The Law of Brutal Rebirth transformed pain into fuel, making severe wounds trigger powerful regenerative bursts. The closer to death, the stronger one became.","The Law of Abyssal Pyre, on the other hand, devoured anything in its path and reformed it into spiritual residue usable by its wielder.","These were the effects of Beginning and Spartan's laws respectively.","One was of the giant race, and the latter was now a true human. Both possessed powerful constitutions and inherent advantages.","Just what would happen if even a fraction of those traits were added to the undead High Drake?","Michael didn't know.","When he first comprehended this law skill, he had tried it out with a few unimportant Rank Four undead. Though the effect had been astonishing, the consumption was demonic.","After that, even though he knew he could use it on most of his undead, he hadn't applied it to any of his truly powerful ones. Instead, he had further refined the method and kept it as a trump card.","He hadn't expected a day like this to come so soon, nor had he expected to underestimate the actual cost of using this law skill.","The moment the skill was cast, Michael felt a massive drain of mental and soul energy leave his body, making him momentarily unstable in the air before he recovered some of his bearing.","\"This is too much!\"","Fortunately, after the initial activation, they only needed to maintain it. Though the maintenance cost wasn't as monstrous as the initial cast, it was still very energy-consuming, if manageable.","Now, with less than ten minutes remaining before he could finally store the Origin Battlefield treasure away, as long as he could escape the sight of the other awakeners, they wouldn't be able to track him. He had that much confidence.","As he felt the consumption of the law skill he had just cast, Michael sensed a dramatic shift behind him and turned around immediately.","Right before his astonished eyes, the undead High Drake began undergoing another transformation.","It started with its body. The already colossal drake trembled as every muscle across its enormous frame violently contracted.","Crunch!","Deep, heavy sounds echoed through the air. Its bones expanded. Its muscles thickened. Its wings stretched outward once more.","The drake's already gigantic body continued growing, passing three hundred and fifty meters before finally approaching six hundred.","The pressure radiating from its existence multiplied.","Michael's pupils narrowed. He hadn't expected such an obvious physical change.","The transformation didn't stop there.","The drake's scales slowly began changing. Every scale across its body gradually lost its original appearance before darkening further and further, settling into a deep black that seemed capable of swallowing light itself.","Even its horns, eyes, and claws underwent the same transformation. The cold green eyes that had previously observed everything calmly darkened until they too became completely black. There was no visible pupil or iris.","Just endless darkness. Anyone meeting those eyes would instinctively feel as though they were staring into a bottomless abyss.","Michael's breathing unconsciously slowed.","\"...This...\"","Before the transformation had completely finished, another phenomenon appeared.","Heat. An unbelievable amount of heat. It erupted from the drake's body without warning. The surrounding air distorted violently.","Large sections of cloud that had somehow begun reforming high above evaporated almost instantly. The plains beneath the drake started changing. Rivers flowing between valleys began producing enormous amounts of steam.","The rocky ground itself gradually turned red.","Michael, standing only a short distance away, immediately felt a wave of scorching heat crash into him. His expression changed.","\"...Hot.\"","His physique had already reached an astonishing level. Ordinary flames couldn't even leave marks on his skin anymore.","Yet simply standing near the transformed High Drake made him feel distinctly uncomfortable. The heat wasn't merely physical. It carried traces of law within it.","Michael instinctively retreated several dozen meters. Only then did the discomfort lessen slightly. He stared at the transformed drake with unconcealed surprise.","\"So this is what happens when Beginning's and Spartan's traits overlap.\"","The High Drake slowly spread its wings. The surrounding sky shook. A faint black haze continuously flowed from the gaps between its scales while waves of unbearable heat rolled outward endlessly.","\"So strong...\"","Michael had expected improvement, but even he hadn't anticipated a mutation of this scale.","Even from their rapidly approaching positions, the four figures chasing him instinctively slowed for the briefest instant.","However, Michael's focus wasn't on them. The moment he recovered his bearing, under the eyes of the four approaching at the fastest speed he had ever witnessed, he threw the Origin Battlefield treasure, which still carried a faint glow, directly into the mouth of the undead High Drake.","As for the treasure being destroyed, he had noticed a while back that as long as the glow still existed, it would be very difficult to actually destroy it.","Additionally, when some monsters became sufficiently proficient in void magic, they could create a stable spatial pocket within their stomach.","For a creature like the undead High Drake, which carried a significant amount of dragon blood, it had naturally mastered this technique.","This was only the first step of Michael's plan. Unfortunately, it produced a different result from what the four approaching figures had anticipated.","Just as he had suspected, none of them actually harbored genuine malice toward him. But this was the supernatural world.","A weak man didn't deserve to hold a treasure, and a strong man couldn't pass on a powerful one. It was simply the rule of the jungle, and if one died because of it, they could only blame themselves for being weak, or in Michael's case, for being greedy.","What none of them had foreseen, including Michael, was that even after the undead High Drake had swallowed the treasure, it still broadcast its location outward through a glow."]},{"number":1081,"title":"Chapter 1081: First Contact","paragraphs":["Though Michael hadn't expected the drake's stomach to work in the first place, he also hadn't expected the treasure to emit an even brighter glow from inside, as though it was afraid of not being noticed.","Was this really the Origin Battlefield? What a damned place to be in. If this was how all its treasures behaved in the future, who in their right mind would be the first to snatch one?","As these thoughts flashed through Michael's mind, he immediately teleported away from his location.","At the same time, the four who had just arrived near his previous position were met with a vicious counterattack from the High Drake.","The transformed drake threw its massive head backward. Its enormous chest expanded once more. The terrifying heat surrounding its body gathered toward its throat.","The surrounding space visibly distorted. Even the void itself rippled under the overwhelming concentration of power.","The four immediately sensed the danger.","The next instant, the High Drake opened its jaws.","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!","A pillar of destruction erupted forth. It wasn't ordinary dragon breath. It resembled a torrent of condensed black flames.","Everything along its path vanished. The void trembled violently. The attack crossed dozens of miles in the blink of an eye, aimed at all four pursuers.","The younger female angel immediately retreated. She knew she couldn't block something of this level.","The other three, however, had no intention of yielding.","The four-winged angel calmly stepped forward. One hand stretched toward the incoming dragon breath.","\"Holy Art...\"","\"...Ocean Sanctuary.\"","Countless azure runes suddenly appeared before him. Water gathered from nowhere, and within a heartbeat, an enormous wall of crystal-clear water stood before the angel. The wall rapidly expanded until it became a barrier stretching for several kilometers.","The dragon breath struck it.","BOOOOOOOOOOM!!","The heavens shook. Steam exploded outward in every direction. The water barrier trembled violently. Gigantic waves surged backward while enormous amounts of water evaporated almost instantly. Yet the barrier held.","Although deep cracks rapidly spread across its surface, the dragon breath failed to break through before its power was exhausted.","The male angel's expression remained calm, though the arm supporting the barrier had shifted back slightly.","At the same moment, the other two also moved.","The crimson-haired man roared as the blazing markings covering his body suddenly ignited.","\"Foul beast! Release the treasure!\"","A deafening cry echoed across the battlefield. Brilliant flames exploded around him as his human form dissolved into fire. A heartbeat later, an enormous phoenix appeared in the sky. Its wings stretched for hundreds of meters.","Every feather seemed forged from living flames. Its mere existence caused the surrounding temperature to rise by another terrifying level.","Unlike the High Drake's oppressive heat, the phoenix's flames possessed astonishing vitality. Everything they touched seemed capable of burning forever.","Meanwhile, the middle-aged sword cultivator calmly adjusted the jade sword beneath her feet and rapidly rose higher until she stood far above everyone else.","She formed a sword seal with two fingers, and the surrounding spiritual energy instantly surged toward her as several energy swords formed around her.","Buzz! Buzz! Buzz!","One sword became ten. Ten became one hundred. One hundred became one thousand. Countless spiritual swords materialized behind her. Within moments, an entire sea of swords floated overhead. The sky itself disappeared beneath the countless blades.","The cultivator lowered her fingers. Every sword quietly pointed toward the transformed High Drake.","Meanwhile, Michael, who had already activated his law to copy Fade's trait while remaining hidden within the surface layer of the void, was sweating buckets.","\"...What the hell...\"","His eyes remained fixed on the battlefield without blinking.","\"They're all so damn powerful!\"","Michael couldn't help but curse inwardly. Although he had expected the three to be extraordinary after sensing their auras, witnessing them exchange blows with his strengthened High Drake made the difference even clearer. None of them looked like ordinary awakeners.","Michael felt the urge to activate Detect. He really wanted to know what classes they possessed. Unfortunately, he could only suppress the impulse.","\"...Forget it.\"","Using either Detect or his Eyes of Truth now might expose him. Fade's trait allowed him to erase almost every trace of his existence, blending into the surface layer of the void like a shadow hidden beneath another shadow.","As long as he remained patient, Michael was extremely confident in his ability to stay hidden.","But the moment he actively observed them with Detect or the Eyes of Truth, the fluctuations produced by those abilities would almost certainly be noticed by those with sharp senses, which those three surely didn't lack.","Michael silently shook his head.","\"I'm not stupid enough to stick my neck out.\"","He had absolutely no doubt that the instant they discovered his exact location, they would dedicate at least some attention to coming after him. Even if they didn't pursue him directly, having their gaze on him would make his next moves extremely inconvenient.","\"Just a little longer...\"","\"Once the incense stops glowing...\"","\"I'll immediately store it away and disappear.\"","This was still his original objective. He never intended to defeat these people. Nor did he wish to reveal more of his trump cards.","As for the High Drake, Michael believed it could hold them off. Perhaps it couldn't defeat all three. But after receiving the traits of Beginning and Spartan through Echoed Bestowal, its combat ability had reached an unbelievable level.","Combined with the Law of Brutal Rebirth, every injury it suffered would only make it more terrifying. Meanwhile, the Law of Abyssal Pyre ensured almost nothing went to waste.","As long as it continued fighting, it would continue devouring energy. It was practically born for prolonged battles.","Still, even if the High Drake could hold them off indefinitely, Michael couldn't. The true limitation wasn't the High Drake. It was himself.","Echoed Bestowal continuously consumed his soul power and mental strength.","Maintaining such an overwhelming enhancement on his strongest undead was anything but cheap.","If the battle dragged on for too long, the High Drake might still remain capable of fighting, but Michael himself would likely collapse from exhaustion first."]},{"number":1082,"title":"Chapter 1082: Special Angel","paragraphs":["Fortunately, only a few minutes remained. If everything proceeded according to plan, he could simply wait it out.","His thoughts had just reached that point when a cold, strange sensation suddenly crawled up his spine.","\"...Wait.\"","Only then did Michael realize something critical.","\"...Where's the fourth one?\"","His pupils contracted. He had been so hyper-focused on the cataclysmic battle between the High Drake and the three monsters that he had subconsciously forgotten someone. The younger angel. She had never joined the fray.","It was at that exact moment a voice resonated through the air.","\"Law Skill...\"","\"Grace of Light.\"","A brilliant, blinding light suddenly erupted in Michael's vision. It was soft at first, but it expanded exponentially. Like countless threads of dawn stretching violently through the void, the light reached toward him with terrifying precision.","Michael's instincts screamed in warning.","Without hesitation, he tore himself out of the surface layer of the void. The next instant, his figure materialized back in open space. Almost immediately, his gaze locked onto the figure floating not far away.","It was the younger angel.","She held a slender white wand in her hand, its surface carved with intricate golden lines that pulsed with a light that made Michael feel instinctively uncomfortable to his core. The aura it radiated was unmistakable.","Epic Grade.","Michael's eyelid twitched.","\"...Again?\"","Why did Epic Grade treasures suddenly feel so common here?","Outside, an item of this caliber would be enough to make powerhouses wage wars until rivers of blood flowed. Yet in the Fourth Layer of the Origin Battlefield, people seemed to pull them out one after another like cheap trinkets.","Setting the wand aside, Michael turned his attention to properly observing her.","Three pairs of pristine wings. Silver-white hair. Emerald eyes. A cold, flawless face that looked as though it were carved from pure moonlight. But what truly shocked Michael wasn't her ethereal beauty—it was her rank.","\"...Rank Three?\"","For a brief moment, Michael was genuinely stunned. He had always known there was a chance he wasn't the only one forced into a higher layer due to abnormal combat power; after all, the universe was vast. But he hadn't expected to run into another anomaly so soon.","Was it her race, her class, or a combination of both?","Though Michael wasn't deeply familiar with the Angel Race, he was no stranger to them either. Like demons, angels possessed their own unique domain.","However, unlike Hell, which was fractured into countless layered worlds, the angelic realm was one enormous, unified cosmos. And the race itself was absurdly powerful.","Even newborn angels started at Rank One at the very least, and those with greater potential could be born directly at Rank Two or Rank Three.","It was utterly unreasonable. If they weren't so inherently blessed, they wouldn't be classified as a race comparable to Dragons and Phoenixes.","However, in the wider universe, angels were not particularly well-liked. Aside from sharing a few arrogant, irritating traits with elves, they were considered cosmic parasites by many civilizations.","Angels could cultivate normally, but their most recognized path was the accumulation of faith. That alone wouldn't have been an issue if they only targeted ownerless realms or cultivated their own spaces.","Unfortunately, angels had a notorious habit of trying to spread their faith throughout the entire universe. Because of that, despite their holy appearance, they were treated somewhat as a public enemy by many major forces.","Michael's gaze sharpened.","A Rank Three angel with an Epic Grade wand. Setting aside the weapon, he was far more wary of her rank. Outside the Origin Battlefield, he wouldn't have given her a second thought, but sharing the same rank in the same elevated layer meant there was surely something special about her.","Michael had a dark expression on his face.","The moment he re-emerged from the void, three terrifying gazes landed on him simultaneously.","For an instant, it felt as though three massive mountains had crashed down upon his shoulders. His muscles tensed, and he prepared to teleport away again.","But contrary to his expectations, those three heavy gazes only lingered on him for a fleeting moment before snapping back to the High Drake. They were completely ignoring him.","Michael froze slightly. \"They're dismissing me?\"","It was then the female angel spoke, her cold voice carrying a hint of surprise.","\"You truly are Rank Three. Lord Seraphiel mentioned it earlier as a suspicion, but I still found it difficult to believe.\"","As she spoke, Michael felt an invisible, intrusive ripple sweep across him.","[Detect]","His eyelid twitched. The stronger he became, the more he understood why having someone use a detection skill on you was so infuriating.","It felt like a stranger trying to peel away your clothes with their eyes—uncomfortable, rude, and extremely annoying.","Michael's expression turned icy.","Seeing that the other three entities weren't moving to attack him, he looked back at the angel girl and retorted.","\"So what? If you can enter this place as a Rank Three, why can't I?\"","The female angel remained silent, her emerald eyes shifting slightly as she evaluated him.","For a moment, neither spoke. Behind them, the High Drake roared in agony and fury. The sky trembled as a torrential rain of swords pounded against its massive body, met by erupting waves of black flames.","Michael didn't bother turning around to watch; his gaze remained locked on the angel.","She held the Epic Grade wand quietly, her expression perfectly calm. But Michael could tell she was studying him just as intensely as he was studying her.","He wasn't afraid of her. Cautious? Certainly. But afraid? No.","If by some ridiculous chance he couldn't deal with her personally, he still had thousands of undead at his disposal.","True, against the three monsters currently battling his High Drake, his legion would amount to little more than cannon fodder, and a fight to the death would only end in mutual destruction.","But against this single angel? Michael refused to believe she could withstand the full, crushing force of his undead army. Even if she possessed abnormal combat power like himself, there had to be a limit.","Still, Michael had absolutely no intention of revealing his trump card.","Still, Michael had absolutely no intention of revealing his trump card.","His eyes casually swept across the horizon.","Although nothing was visible to the naked eye, his sharpened senses could vaguely detect numerous faint energy fluctuations scattered throughout the surrounding areas and deep within the void.","The other Rank Four awakeners were lurking nearby. There were quite a lot of them, but none approached; they simply observed from a safe distance.","Whether they were merely curious or patiently waiting to play the part of the fisherman profiting from the clash between the snipe and the clam, Michael neither knew nor cared. Either possibility was troublesome.","Fortunately, the three strongest entities currently present seemed to have completely underestimated him. From the girl's words, he could tell that from their perspective, he was merely an unusually talented Rank Three carrying a valuable treasure.","That misunderstanding was precisely what Michael wanted.","The longer they believed his only threat was a quick escape, the better.","As for whether their opinions would change in the future, that was a problem for later.","His absolute priority right now was to safely escape with the treasure without sustaining any losses."]},{"number":1083,"title":"Chapter 1083: Creating Distance","paragraphs":["Since the female angel had taken the liberty of using Detect on him, Michael felt no need to be polite. In the first place, the reason he hadn't used any of his detection skills on anyone was to avoid revealing his location.","[Light Mage Level 75]","What surprised him was her reaction.","The female angel's expression, which had remained cold and indifferent from the beginning, finally changed. Her brows furrowed ever so slightly. There was unmistakable displeasure in her emerald eyes.","\"You dared to use Detect on me?\"","Her voice was still calm. Yet the anger beneath it was impossible to miss.","Michael blinked in surprise.","\"...\"","Who exactly did she think she was? The hypocrisy was astonishing. She had just openly used Detect on him moments ago without asking for permission. Now she was angry because he had returned the favor?","If it had been the four-winged angel, the sword cultivator, or that terrifying phoenix, Michael might have understood. People standing at a high level naturally possessed a certain pride.","Even he himself, if curious about the identity of someone weaker than him in several ways, might use Detect on them without permission.","It was the thought process that came with power, and whether it was good or bad couldn't be easily judged by supernaturals.","But what about the female angel? Was he supposed to politely lower his head simply because she happened to be an angel?","Michael couldn't understand the logic.","The female angel slowly raised her wand. Golden light gathered around its tip. Her gaze remained fixed on him.","\"It is indeed impressive for a human to reach the Fourth Layer while only at Rank Three...\" She paused. \"But do not mistake that achievement for equality. You and I are not the same.\"","Michael simply looked at her.","Then he ignored her completely.","Instead, he silently calculated the time. Almost exactly three minutes had already passed since he had activated Echoed Bestowal.","Which meant that if everything went according to plan, the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense would finally stop emitting its cursed light within a few more minutes.","Once that happened, he could immediately store it away and disappear.","That was all he wanted.","Michael truly had no interest in fighting the female angel. He just needed to stall for time.","Unfortunately, the angel clearly wasn't thinking the same thing.","Without another word, the golden light surrounding her wand suddenly condensed. A spear of brilliant radiance shot toward Michael. Its speed exceeded ordinary spells by several times.","Michael's figure blurred as space folded. The spear pierced nothing but empty air before exploding hundreds of meters away.","Boom!","A massive sphere of light blossomed across the sky. Michael reappeared several kilometers farther away. His eyes instinctively shifted toward the distant battlefield, where the High Drake was still fighting.","Black flames clashed against endless sword light while the phoenix's inferno filled half the sky.","Lord Seraphiel remained at the center, calmly defending and counterattacking with one skill after another. Yet none of the three even spared him another glance.","Michael's eyes narrowed thoughtfully.","\"So that's how it is...\"","They truly weren't interested in him. At least, not yet. As long as the High Drake continued holding their attention, they apparently considered him insignificant enough to leave to the younger angel.","A faint look of contemplation appeared in Michael's eyes. The next moment he teleported to another location and didn't stop.","The female angel frowned, then immediately gave chase. Her six wings beat once, and her body transformed into a streak of white light that pursued him relentlessly.","To an outsider, it looked exactly like Michael was desperately trying to escape. But only Michael himself knew the truth.","He wasn't escaping. He was creating distance. It would be a shame if one of the peak Rank Four experts shifted their attention toward him before the timer finished.","\"Since I just need to stall for time, let me play with this angel for a bit. Though Wisdom's new skill is a bit of an energy black hole, it's quite handy. I just need to be patient.\"","To Michael getting something without a big cost out of this was his desired result.","Meanwhile, back on the battlefield, the clash had only become more terrifying.","The transformed High Drake fought without the slightest intention of retreating.","Every sweep of its claws ripped apart the surrounding area, while torrents of black flames continuously erupted from its jaws, forcing the three peak Rank Four experts to remain fully focused.","Lord Seraphiel's skills collided endlessly against the drake's attacks. Fairy Sword Immortal Qing Yue's countless spiritual swords descended like a heavenly river, each strike capable of splitting mountains apart.","The phoenix's flames transformed the battlefield into a sea of fire, constantly crashing against the drake's own scorching aura. Every exchange shook the heavens, and every collision distorted space itself.","Farther away, the hidden Rank Four awakeners silently observed everything.","Naturally, none of them had failed to notice that the younger angel had forced someone else out of the void. And that the newcomer was somehow Rank Three as well.","All of them were surprised.","\"A second one...\"","\"So it wasn't just the angel.\"","\"A human...\"","\"...Interesting.\"","Though this human didn't quite seem fully human somehow, that was the extent of their reaction. No one moved or showed the slightest intention of following the two Rank Threes as they disappeared farther away. Their attention quickly returned to the battlefield.","To them, those two were certainly monsters among Rank Threes. Perhaps even unprecedented geniuses. But what did that have to do with them? No matter how abnormal a Rank Three was, they were still Rank Three.","Wasn't it clear enough from the fact that neither of them could involve themselves in the current battle?","Even if they possessed strong Rank Four combat power, they couldn't possibly fight the several hundreds of awakeners gathered here alone.","Compared to those two, the battle taking place before them was something else entirely. It was a confrontation between existences standing at the absolute peak of Rank Four."]},{"number":1084,"title":"Chapter 1084: Unique Skill and Origin Battlefield Compensation [1]","paragraphs":["Compared to such a battle, two Rank Three geniuses chasing each other across the Fourth Layer simply wasn't worth much attention.","One beastkin chuckled.","\"Let the children play.\" His gaze never left the battlefield. \"What interests me is that treasure.\"","It was the same for many of them.","While most didn't know exactly what the treasure was, and quite a few hadn't even witnessed the moment it descended, they waited in anticipation, with more than a few looking as though they wanted to do far more than just watch.","This was how the supernatural world worked. Where there was treasure, there were people. It didn't matter what it was. If it looked valuable enough, there would be a battle over it.","Compared to such a thing, even a Rank Three human somehow entering the Fourth Layer no longer seemed particularly important. If he survived, there would be plenty of time to investigate him later.","If he died, then he had simply been another genius who failed to grow. The universe had never lacked such people.","If they had known it was Michael who had summoned the creature currently holding its own against three peak Rank Four powerhouses, their thoughts would have been very different.","Including those engaged in the fight, everyone who saw the undead High Drake only perceived it as a powerful combatant that had appeared from nowhere.","Just as one would naturally assume only Rank Four beings would be present in the Fourth Layer, even if the High Drake emitted an aura somewhat similar to that of an undead, no one would immediately think such a powerful creature had been summoned by a Rank Three human.","The gap was simply too vast.","It was also why most of them assumed Michael was the one in danger compared to the angel.","Meanwhile, at the center of the battlefield, the High Drake's enormous claws collided head-on with the phoenix's burning talons.","BOOM!!","The shockwave spread for hundreds of miles. Entire mountain ranges collapsed. The surrounding void shattered repeatedly before rapidly repairing itself under the Origin Battlefield's terrifying laws.","The phoenix was forced backward several hundred meters before stabilizing. Its golden eyes burned with unconcealed fury as they remained fixed upon the colossal drake.","\"Tch.\"","It clicked its tongue in annoyance before speaking toward Lord Seraphiel while dodging another torrent of black flames.","\"Should we have let that human run off?\" Its voice carried obvious dissatisfaction. \"This filthy half-breed lizard is clearly acting together with him.\"","There wasn't the slightest attempt to conceal the disgust in its tone.","The Phoenix Race had never enjoyed good relations with dragonkind.","True Dragons were one thing. Sub-dragons were another entirely.","In the phoenix's eyes, they were merely impure creatures possessing diluted dragon blood.","Even though the transformed High Drake was currently powerful enough to contend against all three of them simultaneously, that did absolutely nothing to lessen its disdain.","Lord Seraphiel calmly blocked another sweeping claw that pushed him back several kilometers before rushing back in an instant and answering without looking toward the phoenix.","\"It doesn't matter.\" His tone was indifferent. \"The treasure is no longer on the human.\"","His sapphire eyes briefly glanced toward the High Drake's abdomen, where the faint purple radiance still shone through layers of flesh.","\"It is inside that creature.\"","He paused briefly to dodge another attack before continuing. On the other side, another sword collided against the drake's neck as Fairy Sword Immortal Qing Yue silently continued attacking without participating in the conversation.","\"The human is indeed somewhat special. But Lady Aurelia will have no problem dealing with him.\"","Lord Seraphiel stopped there, seemingly unwilling to continue speaking. After all, even if they successfully extracted the treasure from the High Drake, the real battle would only begin afterward.","There were already hundreds of Rank Four awakeners hiding nearby. Every one of them was waiting, many patiently preparing to become the final fisherman.","Lord Seraphiel had no intention of discussing strategy with the phoenix. The two of them weren't allies. At best, they were temporary competitors pursuing the same objective.","The phoenix also had no intention of continuing the topic. It had merely been worried that after chasing the human for so long, something unexpected might occur.","After thinking about it again, its concern gradually faded.","\"Perhaps I was overthinking it.\" It snorted coldly. \"That human may be extraordinary...\" \"But there should be a limit to what a Rank Three can accomplish.\"","Its enormous eyes swept across the battlefield.","\"So many people are watching. Even if he somehow escaped, it isn't as though he could steal the treasure a second time.\"","That was common sense to many of the Rank Four awakeners in the surroundings. No matter how monstrous one was, reality remained reality. There were too many Rank Four experts present.","If the treasure left the High Drake, not even the three of them could guarantee they would obtain it with so many people competing for the same thing.","How could a mere Rank Three possibly succeed? The very thought didn't make sense when even they themselves weren't confident.","It was also the reason why, although they had been exchanging attacks with the High Drake, not one of them had actually gone all out. After chasing Michael across half the region, they had already figured out several things.","Unless the human was stupid, something about that treasure was preventing him from storing it. If he could have stored it, he wouldn't have left something broadcasting his location out in the open.","They suspected the issue was with the treasure itself, which was why they were also waiting for the strange purple radiance surrounding it to disappear completely, since the broadcasting effect also weakened as time passed.","Until then, there was little point in exhausting themselves. The High Drake was certainly troublesome. But it wasn't their true objective. Their objective was what lay inside its stomach.","As the three fought, the High Drake suddenly folded its wings. Its gigantic body dropped from the sky like a falling mountain."]},{"number":1085,"title":"Chapter 1085: Unique Skill and Origin Battlefield Compensation [2]","paragraphs":["The phoenix's eyes flashed with lethal intent.","\"Law Skill...\"","\"...Eternal Sunfall.\"","Flames gathered frantically above it, forming a miniature sun that crashed downward. At the same time, Lord Seraphiel raised both hands, his voice echoing across the battlefield.","\"Law Skill.\"","\"Thousandfold Sea Prison.\"","Endless water chains erupted from the empty void, wrapping tightly around the High Drake's massive limbs, wings, and neck.","Only then did Fairy Sword Immortal Qing Yue finally speak.","\"Law Skill.\"","\"Severing Intent.\"","Compared to the phoenix's cataclysmic flames and Seraphiel's churning ocean, her skill produced no grand elemental phenomenon. Yet the instant her fingers lowered, every hidden Rank Four expert felt their skin prickle with sheer terror.","Laws were not limited to the elements. There were laws of fire, water, wind, earth, and lightning. But there were also laws strictly tied to concepts: Peace, Decay, Slaughter, Judgment, and Sharpness. Qing Yue's law clearly belonged to the latter.","The thousands of swords hovering behind her vanished. There was no explosion, no blinding light. They simply bypassed the distance entirely, manifesting instantly around the High Drake.","The next instant, countless deep wounds rent across its massive body. Even its deep-black scales, which had ruthlessly endured fire, water, and brute force, were effortlessly cut open.","The High Drake roared!","Black flames erupted from its open wounds, devouring the lingering sword intent while its flesh regenerated at a terrifying speed. But the phoenix's miniature sun descended immediately after.","BOOOOOOM!","Fire swallowed half the sky. Simultaneously, Seraphiel's water chains tightened, shifting into a vast, crushing ocean prison that sought to completely suppress the drake's movements.","The High Drake struggled violently. Its body burned, its scales split, and its wings were heavily bound. Yet, the more damage it suffered, the more terrifying its aura became.","Pain became fuel. Wounds became strength.","The Abyssal Pyre devoured the flames, the conceptual sword intent, and even parts of the holy water prison, converting it all into a torrent of power that surged back into its body.","For the first time, the expressions of all three peak experts shifted. This was their first time landing a solid, combined attack, and they hadn't expected it to produce an anomaly like this.","The phoenix released an enraged, piercing cry. \"This filthy thing is getting stronger!\"","Without waiting for a reply, its wings spread wide. Countless feathers ignited, shooting forward like a barrage of burning spears.","The High Drake swung its massive tail to intercept.","BOOM!","Half of the flaming feathers shattered upon impact, but the rest pierced deep into its body and detonated. At that exact moment, Seraphiel materialized directly above its head. A spear of heavily condensed water formed in his grasp, and he thrust it downward with absolute precision.","The spear pierced straight into one of the drake's eyes.","The High Drake roared, snapping its jaws upward with blinding speed. Seraphiel's expression warped. He retreated instantly, but the drake's razor-sharp teeth still grazed his arm. Though he desperately avoided losing the limb entirely, holy blood splashed into the air.","The hidden Rank Four awakeners watching from the shadows froze.","\"He almost got taken out...\"","But many also felt it was expected. That drake was simply too monstrous. Fortunately, they weren't the ones fighting it, or they would have perished within a few exchanges.","The three peak experts moved in unison once more, holding nothing back.","The phoenix rose high into the heavens, transforming into a blazing, blinding sun. Seraphiel's wings spread wide as a vast ocean manifested behind him like an entire world descending. High above them all stood Qing Yue, enveloped in a completely silent sword domain.","Three world-ending attacks formed simultaneously.","The High Drake looked upward. Its torn eye was already fully regenerated, the wounds across its body had closed, and its aura broke through its previous limits yet again. It unhinged its jaws. The black flame swirling within its throat burned brighter than ever before as it unleashed its devastating dragon breath.","The three attacks descended. The three distinct powers collided with the dragon breath at the exact same time.","For an instant, the entire battlefield turned a blinding, absolute white. Then, the explosion swallowed reality.","For a brief, agonizing moment... silence.","The entire battlefield vanished beneath an endless sea of white light. Then—","BOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOM!!!","A cataclysmic shockwave erupted outward. Mountains hundreds of miles away exploded into fine dust. Entire forests vanished from existence. The void cracked open repeatedly like shattered glass before desperately repairing itself.","Even the hidden spectators were forced to retreat several miles just to avoid being caught in the devastating aftermath.","When the light finally began to fade, everyone stared intently at the epicenter of the destruction.","But the first thing that greeted their eyes... was not the High Drake. Nor was it the three peak Rank Four experts.","Instead, a tiny creature stood in the dead center of the devastated battlefield.","It was... a rabbit.","A fluffy white rabbit, barely half a meter tall. Its long ears trembled violently, and its crimson eyes were filled with absolute, unadulterated terror. The lingering pressure alone nearly made it faint.","It looked around the apocalyptic wasteland in utter confusion.","\"...Squeak?\"","The battlefield fell completely silent. Every single Rank Four awakener froze in place. Even Seraphiel, Qing Yue, and the phoenix stared blankly at the rodent.","Where... was the drake?","Almost simultaneously, every single head snapped toward a direction nearly a hundred miles away from the battlefield.","A young human stood suspended in the sky.","Michael.","His breathing was heavy, and sweat drenched his forehead. His face was entirely pale from the sheer strain of maintaining Echoed Bestowal for so long. Yet, despite his absolute exhaustion... a tired, almost cheeky smile slowly spread across his face.","His gaze swept across the stunned crowd, finally locking onto Seraphiel.","The four-winged angel's calm, detached expression finally shattered. For the first time since the battle had begun, his pupils shrank into pinpricks.","Inside Michael's hand, a faint purple glow pulsed.","The Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","It was no longer inside the High Drake. It had somehow appeared in Michael's possession the exact moment the drake vanished.","\"...Impossible.\" The phoenix's voice was filled with sheer disbelief. \"How did he—\"","It stopped speaking. Its body had already transformed into a streak of roaring crimson fire.","At that exact same millisecond, Seraphiel and Qing Yue vanished together. The hundreds of hidden Rank Four awakeners reacted almost simultaneously, all of them erupting at top speed toward Michael's location.","No one spared the frightened rabbit another glance.","The rabbit blinked its crimson eyes.","\"...Squeak?\"","It looked around in complete confusion before instinctively trying to hop away.","Watching the tidal wave of countless terrifying figures rushing toward him, Michael merely smiled.","Then, he quietly uttered a single word once more.","\"Swap.\"","Space rippled. And in Michael's place, a second rabbit suddenly appeared in mid-air.","\"...Squeak?\""]},{"number":1086,"title":"Chapter 1086: Unique Skill and Origin Battlefield Compensation [3]","paragraphs":["Resources brought wealth. Wealth brought influence. And influence brought connections.","The past three months had been the first time in Michael's life where he had possessed an abundance of both resources and money.","With the enormous gains from the Land of Origin and his dimension cracks in Aurora, Michael had gradually begun interacting with circles that would once have been completely out of his reach.","One of those connections was naturally Rynne's family. Although Michael hadn't focused exclusively on working with them, they had indeed conducted several mutually beneficial transactions.","As his undead continued evolving, one problem became increasingly obvious. The stronger an undead became, the harder it was to increase its strength rapidly outside of evolution.","Using the vast amount of materials he had gathered, Michael exchanged for several batches of weapons from Rynne's family. None of them were particularly expensive.","Most were Common and Rare, or at most Extraordinary Grade. Many people questioned such a decision, but since it wasn't exactly wasteful, Michael had an easy time doing as he pleased.","With his wealth, purchasing Epic Grade equipment wasn't impossible if he truly wished to. But Michael didn't consider it worthwhile. It felt wasteful when he possessed a talent like Infinite Evolution.","Although he currently couldn't perform large-scale evolution outside his undead legion, that didn't mean such a thing would remain impossible forever. Who could say what the future held?","Perhaps one day, equipping every undead with Epic Grade weapons would still be unrealistic. But Extraordinary Grade? Michael believed that was entirely achievable.","Why waste enormous sums buying equipment today when tomorrow he might simply evolve it himself?","Because of these repeated transactions, Michael's network gradually expanded from various families and organizations to even some independent Rank Four supernaturals.","Whenever he required rare materials, he now possessed enough connections to at least inquire about them.","Naturally, Michael made full use of those connections. Especially when searching for evolution materials.","Among all the creatures under his command, there was one whose evolution he valued as much as his most important undead.","Wisdom.","Ever since evolving into a true Space Beast, Wisdom's potential had increased tremendously. However, Michael still insisted on preparing specialized evolution materials whenever possible.","After all, evolution wasn't merely about raising one's race. The quality of the materials used could subtly influence potential, strengthen the physique, enhance one's bloodline, and sometimes even grant entirely new abilities.","Space-attributed materials remained among the rarest resources in existence. Even with his connections, acquiring them had been anything but easy.","Fortunately, over the past three months Michael had managed to gather enough. Without hesitation, he used every single one on Wisdom, who successfully advanced into Rank Four as a Three-Star Epic Grade creature.","Its race did not change. Its appearance also remained almost identical to before. Perhaps only the faint spatial ripples continuously surrounding its body had become slightly more pronounced.","Most of its previous abilities simply grew stronger. Nearly every skill advanced by another level, and its control over space became incomparably smoother.","But among everything Wisdom gained, there was one newly obtained skill. One that had left even Michael speechless for quite a while.","Michael slowly opened Wisdom's status panel.","[Spatial Substitution]","The user anchors two valid targets within a maximum distance of 100 miles before instantly exchanging their positions through spatial manipulation.","The exchange is absolute once successfully activated, preserving the targets' momentum, orientation, and relative state at the instant of substitution.","Current Conditions:","Targets must not possess strong spatial accomplishment, or targets whose spatial stability greatly exceeds the user's limit may resist the substitution.","Maximum range between both anchors: 100 miles.","Current Cost:","Extremely High Energy Consumption. Consumption increases according to: Distance. Difference in strength between both targets. Stability of surrounding space.","Cooldown: None.","A ripple spread through the surrounding space.","Michael's figure abruptly appeared within a dense forest.","Towering ancient trees stretched toward the sky, their intertwined branches blotting out most of the moonlight. The air carried a thick scent of earth, leaves, and beastly mana.","The moment he arrived, dozens of pairs of crimson eyes turned toward him.","\"...\"","Monster rabbits. They were everywhere. Judging from the aura they emitted, nearly all of them were Rank One, with several Rank Twos scattered among the group.","At the very center, a rabbit nearly two meters tall slowly raised its head.","Rank Three. Its snow-white fur carried faint silver patterns while an unusually dense mana fluctuation surrounded its body. Clearly, this was the nest's leader.","Normally, the sudden appearance of an intruder would have immediately provoked a violent attack. Yet not a single rabbit moved. Every one of them trembled uncontrollably. Their crimson eyes were filled with instinctive terror. Even the Rank Three rabbit had flattened itself against the ground, its entire body shaking violently.","The reason wasn't Michael. It was the shadow looming above him.","The Undead High Drake.","Although Echoed Bestowal had already ended, the colossal undead still hovered silently above the forest.","Its three-hundred-meter body cast an oppressive shadow across the land below. The terrifying pressure leaking from its existence alone was enough to make every living creature within miles instinctively submit.","Michael looked at all this and shook his head. Although they were already quite some distance from the previous battlefield, a creature of this size could easily attract unnecessary attention.","Without hesitation, Michael stretched out his hand.","\"Return.\"","The gigantic High Drake let out one final low growl. Its colossal body suddenly collapsed into countless streams of ash.","The ash surged downward like a living river before pouring directly into Michael's body. Within only a few breaths, the mountain-sized creature had completely disappeared.","Silence returned to the forest.","Michael's knees bent slightly.","\"...Heavy.\"","He instinctively frowned. The moment the High Drake returned, Michael immediately felt as though several weighted objects had been placed upon his shoulders. His muscles tensed instinctively.","Fortunately, this wasn't his first time. Every time one of his engraved undead returned to his body, their passive traits and a few stat points were restored to him.","Michael's body quickly adapted to the restored attributes and weight. Within moments, the strange heaviness gradually disappeared as his movements once again became light and natural."]},{"number":1087,"title":"Chapter 1087: Unique Skill and Origin Battlefield Compensation [4]","paragraphs":["At the same time, warm energy slowly flowed throughout his body.","Michael exhaled softly.","\"Though it's not a full recovery, if I need to run or fight again I can do it without acting desperate.\"","Of course, Michael didn't mean this. If his life was truly in danger, he wouldn't hesitate to use his legendary-grade treasure to attack, or to summon all his powerful undead.","The previous situation, though it looked dangerous, hadn't required any losses to resolve.","\"I feel much better.\"","Michael flexed his fingers as he thought back to the hundreds of Rank Four awakeners he had left behind.","He smiled faintly.","The only thing that mattered now was the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense.","Michael slowly raised his right hand. Inside his palm, the faint purple glow had finally disappeared completely. The incense now rested quietly within his grasp, no longer broadcasting its location to the entire Fourth Layer.","\"...Finally.\"","After all the chasing and the moments balanced on the edge of real danger, it was finally his.","Heavenly Enlightenment Incense","Grade: Epic ★★★","Description: A supreme treasure born naturally within regions blessed by the Origin Will.","Once ignited, the incense releases Heavenly Enlightenment Mist.","Depending on the quantity burned and the intensity of the flame, the user's comprehension may increase by up to ten times.","Duration and effectiveness depend upon the amount consumed.","Michael couldn't wait to try it out, but even he knew this was currently not the right place to do so.","As for using it inside his legendary-grade item, that wasn't possible either.","Since entering the Origin Battlefield, Michael had tried to open a portal into the Mausoleum of Endless Dominion, but nothing happened. Just now he had tried again with the same result.","\"...So I can store things inside, but I can't enter physically?\"","Before entering the Origin Battlefield, he could create a portal and allow his body to enter the legendary-grade treasure's internal space.","But now the battlefield seemed to have restricted that function. He could place items inside and withdraw them, but his true body could not enter.","Of course, this applied only to this body, not the one in the Land of Origin.","Though he wondered whether he could bring his other body to the Origin Battlefield, Michael felt it was better not to attempt such a thing in such an unfamiliar place just yet.","\"It seems the only way to leave this place is through the battlefield's own rules.\"","Unfortunately, there was no exit option yet.","Just as Michael fell into thought, a new panel suddenly appeared before him.","[Compensation package prepared]","[Compensation delivered]","Michael froze in shock.","\"...Now?\"","A strange item appeared inside his storage space. Michael quickly took it out. It looked like a ticket made from pale golden crystal.","Countless tiny runes flowed across its surface, shifting like living light.","Without hesitation, Michael activated Detect.","[Treasure Amplification Voucher]","[Grade: Epic ★★★]","[Type: One-Time Consumable]","[Effect: Upon activation, the effect of any selected treasure below or equal to Legendary Grade will be increased by 200% for a limited duration] [Duration depends on the selected treasure's grade, stability, and energy consumption] Michael stared at the description. Then he slowly blinked.","\"...A 200% boost?\"","For several seconds, he didn't speak. Then his gaze slowly moved toward the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense in his other hand.","A treasure that could already increase comprehension by up to ten times. And now a ticket that could amplify a treasure's effect by 200%.","Michael's heart immediately began beating faster.","\"...Origin Will.\"","His lips slowly curved upward.","\"Your divine heart may be black, but you really do know how to give good treasures.\"","Fortunately, the gaze of the Origin Will was not currently on him.","Michael treated the two items as though they were made of glass.","He carefully placed the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense and the Treasure Amplification Voucher into his storage space. Only then did he finally relax.","Then, without sparing the trembling rabbit nest another glance, his figure blurred and disappeared from the forest.","Even after he left, none of the monster rabbits dared to move. The Rank Three rabbit remained flattened against the ground, its ears pressed tightly to its head.","Several minutes passed in silence. Only after confirming that the terrifying shadow would not return did the rabbits slowly begin breathing again.","Meanwhile, back at the previous battlefield, the atmosphere was indescribably strange.","Hundreds of Rank Four awakeners hovered in the distance, all staring at the empty space where Michael had disappeared.","As for the rabbit, upon sensing so many powerful gazes suddenly sweeping past it, it died from the shock on the spot.","No one spoke for several breaths.","Then the phoenix's furious cry shattered the silence.","\"That human!\"","Its flames surged violently, turning the surrounding sky red. To a proud creature like it, what had just happened was more than failure. It was humiliation.","Not only had a junior tricked it, but worse still, he had stolen the treasure right under its eyes and escaped.","The phoenix's golden eyes burned with killing intent. Of course, it wasn't merely angry. It was curious as well. What exactly had that skill been?","As for Lord Seraphiel, his attention was no longer on the vanished Michael. His gaze had shifted elsewhere.","A short distance away, Lady Aurelia lay weakly on the ground. Her white armor remained undamaged. The Epic Grade wand in her hand was also intact. But her body told a completely different story.","One arm hung unnaturally at her side. Blood stained the gaps between her armor. Her wings were in disarray, several feathers torn away. Her face was pale, and her usually cold emerald eyes looked blank.","She was alive. But clearly, she had suffered badly.","The surrounding Rank Four awakeners stared in shock. They had all assumed the human youth was the one in danger.","After all, he had been facing an angel of the same rank who had entered the Fourth Layer. Yet now, the angel looked as though she had barely survived. As for the human, he had escaped with the treasure.","For the first time, many of the hidden experts silently revised their evaluation of Michael.","That youth was not simply special. He was dangerous.","Someone finally muttered, \"Was that truly a human?\"","Several gazes shifted toward the speaker. The person hesitated, then added, \"For one thing, that human was far too beautiful. Could he be part elf?\"","A nearby human Rank Four awakener immediately frowned.","\"Are you looking down on humans?\"","Her expression remained cold.","\"Is it so hard to believe a human did this?\"","No one answered. A few silently rolled their eyes, but none bothered arguing. The woman who had spoken was one of the stronger Rank Four awakeners present.","They weren't friends, but there was no need to antagonize her over a casual remark.","The human expert also said nothing more.","Truthfully, everyone understood the reason behind the earlier doubt. It was not impossible for someone from a less advantaged race to defeat someone from a higher race.","Such things happened across the universe. Talent, class, inheritance, equipment, experience, and luck all mattered.","But this situation was different. Both Michael and Aurelia had entered the Fourth Layer while still at Rank Three. That alone proved both were uniquely extraordinary even among their own races.","And when comparing a unique angel to a unique human, common sense had subconsciously led everyone to assume the angel would be stronger.","Reality had just slapped that assumption apart.","The human had escaped. The angel had fallen. And the treasure was gone."]},{"number":1088,"title":"Chapter 1088: Timi","paragraphs":["Lord Seraphiel paid no attention whatsoever to the surrounding discussions.","Whether they were questioning Michael's race, or whether some among them were secretly pleased to see the Angel Race suffer such a humiliating setback, none of it mattered to him.","His attention remained solely on Aurelia.","He walked toward her and knelt beside the young angel. Without saying a word, he placed a hand upon her shoulder. A gentle azure radiance spread outward.","The fractured bones slowly shifted back into place and her internal injuries stabilized. The blood staining her armor gradually ceased flowing.","After several breaths, Aurelia's blank eyes slowly regained a trace of focus.","\"...Lord Seraphiel...\"","Her voice was weak. She stared blankly ahead for several moments before the events replayed within her mind.","The human. He had been too powerful. All along, when she had assumed dodging was all he could do, he had simply been playing with her.","Her fingers unconsciously tightened around the undamaged Epic Grade wand.","\"...I failed.\"","Lord Seraphiel said nothing and slowly helped her to her feet. He had experienced far too much in his life to feel anger at losing to a human.","Wasn't that female sword cultivator also a human? He didn't believe he could easily defeat her either. And she was not the only example. Over the centuries, he had encountered humans who defied every expectation their race was supposed to carry.","Fragile in body. Short in lifespan. Unremarkable in bloodline. And yet, somehow, they kept producing individuals without stop.","This was the reason they were considered top race on a grand scale if put together. Using quantity to bread quality was the way of the many human races in the universe.","It was something he had long since made peace with.","Of course, that wasn't to say he had no pride of his own. He simply understood the difference between pride and arrogance.","However Lord Seraphiel character was an anomaly in the angel race as well so most still thought like the female angel even in old age.","Though Aurelia could stand again, her aura remained noticeably weakened. Her emerald eyes unconsciously searched the horizon where Michael had disappeared.","The expression on her face was difficult to read. It wasn't fury, exactly.","For the first time since beginning her cultivation, someone of the same rank had completely outmatched her.","Lord Seraphiel noticed her gaze but said nothing. Instead, he looked once toward the empty battlefield.","\"The treasure has already changed hands. There is no point remaining.\"","As his words fell, spatial ripples quietly spread around them. Without another glance toward the surrounding spectators, the two figures disappeared.","Not far away, Qing Yue was already gone. The Fairy Sword Immortal had vanished long before the conversation among the spectators had even begun.","Whether she intended to continue searching for opportunities, or whether she had simply lost interest in everything that had happened, no one knew. Nor did anyone particularly care.","The phoenix remained suspended in the sky for several moments longer. Its enormous golden pupils burned with unwillingness. Finally, it let out a furious cry that echoed across the Fourth Layer.","\"This isn't over, human.\"","Its blazing body exploded into crimson flames before disappearing into the horizon. Whether it truly intended to search for Michael, or merely wished to vent its humiliation elsewhere, only it knew.","Gradually, the remaining Rank Four awakeners also began dispersing. Some headed deeper into the Fourth Layer. Others carefully searched the ruined battlefield.","A number of them quietly altered their direction, their intentions obvious to anyone paying attention, though whether they could actually find him was another matter entirely.","No one said anything aloud.","The battlefield that had gathered hundreds of Rank Four experts soon became strangely quiet once again. Only the devastated landscape remained as silent evidence of what had just taken place.","Meanwhile, somewhere within the first layer of the Origin Battlefield, a young girl, a boy of similar age, a forest wolf, and a bull-like creature stood before a transparent wall of light that seemed to stretch endlessly toward the heavens.","This was obviously Lily, her tamed beasts, and her new companion from the new world called Earth, who had introduced himself as Timi.","A great many strange things had happened to Timi during the past year.","It had begun on an ordinary Friday evening. He had just returned home after classes. Dinner had been prepared. His younger twin sisters had been arguing over something completely insignificant. Everything had been normal.","Then, without warning, towering black pillars descended from the sky. One moment there had been empty air. The next, gigantic obsidian pillars stretching beyond the clouds stood across the landscape.","Though nothing harmful happened immediately, such a supernatural phenomenon naturally caused widespread panic. Before communication networks completely collapsed, Timi had learned it wasn't just happening in his city, or just his country.","Reports flooded in from every direction. North America. South America. Europe. Africa. Asia. Australia. Even Antarctica. The pillars had appeared across every continent on Earth.","Then, just when everyone's guard had relaxed somewhat after several hours of nothing happening, the pillars opened.","And they came out.","Small red creatures poured out in overwhelming numbers. Green eyes. Twisted horns. Sharp claws. Skin the color of dried blood. They resembled the imps from countless fantasy stories almost perfectly.","Only they were real. And they enjoyed killing.","The military responded immediately. Gunfire filled the cities. Missiles destroyed entire districts. For a while, humanity believed victory was possible.","Then stronger creatures emerged. Winged monsters. Towering giants. Horned beasts whose bodies burned with crimson fire. As the weeks passed, the creatures coming from the pillars became increasingly powerful.","Although no one truly knew what demons were supposed to look like, looking at those monsters, almost everyone instinctively thought of the same place.","Hell.","That was how Earth's apocalypse began.","Timi had once belonged to a family of seven. His parents. His grandfather. His older brother. Himself. And his two younger twin sisters.","Now only three remained. Him. And the twins. The rest had died during the first month."]},{"number":1089,"title":"Chapter 1089: Espers, Prophets and Awakeners","paragraphs":["The memory still haunted Timi every night.","Life afterward had become unimaginably cruel. Food became currency. Medicine became priceless. Trust became a luxury.","Fortunately, the three siblings eventually reached one of humanity's fortified settlements. It wasn't paradise. Far from it. But at least they survived.","Over the following months, Timi gradually adapted to the new world. The timid middle school student disappeared. In his place stood someone capable of killing monsters without trembling, even if they were only weaker ones.","Humanity's greatest turning point came several months after the apocalypse. Researchers discovered something astonishing. Within the bodies of certain demons existed an unusual biological substance.","After countless failed experiments, someone finally managed to refine it into a serum. Those who survived the injection awakened extraordinary abilities.","Superhuman strength. Elemental control. Enhanced senses. Regeneration. Various powers appeared. Those individuals became known as Espers. They were the reason humanity still existed. Without them, Earth would likely have fallen within months.","There was another method as well. Some people discovered that consuming specially prepared monster flesh occasionally produced similar effects. The success rate was dramatically lower, but it was significantly safer.","The serum was different. Its success rate was terrifyingly low. Many people simply died. Others mutated into monsters themselves.","Timi had been offered the serum more than once. Each time, he refused. Not because he lacked courage, but because he lacked the luxury of risking his life.","If he died, who would protect his sisters? He had already witnessed what happened to orphaned children inside the settlements.","The thought alone was enough to make him reject every offer. He would rather remain ordinary than gamble his sisters' future on uncertain odds.","Only one year had passed since the apocalypse. Yet Timi had seen enough.","He had seen people murder one another over a loaf of bread. Watched powerful Espers abuse those too weak to resist. Witnessed settlements abandon thousands simply because there wasn't enough food.","The apocalypse hadn't merely revealed monsters. It had revealed humanity as well.","Because of that, Timi trusted very few people. Perhaps no one, besides his sisters.","Not even the so-called Prophets.","Those mysterious individuals had appeared several months after the pillars among various human survivor groups.","Unlike Espers, their powers seemed different. Stranger.","They claimed to receive revelations from divine beings. They healed and performed miracles. Some possessed abilities surpassing even high-ranking Espers. But every single one preached the same message.","\"Worship. Worship the true gods. Only faith can save humanity.\"","Timi never believed them. For some reason, he felt these so-called divine beings might be no better than the demons themselves.","Fortunately, humanity's luck finally seemed to be changing.","Two months ago, an entirely new group of people began appearing among the survivors. Unlike Espers, these individuals possessed powers that were fundamentally different. And far stronger.","Unfortunately, for ordinary people, almost nothing was known about them. Rumors spread every single day, and none could be confirmed. The only thing everyone agreed upon was that they were helping humanity.","Many of the larger settlements that had been on the verge of collapse had managed to survive because these mysterious individuals suddenly intervened.","For a while, hope slowly returned.","Five days ago, Timi's own life had completely changed. He had become one of the chosen as well.","A strange translucent screen had appeared before his eyes. From that day onward, Timi discovered he could enter an entirely different world. A world unlike Earth.","Unfortunately, only he could enter, and he could not bring his sisters. Because of that, no matter how miraculous the new world was, his time there remained limited. He could never abandon his sisters for long.","Fortunately, his System wasn't limited to that mysterious world. The demons invading Earth also granted experience points. Timi's strength increased every single day.","His second greatest fortune was the talent he had awakened alongside the System.","[Talent: Devour]","Unfortunately, his system gave no descriptions. Just a single name.","Fortunately, his System didn't stop him from experimenting. Through several attempts, Timi discovered what the talent actually did. Its ability wasn't as simple as swallowing things. Rather, it extracted something from a target.","Not everything possessed something worth taking. A rock remained just a rock. An ordinary tree rarely yielded anything. But creatures, especially supernatural creatures, were different.","Demons were by far the best examples. After killing one, Timi could activate Devour on its corpse. Most of the time, tiny streams of energy entered his body. Then a notification would appear.","[Strength +0.1] [Agility +0.2] [Constitution +0.1]","There was no pattern. The attributes obtained seemed completely random. But every successful absorption permanently strengthened him. It was because of this that his physical abilities had increased so rapidly within only five days.","That wasn't the most unbelievable part.","Very occasionally, instead of attribute points, something else appeared. A skill. The probability was absurdly low. But it existed. To date, Timi had only obtained three. The third situation was by far the most valuable experience.","It had belonged to a particularly troublesome demon. Unlike the other monsters that charged directly into settlements, that creature never appeared openly. It hid and silently slaughtered people one after another.","Fortunately, its actual combat ability wasn't particularly high. After tracking it for an entire day, Timi had finally managed to kill it. When he activated Devour, something unexpected happened.","Instead of attribute points, he had obtained a bloodline he could integrate into his body.","The System had called it an Extraordinary Grade Shadow Demon Bloodline. He didn't know what grade meant, but the effect of the bloodline made it clear it was something valuable.","As for the skill, it was called Presence Concealment. Once activated, his presence diminished dramatically. His footsteps. His breathing.","Even the instinctive awareness living creatures possessed toward nearby enemies became blurred.","However, Timi could tell its true power came from the bloodline supporting it. Together with his class, his strength had grown by leaps and bounds thanks to his talent and no level ten creature had ever been able to match him.","This had all been the case until he met a girl.","A girl who called herself Lily."]},{"number":1090,"title":"Chapter 1090 Observation (GT and PS Bonus - )","paragraphs":["It had only been a little over two hours since they had met.","Objectively speaking, that was nowhere near enough time to truly understand another person. But during those two hours, Timi had already learned a few things about Lily.","The first was her personality.","Unless she was an exceptionally skilled actress, Lily was an incredibly lively person. She laughed easily and became excited over the smallest discoveries.","The Origin Battlefield was unimaginably rich. Within only a little over two hours, Timi and Lily had already discovered numerous valuable resources.","Either rare herbs nourished by dense energy grew beneath ancient trees untouched for countless years, or strange ores had naturally formed, each containing astonishing concentrations of mana, along with many other natural resources.","Of course, the truly valuable treasures were rarely found lying in the open. They belonged to the rulers of each territory.","Every powerful boss monster they encountered possessed a nest or dwelling, and those places almost always contained additional resources gathered over years of inhabiting regions rich in energy.","More importantly, defeating one boss guaranteed the appearance of a Treasure Orb. Unlike ordinary monsters, boss creatures never failed to leave one behind.","That alone made hunting them worthwhile. The resources hidden inside their territories were merely an additional reward.","Fortunately, the First Layer wasn't particularly dangerous for Lily and Timi, as both possessed more than enough strength to deal with almost every creature they encountered.","Because of that, the pace at which they accumulated resources was astonishingly fast.","By the time several more hours had passed, the amount of herbs, ores, monster materials, and other valuable resources stored away had already exceeded everything Timi had gathered during the past five days in the Land of Origin combined.","Of course, that had much to do with his limited time there, but the Land of Origin wasn't exactly a wild wilderness like this place either.","As the two grew increasingly familiar, the cold, solemn demeanor Lily had displayed when they first met had completely disappeared. It seemed that once she confirmed he wasn't an enemy, she relaxed almost immediately.","The second thing he noticed was something much harder to describe.","Purity.","Not exactly pure innocence or naivety. Lily clearly wasn't naive. This much was evident in the fact that she wasn't someone who simply believed every stranger she met within the last few hours. But she still possessed a kind of purity that Timi hadn't seen in a very long time.","Watching her, he found himself unconsciously thinking that this was how people their age were supposed to act. There was curiosity. Excitement. Occasional embarrassment.","Even childish competitiveness. When she proudly introduced her tamed beasts, she genuinely looked like an ordinary teenage girl showing off something precious to a new friend.","There were moments she pouted over trivial things. Moments she laughed so hard she had to hold her stomach.","Moments she excitedly asked endless questions about Earth despite barely understanding half of his answers.","For just a brief moment, Timi almost forgot the world he came from.","It had only been one year since Earth's apocalypse. Just one year. Yet people like Lily had almost completely disappeared from his life.","Children no longer acted like children. Teenagers no longer acted like teenagers. Adults had become even worse.","Everyone lived with guarded eyes. Every conversation carried hidden intentions. Every smile could be questioned. Every kindness demanded suspicion.","The apocalypse had forced everyone to mature far too quickly.","No. \"Mature\" wasn't even the correct word. It had forced them to survive. Those were two completely different things.","Timi himself was living proof. A year ago, if someone had told him he would one day calmly cut apart monsters while stepping over corpses without vomiting, he would have called them insane.","Now it had become routine. He couldn't even remember the last time he had hesitated before killing.","The third thing Timi discovered was that Lily was rich. Very rich.","At first, he had merely suspected it. After all, even someone unfamiliar with magical equipment could tell that her armor and weapon were extraordinary.","Now he finally understood why the dark elf they had encountered earlier had immediately assumed Lily came from some noble family.","Naturally, Timi had asked her about it once they had grown more comfortable with each other. She denied it almost immediately.","From what he had gathered over the past few hours, Lily's world didn't even seem to operate under a system of kings and nobles like the area of the Land of Origin he was familiar with.","She also seemed surprisingly ignorant about the power dynamics of her own world, for some reason.","Although she denied being from a noble family, she did admit one thing: her cousin was extremely rich.","According to Lily, her cousin was also incredibly powerful. As for how powerful, Timi had no way of judging. But the first statement he believed without the slightest doubt, because Lily herself was practically walking evidence.","After obtaining her permission, Timi had used Detect on her equipment.","Every single piece, her armor, her sword, even several accessories she wore, were all Rare Grade, Three-Star treasures. Not one piece was lower.","It was as though her cousin considered anything below that grade unworthy of her.","Even Timi, who had only entered this world five days ago, could tell how extravagant that was.","After all, during their journey through the Origin Battlefield, they had already obtained several Treasure Orbs. Yet none of the treasures inside had reached that level.","The highest had been a Rare Grade item obtained from killing a Two-Star Rare Grade level ten boss.","Fortunately, Lily patiently explained the grading system to him. Only then did Timi finally understand just how valuable his own gains had been.","The Extraordinary Grade Shadow Demon Bloodline he had absorbed was far stronger than he had originally imagined.","No wonder the creature had almost wiped out an entire settlement before anyone even realized it existed.","Combined with Presence Concealment, it had become an assassin capable of silently approaching almost any target.","If such an ability had appeared among ordinary demons, the consequences would have been unimaginable."]},{"number":1091,"title":"Chapter 1091 Level 2 Region (GT and PS Bonus - )","paragraphs":["Realizing this, Timi unconsciously became even more cautious about revealing the true extent of his abilities.","If a single Extraordinary Grade bloodline could produce such astonishing effects, then the secrets hidden within his talent, Devour, were likely far greater than he had initially believed.","The fourth thing Timi noticed was that Lily was extremely powerful. He didn't want to admit it at first. But after fighting beside her for several hours, he had reached a conclusion he couldn't deny.","If Lily truly wanted to harm him, she probably wouldn't be able to kill him unless he made a fatal mistake, thanks to his Extraordinary Grade Shadow Demon Bloodline and the various abilities he had obtained through Devour. But hurting him was an ability she absolutely possessed.","Lily's combat style was unlike anything Timi had witnessed on Earth. Even those so-called experts who had been fighting for a full year couldn't match her. Were her skills at intermediate rank?","As for the rank above that, he didn't even know what existed there. In any case, she was a formidable fighter.","Of course, her own strength wasn't the only thing she possessed. There were also her two tamed beasts. The massive bull-like creature. And the forest wolf.","However, Timi wasn't particularly concerned about either of them. Not because they were weak. Objectively speaking, both were much stronger than ordinary monsters of the same level, and had now even maxed up to level ten.","But rather than saying they protected Lily, it was Lily who protected them. Most enemies never even managed to approach the two beasts before Lily had already dealt with the threat herself.","In all honesty, Timi considered both beasts somewhat underwhelming. Compared to Lily herself, they contributed very little to most battles. Still, they weren't his companions. Nor were they his beasts.","Everyone fought differently. Perhaps Lily simply preferred protecting them until they grew stronger. Whatever the reason, Timi kept his thoughts to himself.","After all, commenting on someone else's companions after only knowing them for a few hours would be both rude and unnecessary.","The transparent wall stretched endlessly in both directions. It rose from the earth like a sheet of glass reaching toward the heavens, dividing the land into two completely different regions.","Timi stood before it, his gaze fixed on the faint ripples flowing across its surface. A while earlier, both he and Lily had activated Detect. The result had been identical.","[Level 2 Region Boundary]","Neither of them was unfamiliar with the concept of a region. After all, they were currently standing inside one. Everything they had explored until now belonged to a Level 1 Region.","The strongest monsters they had encountered had only reached Level 10, and among all the bosses they had defeated, the highest grade had merely been a Two-Star Rare creature.","Naturally, the land beyond this boundary should follow the same pattern. Only everything would be stronger.","Timi stood quietly before the wall before finally glancing sideways.","\"So... do we pass through?\"","Lily continued staring at the transparent barrier for several more seconds before nodding slowly.","\"I think so.\"","Neither of them moved immediately. Although they had defeated every opponent they encountered in the Level 1 Region with relative ease, that didn't mean they intended to blindly rush into unknown danger.","After thinking for a while, Lily finally reached a conclusion.","\"Even if the monsters are stronger, I believe they shouldn't be strong enough to threaten our lives as long as we're careful.\"","It wasn't blind confidence, but simply an evaluation based on everything they had experienced so far. Within the Level 1 Region, the two of them had practically walked wherever they pleased.","Not only had they continuously hunted boss monsters when they found one, but several members of other races had even attempted to rob them.","Unfortunately for those people, instead of obtaining treasures, they had only earned themselves painful beatings before fleeing in embarrassment.","Not a single one had managed to force either Timi or Lily into a desperate situation.","If Level 2 was merely one level higher than Level 1, then the difference shouldn't suddenly become so overwhelming that they couldn't survive. At worst, they would simply retreat.","After reaching that conclusion, Lily decided not to risk either of them first. Instead, she allowed the massive bull to approach the boundary. The beast walked forward steadily before its enormous body touched the transparent wall.","Ripples spread gently across its surface. Then the bull passed through without the slightest resistance. Nothing happened. The creature simply continued standing on the opposite side as though nothing had occurred.","The two watched quietly for several moments and had the bull go back and forth repeatedly. Seeing that it remained completely unharmed, they finally relaxed.","Without any further hesitation, Lily stepped through the boundary. Timi followed immediately behind her. The forest wolf crossed last.","The instant all three entered the Level 2 Region, faint ripples spread across the transparent wall once more before returning to complete stillness.","[Current Location: Zeroth Layer]","[Region: Level 2 Wolfhowl Forest]","The moment Lily stepped into the new region, her eyes widened slightly.","\"The mana here feels denser.\"","A faint current of energy drifted through the surrounding forest, brushing against her skin like an invisible breeze. She slowly took a deep breath.","Compared to the Level 1 Region, the spiritual energy filling this place was noticeably richer. It wasn't enough to produce an overwhelming difference, but the change was quite obvious.","A moment later, Timi also sensed the increased mana density.","Although he had never practiced cultivation, he was no longer an ordinary human. His Extraordinary Grade Shadow Demon Bloodline had enhanced every aspect of his body, including his senses.","\"It does feel... different.\"","He couldn't describe it as precisely as Lily. But even he could feel that the air itself seemed heavier. Richer. As though every breath contained more energy than before.","The two exchanged glances.","\"If the mana density is higher, then the treasures should be better as well.\" Lily theorized, and immediately after understanding this, neither of them could hide the excitement in their eyes."]},{"number":1092,"title":"Chapter 1092 Stronger Region (Magic Castle Bonus - )","paragraphs":["The resources Lily and Timi had gathered throughout the Level 1 Region had already been astonishing.","Although the overwhelming majority were raw materials, that didn't reduce their value in the slightest.","Many herbs could be consumed directly to strengthen one's body.","Lily, in particular, had harvested practically everything she came across. She wasn't planning to use any of it herself. Instead, she intended to give everything to her cousin.","Although she didn't fully understand their exact values, she knew her cousin definitely did. Whatever she couldn't use, he would certainly exchange for something more suitable for her.","Meanwhile, Timi's reasoning was much simpler. He gathered everything because it was valuable. Even if he couldn't personally use a particular herb or ore, someone else in the Land of Origin might appreciate it.","As long as something possessed value, there would always be someone willing to trade for it. In exchange, he could obtain whatever resources best suited his own growth.","Because of that, neither of them had shown the slightest intention of leaving behind anything remotely valuable.","After all, no one had ever complained about possessing too many treasures. Of course, they only took as much as they could in consideration of their storage space.","The two continued deeper into the Wolfhowl Forest. The towering trees became denser, their branches intertwining high above to block out much of the light.","Thick roots snaked across the forest floor, while the richer mana made even the ordinary plants appear far more vibrant than those in the Level 1 Region.","Barely ten minutes later, both Lily and Timi stopped at almost the same time.","Twenty meters ahead, a group of wolves slowly emerged from between the trees. There were over twenty of them.","Their dark-gray fur shimmered faintly beneath the dense mana, and every pair of emerald eyes stared directly at the intruders.","Without hesitation, both activated Detect. Panels immediately appeared before them.","[Dire Forest Wolf]","[Level: 5]","[Grade: Rare ★]","[Dire Forest Wolf]","[Level: 6]","[Grade: Rare ★★]","[Dire Forest Wolf]","[Level: 7]","[Grade: Rare ★★]","The two silently read through the information. A strange expression appeared on both their faces.","The levels were nothing special. Level Five. Level Six. Level Seven.","Those were even lower than many monsters they had fought inside the previous region. Yet their grades were completely different.","Every single wolf was at least One-Star Rare. Several had even reached Two-Star Rare.","In the Level 1 Region, a One-Star Rare creature was already qualified to become the ruler of a territory.","A Two-Star Rare monster was unquestionably a boss. Yet here, an entire pack possessed that level of quality.","It was as though boss monsters had suddenly become ordinary beasts.","Before either of them could think any further, a deep growl echoed through the forest.","ROAR!","The lead wolf lowered its body before shooting forward like a gray arrow. The remaining wolves followed immediately.","More than twenty figures burst through the undergrowth simultaneously, surrounding the two from multiple directions with astonishing coordination.","Unfortunately for them, they had chosen the wrong targets.","Lily calmly stepped forward. Her sword left its sheath in a single smooth motion. A silver flash crossed the forest. The charging wolf hadn't even realized what had happened. Its head slid cleanly from its neck.","Blood sprayed into the air as the body continued forward for several more meters before collapsing heavily onto the ground.","Almost simultaneously, Timi also moved. His movements were nearly impossible to follow.","One moment he stood where he was. The next, he had already appeared beside another wolf. His sword swept across with ruthless precision.","A second head flew into the air. Before the corpse even struck the ground, Timi had already disappeared again.","The remaining wolves instinctively tried to change formation, but never got the opportunity. Silver light flashed repeatedly, and dark shadows flickered between the trees. One corpse after another crashed onto the forest floor.","Within only a few breaths, the entire wolf pack had been annihilated.","The forest returned to silence. The only remaining sound was the slow dripping of blood onto the leaves below.","Timi looked at the corpses with a serious expression.","\"We should be careful.\"","Lily nodded with an equally solemn expression.","\"We should be careful.\"","Lily nodded with an equally solemn expression.","\"Yeah.\"","Although they had killed the pack quickly, neither of them was foolish enough to think the fight meant the Level 2 Region was harmless. These wolves had only been ordinary monsters here. Yet in the Level 1 Region, every single one of them would have been treated as a boss-level creature. That meant the danger of this place was fundamentally different.","If ordinary wolves were already One-Star and Two-Star Rare creatures, then what about a Level 10 boss in this region? Would it still be Rare Grade? Or would it be something even higher?","The thought made Lily's grip around her sword tighten.","Timi silently crouched beside one of the corpses and examined it.","\"This place really isn't the same.\"","Lily walked over and stored several of the wolf corpses away.","\"Let's not rush too deep for now. We'll explore the outer area first.\"","Timi nodded.","\"That's safer.\"","The Forest Wolf beside Lily sniffed one of the corpses before letting out a low whine. Lily glanced at it.","\"What? You feel pressured?\"","The wolf lowered its head slightly. Lily sighed and patted it.","\"Then you and Big Bull stay behind us.\"","Timi looked at the two beasts, then at Lily. He still didn't say what he was thinking. The two continued forward, but their pace had clearly slowed.","As Lily and Timi carefully made their way through the Wolfhowl Forest, Michael had finally recovered most of his energy in the Fourth Layer.","Inside a dark cave hidden between two cliffs, he slowly opened his eyes.","\"Almost back to normal.\"","He stood up and stretched his shoulders. After resting for a while, the exhaustion from Echoed Bestowal had faded greatly. His soul still felt slightly strained, but it was no longer painful.","Michael was just about to leave when heavy footsteps echoed from outside the cave. A moment later, a five-meter-tall ape-like monster walked in, dragging a bloody prey in one hand."]},{"number":1093,"title":"Chapter 1093 Venting (Magic Castle Bonus - )","paragraphs":["The monster froze.","Michael froze too.","They stared at each other in silence.","Michael glanced around the cave, then looked back at the ape.","\"...No wonder this place looked like a dwelling. You must have been away for so long that your traces had long since washed off. Or is this just one of your hideouts?\"","Michael activated Detect.","[Ironback Mountain Ape]","[Grade: Extraordinary ★★★]","[Rank: 4]","[Level: 85]","Michael raised an eyebrow.","\"Oh?\"","The ape's eyes immediately turned bloodshot.","ROOOAR!","It threw away the prey in its hand and rushed forward, its massive fist smashing toward Michael like a falling boulder.","Michael calmly raised one hand.","BANG!","His palm caught the fist directly. The impact exploded outward. The cave could not withstand the force at all. Cracks spread across the walls before the entire structure burst apart. Rocks flew everywhere as dust filled the air.","A heartbeat later, the cave was gone.","Michael stood beneath the light of the three moons, one hand still holding the ape's fist. The enormous monster strained with all its strength, but Michael didn't move. He looked up at it and sighed.","\"I just finished resting.\"","His fingers tightened.","CRACK!","The ape's expression changed. Despite its brute appearance, its instincts were exceptionally sharp. The instant pain shot through its hand, it forcefully tore its arm free and retreated several steps.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","Each backward step shattered the rocky ground beneath its feet.","Instead of pursuing immediately, Michael slowly rolled his shoulders. A smile gradually appeared on his face.","The frustration that had accumulated from being chased by hundreds of Rank Four experts, the pressure of constantly calculating every move, and the exhaustion brought by Echoed Bestowal could finally be vented.","The ape, however, interpreted the smile very differently.","It roared furiously. Its chest swelled before it pounded both fists against itself.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","The sound echoed throughout the mountain. Without warning, the gigantic creature vanished.","BOOM!","A fist descended from above. Michael calmly shifted half a step sideways. The fist smashed into the earth. The entire cliff trembled.","Before the ape could recover, Michael's elbow descended onto its forearm.","CRACK!","Bone snapped. The ape howled before swinging its other arm horizontally. Michael lowered his body. The enormous arm swept over his head, uprooting dozens of ancient trees behind him.","The instant the attack missed, Michael's fist struck upward.","BANG!","The punch landed directly beneath the ape's chin. The five-meter monster was actually lifted off its feet. Its enormous body spun through the air before crashing hundreds of meters away.","BOOOOOOM!","A section of the forest disappeared beneath the impact. The ape climbed back to its feet almost immediately. Its breathing had already become noticeably heavier. Blood trickled from the corner of its mouth. Its crimson eyes stared at Michael with increasing disbelief.","It couldn't understand. It was the physically strongest creature throughout this entire territory. How was this tiny creature overpowering it?","ROOOOAR!!","Its roar became even more furious. This time it tore an enormous boulder from the ground and hurled it. Michael didn't dodge. He punched forward.","BOOM!","The mountain-sized rock exploded into countless fragments. The broken pieces rained across the forest like meteors. The ape rushed through the cloud of debris. Its fists became a blur.","BOOM! BANG! BOOM!","Punch after punch descended. The surrounding landscape continuously collapsed. Cliffs broke apart. Ancient trees shattered. The ground split open beneath the relentless barrage.","Yet not a single attack landed on Michael, and every successful dodge was almost immediately followed by a strike of his own.","Gradually, as the fight progressed, the ape realized something. This two-legged being wasn't fighting seriously. He was playing.","Rage instantly exploded inside it. Its aura erupted violently. The surrounding mana surged toward its enormous body. Its muscles visibly expanded. Blue veins spread across its arms. Its fur stood upright.","With another furious roar, it slammed both fists together before smashing downward with enough force to flatten a hill.","Michael finally raised both hands.","BOOOOOOM!!","The collision generated a deafening explosion. A circular shockwave spread for hundreds of meters. The ground beneath Michael's feet sank several meters. Yet he remained standing.","The ape, however, was horrified. Its strongest attack had been stopped. With bare hands.","Michael slowly pushed upward. The ape's gigantic arms were forced higher and higher despite its desperate resistance. Then Michael suddenly disappeared.","The ape's pupils contracted.","Too late.","BANG!","A punch buried itself deep into its stomach. The enormous creature bent nearly ninety degrees. Before it could even cough blood, Michael grabbed one of its arms. He twisted.","CRACK!","The shoulder dislocated. Using the momentum, he swung the five-meter monster completely off the ground.","BOOM!","It smashed into the earth.","BOOM!","Michael slammed it down again. The entire mountain shook.","Again. BOOM!","Again. BOOM!","Again. BOOM!","By the fifth impact, the ape's struggles had noticeably weakened. Its entire body was covered in blood. Several ribs had pierced through its flesh. One eye had swollen shut. Its breathing sounded like a broken bellows.","Finally, it gathered the last of its strength and kicked away from Michael, retreating hundreds of meters in panic. It no longer wished to fight. Its instincts screamed only one thing.","Run.","Michael watched the fleeing figure and smiled faintly.","\"You've already helped me enough.\"","His figure vanished. The distance of several hundred meters disappeared in an instant. The ape had only enough time to widen its remaining eye.","Michael's fist descended.","BOOOOOOM!!","The punch crushed straight through its skull. The gigantic body froze. Michael slowly withdrew his fist. The colossal corpse crashed heavily onto the shattered earth.","Silence returned beneath the three moons.","He exhaled slowly. The frustration that had been weighing on his heart finally disappeared.","It had been a long time since he had experienced being pursued relentlessly. The last time had been back when he was still a Rank Two Awakener.","At that time, he had also been at the very peak of his rank and had found himself being relentlessly chased by a Rank Four officer of the Federation alongside Director Arven.","Now, history had strangely repeated itself. Once again, he was standing at the peak of his current realm.","The coincidence was almost absurd."]},{"number":1094,"title":"Chapter 1094 Origin Ranking (Magic Castle Bonus - )","paragraphs":["Fortunately, neither incident had truly placed his life in genuine danger. Both times, retreating had simply been the wiser choice.","Still, it wasn't an experience Michael particularly enjoyed. The thought of this becoming some strange pattern made even him feel slightly uncomfortable.","If fate decided to repeat itself again after he reached the peak of Rank Four, the ones chasing him would probably be Demigods.","That was a genuinely terrifying thought.","Fortunately, after venting everything on the unfortunate ape, the lingering frustration had finally disappeared completely.","Just then, a faint radiance condensed beside the ape's corpse. Michael's gaze shifted.","\"...A Treasure Orb?\"","He was surprised that his first monster in the Origin Battlefield would actually produce one. At least the orbs were one thing the Origin Battlefield shared with the Land of Origin.","The sphere floated quietly beside the corpse, releasing gentle waves of energy. Without hesitation, Michael reached out and crushed it. The orb dissolved into countless motes of light before gathering together once more.","A folded fan appeared in his hand. Its frame was forged from dark jade-like metal, while its surface shimmered with countless silver patterns resembling flowing wind.","Michael activated Detect.","[Skywind Spirit Fan]","Grade: Extraordinary ★★","Effect: Upon activation, releases compressed wind blades. Can also generate powerful wind currents for flight, defense, or suppression.","Michael nodded slightly.","\"Not bad.\"","It was a relatively ordinary treasure, but a treasure regardless. Michael casually stored both the Skywind Spirit Fan and the ape's corpse.","Just as he was about to leave, a translucent panel suddenly materialized before his eyes, bringing him to a stop.","[Congratulations to all Awakeners on successfully entering the Origin Battlefield] [As this is the first opening of the Origin Battlefield, special protection has been granted by the Origin Will] [The duration of this first expedition has been reduced] [Returning to your respective worlds will become available after the countdown reaches zero] [Remaining Time: 69 Hours 43 Minutes 17 Seconds]","Michael quickly calculated. Three days. Originally seventy-two hours. A little over two hours had already passed since entering the battlefield.","\"So the first expedition only lasts three days...\"","That wasn't necessarily a bad thing. Many people had undoubtedly entered the Origin Battlefield completely unprepared.","Three days was enough to allow everyone to experience this place without being trapped here for too long.","As Michael continued reading, the panel changed once again. The previous notification disappeared before a new one slowly emerged.","[The Origin Rankings are now officially open]","[All participants will be ranked according to their overall performance within the Origin Battlefield] [Rankings will be updated continuously]","[The higher your ranking, the richer your rewards]","Additional panels appeared.","[Origin Ranking Challenge Rules]","[Each participant may issue up to three ranking challenges per month.] [Each participant may be challenged up to three times per month] [Challenges may only be issued against participants within an approved ranking range of ten ranks above] [If challenged, the target may refuse]","[Each participant may refuse up to three challenges three times for each challenge per month] [After three refusals for a challenge, any further refusal will be treated as a forfeit. After three refusals for three challenges, any further refusal will be treated as a forfeit] [Upon forfeiture, the challenger and challenged participant will exchange ranking positions] [Once a ranking challenge begins, both participants will be transferred to a designated battlefield] [Within the battlefield, defeat can only occur through death or voluntary surrender] [All summons, contracted creatures, equipment, talents, skills, and treasures are considered part of the participant's strength] [Monthly rewards will be distributed according to final ranking positions] Michael's expression became thoughtful.","His first thought was whether the rewards would be similar to the Heavenly Enlightenment Incense. If they were, then the Origin Rankings would become something truly terrifying.","The Origin Battlefield was already bound to be a bloody place.","A place where one could die at any moment because of a single treasure, a single opportunity, or even because someone stronger simply disliked them. But even so, awakeners would not desperately risk their lives for just any treasure.","If the monthly rewards were ordinary, Michael dared to say many people would simply ignore the rankings and focus on exploring safely. After all, survival came first.","However, if the rewards were even remotely close in value to the incense he had obtained, then things would be completely different. A Three-Star Epic treasure capable of increasing comprehension by up to ten times.","Even peak Rank Four monsters had chased him like madmen for it. If ranking rewards offered treasures of similar grade, or worse, something even more precious, then the Origin Battlefield would no longer be merely dangerous.","It would become a slaughterhouse.","Michael's eyes narrowed slightly.","\"Monthly rewards...\"","That meant this wasn't a one-time temptation.","\"Looks like this place is going to become even more troublesome than I thought.\"","Then, without hesitation, he selected the option to open the rankings.","The panel shifted.","[Origin Rankings]","[Rank 1: Solmara Veyr]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Celestial Flame Realm]","[Rank 2: Thal'Rokan]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Ancient Dragon Realm]","[Rank 3: Jian Wuhen]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Azure Sword Realm]","[Rank 4: Aureon]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Celestial Dominion]","[Rank 5: Kaelthar]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Titanforge Realm]","[Rank 6: Narael]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Starfall Realm]","[Rank 7: Arven Vale]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Aurora]","Michael's eyes abruptly stopped.","\"...Arven?\"","For a moment, he thought he had read it wrongly. He stared at the seventh name again.","[Rank 7: Arven Vale]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Aurora]","Aurora. The same realm as him. And that name.","Michael's expression became strange.","\"Surely...\"","His lips twitched slightly.","\"This isn't Director Arven from the academy, right?\"","The thought appeared almost immediately. After all, how many Rank Four level 100 awakeners named Arven could Aurora possibly have?","Michael slowly rubbed his chin. Back then, Director Arven had already given him an unfathomable feeling. Even after Michael grew stronger, he still never truly understood how deep the director's strength went.","But Rank 7 in the entire Origin Battlefield?","That was a little too ridiculous."]},{"number":1095,"title":"Chapter 1095: Only A Thousand","paragraphs":["Michael continued reading.","[Rank 8: Vhalros]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Abyssal Bone Realm]","-","[Rank 9: Yue Hanzhen]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Nine Heavens Dao Realm]","-","[Rank 10: Orvath]","[Level: 100]","[Realm: Worldroot Realm]","The ranking revealed very little. Only one's ranking, name, level, and realm. There was no race or class included.","Still, for knowledgeable people, the realm alone already revealed plenty.","A name from the Ancient Dragon Realm was most likely a dragon. A name from the Celestial Dominion was most likely an angel. A name from the Azure Sword Realm or Nine Heavens Dao Realm was most likely a cultivator.","However, despite these interesting speculations, Michael's attention remained fixed on Rank 7.","After a few seconds of silence, Michael finally exhaled.","\"...Director, just what kind of person are you?\"","Michael soon pulled his thoughts away from the name Arven Vale. Whether it truly was Director Arven or not, it had nothing to do with him for the moment.","His gaze shifted downward.","\"Where am I?\"","The ranking panel responded almost immediately.","[Rank 198: Michael Norman]","[Level: 75]","[Realm: Aurora]","Michael froze.","\"...198?\"","He had expected his ranking to be much lower. After all, everyone above him was Level 100.","Even below him, for another fifty positions or so, the names he skimmed past were still almost entirely Level 100 awakeners. Among them, his Level 75 was especially eye-catching.","Michael rubbed his chin with a thoughtful expression.","\"It probably counted my undead.\"","He was confident in himself, but not delusional. On his own, he didn't believe he could truly match a peak Rank Four monster. The only reason his position was this high had to be because of the High Drake.","The ranking rules had already stated that summons, contracted creatures, equipment, skills, and treasures all counted as part of one's strength.","Since his High Drake had fought against three peak Rank Four experts and survived, the Origin Will had clearly used that performance to evaluate him.","Still, Michael didn't fully trust the ranking.","\"This initial list is probably inaccurate.\"","After all, what if some terrifying person had entered the Origin Battlefield and done nothing for the past two hours?","What if someone was hiding their strength? What if someone had not encountered any strong enemies yet?","The ranking was based on early performance, not absolute strength. In a few days, it would most likely change drastically. Perhaps his own rank would be pushed down very soon.","As for whether he wanted to compete for the rankings, Michael decided to take a wait and see approach. He had no intention of eagerly fighting Level 100 monsters for monthly rewards without knowing what they were capable of.","Who knew what trump cards they had hidden?","Fortunately, the challenge system did leave him an escape route. If defeat became unavoidable, he could always choose to surrender. This made Michael considerably less resistant toward the ranking system.","After closing the leaderboard, he looked around at the various options floating before him.","\"...Hm?\"","There seemed to be more functions than he had initially noticed. His gaze soon landed on one labeled: [Personal Profile]","Without much hesitation, Michael selected it. The moment the panel expanded, he couldn't help but smile faintly.","\"Compared to the Land of Origin, this place really does feel more game-like.\"","Back when he had still been an ordinary person before awakening, countless rumors had described the mysterious world only awakeners could enter as something similar to a game.","Though the Land of Origin had done justice to that rumor in its own way, it still felt very real. Now that he was standing inside the Origin Battlefield himself, he had to admit it matched that old imagination surprisingly well.","The only difference was that death here was real. At least in the Land of Origin, one did not truly die.","Michael's attention returned to the panel.","[Profile]","Name: Michael Norman","Realm: Aurora","Level: 75","Current Rank: 198","Highest Rank Achieved: 198","Number of Victories: 0","Number of Defeats: 0","Number of Matches: 0","Monthly Reward Distribution In: 717 Hours 42 Minutes 11 Seconds Michael glanced at the final line.","\"...Thirty days.\"","More accurately, one month. Originally seven hundred and twenty hours. Now, just over two hours had already passed since everyone entered the Origin Battlefield.","Michael continued browsing through the profile. Besides the basic information, there wasn't anything else available yet.","\"It looks like more functions haven't been unlocked yet...\"","Michael wasn't particularly disappointed. The Origin Battlefield had only opened a little over two hours ago. If every function were available immediately, there would be little sense of progression.","Michael closed the profile panel. Since there was nothing else available for now, his attention naturally returned to the rankings.","A thought suddenly crossed his mind as he looked at his rank again.","Among the nearly two hundred names above him, he seemed to be the only Level 75. In other words, the only Rank Three.","Michael recalled the angel he had encountered earlier. The female angel was also Rank Three. And if she existed, then he wasn't the only Rank Three who had entered the Fourth Layer.","What he didn't know was whether it was just the two of them in the Fourth Layer, or if there were more, and if there were more, whether they had made it into the rankings.","Curiosity immediately surfaced in Michael's heart. Without wasting another second, he rapidly scrolled downward. The names passed before his eyes one after another.","Rank 250...","Rank 300...","Rank 400...","Rank 500...","His gaze swept across the list at astonishing speed until finally the list stopped at exactly one thousand entries.","Michael stared at the bottom of the list.","\"...Only a thousand.\"","A part of him had wondered if the rankings covered all awakeners in this layer. Now it seemed only one thousand awakeners in the entire Fourth Layer could occupy a ranking position.","Considering the sheer scale of the Origin Battlefield and the countless awakeners scattered throughout it, making the rankings at all was already an extraordinary achievement.","The fact that he had somehow entered at Rank 198 became even more absurd."]},{"number":1096,"title":"Chapter 1096: Challenged","paragraphs":["Michael gaze settled on the final entry.","[Rank 1000: Khoran]","[Level: 80]","[Realm: Ironpeak Realm]","\"Tsk. Even the weakest person currently occupying the rankings was still a Rank Four Awakener.\"","\"But...\"","As he muttered this, Michael's eyes shifted upward.","[Rank 999: Elys Arden]","[Level: 75]","[Realm: Verdant Eclipse Realm]","\"...Another Level 75.\"","Michael's expression became thoughtful.","Putting aside the ranking placement between second to last place and last place proved it couldn't be something that could be trusted , this was a Rank Three, just like him.","However, Verdant Eclipse Realm didn't sound like the realm of the angel civilization. If it wasn't, then this wasn't the female angel he had encountered earlier.","Including himself, there were only eight participants below Level 100, and every one of them was Level 75. The remaining nine hundred and ninety-two ranked participants were all Level 100.","While Michael wondered which among the eight was the female angel, since he didn't know her name and classes weren't listed, and none of the realms obviously pointed to angels, he didn't focus on it for too long.","He had a feeling they would cross paths again in the future.","What he was more curious about was whether these eight Rank Three participants were truly all that existed in the entire Fourth Layer.","Though it was possible, Michael felt it was a bit too few considering the seemingly infinite scale of the universe. But then again, to enter the Fourth Layer as a Rank Three, one had to have surpassed the extreme threshold of the previous layer.","Simply being able to compete with a Rank Four awakener as a Rank Three wouldn't be enough.","Michael's curiosity was finally satisfied.","He was just about to dismiss the panel and leave for another location when a new notification suddenly appeared before him.","[Ranking Challenge Request Received]","Michael blinked.","\"...Already?\"","A rather strange expression appeared on his face. To him, the hidden danger of the ranking system had been obvious almost immediately. Anyone with enough experience should have realized it even faster.","The rankings had only opened moments ago. Nobody knew anyone else's true strength or what terrifying trump cards others possessed. Blindly challenging strangers seemed reckless.","Then, almost as quickly, the answer occurred to him.","\"...My level.\"","Level seventy-five. Compared to the sea of Level 100s occupying the rankings, he practically looked like the weakest person available. To everyone else, he probably appeared to be an easy target.","Michael almost laughed.","\"So they picked the softest-looking fruit first.\"","Before he could simply ignore the notification, another panel abruptly appeared.","[Ranking Challenge Pending]","Challenger: Rank 206","Decision Time Remaining: 04:58","The seconds immediately began counting downward.","04:57...","04:56...","Michael raised an eyebrow.","\"So there's a time limit.\"","[Challenge Information]","Refusing this challenge will consume one refusal against this challenger.","Remaining Refusals Against This Challenger: 3/3","Remaining Universal Challenge Refusals This Month: 3/3","If all refusals against this challenger are exhausted, any further refusal will be treated as a forfeit.","Upon forfeiture, both participants will immediately exchange ranking positions.","Hint: Successfully defending your ranking in three official matches during a monthly cycle grants temporary challenge protection. Protected participants can refuse additional ranking challenges without issues until the next monthly settlement. However, accepting a challenge and losing will result in a rank switch.","Michael quietly read every line.","\"I see...\"","The challenge system was even more complete than he had expected. Overall, it was surprisingly well-balanced.","\"It seems the Origin Will has already considered most loopholes.\"","Heavens knew how long this battlefield had been waiting to be activated. There was truly a great deal to learn here.","Michael's gaze drifted back toward the countdown with a thoughtful expression.","As for the challenge request, Michael wasn't particularly nervous. Rank 206. Only eight places below him. This most likely meant the challenger's combat strength had been evaluated at around the same level as his own.","At least, according to the Origin Will. Whether that evaluation reflected reality was another matter entirely.","Michael rested his chin on his hand.","\"...Now the real question is, do I accept?\"","In the end, Michael's curiosity finally won.","He glanced at the steadily decreasing countdown and made his decision.","\"Accept.\"","The moment the words left his mouth, the panel dissolved into countless motes of blue light.","A shimmering portal silently opened before him. Without hesitation, Michael stepped through.","The surrounding space twisted. When his vision cleared, he found himself standing within an endless expanse of darkness.","Before Michael could inspect his surroundings, another translucent panel appeared before him.","[Ranking Challenge Accepted]","[Awaiting defender's battlefield selection]","[The defending participant has the authority to select the battlefield environment] [Different environments may possess different natural characteristics, which can influence the effectiveness of various abilities] [With the existence of environments, one cannot remain in the void] Before Michael could fully process what he had just read, another panel immediately appeared.","[Available Battlefields]","Endless Plains Ancient","Forest Frozen","Tundra Volcanic Region","Mountain Range","Underground Caverns","Ruined City Endless","Ocean Floating Islands","Crystal Canyon Storm Valley","Chaotic Rift ...","Michael slowly examined the list.","Every battlefield possessed unique natural conditions.","He found that he could even merge some environments. However, whatever option he chose would work both for and against him.","Michael nodded inwardly.","\"A reasonable system.\"","The defender already occupied the higher rank. Allowing them to choose the battlefield meant challengers wouldn't always be at the mercy of a scheming opponent.","This would also make challengers weigh their decision carefully before issuing one.","Michael's gaze swept across the countless battlefield options.","There were ordinary environments. And there were extreme ones.","A blazing volcanic world where rivers of magma flowed endlessly.","An endless ocean beneath perpetual storms.","A shattered mountain range covered in violent spatial cracks.","A ruined city swallowed by poisonous mist.","As he continued reading, two options immediately caught his attention.","[Land of Eternal Death]","Description: A world saturated with dense death energy. Extended exposure gradually erodes vitality.","[Frozen Rain Expanse]","Description: A frozen world beneath an endless black sky. Cold rain never ceases to fall. Every drop contains dense Yin and cold energy that slowly drains warmth and life from living beings."]},{"number":1097,"title":"Chapter 1097: What Advantage Did I Say I Have Again?","paragraphs":["Michael's eyes lingered on the two descriptions.","To most awakeners, these two battlefields would probably be among the worst possible choices.","Simply existing inside either environment would constantly consume their energy. Their movements would gradually become sluggish while their vitality slowly weakened.","Yet for Michael, the exact opposite was true. He himself cultivated Death Energy. His undead practically thrived on it. Inside such an environment, they would feel as comfortable as fish returning to water.","It might not be enough to make them overwhelmingly stronger, but fighting in a place naturally filled with compatible energy was always preferable to fighting somewhere completely hostile.","After only a brief moment of consideration, Michael made his decision.","\"The Land of Eternal Death and the Frozen Rain Expanse.\"","[Battlefield Created Successfully]","Name: Deathfrost Rainlands","Description: A world where endless freezing rain falls beneath a sky consumed by death. Dense Death Energy and Yin Cold Energy permeate every corner of the battlefield.","Living creatures continuously suffer the erosion of both vitality and warmth, while beings aligned with negative energies naturally recover and become more active within the environment.","The instant he confirmed his choice, the surrounding darkness trembled. The battlefield selection panel disappeared. Space distorted.","Then the world changed.","An endless gray sky stretched overhead. Black clouds covered the heavens completely.","Drizzle. Drizzle.","Cold rain descended endlessly from above. Every raindrop carried a faint trace of gray Death Energy mixed with biting Yin Cold.","The earth beneath his feet had long since frozen solid, yet instead of white snow, the entire landscape was covered in black frost.","Dead forests stood silently in the distance. Not a single leaf remained upon their twisted branches. Gray mist drifted lazily across the frozen ground, making the entire world resemble a realm abandoned by life itself.","Michael slowly inhaled.","The surrounding Death Energy naturally entered his body. Rather than discomfort, he felt his condition improving slightly.","A faint smile appeared on his face.","\"This place will do.\"","A final panel appeared before him.","[Battlefield: Deathfrost Rainlands]","[Match Status: Active]","[Ranking Challenge Participants]","Defender: Michael Norman","Rank: 198","Level: 75","Realm: Aurora","-","VS","-","Challenger: Varek Dros","Rank: 206","Level: 100","Realm: Ironpeak Realm","[Victory Conditions]","Eliminate the opposing participant.","Opposing participant voluntarily surrenders.","Michael looked around. There was no one in sight. Only the endless frozen wasteland and the ceaseless black rain.","He narrowed his eyes slightly.","\"So we've been placed separately...\"","The match had already begun. Both participants had entered the same battlefield, but they would have to find each other first.","\"I wonder if it will work.\"","Michael's first instinct was to test the earlier notification that stated one could not remain in the void with the existence of environments.","If that restriction also affected teleportation, his mobility would be greatly reduced.","Without hesitating, Michael focused on a jagged cliff rising several hundred meters away.","Space around him distorted.","Whoosh!","His figure vanished. A fraction of a second later, he appeared atop the cliff overlooking the frozen wasteland.","\"...It worked.\"","Michael turned to observe his surroundings. He looked down at his own hands before silently sensing the surrounding space.","\"So that's what it meant. The battlefield hadn't prohibited teleportation itself. Instead, it prevented participants from remaining inside the void.\"","Michael understood the theory immediately. His own teleportation only involved momentarily passing through the void before emerging almost instantly.","The time spent there was practically negligible.","However, there were spatial abilities that allowed users to hide inside the void or even launch attacks from that hidden dimension.","Those techniques were most likely what the Origin Will had restricted seeing as the surface level of the void was still accessible.","Michael nodded inwardly.","\"That makes far more sense.\"","Otherwise, countless spatial talents would have become almost useless the moment a ranking battle began.","Instead, the battlefield only prevented participants from abusing the void as a place to hide or continuously move through.","It wasn't a restriction on spatial abilities. It was a restriction on using the void itself as part of the battlefield.","After confirming this, Michael slowly surveyed his surroundings from atop the cliff. The visibility wasn't particularly good.","Gray mist drifted endlessly across the land while black rain continuously fell from the heavens and dead forests stretched toward the horizon, broken only by scattered mountains and frozen valleys.","Even from this height, he couldn't see another living figure.","\"It seems we were placed quite far apart.\"","Michael wasn't surprised. If both participants were dropped beside each other, there would be little purpose in creating such an enormous battlefield.","Searching for the opponent was clearly intended to be part of the challenge itself.","His perception spread outward. Within the Deathfrost Rainlands, his senses felt noticeably sharper than usual.","The drifting Death Energy almost seemed willing to carry information back to him. Still, there were no signs of another living being within range.","Michael's gaze shifted toward the endless dead forest in the distance.","\"If I were the challenger...\"","His eyes narrowed slightly.","\"...I'd probably head for higher ground first as well.\"","With that thought, Michael stepped off the cliff.","Instead of falling, he teleported repeatedly across the frozen landscape, each spatial jump carrying him several hundred meters closer to the heart of the battlefield, while he continuously searched for the Level 100 Rank Four Awakener who was, at that very moment, undoubtedly searching for him as well.","However, what Michael hadn't expected was his opponent to reveal their own location openly.","Standing atop another mountain several kilometers away was a massive skeletal dragon.","Its wings stretched well over thirty meters. Its eye sockets burned with ghostly emerald flames.","Standing upon its skull was a broad-shouldered man clad in armor forged from black bone.","Even from several kilometers away, Michael could clearly sense the aura of a peak Rank Four Awakener.","\"...\"","Michael's expression stiffened. His lips twitched involuntarily.","\"So that's how it is. Oh, what a great home advantage.\"","His gaze slowly shifted from the rider back to the bone dragon beneath him. Then toward the countless wisps of Death Energy drifting throughout the battlefield.","His lips twitched again."]},{"number":1098,"title":"Chapter 1098: So This Is How To Play Necromancer? [1]","paragraphs":["\"This is actually my first time dealing with an awakener who uses undead creatures too. I wonder what class he has. Necromancer? Dark Knight? Something else?\"","Unfortunately, though he was curious, Michael couldn't use Detect on the fellow.","Though one's abilities and skills grew stronger as they advanced in rank, his current distance exceeded the range of Detect, and he didn't dare move closer in case the other party dragged him into their domain.","Though a domain involved entering a separate layer of space, Michael didn't think the Origin Battlefield, especially at the Fourth Layer, would restrict awakeners from using one.","This was different from when he had fought the royal family of the Black Serpent Empire.","Back then, thanks to his combat prowess, they hadn't known he wasn't actually at their rank and couldn't use a domain against him. But in the Origin Battlefield, one's level was already out in the open. He wouldn't expect peak Rank Four supernaturals to not use every advantage available when needed.","Keeping his distance was the wiser decision for now. In any case, once they started fighting, he would figure out the other party's fighting style soon enough.","Besides, one should always be careful about judging an awakener purely by their class. Who could one blame if someone with a Mage class fought like a Knight?","The moment he saw the colossal skeletal dragon, he immediately activated one of his engravings and summoned his undead High Drake.","A deafening roar split the Deathfrost Rainlands as a massive draconic figure burst into existence above Michael.","Unlike the skeletal dragon in the distance, the High Drake still possessed most of its flesh. Reddish scales covered its enormous body.","Death Energy leaked continuously from it, and its green eyes immediately locked onto the distant bone dragon.","At almost the exact same moment, the armored man standing atop the skeletal dragon had moved as well.","The bone dragon let out a thunderous roar before beating its enormous wings.","BOOM!","The mountain beneath it cracked as the gigantic creature launched itself into the air. Its rider remained standing calmly atop its skull, showing no intention of hiding behind his mount.","Michael's High Drake answered with a roar of its own.","The two draconic creatures accelerated toward one another through the freezing rain. The distance between them rapidly disappeared.","Five kilometers. Four. Three.","Neither side slowed. The surrounding air trembled beneath the pressure radiating from the two flying monsters.","Although his High Drake wasn't currently receiving the amplification from his law skill, that hardly meant it was weak. Its base strength alone already surpassed the overwhelming majority of peak Rank Four supernaturals.","The two dragons opened their jaws almost simultaneously. Energy gathered violently. The bone dragon's throat filled with blue radiance. Michael's High Drake condensed dense red fiery energy that mixed with the surrounding Yin Cold, forming a sphere so compressed that the nearby rain evaporated before touching it.","The two riders watched silently.","Then—","ROOOAAARRR!!","BOOM!","Twin dragon breaths erupted across the battlefield. The blue torrent from the skeletal dragon tore through the sky like a river of ghostly fire.","Michael's High Drake answered with an immense pillar of red destructive energy. The two attacks collided midway between the dragons.","The world exploded.","An enormous shockwave swept across the frozen landscape, scattering gray mist for kilometers as black rain was blown completely away from the collision point.","The clash continued for several long seconds.","Neither dragon gave ground. Blue flames devoured red fiery energy while the undead High Drake's dragon breath steadily eroded the ghostly fire with overwhelming density.","Below them, entire sections of the dead forest were flattened by the pressure alone.","The very first exchange of the battle had already reached a level capable of annihilating ordinary Rank Four awakeners.","However, both Michael and Varek knew this was nothing more than a warm-up. Dragon Breath was devastating, but it was also the most straightforward method of testing an opponent's strength.","Neither of them had expected the exchange to decide the battle.","The instant the two torrents of energy dispersed into the freezing rain, both dragons beat their wings and separated, creating several hundred meters of distance between themselves.","Varek moved first.","Standing atop the skull of his skeletal dragon, he slowly brought both palms together. An enormous quantity of energy surged toward him. The air trembled.","One after another, pitch-black magic circles bloomed across the sky.","Ten. Twenty. Fifty. One hundred.","Their sizes varied dramatically. Some were barely a meter across, while others exceeded twenty meters in diameter, rotating slowly above the battlefield like gateways into another world.","The next moment, countless razor-sharp tips seemingly made from bone slowly emerged from within the circles.","Some were no larger than ordinary javelins. Others were colossal, each exceeding thirty meters in length, resembling gigantic lances capable of piercing mountains.","The freezing rain rattled against the countless white spears as they continued emerging from the arrays.","\"...\"","Michael's eyebrows rose in genuine surprise.","\"I know this skill!\"","He was genuinely surprised, not simply because of the sheer scale, but because this was one of the undead skills he possessed himself.","Bone Spear.","Granted, the version before him was obviously many times stronger than the one Michael currently wielded.","After all, Varek was a genuine peak Rank Four awakener who had likely spent years adding his own modifications to the spell, perfecting it for his own use.","Michael smiled as a slightly crazy idea came to him.","Ever since suspecting the other party might be a Necromancer, even knowing the other party was a Level 100 awakener, this was the first time Michael had come across an awakener like himself.","He couldn't help but want to see how such a person fought, and whether there was anything worth learning from them.","\"If that's what you want...\"","\"Then let's compare.\"","Michael's energy erupted outward.","Unlike Varek, Michael didn't possess a Level 100 status. But there was one thing he had absolute confidence in.","His mana reserves."]},{"number":1099,"title":"Chapter 1099: So This Is How To Play Necromancer? [2]","paragraphs":["Even though he was only Level 75 and hadn't yet reached Rank Four, there were very few Rank Four awakeners he believed could rival him in pure energy reserves.","After everything he had accumulated since awakening, his mana pool had long surpassed what should have been possible for his level.","Michael extended a single hand toward the sky.","Blackish-green magic circles appeared one after another above the High Drake.","One. Five. Ten. Twenty. Thirty.","The number continued increasing. Bone spearheads slowly emerged from every array, identical in shape to Varek's own spell.","Across the battlefield, Varek's expression finally changed.","\"...Interesting.\"","His voice drifted across the frozen wasteland.","\"But young man, I advise you to be careful. Just because you're at a lower rank than me doesn't mean I'll take it easy on you. To avoid accidents that could lead to your death, it would be better if you surrendered quickly.\"","Michael merely smiled and didn't reply.","Please.","What was that awakener thinking? That he would surrender so easily when neither of them had truly shown what they were capable of?","\"Fortunately... I'm quite familiar with the spear.\"","As Michael spoke, the sky rapidly filled with countless Bone Spears.","The gigantic variants cast enormous shadows over the frozen forests below. Bone Spears filled the sky until it resembled a forest suspended in the heavens.","Every spear radiated dense energy, their razor-sharp tips aimed toward the opposing awakener.","The freezing rain seemed insignificant beneath the overwhelming magical pressure gathering above the Deathfrost Rainlands.","Then both men moved. Without a word or warning. They lowered their hands almost simultaneously.","The world erupted.","BOOM!","Hundreds of Bone Spears screamed through the air. The sky darkened as countless white projectiles crossed the battlefield from opposite directions. The collision came almost instantly.","BOOM! BOOM! BOOM! BOOM!","One Bone Spear met another.","The heavens exploded repeatedly.","Spears shattered into clouds of bone fragments before their Death Energy detonated violently, producing shockwaves that rippled through the freezing rain.","The battlefield trembled. For several seconds, neither side gained an advantage. Every spear Michael launched was intercepted by one of Varek's.","Every spear Varek fired found an equal counterpart. The barrage continued relentlessly. It was less like two awakeners exchanging spells and more like two armies bombarding one another.","Explosions echoed without pause. Entire sections of dead forest disappeared beneath the falling debris. The frozen ground split open again and again under the continuous impacts.","Unfortunately, in the end, Varek's superior realm and experience granted him more refined control and stronger individual Bone Spears.","Michael compensated through sheer quantity and an almost unreasonable mana reserve. For the moment, the two advantages balanced one another. But it could only last for so long.","Several of Varek's larger spears overpowered Michael's smaller ones after destroying them and continued flying forward, their momentum only slightly reduced.","The surviving lances descended toward him like falling mountains.","Michael didn't hesitate.","Space distorted.","Whoosh!","He vanished from the drake's back. A fraction of a second later, he reappeared hundreds of meters away in the freezing sky.","The enormous Bone Spears tore through the space he had occupied.","BOOOOM!!","The explosions swallowed his previous position entirely. Even his High Drake was forced to dive violently to avoid the expanding shockwaves. The blast wave rolled across the battlefield like a tsunami, flattening everything beneath it.","Michael narrowed his eyes in annoyance.","Far in the distance, Varek watched the young necromancer calmly, but inside he was beginning to feel a trace of unease.","As expected, someone who could enter a space meant for Rank Four while still at Rank Three had to be something special.","To think the person he was more than twenty levels above dared to compete with him in raw mana. The audacity alone was remarkable.","However, though the young man was full of surprises, Varek didn't believe he would be the one losing this match.","Michael had only just steadied himself in the air when his eyes narrowed.","\"...Hm? So the bone spears weren't the true attack?\"","It appeared that while Michael had been focused on countering the overwhelming barrage, two magic circles had quietly remained active behind the collapsing sea of explosions.","Unlike the hundreds of circles used for Bone Spear, these two had been concealed by the constant detonations. Only now, after the barrage had subsided, did they fully reveal themselves.","They also just happened to be circles Michael could recognize, and could replicate himself if he chose to.","\"...Undead Summoning.\"","He recognized the spell immediately.","Though it had been modified and was far more complex than anything he knew, Michael was confident it was indeed the Undead Summoning skill.","The two enormous circles pulsed once. Then tore open.","ROOOOAR!","A skeletal wyvern burst from the first portal, its massive wings scattering freezing rain as emerald soul flames blazed within its hollow eyes.","From the second emerged another undead creature.","This one resembled a gigantic bone chimera, four-legged and covered in overlapping skeletal plates, with an enormous skull and a barbed tail formed entirely from sharpened vertebrae.","The two undead landed beside Varek's dragon almost instantly, making it three undead behemoths, all seemingly at level 100.","Michael couldn't help but smile bitterly.","Truthfully, he hadn't used Undead Summoning very often after obtaining stronger methods like his engravings or storage treasures that offered greater convenience.","Since the other party had gotten a little more serious, Michael also responded in kind and summoned two creatures of his own.","Soon, two figures were standing by his side. Their auras were unmistakably Rank Four.","The two were the ancestors of the Black Serpent Empire, now both at level 98. Just two levels below the peak, but still far from it.","Immediately after appearing, their bodies began changing.","Their human forms elongated rapidly. Within seconds, the two elderly figures had transformed into enormous serpents, each well over three meters in length.","Hiss!","The pair coiled through the freezing air beside Michael's High Drake, their enormous eyes immediately locking onto Varek's newly summoned undead."]},{"number":1100,"title":"Chapter 1100: So This Is How To Play Necromancer? [3]","paragraphs":["Knowing the other party was getting serious, though Michael was curious to see how other necromancers fought, he wouldn't completely joke with his life.","The instant the two undead Black Serpent Empire ancestors transformed into their true forms, he cast a skill the very next second.","\"Death Ground!\"","[Class Skill]: Death's Ground {Perfect Mastery}","[Description]:","The user designates an area as consecrated ground. The domain pulses with the authority of death itself, enforcing the user's will upon all that stands within it.","Undead under the user's command are recognized as extensions of that authority.","The domain persists as long as the user maintains focus or remains within range.","[Effect 1]: All undead within the domain receive +35% Durability, +25% Regeneration, and +20% to all attributes.","[Effect 2]: Fallen enemies within the domain have a chance to rise as undead under the user's temporary command.","[Effect 3]: The domain passively suppresses the combat ability of living enemies within range by 10%.","[Stat Buff]: Strength +10%, Constitution +25%, Agility +10%, Intelligence +20%","[Range]: Scales with Intelligence. At perfect mastery, base range is significantly expanded.","Compared to the amount of energy using his law skill would consume, though the increase wasn't as monstrous, it was still very significant.","Michael's three undead had their power shoot up by varying degrees, making even the two Level 98 undead not fall behind in might compared to the opponent's fully Level 100 undead.","Thanks to his class further boosting dark-related arts, the increase on his undead was actually a bit stronger than what the skill description showed.","The moment Death's Ground spread outward, the entire Deathfrost Rainlands seemed to respond. Gray mist surged from him, expanding rapidly until it swallowed several miles around him.","The freezing rain became heavier, each drop carrying denser death energy than before. When one added the environment to the calculation, the increase the undead received was even greater than usual.","Varek's eyes narrowed.","\"So you also have a domain-type skill...\"","His annoyance became even more obvious.","To be honest, he hadn't challenged Michael because of some deep scheme.","It was spite. Seeing a Level 75 awakener ranked above him had made him feel uncomfortable.","No matter how special the other party was, Varek had entered the Fourth Layer as a genuine peak Rank Four necromancer.","Being placed below a Rank Three being was naturally humiliating.","Before entering the arena, he had expected a simple victory. And in all honesty, his judgment had not been completely wrong.","If his opponent had been almost anyone else at this ranking range, he might already have won.","Unfortunately, his opponent was Michael.","Knowing the other party was very strong, potentially stronger than any single one of the three that had faced his undead High Drake earlier, Michael had no choice but to fight seriously.","Across the battlefield, Varek also quickly steadied his thoughts. Michael was troublesome. That much was undeniable. But troublesome did not mean undefeatable.","Since Michael had used a support skill to strengthen his undead, it was only fair that he used one as well.","Varek raised his bone staff. A dark ring of light spread beneath his feet.","\"Bone King's Command.\"","The skeletal dragon beneath him released a thunderous roar. The wyvern's wings expanded. The bone chimera lowered its body as sharp bone spikes erupted across its back.","At the same time, a crown-shaped mark appeared above the heads of all three undead. Their auras rose together, and the soul flames in their eyes burned brighter.","Michael's gaze sharpened slightly.","\"So he had a strengthening skill too.\"","The next moment, both sides moved.","The skeletal dragon opened its enormous jaws first.","ROOOOOAR!!","A torrent of pale-green dragon breath erupted forward. The freezing rain evaporated wherever it passed, leaving behind a trail of distorted air as the attack surged across the battlefield.","The High Drake reacted immediately. Its green eyes flared as it spread its enormous wings. Deep within its throat, blazing red flames rapidly gathered before erupting outward.","BOOOOOOM!!","A pillar of scarlet fire roared across the battlefield. The two breaths collided head-on.","The impact detonated like a collapsing volcano, generating violent shockwaves that swept across the frozen landscape. Dead forests were uprooted while countless chunks of black ice were hurled into the sky.","At almost the same instant, the skeletal wyvern folded its wings before diving toward one of the Black Serpent ancestors.","The serpent surrounded by blue flames slowly raised its enormous head. Its pupils narrowed. The blue fire coating its scales intensified until it resembled an ocean of sapphire flames.","Hiss!","Rather than retreat, it lunged directly toward the descending wyvern. The instant the two entered striking distance, the serpent opened its jaws. A torrent of azure fire burst skyward.","The skeletal wyvern beat its massive wings. Dark winds crashed against the incoming inferno.","BOOOOM!!","Blue flames erupted across its skeletal frame. Several ribs cracked beneath the impact, yet the wyvern forced its way through the sea of fire. Its razor-sharp claws slashed downward.","The serpent's enormous body twisted gracefully through the air. The claws barely grazed its scales before its burning tail whipped upward like a blazing spear.","BANG!","The strike smashed directly into the wyvern's ribs, sending the undead creature tumbling across the dark sky.","Meanwhile, the bone chimera had already charged toward the second Black Serpent ancestor.","Unlike its sibling, this serpent wasn't surrounded by blue flames. Soft pink fire danced elegantly around its enormous body. The flames appeared gentle. Almost beautiful.","The serpent coiled through the air before opening its mouth. Instead of launching ordinary fire, dozens of flower-shaped flames blossomed into existence.","Each resembled a fully bloomed lotus crafted entirely from pink fire. The blossoms drifted silently toward the charging chimera.","At first glance, they appeared harmless. Then they exploded upon contact.","BOOOOM!!","Pink flames erupted violently. Before the chimera could recover, more blossoms attached themselves across its massive skeletal body.","One. Three. Seven. In the blink of an eye, dozens of flaming flowers had bloomed across its bones.","The next moment, every blossom detonated simultaneously."]}]);
